/* 文法章節：26 章（句子基礎、時態、助動詞與語態、不定詞動名詞分詞、形容詞副詞比較、連接詞與子句、假設與特殊句型），每章有學習目標、先備章節，每一節依序是核心規則、進階補充（摺疊）、結構圖解（parse: S 主詞・V 動詞・O 受詞・C 補語・M 修飾・J 連接）、例句、常見錯誤（mistakes[].sec）與 1–2 題小練習，章末有統測重點與 8 題小測驗。由 AI 撰寫；第二版經資深教師角度逐句審查修正，題目由不看答案的解題者、圖解由不看答案的分析者驗證；無法確認的地方列在 pending（顯示為「待審」）。[[ ]] 標出例句裡的文法重點，**粗體** 標出關鍵詞。 */
window.GRAMMAR_DATA = {"units":[["basic","句子基礎","🧱","句型、問句、名詞、代名詞、介系詞、主詞動詞一致","句子基礎"],["tense","時態","⏰","現在式、過去式、未來式、完成式","時態"],["verb","助動詞與語態","🔧","助動詞、被動語態、使役與感官動詞","助動詞・語態"],["verbal","不定詞、動名詞與分詞","🔀","to V、V-ing、分詞、分詞構句","不定詞・分詞"],["adj","形容詞、副詞與比較","🎨","形容詞與副詞、比較級與最高級","形容詞・比較"],["clause","連接詞與子句","🔗","連接詞、關係子句、名詞子句","連接詞・子句"],["special","假設與特殊句型","✨","假設語氣、倒裝句、強調句","假設・倒裝"]],"chapters":[{"id":"g-sentence","unit":"basic","level":"A2","title":"句子的基本結構","en":"Sentence patterns","lead":"句子的骨架是 S + V，動詞決定後面要接受詞、補語，或什麼都不接。","goals":["能找出句子的主詞、動詞、受詞和補語","能分辨五大句型，判斷動詞後面要接什麼","能在連綴動詞和受詞補語的位置選對詞類"],"prereq":[],"pending":[{"where":"sections[1]","note":"be + 地點片語，部分教材歸為 S+V 加地方副詞；本站標為補語，統測慣例待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"詞類：字在句中的角色","text":["英文的字依功能分成不同**詞類**，詞類決定它能放在句中哪個位置。"],"adv":["同一個字可能有不同詞類，要看它在句中的用法：a fast train 的 fast 是形容詞，run fast 的 fast 是副詞。-ly 副詞的變化詳見〈形容詞與副詞〉。"],"table":{"cols":["詞類","在句中的角色","例子"],"rows":[["名詞、代名詞","當主詞、受詞或補語","[[Amy]] likes [[mangoes]]."],["動詞","說明動作或狀態，完整的句子一定要有","Amy [[likes]] mangoes."],["形容詞","修飾名詞，或當補語","[[spicy]] noodles / It's [[spicy]]."],["副詞","修飾動詞、形容詞、副詞或整句","run [[fast]] / [[very]] cold"],["介系詞","後接名詞、代名詞受格或動名詞，組成介系詞片語，當修飾語或補語","[[at]] the night market / [[with]] him"]]},"parse":{"en":"The new student speaks English really well.","zh":"那位新同學英文說得很好。","parts":[["The new student","S"],["speaks","V"],["English","O"],["really well.","M","副詞，修飾 speaks"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The [[new]] student speaks English [[really well]].","zh":"那位新同學英文說得很好。"},{"en":"My dad works [[at]] a convenience store [[near]] our school.","zh":"我爸在我們學校附近的便利商店上班。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Jason is a ______ runner. He always wins first place in the school race.","options":["quick","quickly","quickness"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：形容詞修飾名詞。空格後是名詞 runner，要用形容詞 quick。(B) quickly 是副詞，修飾動詞，如 run quickly；(C) quickness 是名詞，不能修飾 runner。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Jenny sat next to ______ on the MRT this morning.","options":["I","me","my"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：介系詞後接代名詞受格。next to 是介系詞，後面用受格 me。(A) I 是主格，用來當主詞；(C) my 是所有格，後面要接名詞，如 my brother。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"句子成分：S、V、O、C","text":["**主詞 (S)** 是句子在說的人或事物；**動詞 (V)** 說明主詞做什麼或處於什麼狀態。完整的句子都要有 S 和 V，祈使句則省略主詞 you。","**受詞 (O)** 是動作的對象，放在及物動詞後面；**補語 (C)** 補充說明主詞或受詞「是什麼、怎麼樣」。","當**修飾語**的副詞、介系詞片語不算句型成分，拿掉後剩下骨架；但當補語的不能拿掉，如 She is in the kitchen. 的 in the kitchen 是地點補語。"],"adv":["put（放）後面一定要接地點，live（居住）通常也要，例如 put the book on the desk、live in Taipei，這些介系詞片語不能拿掉。"],"table":{"cols":["成分","誰可以當","例句"],"rows":[["主詞 S","名詞、代名詞主格、動名詞","[[My mom]] sells scallion pancakes."],["動詞 V","be 動詞、一般動詞","My mom [[sells]] scallion pancakes."],["受詞 O","名詞、代名詞受格、動名詞、不定詞","Kevin called [[me]]. / I enjoy [[swimming]]."],["補語 C","形容詞、名詞、介系詞片語","This bubble tea is [[too sweet]]. / Mom is [[at work]]."]]},"parse":{"en":"Mom is in the kitchen right now.","zh":"媽媽現在在廚房。","parts":[["Mom","S"],["is","V"],["in the kitchen","C","地點補語"],["right now.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My brother [[plays]] [[basketball]] after school.","zh":"我弟弟放學後會去打籃球。"},{"en":"The night market [[is]] [[really crowded]] on Saturdays.","zh":"夜市星期六都人擠人。"},{"en":"Grandpa [[is]] [[at the park]] with his friends.","zh":"爺爺和朋友在公園。"}],"practice":[{"q":"A: Where's Mom? B: She ______. She's making dinner.","options":["in the kitchen","is","is in the kitchen","cooking in the kitchen"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：句子要有動詞，be 後的地點補語不能省略。(C) 有動詞 is 也有地點，句意完整。(A) 少了動詞 is；(B) 只說 She is. 缺少地點補語；(D) cooking 前面少了 be 動詞。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"S+V 與 S+V+O","text":["**不及物動詞**後面不接受詞，形成 S+V，如 arrive、happen、sleep。要接對象時，先加介系詞：listen to music、wait for the bus。","**及物動詞**後面要接受詞，形成 S+V+O。discuss、enter、reach（到達）、marry 直接接受詞，不說 discuss about。","很多動詞兩種用法都有，例如 I'm eating. 和 I'm eating lunch. 都對。"],"adv":["「和某人結婚」說 marry sb 或 get married to sb，不說 marry with sb。","名詞 discussion 則可以接 about：a discussion about the trip。"],"formula":"S + V（不及物）／S + V + O（及物）","parse":{"en":"We discussed the class trip at lunch.","zh":"我們午餐時討論了校外教學。","parts":[["We","S"],["discussed","V","及物動詞"],["the class trip","O"],["at lunch.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The MRT train [[arrived]] two minutes late.","zh":"捷運晚了兩分鐘才進站。"},{"en":"Yu-ting [[listens to]] K-pop on her way to school.","zh":"雨婷上學路上都會聽韓團的歌。"},{"en":"Our class [[discussed]] the plan for the school fair.","zh":"我們班討論了園遊會的計畫。"}],"practice":[{"q":"After a four-hour train ride, we finally ______ Kaohsiung at noon.","options":["arrived","reached","got","went"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：及物與不及物動詞。reach 是及物動詞，直接接地點 Kaohsiung。(A) arrive 不及物，要說 arrived in；(C) get 要說 got to；(D) go 要說 went to。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"S+V+C：連綴動詞","text":["be 動詞和**連綴動詞**後面接補語，說明主詞是什麼或怎麼樣。常見的連綴動詞有 look、sound、feel、seem、become、smell、taste、get。","look、feel、taste 等連綴動詞後的補語用**形容詞**，不用副詞：說 look tired，不說 look tiredly。","同一個動詞當**一般動詞**時（look at、taste the soup），修飾動作要用副詞：taste the soup carefully。"],"adv":["I don't feel well. 的 well 是形容詞，指「身體好」。be 動詞後也可接地點副詞或介系詞片語：She is here. / He is at school.","become 可直接接名詞（become a nurse）；look、sound、feel、seem 接名詞時，美式英語通常加 like：look like a model。"],"formula":"S + be 動詞／連綴動詞 + 形容詞（或名詞）","parse":{"en":"You look tired today.","zh":"你今天看起來很累。","parts":[["You","S"],["look","V","連綴動詞"],["tired","C","主詞補語"],["today.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"You [[look tired]]. Did you stay up late again?","zh":"你看起來好累，又熬夜了嗎？"},{"en":"This stinky tofu [[smells terrible]] but [[tastes great]].","zh":"這臭豆腐聞起來很臭，吃起來卻很讚。"},{"en":"My cousin [[became a nurse]] after college.","zh":"我表姊大學畢業後當了護理師。"},{"en":"A trip to Kenting this summer? That [[sounds like]] fun!","zh":"今年暑假去墾丁玩？聽起來很好玩！"}],"practice":[{"q":"This milk tea smells ______. Can I try some?","options":["sweetly","sweetness","sweet"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：連綴動詞 + 形容詞。smell 在這裡是「聞起來」，是連綴動詞，後面用形容詞 sweet 當補語。(A) sweetly 是副詞；(B) sweetness 是名詞，不能直接放在 smell 後當補語。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"S+V+O+O：人＋物","text":["give、send、buy 等動詞可接兩個受詞，順序是**人＋物**：give sb sth。人是間接受詞，物是直接受詞。","物放前面時，人前面要加介系詞：give sth to sb。傳給對方用 **to**；替對方做或買用 **for**。","物是代名詞時，通常說 give it to me。explain、describe 不能接兩個受詞：不說 explain me sth，要說 explain sth to sb。"],"adv":["要解釋的內容很長或是子句時，explain 也可以把 to sb 放前面：Can you explain to me why you were late?"],"formula":"S + V + 人 + 物 = S + V + 物 + to/for + 人","table":{"cols":["介系詞","常見動詞","例子"],"rows":[["to","give, send, show, tell, lend, teach","lend my notes [[to]] Amy"],["for","buy, make, cook, get","cook dinner [[for]] my family"]]},"parse":{"en":"Grandma gave me a red envelope on Lunar New Year's Eve.","zh":"除夕夜奶奶給了我一個紅包。","parts":[["Grandma","S"],["gave","V"],["me","O","間接受詞"],["a red envelope","O","直接受詞"],["on Lunar New Year's Eve.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Grandma gave [[me a red envelope]] on Lunar New Year's Eve.","zh":"除夕夜奶奶給了我一個紅包。"},{"en":"Can you send [[the photos to me]] tonight?","zh":"你今晚可以把照片傳給我嗎？"},{"en":"Dad made [[pancakes for us]] on Sunday morning.","zh":"爸爸星期天早上做了鬆餅給我們吃。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My uncle bought ______ for my sixteenth birthday.","options":["a new phone me","me a new phone","to me a new phone","a new phone to me"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：S+V+O+O，人＋物。buy sb sth，人在前不加介系詞：bought me a new phone。(A) 物在前時，人前要加 for；(C) 人在前不加 to；(D) buy 要用 for，不用 to。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"S+V+O+C：受詞＋補語","text":["受詞後接**受詞補語**，說明受詞是什麼或怎麼樣，如 make、keep、find、call、elect。補語常用形容詞或名詞，不用 happily 這類副詞。","分辨 OO 和 OC：make me a cake 的 me ≠ a cake（S+V+O+O）；make me happy 的 me = happy（S+V+O+C）。","「覺得做某事很…」用**虛受詞** it 代替後面的 to V：find it hard to V。受詞補語是原形、V-ing、p.p. 時，詳見〈使役動詞與感官動詞〉。"],"adv":["make 也常這樣用虛受詞 it：The MRT makes it easy to get around Taipei.","to V 是 find 的真受詞時才放 it（find it hard to V）；I found a way to fix it. 的 to V 修飾 a way，不加 it。"],"formula":"S + V + O + C（形容詞／名詞）","parse":{"en":"The long bus ride made everyone sleepy.","zh":"公車坐了好久，大家都昏昏欲睡。","parts":[["The long bus ride","S"],["made","V"],["everyone","O"],["sleepy.","C","受詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The hot weather [[made]] everyone [[sleepy]] in class.","zh":"天氣太熱，大家上課都昏昏欲睡。"},{"en":"Please [[keep]] the door [[open]] to let in some fresh air.","zh":"請把門開著，讓新鮮空氣進來。"},{"en":"Our class [[elected]] Tina [[class president]].","zh":"我們班選 Tina 當班長。"},{"en":"I [[find it hard]] to get up early on Mondays.","zh":"每到星期一，我都覺得早起好難。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Grandma's thick blanket keeps me ______ on cold winter nights.","options":["warm","warmly","warmth"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：S+V+O+C，受詞補語用形容詞。keep me warm 表示讓我保持溫暖，me = warm。(B) warmly 是副詞，不說 keep me warmly；(C) warmth 是名詞，我 ≠ 溫暖本身。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"She sings very good.","right":"She sings very [[well]].","why":"修飾動詞 sings 要用副詞 well；good 是形容詞。","sec":0},{"wrong":"My sister very tall.","right":"My sister [[is]] very tall.","why":"句子一定要有動詞；這裡缺 be 動詞，very tall 前要加 is。","sec":1},{"wrong":"We discussed about the school trip in class.","right":"We [[discussed]] the school trip in class.","why":"discuss 是及物動詞，直接接受詞，不加 about。","sec":2},{"wrong":"I'm waiting you at Taipei Main Station.","right":"I'm [[waiting for]] you at Taipei Main Station.","why":"wait 接要等的人或事物時，要先加 for。","sec":2},{"wrong":"This bubble tea tastes well.","right":"This bubble tea tastes [[good]].","why":"taste 是連綴動詞，後面接形容詞 good，不接副詞 well。","sec":3},{"wrong":"You look like tired today.","right":"You [[look tired]] today.","why":"look 後面直接接形容詞 tired，不加 like。","sec":3},{"wrong":"Can you explain me this question?","right":"Can you explain this question [[to me]]?","why":"explain 不能接兩個受詞，要用 explain sth to sb。","sec":4},{"wrong":"Dad bought a new bike to me.","right":"Dad bought a new bike [[for]] me.","why":"buy 把物放前面時，人前面用 for，不用 to。","sec":4},{"wrong":"Her jokes always make us happily.","right":"Her jokes always make us [[happy]].","why":"make + O + C，補語說明受詞狀態，用形容詞 happy。","sec":5},{"wrong":"I find hard to wake up early.","right":"I [[find it hard]] to wake up early.","why":"find + 形容詞 + to V 時，to V 是真受詞，要先放虛受詞 it。","sec":5}],"tips":["連綴動詞後的空格選形容詞：把動詞換成 be 動詞仍通順，就別選 -ly 副詞。","句子重組先找動詞：give、show 類物放前面時加 to，buy、make 類加 for。","discuss、enter、marry 直接接受詞，選項有 discuss about、marry with 就是陷阱。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Mom's beef noodles always taste ______.","options":["well","great","nicely","deliciously"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：媽媽做的牛肉麵總是很好吃。taste 是連綴動詞，後面接形容詞 great；well、nicely、deliciously 在這裡都是副詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"It was Leo's birthday, so his sister bought a new backpack ______ him.","options":["to","at","for","of"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：那天是 Leo 的生日，所以姊姊買了一個新背包給他。buy 把物放前面時，人前面用 for（替對方買），不用 to。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The good news from the hospital made the whole family ______.","options":["happy","happily","happiness","unhappily"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：醫院傳來的好消息讓全家人都很開心。make + O + C，補語說明受詞狀態，用形容詞 happy；happily、unhappily 是副詞；happiness 雖是名詞，但全家人 ≠ 快樂本身。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"We ______ the plan for our class trip at lunch.","options":["discussed about","talked","spoke","discussed"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我們午餐時討論了校外教學的計畫。discuss 是及物動詞，直接接受詞，不加 about；talk、speak 要加 about 才能接這個受詞。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Grandma tasted the soup ______ before adding more salt.","options":["careful","carefully","care","caring"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：奶奶加鹽之前先小心地嚐了湯。這裡的 taste 是一般動詞「嚐」，後面有受詞 the soup，修飾動作要用副詞 carefully，不用形容詞 careful。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I don't understand this math problem. Could you ______?","options":["explain me it","explain me","explain it to me","explain to me it"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我看不懂這題數學，你可以解釋給我聽嗎？explain 不能接兩個受詞，要用 explain sth to sb；受詞是代名詞 it 時要放在 to me 前面，(D) 錯。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Many students find ______ to get up at six every morning.","options":["it hard","hard","hardly","it hardly"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：很多學生覺得每天早上六點起床很難。真正的受詞 to V 放在後面，先用虛受詞 it 代替，find it + 形容詞 + to V。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The coach ______ Jason team captain because he never misses practice.","options":["gave","told","showed","made"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：因為 Jason 從不缺席練習，教練讓他當隊長。Jason = team captain，是 S+V+O+C，用 make；give、tell、show 接的是「人＋物」。故選 (D)。"}]},{"id":"g-question","unit":"basic","level":"A2","title":"疑問句與附加問句","en":"Questions and question tags","lead":"問句把 be/助動詞移前，否則借 do，疑問詞當主詞除外；附加問句通常正負相反。","goals":["能用 be、助動詞或 do 造 Yes/No 問句","能分辨疑問詞當主詞與當受詞的問句","能依前句的動詞和正負寫出附加問句"],"prereq":["g-sentence"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[5].adv","note":"肯定祈使句可接 won't you、could you 等；統測是否只以 will you 為標準答案待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"Yes/No 問句","text":["句中有 **be 動詞**或**助動詞**（can、will、should、完成式的 have…），把第一個移到主詞前面：Has Ben been waiting?","只有一般動詞時，借用 **do/does/did** 放主詞前，後面的動詞改回原形。","簡答重複 be 動詞或助動詞，主詞換成代名詞，be 動詞依新主詞變化：Are you…? → Yes, I am.／Did Amy…? → No, she didn't."],"adv":["表示「擁有」的 have 是一般動詞，問句要借 do：Do you have a pen?","肯定簡答不縮寫：Yes, I am.（不說 Yes, I'm.）；否定簡答可以縮寫：No, I'm not.／No, I didn't."],"formula":"Be/助動詞 + S …?／Do/Does/Did + S + 原形動詞 …?","table":{"cols":["動詞","直述句","問句"],"rows":[["be 動詞","Amy [[is]] hungry.","[[Is]] Amy hungry?"],["助動詞","You [[can]] swim.","[[Can]] you swim?"],["兩個以上助動詞（移第一個）","Ben [[has]] been waiting.","[[Has]] Ben been waiting?"],["一般動詞（現在）","He [[likes]] tea.","[[Does]] he [[like]] tea?"],["一般動詞（過去）","They [[went]] home.","[[Did]] they [[go]] home?"]]},"parse":{"en":"Does your brother work at the night market?","zh":"你哥哥在夜市打工嗎？","parts":[["Does","V","助動詞"],["your brother","S"],["work","V"],["at the night market?","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Are]] you ready for the math quiz tomorrow?","zh":"明天的數學小考你準備好了嗎？"},{"en":"[[Can]] you help me carry these boxes?","zh":"你可以幫我搬這些箱子嗎？"},{"en":"[[Does]] your brother [[work]] at the night market?","zh":"你哥哥在夜市打工嗎？"},{"en":"[[Did]] you [[take]] the MRT to school today?","zh":"你今天是搭捷運上學的嗎？"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ your parents at home now?","options":["Are","Is","Do","Does"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：be 動詞問句，be 動詞移到主詞前。at home 前要用 be 動詞，主詞 your parents 是複數，用 Are。(B) Is 配單數主詞；(C) Do、(D) Does 用在一般動詞的問句，這句沒有一般動詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"A: ______ you finished your science report? B: Yes, I have.","options":["Do","Did","Have","Has"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：完成式的 have 是助動詞，直接移到主詞前。finished 是 p.p.，答句也用 have。(A) Do、(B) Did 後面要接原形 finish；(D) Has 配第三人稱單數，不配 you。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"wh- 疑問詞問句","text":["**疑問詞**放句首，後面接 Yes/No 問句的語序（疑問詞當主詞時例外，見後）。回答要給具體資訊，不用 Yes/No。"],"adv":["疑問詞後面接名詞時，整組放句首：What time does the movie start?／What kind of music do you like?","間接問句（Do you know where he lives?）語序不同，詳見〈名詞子句與間接問句〉。"],"formula":"疑問詞 + be/助動詞/do/does/did + S …?","table":{"cols":["疑問詞","問什麼","例句"],"rows":[["what","什麼","[[What]] do you want for lunch?"],["who","誰","[[Who]] is your homeroom teacher?"],["where","哪裡","[[Where]] do you live?"],["when","什麼時候","[[When]] does the concert start?"],["why","為什麼","[[Why]] are you so tired?"],["how","怎麼、如何","[[How]] do you get to school?"]]},"parse":{"en":"What does your mom usually cook on Sundays?","zh":"你媽媽星期天通常煮什麼？","parts":[["What","O","疑問詞當受詞"],["does","V","助動詞"],["your mom","S"],["usually","M","頻率"],["cook","V"],["on Sundays?","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Where are]] you going after school?","zh":"放學後你要去哪裡？"},{"en":"[[Why did]] Kevin quit his part-time job?","zh":"Kevin 為什麼把打工辭掉了？"},{"en":"[[What does]] your mom usually cook on Sundays?","zh":"你媽媽星期天通常煮什麼？"}],"practice":[{"q":"A: ______ does the night market open? B: At five o'clock.","options":["What","Where","Who","When"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：疑問詞要配合答句的資訊。答句 At five o'clock 是時間，用 When。(A) What 問時間要說 What time；(B) Where 問地點；(C) Who 問人。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"A: Where ______ last weekend? B: I went to Kenting with my family.","options":["you went","did you go","did you went","you did go"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：wh- 問句的語序是疑問詞 + did + S + 原形動詞。(A) you went 是直述句語序；(C) did 後面要用原形 go；(D) did 要放在主詞前面。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"how 的常見組合","text":["**how many** 接可數複數名詞，**how much** 接不可數名詞，也用來問價錢。","how often 問頻率，答 once a week、every day；how long 問多久或多長，答 for two hours、about 30 minutes。"],"adv":["homework、furniture、information 等是不可數名詞，要用 how much，不用 how many。"],"table":{"cols":["組合","問什麼","例句"],"rows":[["how many + 複數名詞","多少（可數）","[[How many]] classes do you have today?"],["how much + 不可數名詞","多少（不可數）","[[How much]] homework do you have?"],["how much","價錢","[[How much]] is this bubble tea?"],["how often","頻率","[[How often]] do you go jogging?"],["how long","多久、多長","[[How long]] is the movie?"]]},"parse":{"en":"How many classes do you have today?","zh":"你今天有幾堂課？","parts":[["How many classes","O","疑問詞片語當受詞"],["do","V","助動詞"],["you","S"],["have","V"],["today?","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[How much]] did you pay for your new phone?","zh":"你的新手機花了多少錢？"},{"en":"[[How often]] do you visit your grandparents in Tainan?","zh":"你多久去台南看一次爺爺奶奶？"},{"en":"[[How long]] does it take to get to Taichung by high-speed rail?","zh":"搭高鐵到台中要多久？"}],"practice":[{"q":"A: ______ is this pair of sneakers? B: It's 1,200 dollars.","options":["How long","How often","How many","How much"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：how much 可以問價錢。答句是價錢，用 How much。(A) How long 問時間或長度；(B) How often 問頻率；(C) How many 問可數名詞有多少。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"A: How ______ students are there in your class? B: Thirty-two.","options":["much","often","many"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：how many + 可數複數名詞。students 是可數複數，用 many。(A) much 接不可數名詞；(B) often 問頻率，後面不接名詞。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"主詞疑問句","text":["疑問詞本身就是**主詞**時，直接接動詞，不加 do/does/did。who、what 當主詞，動詞一般用單數：Who wants pizza?","比較：Who **called you**?（誰打給你？who 是主詞）／Who **did you call**?（你打給誰？who 是受詞）","what、how many + 名詞當主詞也直接接動詞；how many + 複數名詞配**複數動詞**：How many students live here?"],"adv":["What are your plans? 的主詞是 your plans，疑問詞不是主詞，所以用 are；Who are your best friends? 也一樣。"],"formula":"Who/What + V …?（疑問詞當主詞）","parse":{"en":"Who made this beef noodle soup?","zh":"這碗牛肉麵是誰煮的？","parts":[["Who","S","疑問詞當主詞"],["made","V"],["this beef noodle soup?","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Who made]] this beef noodle soup? It's amazing!","zh":"這碗牛肉麵是誰煮的？太好吃了！"},{"en":"[[What happened]] at the basketball game yesterday?","zh":"昨天的籃球比賽發生了什麼事？"},{"en":"[[How many]] students [[joined]] the dance club this year?","zh":"今年有多少學生加入熱舞社？"}],"practice":[{"q":"A: Who ______ the window? B: Leo did. He was playing basketball in the classroom.","options":["did you break","breaks","broke"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：疑問詞當主詞，直接接動詞，不加 did。答句 Leo did 表示 who 是主詞、時間是過去，用 broke。(A) 主詞疑問句不加 did you；(B) breaks 是現在式，和答句的 did 不合。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"What ______ your plans for summer vacation?","options":["are","is","does"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：疑問詞不是主詞時，動詞看真正的主詞。這句主詞是複數的 your plans，what 是補語，用 are。(B) is 配單數主詞；(C) does 後面要接原形動詞，這句沒有。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"附加問句：前肯後否、前否後肯","text":["**附加問句**放在句尾，向對方確認「對吧？」。前句肯定，附加問句用否定；前句否定，附加問句用肯定。","用前句的 be 動詞或助動詞（有兩個以上時用第一個），一般動詞改用 do/does/did，時態要一致；主詞換成**代名詞**，否定用縮寫。"],"adv":["回答看事實：Tim isn't coming, is he? 若他真的不來，答 No, he isn't.（中文是「對，他不來」）。"],"formula":"肯定句, 否定附加?／否定句, 肯定附加?","table":{"cols":["前句","附加問句"],"rows":[["Mia [[is]] your cousin,","[[isn't she]]?"],["You [[can]] swim,","[[can't you]]?"],["Ben [[plays]] the guitar,","[[doesn't he]]?"],["They [[went]] to Kenting,","[[didn't they]]?"],["You [[haven't]] eaten yet,","[[have you]]?"],["It [[won't]] rain tomorrow,","[[will it]]?"]]},"parse":{"en":"Mia is not your cousin, is she?","zh":"Mia 不是你的表姊妹，對吧？","parts":[["Mia","S"],["is","V"],["not","M","否定"],["your cousin,","C","主詞補語"],["is","V","附加問句的動詞"],["she?","S","附加問句的主詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The MRT is really crowded today, [[isn't it]]?","zh":"今天捷運真的好擠，對吧？"},{"en":"You finished the science report, [[didn't you]]?","zh":"你的自然科報告寫完了，對吧？"},{"en":"Your sister doesn't eat spicy food, [[does she]]?","zh":"你姊姊不吃辣，對吧？"}],"practice":[{"q":"Your brother plays basketball after school, ______?","options":["doesn't he","isn't he","don't he","does he"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：前句是一般動詞，附加問句借 do/does/did，前肯後否。plays 是現在式、主詞是第三人稱單數，用 doesn't he。(B) 前句沒有 be 動詞；(C) don't 不配 he；(D) does he 是肯定。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The MRT was really crowded this morning, ______?","options":["isn't it","didn't it","wasn't it","was it"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：附加問句沿用前句的 be 動詞，時態一致，前肯後否。前句是 was，用 wasn't it。(A) isn't 時態不對；(B) 前句有 be 動詞，不借 did；(D) was it 是肯定。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"附加問句的特例","text":["固定說法要背：肯定的 **I am** 配 aren't I（I'm not 仍配 am I），**Let's** 配 shall we，祈使句一般配 will you。","前句有 never、hardly、seldom、little、few、no、nothing 等**否定字**，整句算否定，附加問句用肯定。"],"adv":["肯定祈使句也可用 won't you（邀請）或 can you、could you（請託）；否定祈使句 Don't… 只配 will you。","unhappy、dislike 這類帶否定字首的字不算否定字，照肯定句處理：She is unhappy, isn't she?；a little、a few 也不算。"],"table":{"cols":["前句","附加問句","例句"],"rows":[["I am …","用 aren't I","I'm next, [[aren't I]]?"],["Let's …","用 shall we","Let's go, [[shall we]]?"],["祈使句","一般用 will you","Don't be late, [[will you]]?"],["never、hardly、seldom、little、few、no…","前句算否定，附加用肯定","She never cooks, [[does she]]?"],["this / that","代名詞用 it","That's your bike, [[isn't it]]?"],["There is/are …","主詞用 there","There's a quiz today, [[isn't there]]?"],["everyone / nobody","代名詞用 they，動詞用複數","Everyone is here, [[aren't they]]?"],["everything / nothing","代名詞用 it","Nothing happened, [[did it]]?"]]},"parse":{"en":"Jason hardly ever studies, does he?","zh":"Jason 幾乎都不讀書，對吧？","parts":[["Jason","S"],["hardly ever","M","否定字，整句算否定"],["studies,","V"],["does","V","附加問句的助動詞"],["he?","S","附加問句的主詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I'm on time, [[aren't I]]?","zh":"我沒遲到吧？"},{"en":"Let's grab some bubble tea after class, [[shall we]]?","zh":"下課後我們去買珍奶，好不好？"},{"en":"Pass me the soy sauce, [[will you]]?","zh":"幫我拿一下醬油，好嗎？"},{"en":"Jason hardly ever studies, [[does he]]?","zh":"Jason 幾乎都不讀書，對吧？"}],"practice":[{"q":"I'm your best friend, ______?","options":["am not I","aren't I","isn't I","don't I"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：肯定的 I am，附加問句固定用 aren't I。(A) am not I 語序不對；(C) isn't 不配 I；(D) 前句是 be 動詞，不借 do。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Nobody likes the new school uniform, ______?","options":["does it","don't they","doesn't he","do they"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：nobody 是否定字，前句算否定，附加問句用肯定，代名詞用 they。(A) it 指事物，不指人；(B) don't they、(C) doesn't he 都是否定。故選 (D)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"Does she likes Korean dramas?","right":"Does she [[like]] Korean dramas?","why":"已經用了 does，後面的動詞要改回原形 like。","sec":0},{"wrong":"Are you like spicy food?","right":"[[Do]] you like spicy food?","why":"like 是一般動詞，問句借 do，不用 be 動詞。","sec":0},{"wrong":"Where you went last weekend?","right":"Where [[did you go]] last weekend?","why":"疑問詞後仍用問句語序：借 did 放主詞前，動詞改回原形。","sec":1},{"wrong":"How many homework do you have tonight?","right":"[[How much]] homework do you have tonight?","why":"homework 是不可數名詞，要用 how much。","sec":2},{"wrong":"What did happen at school today?","right":"What [[happened]] at school today?","why":"what 是主詞，直接接過去式動詞，不加 did。","sec":3},{"wrong":"What is your plans for the weekend?","right":"What [[are]] your plans for the weekend?","why":"主詞是複數的 your plans，what 不是主詞，所以用 are。","sec":3},{"wrong":"She likes cats, isn't she?","right":"She likes cats, [[doesn't she]]?","why":"前句是一般動詞 likes，附加問句用 doesn't，不是 isn't。","sec":4},{"wrong":"They went to Kenting last week, don't they?","right":"They went to Kenting last week, [[didn't they]]?","why":"前句是過去式 went，附加問句時態要一致，用 didn't。","sec":4},{"wrong":"He never lies, doesn't he?","right":"He never lies, [[does he]]?","why":"never 讓前句變成否定，附加問句要用肯定。","sec":5},{"wrong":"Everyone is ready, isn't he?","right":"Everyone is ready, [[aren't they]]?","why":"everyone 在附加問句用 they，be 動詞跟著用複數 aren't。","sec":5}],"tips":["附加問句先找前句動詞：be 動詞、助動詞照抄，一般動詞換 do/does/did，再把肯定否定反過來。","前句有 never、hardly 等否定字就算否定；Let's 配 shall we，祈使句通常配 will you。","對話題看答句選疑問詞：頻率選 how often，一段時間選 how long，價錢或不可數選 how much。"],"quiz":[{"q":"A: ______ your sister work at a hotel? B: Yes, she does.","options":["Is","Do","Does","Has"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：你姊姊在飯店工作嗎？是的。work 是一般動詞，主詞 your sister 是第三人稱單數，要用 Does + 原形動詞發問。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"A: ______ do you go swimming? B: About twice a week.","options":["How often","How long","How far","How many"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：你多常去游泳？大約一週兩次。答句說的是頻率，要用 how often；how long 問的是一段時間。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Tina can speak Japanese, ______?","options":["can she","doesn't she","isn't she","can't she"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Tina 會說日文，對吧？前句肯定、助動詞是 can，附加問句用否定的 can't，主詞換成代名詞 she。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"A: Who ______ last night? B: Amy did. She needed help with her homework.","options":["did you call","called you","you called","did you called"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：昨晚誰打電話給你？是 Amy，她需要人幫忙寫作業。答句 Amy did 表示 who 是主詞，直接接 called you；did you call 是問「你打給誰」。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"A: ______ furniture did you buy for your new room? B: Just a desk and a bed.","options":["How many","How often","How much","How long"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：你為新房間買了多少家具？只有一張書桌和一張床。furniture 是不可數名詞，要用 how much，不能用 how many。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Mr. Lin hardly ever gives us homework, ______?","options":["does he","doesn't he","is he","isn't he"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：林老師幾乎不出功課給我們，對吧？hardly 是否定字，前句算否定，附加問句用肯定；gives 是一般動詞，用 does。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Let's take the MRT to Tamsui this Saturday, ______?","options":["will we","don't we","won't you","shall we"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：這週六我們搭捷運去淡水，好嗎？Let's 開頭的句子，附加問句固定用 shall we。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Don't forget to bring your student ID card, ______?","options":["do you","don't you","will you","shall we"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：別忘了帶學生證，好嗎？否定祈使句 Don't… 的附加問句只用 will you；do you、don't you 都不對。故選 (C)。"}]},{"id":"g-noun","unit":"basic","level":"A2","title":"名詞、冠詞與數量詞","en":"Nouns, articles and quantifiers","lead":"先判斷名詞可不可數，再決定加不加 -s、a/an，配 many 還是 much。","goals":["能分辨可數與不可數名詞，並寫對複數","能依發音與語意選用 a/an、the 或不加冠詞","能依名詞與句意選對 many、much、few 等字"],"prereq":["g-sentence"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[4].adv","note":"樂器加 the 是課本慣例；美式口語常說 play guitar，統測是否接受不加 the 待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"可數與不可數名詞","text":["**可數名詞**有單複數：單數前面通常要加 a/an、the、my 等字，複數大多加 -s/-es，例如 a book、two books。","**不可數名詞**不加 -s，也不加 a/an，像 money、advice、information、furniture、homework。中文覺得能數的，英文不一定可數。","要數不可數名詞，借用**單位詞**：a piece of advice、two pieces of furniture、two cups of coffee，複數加在單位詞上。"],"adv":["有些名詞依字義可數或不可數：time 時間（不可數）／three times 三次（可數）；點飲料時 two coffees 指兩杯咖啡。"],"table":{"cols":["不可數（不加 -s）","可以這樣說","可數的相關字"],"rows":[["advice 建議","[[a piece of]] advice","a suggestion"],["information 資訊","[[a piece of]] information","a fact"],["furniture 家具","[[a piece of]] furniture","a chair、a desk"],["homework 作業","[[a lot of]] homework","an assignment"],["news 新聞、消息（字尾有 s 仍不可數）","[[a piece of]] news","a news story"],["luggage 行李","[[a piece of]] luggage","a suitcase"]]},"parse":{"en":"Ms. Lin gave me a piece of advice before the exam.","zh":"考試前，林老師給了我一個建議。","parts":[["Ms. Lin","S"],["gave","V"],["me","O","間接受詞"],["a piece of advice","O","直接受詞"],["before the exam.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Ms. Lin gave me [[a piece of advice]] before the exam.","zh":"考試前，林老師給了我一個建議。"},{"en":"We have [[a lot of homework]] this weekend.","zh":"這個週末作業好多。"},{"en":"My parents bought [[two pieces of furniture]] for my new room.","zh":"爸媽幫我的新房間買了兩件家具。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Ms. Wang gave us a lot of ______ for the long weekend.","options":["homework","homeworks","a homework"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：不可數名詞不加 -s，也不加 a/an。homework 不可數，a lot of 後面直接接 homework。(B) 不可數名詞不能加 -s；(C) 不可數名詞前不能加 a。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"複數名詞的變化","text":["可數名詞變複數大多加 **-s**；字尾是 -s、-sh、-ch、-x、-z 加 -es，子音 + y 去 y 加 -ies，其他字尾見下表。","少數名詞是**不規則變化**（child → children）或單複同形（fish、sheep），要直接背。"],"adv":["person 的複數通常用 people（two people）；quiz 的複數要重複 z，寫成 quizzes。","-ch 唸 /k/ 時只加 -s：stomach → stomachs。"],"table":{"cols":["字尾","變化","例子"],"rows":[["一般名詞","加 -s","book → [[books]]、student → [[students]]"],["-s、-sh、-ch、-x、-z","加 -es","bus → [[buses]]、watch → [[watches]]、quiz → [[quizzes]]"],["子音 + o","常加 -es（例外 photos、pianos）","tomato → [[tomatoes]]、potato → [[potatoes]]"],["子音 + y","去 y 加 -ies","city → [[cities]]、baby → [[babies]]"],["母音 + y","直接加 -s","key → [[keys]]、toy → [[toys]]"],["-f、-fe","多改 -ves（例外 roofs）","leaf → [[leaves]]、knife → [[knives]]"],["不規則","要直接背","child → [[children]]、tooth → [[teeth]]、man → [[men]]"],["單複同形","不變","fish → [[fish]]、sheep → [[sheep]]、deer → [[deer]]"]]},"parse":{"en":"Grandma grows tomatoes and potatoes on her farm in Yilan.","zh":"阿嬤在宜蘭的農地種番茄和馬鈴薯。","parts":[["Grandma","S"],["grows","V"],["tomatoes and potatoes","O"],["on her farm in Yilan.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Grandma grows [[tomatoes]] and [[potatoes]] on her farm in Yilan.","zh":"阿嬤在宜蘭的農地種番茄和馬鈴薯。"},{"en":"The [[children]] caught five [[fish]] at the night market.","zh":"孩子們在夜市撈到五條魚。"},{"en":"Don't forget to brush your [[teeth]] after lunch.","zh":"午餐後別忘了刷牙。"}],"practice":[{"q":"We visited three ______ in Japan last summer.","options":["city","citys","cities","cityes"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：子音 + y 結尾的名詞，複數去 y 加 -ies。three 後面要接複數，city 變 cities。(A) city 是單數；(B) citys、(D) cityes 拼法錯誤。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"冠詞 a／an：看發音","text":["單數可數名詞第一次提到，或指「一個、任何一個」時，用 **a/an**。","a 或 an 看的是**發音**，不是字母：子音開頭用 a，母音開頭用 an。","hour 的 h 不發音，所以說 an hour；university 的 u 唸 /ju/，是子音開頭，所以說 a university。"],"adv":["說職業或身分時，單數名詞前通常也要加 a/an：My mom is a nurse. He is an engineer.","縮寫看第一個字母的唸法：M 唸 /ɛm/，所以說 an MRT station；X 唸 /ɛks/，所以說 an X-ray。"],"table":{"cols":["用 an（母音開頭）","用 a（子音開頭）"],"rows":[["[[an]] apple、[[an]] umbrella","[[a]] university、[[a]] uniform"],["[[an]] hour、[[an]] honest boy","[[a]] house、[[a]] hotel"],["[[an]] MRT station、[[an]] X-ray","[[a]] one-way ticket、[[a]] European city"]]},"parse":{"en":"Jason bought an umbrella at a convenience store.","zh":"Jason 在便利商店買了一把傘。","parts":[["Jason","S"],["bought","V"],["an umbrella","O"],["at a convenience store.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I waited for [[an hour]] at the bus stop this morning.","zh":"我今天早上在公車站等了一個小時。"},{"en":"My sister goes to [[a university]] in Tainan.","zh":"我姊姊在台南念大學。"},{"en":"There's [[an MRT station]] right next to our school.","zh":"我們學校旁邊就有一個捷運站。"}],"practice":[{"q":"There is ______ university near my home, so the area is full of students.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：a/an 看發音，不看字母。university 的 u 唸 /ju/，是子音開頭，用 a。(B) an 用在母音開頭的字；(C) the 指特定的，There is 介紹新的事物時不用。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"定冠詞 the","text":["**the** 指「特定的」人事物：前面提過的、雙方都知道是哪一個的，或被後面的修飾語限定成特定那一個的名詞（the boy next to Amy）。","**獨一無二**的事物（the sun、the moon）、序數（the first）、最高級（the best）及 the only、the same 前面用 the。"],"adv":["名詞後面有修飾語不一定用 the：只是其中一個時仍用 a，如 a boy in my class（班上的某個男生）。","前面有所有格就不加 the：my best friend、my first trip、Taiwan's tallest building。"],"table":{"cols":["用法","例子"],"rows":[["前面提過","I bought a pen. [[The]] pen was cheap."],["雙方都知道","Can you close [[the]] window?"],["修飾語限定成特定那一個","[[the]] boy next to Amy（對比 a boy in my class：其中一個）"],["獨一無二","[[the]] sun、[[the]] moon、[[the]] world"],["序數","[[the]] first time、[[the]] third floor"],["最高級","[[the]] tallest building、[[the]] best"],["the only、the same","[[the]] only way、[[the]] same class"],["有所有格就不加 the","[[my]] best friend、[[my]] first trip"]]},"parse":{"en":"The boy next to Amy is my cousin.","zh":"Amy 旁邊那個男生是我表哥。","parts":[["The boy","S"],["next to Amy","M","修飾 the boy"],["is","V"],["my cousin.","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"We got a puppy last week. [[The]] puppy sleeps all day.","zh":"我們上週養了一隻小狗，牠整天都在睡。"},{"en":"[[The]] boy next to Amy is my cousin.","zh":"Amy 旁邊那個男生是我表哥。"},{"en":"Taipei 101 was once [[the tallest]] building in [[the world]].","zh":"台北 101 曾經是全世界最高的大樓。"},{"en":"This is [[the first]] time I've tried stinky tofu.","zh":"這是我第一次吃臭豆腐。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Look at ______ moon! It's so round and bright tonight.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：獨一無二的事物前面用 the。天上的月亮只有一個，說 the moon。(A) a 和 (B) an 表「一個、任何一個」，不能用在獨一無二的事物；而且 moon 是子音開頭，也不會用 an。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"不加冠詞的情況","text":["下列名詞前通常**不加冠詞**：by 後面的交通工具（by bus、by MRT；走路說 on foot）、三餐、球類、語言和學科。","少數**固定說法**表示去做該處的本來用途，不加冠詞：go to school（上學）、go to bed（睡覺）、go to church（做禮拜）；只是去那個地點就加 the。"],"adv":["這類說法只限 school、bed、church、class、work 等少數字，不能類推；美式英語去醫院看病仍說 go to the hospital。","樂器前常加 the（play the piano）；美式口語也常省略，如 play guitar。"],"table":{"cols":["類別","不加冠詞","要加冠詞時"],"rows":[["交通","go [[by bus]]、go [[by MRT]]","take [[the]] MRT、take [[a]] taxi"],["固定說法（本來用途）","go to school（上學）","go to [[the]] school（去學校辦事）"],["三餐","have breakfast、eat lunch","have [[a]] big breakfast（前有形容詞常加 a）"],["球類／樂器","play basketball","play [[the]] guitar（樂器常加 the，美式口語也常省略）"],["語言、學科","speak English、study math","[[the]] English language"]]},"parse":{"en":"I usually go to school by MRT.","zh":"我通常搭捷運上學。","parts":[["I","S"],["usually","M","頻率"],["go","V"],["to school","M","地點"],["by MRT.","M","方式"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I usually [[go to school]] [[by MRT]].","zh":"我通常搭捷運上學。"},{"en":"My dad and I [[play basketball]] after [[dinner]].","zh":"我和爸爸晚餐後會去打籃球。"},{"en":"Mom went to [[the school]] to talk to my teacher.","zh":"媽媽去學校找我的老師談話。"},{"en":"We had [[a big breakfast]] at our hotel in Hualien.","zh":"我們在花蓮的飯店吃了一頓豐盛的早餐。"}],"practice":[{"q":"It's almost midnight, and I'm really tired. I'm going to ______ now.","options":["bed","the bed","a bed"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：go to bed 是固定說法，表示上床睡覺，不加冠詞。(B) the bed 只指那張床這個位置，不是「去睡覺」；(C) a bed 表「一張床」，語意不通。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"數量詞：多與少","text":["**many、few** 接可數複數，**much、little** 接不可數；some、any、a lot of 兩種都能接。much 多用於否定句和疑問句。","**a few／a little** 表「有一些」，**few／little** 表「幾乎沒有」。some 多用於肯定句，any 多用於否定句、疑問句。","**a number of** + 複數名詞＝許多；**the number of** + 複數名詞＝…的數目，動詞詳見〈主詞與動詞一致〉。"],"adv":["請求或提供東西時常用 some：Would you like some tea? 肯定句的 any 表「任何」：Any student can join the club.","if 子句裡也常用 any：If you have any questions, ask Ms. Chen."],"table":{"cols":["接可數複數","接不可數","兩種都可以"],"rows":[["many（很多）","much（很多）","a lot of / lots of"],["a few（一些）","a little（一些）","some（多用於肯定句）"],["few（幾乎沒有）","little（幾乎沒有）","any（多用於否定、疑問句）"],["a number of（許多）","a great deal of（許多）","plenty of（很多）"]]},"parse":{"en":"Few students knew the answer because the question was so hard.","zh":"這題太難了，幾乎沒有學生答得出來。","parts":[["Few students","S"],["knew","V"],["the answer","O"],["because the question was so hard.","M","原因子句"]]},"ex":[{"en":"There isn't [[much]] milk left in the fridge.","zh":"冰箱裡的牛奶不多了。"},{"en":"I have [[a few]] good friends in my new class.","zh":"我在新班級有幾個好朋友。"},{"en":"[[Few]] students knew the answer because the question was so hard.","zh":"這題太難了，幾乎沒有學生答得出來。"},{"en":"[[A number of]] tourists visit Jiufen every weekend.","zh":"每個週末都有許多遊客到九份。"}],"practice":[{"q":"How ______ students are there in your class?","options":["much","many","little"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：many 接可數複數，much 接不可數。students 是可數複數，問「有多少」用 how many。(A) much 和 (C) little 都只接不可數名詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Mia isn't lonely at her new school. She has already made ______ friends.","options":["a few","few","a little"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：a few 表「有一些」，few 表「幾乎沒有」，都接可數複數。她不孤單，表示交到一些朋友，用 a few。(B) few 語意相反；(C) a little 只接不可數名詞。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"Can you give me some advices?","right":"Can you give me some [[advice]]?","why":"advice 是不可數名詞，不加 -s。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"I have many homeworks today.","right":"I have [[a lot of homework]] today.","why":"homework 不可數，不加 -s，也不配 many，改用 a lot of。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Grandpa keeps ten sheeps on his farm.","right":"Grandpa keeps ten [[sheep]] on his farm.","why":"sheep 單複同形，複數不加 -s。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"There is a MRT station near my house.","right":"There is [[an]] MRT station near my house.","why":"M 唸成 /ɛm/，以母音開頭，所以用 an。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"My mother is nurse.","right":"My mother is [[a nurse]].","why":"單數可數名詞前要有冠詞，說職業也一樣：a nurse。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Amy is tallest girl in our class.","right":"Amy is [[the tallest]] girl in our class.","why":"最高級前面要加 the。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Kevin is my the best friend.","right":"Kevin is [[my best]] friend.","why":"前面已有所有格 my，就不再加 the。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"Let's play the basketball after school.","right":"Let's [[play basketball]] after school.","why":"球類運動前不加冠詞：play basketball。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"I have very few money left this month.","right":"I have very [[little]] money left this month.","why":"money 不可數，「很少」要用 little；few 只接可數複數。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"There are much people at the night market tonight.","right":"There are [[many]] people at the night market tonight.","why":"people 是可數複數，要用 many，不能用 much。"}],"tips":["空格後是名詞時，先判斷可不可數：advice、information、homework 不加 -s，也不配 many。","選擇題考 a／an 只看開頭發音，別被字母騙：an hour、an MRT station、a university。","few／little 題分兩步：先看名詞可不可數，再看句意是「有一些」還是「幾乎沒有」。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Mr. Chen gave me some useful ______ about choosing a college.","options":["advices","advice","an advice","pieces of advices"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：陳老師給了我一些選大學的實用建議。advice 是不可數名詞，不加 -s，也不加 an。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Kevin waited for ______ hour at the train station, but his friend never showed up.","options":["a","the","any","an"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Kevin 在火車站等了一個小時，朋友卻一直沒出現。hour 的 h 不發音，以母音開頭，要用 an。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"My aunt has three ______, and all of them love bubble tea.","options":["child","childs","children","childrens"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我阿姨有三個小孩，他們都愛喝珍奶。child 的複數是不規則的 children，不加 -s。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I usually go to school ______ bus, but today my dad drove me.","options":["by","by a","by the","with"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我通常搭公車上學，但今天爸爸開車載我。by + 交通工具表示交通方式，中間不加冠詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Ming's family sells ______ cheapest scallion pancakes in Tainan.","options":["a","an","the","any"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：阿明家賣的是台南最便宜的蔥油餅。最高級 cheapest 前面要加 the，不用 a/an。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"How ______ luggage are you bringing on your trip to Japan?","options":["many","much","few","a lot of"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：你去日本旅行要帶多少行李？luggage 是不可數名詞，問多少用 how much；how many 接可數複數。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"______ fans were waiting for taxis outside the stadium after the game, so we decided to take the MRT home.","options":["A number of","The number of","A great deal of","A little"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：比賽後許多球迷在球場外等計程車，所以我們搭捷運回家。fans 是可數複數，a number of＝許多；the number of 是「…的數目」，語意不通；a great deal of、a little 只接不可數。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Don't worry. We still have ______ time, so we don't need to run to the MRT station.","options":["few","a few","little","a little"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：別擔心，我們還有一點時間，不用跑去捷運站。time 指時間時不可數，先刪 few、a few；句意是「還有一些」，用 a little；little 表「幾乎沒有」。故選 (D)。"}]},{"id":"g-pronoun","unit":"basic","level":"A2","title":"代名詞","en":"Pronouns","lead":"代名詞看功能選格：當主詞用主格，當動詞或介系詞的受詞用受格。","goals":["能依主詞或受詞的功能選對代名詞的格","能分辨 another、the other、others","能用虛主詞 it 和虛受詞 it 造句"],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-noun"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[2].adv","note":"each other 用於兩者、one another 用於三者以上的區分，統測是否仍會考待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"主格與受格","text":["**主格**當主詞，通常在動詞前面（疑問句則放在助動詞或 be 動詞後：Do you…?）；**受格**當受詞，放在及物動詞或介系詞後面。","兩個人並列時也一樣：for Amy and me、between you and me。不確定時，拿掉另一個人再唸一次：for me。"],"adv":["並列時習慣把 I 或 me 放在最後：Kevin and I、for Amy and me。","口語回答 Who is it? 常說 It's me. 或 Me.；It is I. 是很正式的說法。"],"table":{"cols":["主格","受格","所有格","所有格代名詞"],"rows":[["I","me","my","mine"],["you","you","your","yours"],["he","him","his","his"],["she","her","her","hers"],["it","it","its","—"],["we","us","our","ours"],["they","them","their","theirs"]]},"parse":{"en":"Did you see him at the MRT station?","zh":"你在捷運站有看到他嗎？","parts":[["Did","V","助動詞"],["you","S","主格"],["see","V"],["him","O","受格"],["at the MRT station?","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Kevin and [[I]] take the MRT to school every day.","zh":"我和 Kevin 每天搭捷運上學。"},{"en":"Grandma made dumplings for my sister and [[me]].","zh":"奶奶包了水餃給我和妹妹吃。"},{"en":"Did [[you]] see [[him]] at the MRT station?","zh":"你在捷運站有看到他嗎？"},{"en":"Just between you and [[me]], I failed the math quiz.","zh":"偷偷跟你說，我數學小考不及格。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My brother stayed up late. Did ______ finish his science report?","options":["he","him","his"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：代名詞看功能選格。空格是 finish 的主詞，疑問句的主詞放在助動詞 Did 後面，仍用主格 he。(B) him 是受格，只能當受詞；(C) his 是所有格，後面要接名詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Ms. Wang took a photo of Tina and ______.","options":["I","me","my"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：介系詞後面用受格。Tina and ___ 是 of 的受詞，拿掉 Tina and 就是 of me。(A) I 是主格，只能當主詞；(C) my 是所有格，後面要接名詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"所有格與所有格代名詞","text":["**所有格**（my、your、his…）後面要接名詞；**所有格代名詞**（mine、yours、his…）等於「所有格＋名詞」，後面不再接名詞。","「我的一位朋友」說 **a friend of mine**：a 和 my 不能連用，of 後面也不用受格 me。","its 是 it 的所有格，沒有撇號；it's 是 it is 或 it has 的縮寫。"],"adv":["所有格代名詞當主詞時，動詞看它代替的名詞：My shoes are white; hers are black.（hers = her shoes）"],"formula":"a + N + of + 所有格代名詞（a friend of mine）","parse":{"en":"A classmate of mine works part-time at a bubble tea shop.","zh":"我有個同學在手搖飲店打工。","parts":[["A classmate of mine","S","我的一位同學"],["works","V"],["part-time","M"],["at a bubble tea shop.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"This isn't my umbrella. [[Mine]] is blue.","zh":"這不是我的傘，我的是藍色的。"},{"en":"Our classroom is bigger than [[theirs]].","zh":"我們的教室比他們的大。"},{"en":"[[A classmate of mine]] works part-time at a bubble tea shop.","zh":"我有個同學在手搖飲店打工。"},{"en":"Our cat is licking [[its]] paw again.","zh":"我們家的貓又在舔牠的腳掌了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"This isn't my pencil case. ______ is pink.","options":["My","Mine","Me","I"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：所有格代名詞 = 所有格 + 名詞。空格當主詞，後面沒有名詞，Mine = my pencil case。(A) My 後面要接名詞；(C) Me 是受格，不能當主詞；(D) I 是「我」，不是「我的」。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The bubble tea shop changed ______ name last month.","options":["its","it's","it"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：its 是 it 的所有格。空格後接名詞 name，要用所有格 its（它的）。(B) it's 是 it is 或 it has 的縮寫；(C) it 是主格或受格，不能直接放在名詞前。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"反身代名詞","text":["主詞和受詞是**同一個人或事物**時，受詞用**反身代名詞**：Ken hurt himself. 是 Ken 傷到自己；Ken hurt him. 則是傷到別人。","常用：**enjoy oneself**（玩得愉快）、help oneself to（自行取用）、teach oneself（自學）、**by oneself**（獨自；靠自己）。","They blamed themselves. 是怪自己；They blamed each other. 是互相責怪。each other／one another 不能當主詞。"],"adv":["表示位置的介系詞後面常用一般受格：She put her bag beside her.（不用 herself）","課本常說 each other 用於兩者、one another 用於三者以上；現在一般用法兩者常互換。"],"table":{"cols":["主格","反身代名詞"],"rows":[["I","myself"],["you","yourself（一人）／yourselves（多人）"],["he","himself（不說 hisself）"],["she","herself"],["it","itself"],["we","ourselves"],["they","themselves（不說 theirselves）"]]},"parse":{"en":"Ken hurt himself during basketball practice.","zh":"Ken 練籃球時弄傷了自己。","parts":[["Ken","S"],["hurt","V"],["himself","O","反身代名詞"],["during basketball practice.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Did you [[enjoy yourselves]] at the night market?","zh":"你們逛夜市玩得開心嗎？"},{"en":"My little brother learned to ride a bike [[by himself]].","zh":"我弟弟自己學會騎腳踏車。"},{"en":"Be careful, or you'll cut [[yourself]] with that knife.","zh":"小心那把刀，別割到自己。"},{"en":"Jay and his sister often help [[each other]] with homework.","zh":"Jay 和妹妹常互相幫忙寫功課。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Tom and Mia, please help ______ to the drinks.","options":["yourself","yourselves","you","your"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：help oneself to 自行取用。對象是 Tom 和 Mia 兩個人，反身代名詞用複數 yourselves。(A) yourself 只指一個人；(C) you 不是反身代名詞，主受同一人要用反身；(D) your 是所有格，後面要接名詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"不定代名詞：one、other","text":["**one** 代替前面提過的可數名詞，指「同一種，但不是同一個」，複數用 ones；**it** 指的就是那一個東西。不可數名詞不用 one 代替。","有 **the** 表示「特定的、剩下的」，沒有 the 表示「還有別的」。another 可單獨用，或後接單數名詞。","複數不接名詞時要加 s：other students = **others**，the other students = **the others**。"],"adv":["another 後面接數字時，可接複數名詞：another two days（再兩天）。"],"table":{"cols":["說法","意思","例句"],"rows":[["one … the other","兩者中，一個…另一個","One is white; [[the other]] is black."],["one … another … the other","三者中，一個…另一個…最後一個","One is red, [[another]] is blue, and [[the other]] is green."],["another","不特定的另一個","Can I have [[another]] cookie?"],["some … others","有些…有些（還有別的）","Some like tea; [[others]] like coffee."],["some … the others","有些…其餘全部","Some of us walked; [[the others]] took the MRT."]]},"parse":{"en":"Some of my classmates went home, but the others stayed to practice.","zh":"有些同學回家了，其他人都留下來練習。","parts":[["Some of my classmates","S"],["went","V"],["home,","M","地點"],["but","J"],["the others","S","其餘的同學"],["stayed","V"],["to practice.","M","目的"]]},"ex":[{"en":"These shoes are too small. Do you have bigger [[ones]]?","zh":"這雙鞋太小了，有大一點的嗎？"},{"en":"I lost my umbrella, so I bought a new [[one]].","zh":"我的傘弄丟了，所以買了一把新的。"},{"en":"I have two part-time jobs. One is at a cafe, and [[the other]] is at a bookstore.","zh":"我有兩份打工，一份在咖啡店，另一份在書店。"},{"en":"Some of my classmates went home, but [[the others]] stayed to practice.","zh":"有些同學回家了，其他人都留下來練習。"}],"practice":[{"q":"These shoes are too big. Can I try on smaller ______?","options":["one","ones","it","them"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：one/ones 代替前面提過的可數名詞。要試的是同一種但不是同一雙，shoes 是複數，用 ones。(A) one 是單數，前面也沒有 a；(C) it、(D) them 指的就是原來那雙，不能接在 smaller 後面。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I don't like this color. Can you show me ______ one?","options":["another","other","others"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：another + 單數名詞，表示不特定的另一個。one 是單數，前面用 another。(B) other 接單數名詞時前面要有 the 等字（the other one）；(C) others 是代名詞，後面不再接名詞。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"each、both、all、none","text":["說兩者用 **both**（都）、either（任一）、neither（都不）；三者以上用 **all**（都）、any（任一）、none（都不）。","**each** 可當代名詞（each of us）；**every** 不能單獨用，後面要接單數名詞或 one（every one of us，不說 every of us）。","all、any、none 也可用於**不可數名詞**：all the money、none of the milk。動詞單複數詳見〈主詞與動詞一致〉。"],"adv":["none 用來回答 how many、how much；回答 who 時用 no one：Who called? No one.","each 可用於兩者（each of my parents）；every 用於三者以上。"],"table":{"cols":["兩者","三者以上","意思"],"rows":[["both","all","都"],["either","any","任何一個"],["neither","none","都不"]]},"parse":{"en":"Each of us has a locker at school.","zh":"我們每個人在學校都有一個置物櫃。","parts":[["Each of us","S","each 當代名詞"],["has","V"],["a locker","O"],["at school.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Both]] of my parents work at the hospital.","zh":"我爸媽都在醫院上班。"},{"en":"You can take [[either]] bus; they both stop at Taipei Main Station.","zh":"兩班公車搭哪一班都可以，都會停台北車站。"},{"en":"I called three classmates, but [[none]] of them answered.","zh":"我打給三個同學，結果沒有一個接。"},{"en":"[[Each]] of us [[has]] a locker at school.","zh":"我們每個人在學校都有一個置物櫃。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My parents are teachers. ______ of them work at the same school.","options":["Both","All","Either","Neither"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：兩者說「都」用 both。parents 是兩個人，兩人都在同一所學校，用 Both。(B) All 用在三者以上；(C) Either 是「任一」；(D) Neither 是「都不」，句意不通。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"______ student in our class has a smartphone.","options":["Every","All","Both"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：every 後接單數名詞。student 是單數，動詞 has 也是單數，用 Every。(B) All 後面要接複數名詞（all students）；(C) Both 指兩者，也要接複數名詞。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"虛主詞與虛受詞 it","text":["to V 或 that 子句當主詞時，通常移到句尾，主詞位置改放**虛主詞 it**：It is fun to go camping.","find、make、think、consider 的受詞是 to V 或 that 子句、又有補語時，先放**虛受詞 it**：find it hard to…，it 不能省略。","It is + adj + for/of sb + to V 的用法，詳見〈不定詞 to V〉。"],"adv":["補語也可以是名詞：I make it a rule to walk to school every day.（我堅持每天走路上學。）","It was Tom that broke the window. 是強調句，不是虛主詞，詳見〈強調句與常用句型〉。"],"formula":"It is + adj + to V/that…／find/make/think + it + adj/N + to V","parse":{"en":"My sister finds it hard to wake up before seven.","zh":"我姊覺得七點前起床很難。","parts":[["My sister","S"],["finds","V"],["it","O","虛受詞"],["hard","C","受詞補語"],["to wake up before seven.","O","真受詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[It]] is fun [[to go]] to the night market with friends.","zh":"跟朋友一起逛夜市很好玩。"},{"en":"[[It]] is strange [[that]] Amy hasn't texted me all day.","zh":"Amy 一整天都沒傳訊息給我，真奇怪。"},{"en":"My sister [[finds it hard]] to wake up before seven.","zh":"我姊覺得七點前起床很難。"},{"en":"The new MRT line [[makes it]] easier to visit my grandma.","zh":"新的捷運線讓我去看外婆方便多了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ is not easy to get up early on cold mornings.","options":["It","This","That","There"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：虛主詞 it。真正的主詞 to get up early… 移到句尾，主詞位置放 It。(B) This、(C) That 不能當虛主詞；(D) There 用在「有…」的句型，後面接名詞，不接形容詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"I find ______ strange that Leo didn't come to school today.","options":["it","this","that"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：虛受詞 it。find 的真正受詞是 that 子句，放到補語 strange 後面，受詞位置先放 it。(B) this、(C) that 不能當虛受詞，(C) 還會和後面的 that 重複。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"Mom bought tickets for my brother and I.","right":"Mom bought tickets for my brother and [[me]].","why":"介系詞 for 後面要用受格 me，並列時也一樣。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"Me and my brother went to the night market last night.","right":"[[My brother and I]] went to the night market last night.","why":"當主詞要用主格 I，不用受格 me；習慣把 I 放在後面。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Grace is a good friend of me.","right":"Grace is a good friend of [[mine]].","why":"a friend of 後面接所有格代名詞 mine，不用受格 me。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"The dog is wagging it's tail.","right":"The dog is wagging [[its]] tail.","why":"名詞前的所有格是 its；it's 是 it is 或 it has 的縮寫。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"We enjoyed very much at the party.","right":"We enjoyed [[ourselves]] very much at the party.","why":"enjoy 是及物動詞，要接受詞；玩得愉快說 enjoy oneself。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"I have two cousins. One lives in Tainan, and another lives in Taichung.","right":"I have two cousins. One lives in Tainan, and [[the other]] lives in Taichung.","why":"只有兩個時，剩下的那一個用 the other，不用 another。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"I have three roommates, and both of them come from Tainan.","right":"I have three roommates, and [[all]] of them come from Tainan.","why":"三者以上的「都」用 all；both 只用在兩者。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"Every of the students has to wear a uniform.","right":"[[Each]] of the students has to wear a uniform.","why":"every 不能直接接 of，要說 each of 或 every one of。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"This app makes easy to find a YouBike station nearby.","right":"This app makes [[it]] easy to find a YouBike station nearby.","why":"make 的真正受詞是 to V 時，要先放虛受詞 it，再接形容詞和 to V，it 不能省略。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"Is fun to play basketball with my classmates.","right":"[[It]] is fun to play basketball with my classmates.","why":"英文句子要有主詞；to V 移到句尾時，主詞位置放虛主詞 It。"}],"tips":["空格是動詞或介系詞的受詞就選受格；表示「某人的」而後面沒有名詞，選 mine、yours 等所有格代名詞。","先數總數：兩者用 one…the other；不特定的另一個用 another；剩下全部用 the others。","先看說了幾個：兩個用 both、either、neither；三個以上或不可數用 all、any、none。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Our teacher asked Amy and ______ to clean the blackboard after class.","options":["I","me","my","mine"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：老師叫 Amy 和我下課後擦黑板。Amy and me 是 asked 的受詞，要用受格；拿掉 Amy and 就是 asked me。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Jenny is a good friend of ______. We've known each other since elementary school.","options":["me","my","mine","I"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Jenny 是我的好朋友，我們從國小就認識了。「我的一位朋友」說 a friend of mine，of 後面接所有格代名詞，不用受格 me。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Leo is only four, but he put on his shoes all by ______.","options":["him","his","he","himself"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Leo 才四歲，卻自己把鞋子穿好了。by oneself 表示「獨自、靠自己」，he 的反身代名詞是 himself。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"This phone is too slow. I want to buy a new ______ with a better camera.","options":["one","it","ones","other"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：這支手機太慢了，我想買一支相機更好的新手機。要買的是同類但不同的一支，用 one 代替 phone；it 指原來那一支，ones 是複數。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Mr. Chen has two sons. One is a nurse, and ______ is a police officer.","options":["another","the other","other","others"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：陳先生有兩個兒子，一個是護理師，另一個是警察。兩者中剩下的那一個用 the other；another 表示還有別的，不能用在只有兩個時。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Some people love stinky tofu, while ______ can't stand its smell.","options":["others","other","the other","each other"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：有些人很愛臭豆腐，有些人卻受不了它的味道。some…others 表示「有些…有些」；other 不能單獨當主詞，the other 指兩者中的另一個，each other 不能當主詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"I have three sisters, but ______ of them likes durian.","options":["neither","either","both","none"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我有三個姊妹，但沒有一個喜歡榴槤。三者以上的「都不」用 none；neither、either、both 都只用在兩者。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Smartphones make ______ easy for us to keep in touch with friends.","options":["them","its","it","one"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：智慧型手機讓我們很容易和朋友保持聯絡。真正的受詞是後面的 to keep in touch with friends，要先用虛受詞 it 代替：make it + adj + to V。故選 (C)。"}]},{"id":"g-preposition","unit":"basic","level":"A2","title":"介系詞","en":"Prepositions","lead":"in 在範圍內、on 特定日子或表面、at 一個點；介系詞後動詞用 V-ing。","goals":["能依時間和地點選對 in、on、at","能用對方向、位置介系詞和交通方式的說法","能在介系詞後用 V-ing，並用對常見搭配"],"prereq":["g-sentence"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[4].adv","note":"but、except 後接原形動詞時，有些文法書視為連接詞而非介系詞；本站列為例外，分類待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"時間：in／on／at","text":["**in** 用於較長的時間：年、月、季節，以及一天中的時段 in the morning、in the afternoon、in the evening。","**on** 用於特定某一天：星期、日期、生日、節日當天；一天的時段加上星期或日期也用 on：on Monday morning、on the morning of May 5。","**at** 用於時刻：at 7:00、at noon；at night 是固定說法。時間詞前有 this、next、last、every 就不加介系詞：next Monday。"],"adv":["morning 前有形容詞、指某個特定的早上時也常用 on：on a rainy morning；但 early、late 仍用 in：in the early morning。","today、tomorrow、yesterday 前也不加介系詞。週末美式說 on the weekend 或 on weekends，英式說 at the weekend。"],"table":{"cols":["介系詞","用於","例子"],"rows":[["in","年、月、季節","[[in]] 2025、[[in]] May、[[in]] summer"],["in","一天中的時段","[[in]] the morning、[[in]] the evening"],["on","星期、日期","[[on]] Monday、[[on]] May 5"],["on","生日、節日；星期／日期 + 時段","[[on]] my birthday、[[on]] Friday night"],["at","時刻","[[at]] 7:00、[[at]] noon、[[at]] midnight"],["at","固定說法","[[at]] night、[[at]] the moment"],["不加","this／next／last／every 開頭","this morning、next Monday、every day"]]},"parse":{"en":"Our class has PE on Thursday afternoons.","zh":"我們班每週四下午上體育課。","parts":[["Our class","S"],["has","V"],["PE","O"],["on Thursday afternoons.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My cousin was born [[in]] 2009, and her birthday is [[on]] March 12.","zh":"我表妹 2009 年出生，生日是 3 月 12 日。"},{"en":"The first MRT train leaves [[at]] 6 a.m.","zh":"捷運首班車早上六點發車。"},{"en":"Our class has PE [[on]] Thursday afternoons.","zh":"我們班每週四下午上體育課。"},{"en":"Kevin studies [[at night]], so he is always sleepy [[in the morning]].","zh":"Kevin 都在晚上讀書，所以早上總是很睏。"}],"practice":[{"q":"We have a math test ______ Friday.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：星期前用 on。Friday 是星期幾，要說 on Friday。(A) in 用於年、月、季節或 in the morning；(C) at 用於時刻，如 at 8:00。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Our school bus leaves ______ 6:50 every morning.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：時刻用 at。6:50 是時刻，要說 at 6:50。(A) in 用於年、月或一天中的時段；(B) on 用於星期、日期。every morning 前有 every，不加介系詞。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"地點：in／on／at","text":["**in** 表示在某個空間或範圍「裡面」，如城市、國家、房間：in Taipei、in the classroom。","**on** 表示在「表面上」、有接觸：on the wall、on the desk；樓層和街道也用 on，如 on the third floor。","**at** 表示在某個「點」或做某事的場所：at the bus stop、at the door、at school、at home。"],"adv":["同一個地方有時 at、in 都可以：at the library 把它當成一個地點，in the library 強調在建築物裡面。"],"table":{"cols":["介系詞","概念","例子"],"rows":[["in","在空間、範圍裡面","[[in]] Taipei、[[in]] my bag"],["in","圖片裡、天空中","[[in]] the picture、[[in]] the sky"],["on","在表面上（有接觸）","[[on]] the wall、[[on]] the table"],["on","樓層、街道","[[on]] the 2nd floor、[[on]] Main Street"],["at","某個點、門牌地址","[[at]] the bus stop、[[at]] 25 Main Street"],["at","做某事的場所","[[at]] school、[[at]] work、[[at]] home"]]},"parse":{"en":"My mom is still at work.","zh":"我媽媽還在上班。","parts":[["My mom","S"],["is","V"],["still","M"],["at work.","C","地點補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Amy's grandparents live [[in]] Tainan.","zh":"Amy 的爺爺奶奶住在台南。"},{"en":"There is a big map of Taiwan [[on]] the wall.","zh":"牆上有一張很大的台灣地圖。"},{"en":"I'll wait for you [[at]] the bus stop near the convenience store.","zh":"我在便利商店附近的公車站等你。"},{"en":"My mom is still [[at]] work, but Dad is [[at]] home.","zh":"媽媽還在上班，不過爸爸在家。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Look! There's a big spider ______ the ceiling.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：表面上用 on。蜘蛛貼在天花板的表面，要說 on the ceiling。(A) in 表示在空間裡面；(C) at 表示在某個點，如 at the door。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Let's meet ______ the bus stop near school.","options":["in","on","at"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：某個「點」用 at。公車站是一個地點，要說 at the bus stop。(A) in 表示在城市、房間等範圍裡面；(B) on 表示在表面上。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"方向與位置","text":["**表位置**：between（多指兩者之間）、among（三者以上的一群之中）、behind（在…後面）、in front of（在…前面）、next to（在…旁邊）。","**表方向**常接在 go、walk、run 等動作動詞後：into（進入）、onto（到…上面）、across（橫越）、through（穿過）、along（沿著）。","across 是在表面上從一邊到另一邊，如過馬路、過橋；through 是從內部穿過，如隧道、森林、人群。"],"adv":["in front of 是在某物外面的前方；in the front of 是在某物裡面的前段，如 in the front of the bus（公車前段）。","between 也可用於三者以上，但限於一個個分開的對象，如 between the three countries；考試先記「兩者 between、一群 among」。"],"table":{"cols":["介系詞","意思","例子"],"rows":[["between / among","兩者之間／一群之中","[[between]] you and me、[[among]] the trees"],["behind / in front of","在…後面／在…前面","[[behind]] the door、[[in front of]] the station"],["next to","在…旁邊","[[next to]] the bank"],["into / onto","進入／到…上面","run [[into]] the room、jump [[onto]] the bed"],["across","橫越（表面）","walk [[across]] the street"],["through","穿過（內部）","go [[through]] the tunnel"],["along","沿著","walk [[along]] the beach"]]},"parse":{"en":"Ben sits between Lisa and me in math class.","zh":"數學課時 Ben 坐在 Lisa 和我中間。","parts":[["Ben","S"],["sits","V"],["between Lisa and me","M","位置"],["in math class.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Ben sits [[between]] Lisa and me in math class.","zh":"數學課時 Ben 坐在 Lisa 和我中間。"},{"en":"The cat ran [[into]] the kitchen and jumped [[onto]] the table.","zh":"貓跑進廚房，跳上了餐桌。"},{"en":"We walked [[through]] the crowded night market to buy stinky tofu.","zh":"我們穿過擁擠的夜市去買臭豆腐。"},{"en":"We rode our bikes [[along]] the river and then [[across]] the bridge.","zh":"我們沿著河邊騎腳踏車，然後騎過那座橋。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Mr. Lin parked his car ______ the school gate.","options":["in front of","among","into","through"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：表位置的 in front of。車停在校門前面，要說 in front of the school gate。(B) among 用於一群之中；(C) into 表示進入；(D) through 表示從內部穿過，都不合句意。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"On a hot day, Leo jumped ______ the swimming pool.","options":["among","into","between"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：表方向的 into。跳「進」泳池，要用 into，表示從外面進到裡面。(A) among 用於三者以上的一群之中；(C) between 用於兩者之間，泳池只有一個，都不對。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"交通方式：by／on／in","text":["只說「搭什麼交通工具」時用 **by + 交通工具**，中間不加 a、the、my：by bus、by MRT、by train、by car。","交通工具前有 a、the、my 等字時，一般不用 by：公車、火車、捷運、腳踏車、機車用 **on**；汽車、計程車用 **in**。","走路說 **on foot**，或直接說 walk to school。用動詞 take 要加冠詞：take the bus = go by bus。"],"adv":["大致的判斷：能在裡面站起來走動的（公車、火車、飛機）用 on，只能坐著的（汽車、計程車）用 in；騎在上面的腳踏車、機車也用 on。"],"formula":"by + 交通工具（不加 a/the/my）；on/in + a/the/my + 交通工具","table":{"cols":["交通工具","只說方式","前面有 a/the/my"],"rows":[["公車","[[by]] bus","[[on]] the bus"],["捷運","[[by]] MRT","[[on]] the MRT"],["火車","[[by]] train","[[on]] the 8:00 train"],["腳踏車","[[by]] bike","[[on]] my bike"],["汽車","[[by]] car","[[in]] my dad's car"],["計程車","[[by]] taxi","[[in]] a taxi"]]},"parse":{"en":"Most of my classmates come to school by bus.","zh":"我們班大部分同學都搭公車上學。","parts":[["Most of my classmates","S"],["come","V"],["to school","M","地點"],["by bus.","M","交通方式"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Most of my classmates come to school [[by bus]] or [[by MRT]].","zh":"我們班大部分同學都搭公車或捷運上學。"},{"en":"Jenny lives close to school, so she goes there [[on foot]].","zh":"Jenny 住得離學校很近，所以走路上學。"},{"en":"I saw my old teacher [[on]] the train to Kaohsiung.","zh":"我在往高雄的火車上看到以前的老師。"},{"en":"We went to Kenting [[in]] Dad's new car last summer.","zh":"去年夏天我們坐爸爸的新車去墾丁。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Lisa usually goes to work ______ MRT.","options":["by","on","in"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：by + 交通工具，中間不加冠詞。MRT 前沒有 the，要說 by MRT。(B) on 要接 the：on the MRT；(C) in 用於汽車、計程車，而且也要接 a、the 等字。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Kevin goes to school ______ his bike every day.","options":["by","on","in"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：交通工具前有 my、his 等字時不用 by。his bike 是腳踏車，要說 on his bike。(A) by 後面不能加 his，要說 by bike；(C) in 用於汽車、計程車。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"介系詞 + V-ing","text":["介系詞後面接名詞或受格代名詞；要接動詞時用**動名詞 V-ing**，不用原形動詞或 to V。","常見的有 be good at、be interested in、be afraid of、thank you for、how about、without 等。","注意 look forward to 的 to 是介系詞，後面也接 V-ing，詳見〈動名詞與不定詞的選擇〉。"],"adv":["例外：but、except 表「除了」時可接原形動詞，如 do nothing but sleep；have no choice but to V 則接 to V。","介系詞後也可接名詞子句或「疑問詞 + to V」：interested in what you said、about how to get there。"],"formula":"介系詞 + N／V-ing","parse":{"en":"Mia left the party without saying goodbye.","zh":"Mia 沒說再見就離開了派對。","parts":[["Mia","S"],["left","V"],["the party","O"],["without saying goodbye.","M","介系詞 + V-ing"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Eric is really good [[at playing]] basketball.","zh":"Eric 很會打籃球。"},{"en":"Thanks [[for helping]] me with my English homework.","zh":"謝謝你幫忙我寫英文作業。"},{"en":"How [[about going]] to the night market after class?","zh":"下課後去逛夜市怎麼樣？"},{"en":"Mia left the party [[without saying]] goodbye.","zh":"Mia 沒說再見就離開了派對。"}],"practice":[{"q":"How about ______ bubble tea after school?","options":["get","getting","to get"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：介系詞後接 V-ing。about 是介系詞，How about 後面用 getting。(A) get 是原形動詞，(C) to get 是不定詞，都不能直接放在介系詞後面。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Tom went to bed without ______ his teeth.","options":["brush","to brush","brushing"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：介系詞後接 V-ing。without 是介系詞，後面用 brushing。(A) brush 是原形動詞，(B) to brush 是不定詞，都不能接在 without 後面。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"常見介系詞搭配","text":["有些形容詞或動詞要搭配固定的介系詞，從中文看不出來，要**整組背**。例如「和…不同」是 different from，不用 with。","片語動詞（如 give up、pick up）請見網站的片語頁。"],"adv":["美式也常說 different than，英式也說 different to；考試最穩的寫法是 different from。"],"table":{"cols":["搭配","意思","例子"],"rows":[["be different from","和…不同","different [[from]] mine"],["be interested in","對…有興趣","interested [[in]] music"],["be afraid of","害怕…","afraid [[of]] dogs"],["depend on","依賴；取決於","depend [[on]] the weather"],["be proud of","以…為榮","proud [[of]] you"],["be famous for","因…而有名","famous [[for]] its night markets"],["be full of","充滿…","full [[of]] people"],["be worried about","擔心…","worried [[about]] the test"]]},"parse":{"en":"Many students depend on their parents for pocket money.","zh":"很多學生的零用錢都靠父母給。","parts":[["Many students","S"],["depend on","V","動詞 + 介系詞"],["their parents","O"],["for pocket money.","M","在哪方面依賴"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My school uniform is different [[from]] my brother's.","zh":"我的制服和我哥哥的不一樣。"},{"en":"Leo is very interested [[in]] Korean food.","zh":"Leo 對韓國料理很有興趣。"},{"en":"My little sister is afraid [[of]] the dark.","zh":"我妹妹怕黑。"},{"en":"Many students [[depend on]] their parents for pocket money.","zh":"很多學生的零用錢都靠父母給。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My little brother is afraid ______ big dogs.","options":["at","of","with"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：固定搭配 be afraid of。「害怕…」要說 afraid of。(A) at 常和 good 連用：be good at；(C) with 不和 afraid 搭配。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Grace is worried ______ her math test tomorrow.","options":["in","at","about"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：固定搭配 be worried about。「擔心…」要說 worried about。(A) in 常和 interested 連用：be interested in；(B) at 常和 good 連用：be good at。故選 (C)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"I was born on 2008.","right":"I was born [[in]] 2008.","why":"年份用 in；on 用於特定日期，如 on May 5。","sec":0},{"wrong":"I'll see you on next Monday.","right":"I'll see you [[next Monday]].","why":"時間詞前有 next、last、this、every 時，不加介系詞。","sec":0},{"wrong":"Look at the birds on the sky.","right":"Look at the birds [[in]] the sky.","why":"天空中的鳥、圖片裡的人或物用 in，不用 on。","sec":1},{"wrong":"My aunt lives at Taichung.","right":"My aunt lives [[in]] Taichung.","why":"在城市、國家裡面用 in；at 用於一個點，如 at the bus stop。","sec":1},{"wrong":"The post office is in front the bank.","right":"The post office is in front [[of]] the bank.","why":"in front of 是一組，of 不能省略。","sec":2},{"wrong":"I go to school by my bike.","right":"I go to school [[by bike]].","why":"by 和交通工具中間不加 my、the；也可說 on my bike。","sec":3},{"wrong":"I take bus to school every day.","right":"I take [[the bus]] to school every day.","why":"take 後的交通工具要加冠詞：take the bus；不加冠詞要說 by bus。","sec":3},{"wrong":"Jason is good at play basketball.","right":"Jason is good at [[playing]] basketball.","why":"介系詞後面接 V-ing，不接原形動詞。","sec":4},{"wrong":"My answer is different with yours.","right":"My answer is different [[from]] yours.","why":"「和…不同」要用 different from，不用 with。","sec":5},{"wrong":"This town is famous of its hot springs.","right":"This town is famous [[for]] its hot springs.","why":"「因…而有名」是 be famous for，不用 of。","sec":5}],"tips":["時間題先看線索：年月季節用 in，星期日期用 on，幾點用 at；有 this、next、every 就不加。","空格前是 of、in、at、for、without 等介系詞時，動詞用 V-ing，綜合測驗常考。","搭配題看空格前的字：different 配 from、depend 配 on、afraid 配 of，要整組背。"],"quiz":[{"q":"My birthday is ______ May 5.","options":["in","on","at","for"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我的生日是 5 月 5 日。特定的日期用 on；in 用於年、月，at 用於時刻。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"My grandparents live ______ Kaohsiung.","options":["in","on","at","to"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我的祖父母住在高雄。在城市、國家裡面用 in；at 用於一個點，如 at the bus stop。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The convenience store is ______ the bakery and the bookstore.","options":["among","along","into","between"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：便利商店在麵包店和書店之間。between A and B 表示「在兩者之間」；among 用於一群之中。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Tina is afraid of ______ alone at night.","options":["walk","walking","to walk","walked"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Tina 害怕晚上獨自走路。of 是介系詞，後面要接 V-ing，不能接原形動詞或 to V。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Whether we can go hiking tomorrow depends ______ the weather.","options":["on","at","in","with"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我們明天能不能去爬山要看天氣。depend on 表示「取決於」，是固定搭配。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The train goes ______ a long tunnel before it reaches Hualien.","options":["across","onto","through","between"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：火車抵達花蓮前會穿過一條長隧道。從內部穿過用 through；across 是在表面上從一邊到另一邊。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"My dad jogs along the river ______ Sunday mornings.","options":["in","at","on","by"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我爸爸每週日早上沿著河邊慢跑。單說 in the morning，但 morning 前面加了星期（Sunday mornings）時要用 on。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Last weekend, we traveled around Taitung ______ my uncle's car.","options":["by","on","at","in"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：上週末我們坐叔叔的車在台東到處玩。交通工具前有 my、the 等字時不能用 by；汽車要用 in。故選 (D)。"}]},{"id":"g-agree","unit":"basic","level":"B1","title":"主詞與動詞一致","en":"Subject–verb agreement","lead":"先找出真正的主詞，判斷單數還是複數，再決定動詞形式。","goals":["能找出真正的主詞，判斷動詞單複數","能用就近原則判斷 either…or 等句型","能分辨 a number of、the number of"],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-present","g-noun"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[1].adv","note":"what 子句後接複數補語時用單數或複數，各家說法不一；統測是否接受複數待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"先找主詞：第三人稱單數","text":["第三人稱單數主詞（he、she、it、單數或不可數名詞）在**現在簡單式**肯定句中，一般動詞加 -s/-es，be 用 is，have 用 has；does、can 後用原形。","動詞看**真正的主詞**，修飾主詞的介系詞片語不算（the price of these shoes 看 price）；a number of、most of 看 of 後名詞。","There is/are 句的主詞在動詞**後面**：接單數或不可數名詞用 is（過去式 was），接複數名詞用 are（過去式 were）。"],"adv":["-s/-es 的拼字（watch → watches、study → studies）詳見〈現在簡單式與現在進行式〉。","most of、some of、half of 接複數名詞用複數，接單數或不可數名詞用單數：Most of the money is gone."],"formula":"第三人稱單數主詞 + V-s／is／has／does（現在簡單式）","parse":{"en":"The price of these sneakers is too high for me.","zh":"這雙球鞋對我來說太貴了。","parts":[["The price","S"],["of these sneakers","M","修飾 price"],["is","V"],["too high","C","主詞補語"],["for me.","M"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My sister [[works]] part-time at a bubble tea shop.","zh":"我姊姊在一家手搖飲店打工。"},{"en":"[[The price]] of these sneakers [[is]] too high for me.","zh":"這雙球鞋對我來說太貴了。"},{"en":"There [[are two night markets]] near my school.","zh":"我們學校附近有兩個夜市。"},{"en":"There [[is some milk tea]] left in the fridge.","zh":"冰箱裡還剩一些奶茶。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My little brother ______ his teeth before bed every night.","options":["brush","brushes","brushing","are brushing"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：現在簡單式肯定句，第三人稱單數主詞 + V-s/-es。主詞 my little brother 是單數，every night 表習慣，用 brushes。(A) brush 少了 -es；(C) brushing 前面缺 be 動詞；(D) are 不配單數主詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The key to these lockers ______ on the teacher's desk.","options":["is","are","be"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：動詞看真正的主詞，主詞後的介系詞片語不算。主詞是 the key，單數，用 is。(B) are 是被 lockers 誤導；(C) be 是原形，不能直接當句子的動詞。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"V-ing、to V、子句當主詞","text":["**動名詞**、不定詞或名詞子句當主詞時，通常看成「**一件事**」，動詞用單數；主詞裡的名詞是複數也一樣。","to V 當主詞較正式，常改用虛主詞 It（It is hard to…），詳見〈不定詞 to V〉。"],"adv":["兩個動名詞用 and 連接、指兩件事時用複數：Swimming and cycling are my favorite sports.","what 子句指「…的東西」且後接複數名詞時，也可用複數（What she bought were two books.），但用單數較保險。"],"formula":"V-ing／to V／名詞子句 + 單數動詞","parse":{"en":"Playing mobile games all night is bad for your eyes.","zh":"整晚打手遊對眼睛很傷。","parts":[["Playing mobile games all night","S","動名詞當主詞"],["is","V"],["bad","C","主詞補語"],["for your eyes.","M"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Playing]] mobile games all night [[is]] bad for your eyes.","zh":"整晚打手遊對眼睛很傷。"},{"en":"[[Learning]] five new words a day [[helps]] me a lot.","zh":"每天背五個新單字對我很有幫助。"},{"en":"[[What]] Mom cooks on Sundays [[is]] always delicious.","zh":"媽媽星期天煮的菜總是很好吃。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Reading comics before bed ______ me relax.","options":["help","helps","helping"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：動名詞片語當主詞，看成一件事，用單數。主詞是 reading，不是 comics，現在簡單式一般動詞加 -s，用 helps。(A) help 是被複數 comics 誤導；(C) helping 不能單獨當句子的動詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"each、every 等用單數","text":["**each、every** 後接單數名詞，動詞用單數；each of the + 複數名詞，主詞仍是 each，也用單數。","-one、-body、-thing 結尾的**不定代名詞**（如 everyone、nobody）當單數。either／neither of + 複數名詞，正式用法也接單數。"],"adv":["each 放在複數主詞後面時，動詞看前面的複數主詞，用複數：They each have a locker.","口語常聽到 Neither of them are…，但寫作和考試建議用單數。"],"parse":{"en":"Each of my classmates has a different dream.","zh":"我們班每個同學的夢想都不一樣。","parts":[["Each","S"],["of my classmates","M","修飾 each"],["has","V"],["a different dream.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Every student has]] to wear a uniform on Mondays.","zh":"每個學生星期一都要穿制服。"},{"en":"[[Each of]] my classmates [[has]] a different dream.","zh":"我們班每個同學的夢想都不一樣。"},{"en":"[[Nobody]] in my family [[likes]] durian.","zh":"我家沒有人喜歡榴槤。"},{"en":"[[Neither of]] the two answers [[is]] correct.","zh":"這兩個答案都不對。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Every room in this hotel ______ a great view of Taipei 101.","options":["have","has","having"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：every + 單數名詞當主詞，動詞用單數。主詞是 every room，in this hotel 只是修飾語，用 has。(A) have 配複數主詞；(C) having 不能單獨當句子的動詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Nobody in my class ______ the answer to this question.","options":["knows","know","knowing"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：nobody 等不定代名詞當單數。主詞是 nobody，in my class 是修飾語，現在簡單式用 knows。(B) know 配複數主詞；(C) knowing 不能單獨當句子的動詞。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"兩個主詞：看 A 還是 B","text":["A and B、both A and B 用複數；A **as well as** B、A (together) with B 重點在 A，後面只是補充，動詞看 A。","either A or B、neither A nor B、not only A but also B 的動詞看離它最近的 B，稱為**就近原則**。意思詳見〈連接詞〉。"],"adv":["A and B 指同一人或同一件事時用單數，如 bread and butter（塗奶油的麵包）。"],"table":{"cols":["句型","動詞看","例子"],"rows":[["A and B / both A and B","複數","Amy and Ben [[are]] twins."],["A as well as B","A","Amy, as well as her friends, [[likes]] K-pop."],["A with B / A together with B","A","Ben, with his dog, [[goes]] jogging every day."],["either A or B","B","Either you or Ben [[has]] the key."],["neither A nor B","B","Neither Ben nor his parents [[are]] at home."],["not only A but also B","B","Not only Amy but also her parents [[are]] here."]]},"parse":{"en":"Neither my parents nor my sister eats spicy food.","zh":"我爸媽和我姊都不吃辣。","parts":[["Neither my parents nor my sister","S","就近看 sister"],["eats","V"],["spicy food.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[My mom]], as well as my aunts, [[works]] at a hospital.","zh":"我媽媽在醫院上班，阿姨們也是。"},{"en":"Either you or [[your brother has]] to walk the dog tonight.","zh":"今晚不是你就是你弟弟要去遛狗。"},{"en":"Neither my parents nor [[my sister eats]] spicy food.","zh":"我爸媽和我姊都不吃辣。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Either my mom or my dad ______ me up after cram school every day.","options":["pick","picking","picks"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：either A or B 的動詞看最近的 B（就近原則）。B 是 my dad，單數，現在簡單式用 picks。(A) pick 配複數主詞；(B) picking 不能單獨當句子的動詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Jenny and her brother ______ in the school band.","options":["is","are","has"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：A and B 當主詞是兩個人，動詞用複數。Jenny and her brother 是兩人，用 are。(A) is 只配單數主詞；(C) has 是單數形，has in the band 也不合文法。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"數量：number 與時間金錢","text":["**a number of** + 複數名詞 = 許多，動詞用複數；**the number of** + 複數名詞 = …的數目，主詞是 number，動詞用單數。","時間、金錢、距離視為**一個整體**（一段時間、一筆錢）時，動詞用單數。"],"adv":["強調時間一年年過去時可用複數，如 Three years have passed since we met."],"formula":"a number of + 複數 N + 複數 V／the number of + 複數 N + 單數 V","parse":{"en":"The number of tourists in Jiufen has grown a lot.","zh":"九份的觀光客人數成長了很多。","parts":[["The number","S"],["of tourists in Jiufen","M","修飾 number"],["has grown","V"],["a lot.","M","程度"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[A number of]] students [[are]] waiting for the school bus.","zh":"有不少學生在等校車。"},{"en":"[[The number of]] tourists in Jiufen [[has]] grown a lot.","zh":"九份的觀光客人數成長了很多。"},{"en":"[[Five hundred dollars is]] too much for a phone case.","zh":"一個手機殼要五百塊，太貴了。"},{"en":"[[Two hours is]] not enough to see the whole museum.","zh":"兩個小時根本逛不完整間博物館。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The number of students in our school ______ about 1,500.","options":["are","is","have"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：the number of + 複數名詞，主詞是 number，動詞用單數。全校學生人數約 1,500 人，用 is。(A) are 是被 students 誤導；(C) have 是複數形，語意也不對。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Ten kilometers ______ too far to walk in this hot weather.","options":["is","are","were"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：距離視為一個整體，動詞用單數。ten kilometers 是一段距離，現在簡單式用 is。(B) are 把距離當成很多個；(C) were 是複數又是過去式。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"集合名詞與 the + 形容詞","text":["**集合名詞** family、class、team 視為一個整體時用單數，美式英語幾乎都這樣用。","**police** 恆用複數（一位警察是 a police officer）。the + 形容詞指一群人時（the rich、the elderly）表「…的人們」，動詞用複數。"],"adv":["強調個別成員時，英式可用複數（My family are all tall.），美式多改說 My family members are…。","the + 形容詞若指抽象的事物則用單數：The unknown is scary.（未知的事物令人害怕。）"],"parse":{"en":"The police are looking for the stolen scooter.","zh":"警方正在找那台被偷的機車。","parts":[["The police","S","恆用複數"],["are looking for","V"],["the stolen scooter.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[My family is]] going to Hualien this weekend.","zh":"我們全家這週末要去花蓮。"},{"en":"[[The police are]] looking for the stolen scooter.","zh":"警方正在找那台被偷的機車。"},{"en":"[[The elderly get]] a discount on the Taipei MRT.","zh":"長者搭台北捷運有優惠。"}],"practice":[{"q":"In this city, the rich ______ in big houses on the hill.","options":["lives","living","live"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：the + 形容詞指一群人，動詞用複數。the rich 是有錢人們，現在簡單式用 live。(A) lives 把 the rich 當成單數；(B) living 不能單獨當句子的動詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The police ______ checking every scooter on this road.","options":["is","are","has"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：police 恆用複數。the police 指警方，動詞用 are。(A) is 是單數用法；(C) has 也是單數形，has checking 更不合文法。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"Each of the students have a locker.","right":"Each of the students [[has]] a locker.","why":"each of + 複數名詞，主詞是 each，動詞用單數。","sec":2},{"wrong":"There is many people at the night market.","right":"There [[are]] many people at the night market.","why":"There is/are 看後面的名詞，people 是複數。","sec":0},{"wrong":"Playing video games are my favorite hobby.","right":"Playing video games [[is]] my favorite hobby.","why":"動名詞片語當主詞是一件事，用單數；games 不是主詞。","sec":1},{"wrong":"My brother, as well as his friends, are coming to the party.","right":"My brother, as well as his friends, [[is]] coming to the party.","why":"A as well as B 動詞看 A，my brother 是單數。","sec":3},{"wrong":"The number of students are getting smaller.","right":"The number of students [[is]] getting smaller.","why":"the number of 的主詞是 number，動詞用單數。","sec":4},{"wrong":"Does your sister works at a bubble tea shop?","right":"Does your sister [[work]] at a bubble tea shop?","why":"疑問句由 does 承擔 -s，後面的動詞用原形 work。","sec":0},{"wrong":"Everyone in my class have a smartphone.","right":"Everyone in my class [[has]] a smartphone.","why":"everyone 是不定代名詞，當單數，用 has。","sec":2},{"wrong":"Either Tom or his sisters is going to cook dinner.","right":"Either Tom or his sisters [[are]] going to cook dinner.","why":"就近原則：動詞看 B，his sisters 是複數。","sec":3},{"wrong":"The police is looking for the missing girl.","right":"The police [[are]] looking for the missing girl.","why":"police 恆用複數，動詞用 are。","sec":5}],"tips":["先劃掉主詞後的介系詞片語、as well as 片語；a number of、most of 例外，看 of 後名詞。","看到 either…or、neither…nor、not only…but also，動詞看離它最近的 B（就近原則）。","選項常同時考時態：先刪掉單複數不合的，再看 last、now、already 等時間詞。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Everyone in my family ______ spicy hot pot.","options":["love","loves","loving","are loving"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我家每個人都愛吃麻辣鍋。everyone 雖然指很多人，文法上是單數，現在簡單式肯定句的一般動詞要加 -s。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Playing basketball with my friends ______ the best part of my day.","options":["is","are","be","being"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：和朋友打籃球是我一天中最棒的時光。動名詞片語當主詞，看成一件事，用單數 is；friends 是介系詞的受詞，不是主詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"There ______ many people at the Shilin Night Market last Saturday.","options":["is","was","are","were"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：上週六士林夜市人很多。There is/are 看後面的名詞，people 是複數；又有 last Saturday，要用過去式 were。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"______ students in my class have part-time jobs on weekends.","options":["The number of","A number of","Each of the","One of the"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我們班有不少同學週末在打工。動詞是複數 have，只有 a number of（許多）配複數；其餘選項的主詞是 number、each、one，都配單數。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Mr. Lin, together with his students, ______ cleaning the beach now.","options":["is","are","were","has"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：林老師現在正和學生一起淨灘。A together with B 動詞看 A，主詞是 Mr. Lin，用單數 is；are、were 是被 students 誤導。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Neither Kevin nor his friends ______ interested in the new horror movie.","options":["is","has","are","was"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Kevin 和他的朋友都對那部新恐怖片沒興趣。neither A nor B 動詞看最近的 B，friends 是複數，用 are；選 is 是誤看 Kevin。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The police ______ already caught the man who stole Ms. Wang's scooter.","options":["has","is","was","have"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：警方已經抓到偷走王小姐機車的男子。police 恆為複數，現在完成式用 have + p.p.；has 是單數主詞的用法。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"I really want those sneakers, but three thousand dollars ______ too much for me right now.","options":["are","were","is","have been"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我很想要那雙球鞋，但三千塊對現在的我來說太多了。金錢視為一筆金額，用單數；right now 用現在式 is。故選 (C)。"}]},{"id":"g-present","unit":"tense","level":"A1","title":"現在簡單式與現在進行式","en":"Present simple and present continuous","lead":"習慣與事實用現在簡單式；此刻正在進行、暫時的事用 be + V-ing。","goals":["能依時間線索選用現在簡單式或現在進行式","能正確寫出第三人稱單數動詞和 V-ing 拼字","能放對頻率副詞，並避免狀態動詞用進行式"],"prereq":["g-sentence"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[0].adv","note":"時刻表未來事件用 will 也合文法；若選項同時有 leaves 和 will leave，統測如何給分待確認。"},{"where":"sections[4].adv","note":"英式拼字 travelling、cancelling 在統測是否算錯待確認；本章練習只考美式拼字。"}],"sections":[{"h":"現在簡單式的用法","text":["**現在簡單式**表示經常重複的**習慣**，也用來說一般事實和不變的真理，常和 every day、on weekends 等時間詞連用。","火車、公車、課程、電影等**時刻表**上的未來事件，常用現在簡單式：The train leaves at 8."],"adv":["時刻表的未來事件用 will 也合文法（The train will leave at 8:15.），但現在簡單式最常見。其他未來說法詳見〈未來式〉。"],"formula":"肯定句：S + 一般動詞原形（第三人稱單數加 -s/-es）","table":{"cols":["用法","例句"],"rows":[["習慣","I [[take]] the MRT to school every day."],["事實","My mom [[works]] at a hospital."],["真理","Water [[boils]] at 100°C."],["時刻表","The train [[leaves]] at 8:15."]]},"parse":{"en":"My grandma gets up at five every morning.","zh":"我奶奶每天早上五點就起床。","parts":[["My grandma","S"],["gets up","V"],["at five","M","時間"],["every morning.","M","頻率"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Kevin [[plays]] basketball with his classmates every Friday.","zh":"Kevin 每週五都和同學打籃球。"},{"en":"My grandma [[gets]] up at five every morning.","zh":"我奶奶每天早上五點就起床。"},{"en":"The sun [[rises]] in the east.","zh":"太陽從東方升起。"},{"en":"The bus to Kenting [[leaves]] at 7:30 tomorrow morning.","zh":"開往墾丁的巴士明天早上七點半發車。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My parents ______ at a night market on weekends.","options":["work","works","working","is work"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：現在簡單式表習慣。on weekends 表示固定的習慣，主詞 my parents 是複數，用原形 work。(B) works 用於第三人稱單數；(C) working 前面少了 be 動詞；(D) is work 是 be 動詞加原形，不合文法。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"第三人稱單數加 -s","text":["**現在簡單式**肯定句中，主詞是**第三人稱單數**（he、she、it、Amy、my dog）時，一般動詞加 -s/-es；I、you、we、they 和複數主詞用原形。","否定句：第三人稱單數用 **doesn't + 原形**（She doesn't eat beef.），其他主詞用 don't + 原形。","do/does 問句中，一般動詞也用原形（Does she eat beef?）；助動詞 can、will 後面也接原形（He can swim.）。問句詳見〈疑問句與附加問句〉。"],"adv":["be 動詞不套用加 -s 的規則：I am、he/she/it is、you/we/they are。","主詞是 everyone、each 或 A as well as B 時，動詞用單數還是複數，詳見〈主詞與動詞一致〉。"],"formula":"肯定句：he/she/it + V-s / V-es / V-ies（have→has）","table":{"cols":["動詞字尾","規則","例子"],"rows":[["大部分動詞","直接加 -s","eat→eats, play→plays"],["-s、-x、-sh、-ch","加 -es","watch→watches, fix→fixes"],["go、do","加 -es","go→goes, do→does"],["子音 + y","去 y 加 -ies","study→studies, cry→cries"],["母音 + y","直接加 -s","buy→buys, enjoy→enjoys"],["have","特殊變化","have→has"]]},"parse":{"en":"My sister watches Korean dramas every night.","zh":"我妹妹每天晚上都在追韓劇。","parts":[["My sister","S"],["watches","V"],["Korean dramas","O"],["every night.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My sister [[watches]] Korean dramas every night.","zh":"我妹妹每天晚上都在追韓劇。"},{"en":"Tom [[studies]] in the library after school.","zh":"Tom 放學後都在圖書館讀書。"},{"en":"Mia [[has]] a part-time job at a bubble tea shop.","zh":"Mia 在一家手搖飲店打工。"},{"en":"My dad [[doesn't drink]] coffee at night.","zh":"我爸晚上不喝咖啡。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Amy ______ English for an hour every night.","options":["study","studys","studies"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：第三人稱單數 -ies。肯定句主詞 Amy 是第三人稱單數，study 以「子音 + y」結尾，去 y 加 -ies。(A) study 少了字尾變化；(B) studys 拼字錯誤。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Does your brother ______ spicy food?","options":["like","likes","liking"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：問句的一般動詞用原形。Does 已經表示第三人稱單數，後面的動詞用原形 like。(B) likes 重複加了 -s；(C) liking 不能接在 does 後面。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"頻率副詞的位置","text":["**頻率副詞**表示多常做某事：always（總是）＞usually（通常）＞often（常常）＞sometimes（有時）＞seldom（很少）＞never（從不）。","位置口訣：放在 **be 動詞後**、**一般動詞前**；有助動詞時放助動詞後（I can never…）。"],"adv":["sometimes、usually 也可放句首（Sometimes I walk to school.）。"],"formula":"S + be + 頻率副詞／S + 頻率副詞 + 一般動詞","table":{"cols":["句中動詞","位置","例句"],"rows":[["be 動詞","be 動詞後","Amy [[is always]] busy."],["一般動詞","一般動詞前","I [[usually walk]] to school."],["助動詞","助動詞後","You [[can always]] ask me."]]},"parse":{"en":"We often eat at the night market on weekends.","zh":"我們週末常去夜市吃東西。","parts":[["We","S"],["often","M","頻率副詞"],["eat","V"],["at the night market","M","地點"],["on weekends.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Jason [[is never]] late for his part-time job.","zh":"Jason 打工從不遲到。"},{"en":"We [[often eat]] at the night market on weekends.","zh":"我們週末常去夜市吃東西。"},{"en":"My brother [[sometimes helps]] out at our family's noodle shop.","zh":"我哥有時會去我們家的麵店幫忙。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Mandy ______ her bike to school.","options":["rides usually","usually rides","usually ride"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：頻率副詞放在一般動詞前。usually 要放在 rides 前面；肯定句主詞 Mandy 是第三人稱單數，動詞加 -s。(A) 副詞不能夾在動詞和受詞中間；(C) ride 少了 -s。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"My little sister ______ hungry in the morning.","options":["never","is never","does never"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：頻率副詞放在 be 動詞後。hungry 是形容詞，句子需要 be 動詞，never 放在 is 後面。(A) 句子少了動詞；(C) 形容詞前要用 be 動詞，不能用 does。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"現在進行式的用法","text":["**現在進行式**表示說話**此刻正在**進行的動作，常和 now、right now、Look!、Listen! 連用。","也可以表示**這段期間**暫時的情況（these days、this week），或**正在改變**的情形（getting、becoming）。"],"adv":["現在進行式也能表示已安排好的未來，詳見〈未來式〉。"],"formula":"S + am/is/are (+ not) + V-ing","table":{"cols":["用法","例句"],"rows":[["此刻正在","Mom [[is cooking]] dinner now."],["這段期間","Ben [[is working]] at a café this summer."],["改變中","It [[is getting]] hotter and hotter."]]},"parse":{"en":"Leo is taking the bus to school today.","zh":"Leo 今天搭公車上學。","parts":[["Leo","S"],["is taking","V"],["the bus","O"],["to school","M","方向"],["today.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Listen! Someone [[is playing]] the piano in the music room.","zh":"你聽！有人在音樂教室彈鋼琴。"},{"en":"Ryan [[is practicing]] for the school singing contest this week.","zh":"Ryan 這禮拜都在為學校的歌唱比賽練習。"},{"en":"Bubble tea [[is getting]] more expensive these days.","zh":"最近手搖飲越來越貴了。"},{"en":"Leo usually [[rides]] his bike to school, but today he [[is taking]] the bus.","zh":"Leo 平常騎腳踏車上學，但今天是搭公車。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Listen! Someone ______ at the door.","options":["knocks","is knocking","knocking"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：現在進行式表此刻正在。Listen! 表示說話此刻正在發生，用 is + V-ing。(A) knocks 是表習慣或事實的現在簡單式；(C) knocking 前面少了 be 動詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"V-ing 的拼字","text":["大部分動詞直接加 -ing。字尾是不發音的 **e**，去 e 再加 -ing（make→making）；see、be 的 e 有發音，直接加。","以「**子音 + 母音 + 子音**」結尾的單音節動詞，重複字尾再加 -ing（run→running）；w、x、y 結尾不重複（fix→fixing）。","字尾 **-ie** 改 y 再加 -ing（lie→lying、die→dying）。"],"adv":["同樣結尾、重音在後的雙音節動詞也重複（begin→beginning、forget→forgetting），重音在前不重複（visit→visiting）。","美式拼字 traveling 不重複 l；英式拼字會重複（travelling、cancelling），課外讀物可能看到。"],"table":{"cols":["動詞字尾","規則","例子"],"rows":[["大部分動詞","直接加 -ing","read→reading, play→playing"],["不發音的 e","去 e 加 -ing","make→making, write→writing"],["子音 + 母音 + 子音（單音節）","重複字尾加 -ing","run→running, swim→swimming"],["-ie","ie 改 y 加 -ing","lie→lying, die→dying"]]},"parse":{"en":"Dad is making beef noodles in the kitchen.","zh":"爸爸正在廚房煮牛肉麵。","parts":[["Dad","S"],["is making","V"],["beef noodles","O"],["in the kitchen.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Dad [[is making]] beef noodles in the kitchen.","zh":"爸爸正在廚房煮牛肉麵。"},{"en":"Look! Eric [[is running]] to catch the bus.","zh":"你看！Eric 正跑去趕公車。"},{"en":"Our cat [[is lying]] on my homework again!","zh":"我們家的貓又躺在我的作業上了！"}],"practice":[{"q":"Mom is ______ dumplings in the kitchen.","options":["makeing","making","makking"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：V-ing 拼字。make 字尾是不發音的 e，去 e 再加 -ing，寫成 making。(A) makeing 沒有去 e；(C) makking 不該重複 k，make 不是「子音 + 母音 + 子音」結尾。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"不用進行式的狀態動詞","text":["**狀態動詞**表示想法、喜好、擁有等狀態，不是動作，通常不用進行式；就算說的是「現在」，也用現在簡單式。","常見的有 know、understand、think（認為）、like、love、want、need、belong to、own，以及表「擁有」的 have。","但 have 表「吃、喝、度過」、think 表「考慮」時是**動作**，可以用進行式：We're having lunch.／I'm thinking about it."],"adv":["口語偶爾會聽到 I'm loving it 這類說法，但寫作和考試請用現在簡單式（I love it.）。"],"table":{"cols":["類別","動詞","例句"],"rows":[["想法","know, understand, think（認為）","I [[know]] the answer."],["喜好、需求","like, love, want, need","She [[wants]] a new phone."],["擁有","have, own, belong to","Jay [[has]] a new laptop."]]},"parse":{"en":"My uncle owns a small breakfast shop in Taichung.","zh":"我叔叔在台中開了一家小早餐店。","parts":[["My uncle","S"],["owns","V"],["a small breakfast shop","O"],["in Taichung.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I [[don't understand]] this math problem. Can you help me?","zh":"我看不懂這題數學，你可以教我嗎？"},{"en":"My uncle [[owns]] a small breakfast shop in Taichung.","zh":"我叔叔在台中開了一家小早餐店。"},{"en":"This umbrella [[belongs]] to my brother.","zh":"這把傘是我哥的。"},{"en":"We [[are having]] dinner now, so I'll call you back later.","zh":"我們正在吃晚餐，等一下再回你電話。"}],"practice":[{"q":"This blue backpack ______ to my cousin.","options":["belongs","is belonging","belong"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：狀態動詞不用進行式。belong to 表示「屬於」，是狀態，用現在簡單式；主詞是單數，用 belongs。(B) is belonging 誤用進行式；(C) belong 少了 -s。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"My mom is work at a hospital.","right":"My mom [[works]] at a hospital.","why":"is 不能直接接原形動詞；說事實用現在簡單式 works。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"My mother cook dinner every day.","right":"My mother [[cooks]] dinner every day.","why":"現在簡單式肯定句，主詞 my mother 是第三人稱單數，cook 要加 -s。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"He doesn't likes spicy food.","right":"He doesn't [[like]] spicy food.","why":"doesn't 後面接原形動詞，like 不再加 -s。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"I go always to the night market on Fridays.","right":"I [[always go]] to the night market on Fridays.","why":"頻率副詞要放在一般動詞前面。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"Amy always is busy on Mondays.","right":"Amy [[is always]] busy on Mondays.","why":"頻率副詞要放在 be 動詞後面。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"My brother playing video games now.","right":"My brother [[is playing]] video games now.","why":"現在進行式不能少了 be 動詞：is + V-ing。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Look! It rains outside.","right":"Look! It [[is raining]] outside.","why":"Look! 表示眼前正在發生，要用現在進行式 is raining。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"Jenny is writting a birthday card for her mom.","right":"Jenny is [[writing]] a birthday card for her mom.","why":"write 字尾是不發音的 e，去 e 加 -ing，t 不重複。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"Look! Those kids are runing on the playground.","right":"Look! Those kids are [[running]] on the playground.","why":"run 是「子音 + 母音 + 子音」結尾的單音節動詞，要重複 n。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"I am knowing her phone number.","right":"I [[know]] her phone number.","why":"know 是狀態動詞，不用進行式。"}],"tips":["時間線索：every day、usually 選簡單式；now、Look!、Listen! 選進行式（狀態動詞除外）。","陷阱題：know、want、belong、own 等狀態動詞，就算句中有 now 也不用進行式。","頻率副詞題先看位置：be 動詞後、一般動詞前；再看主詞，肯定句的第三人稱單數一般動詞加 -s。"],"quiz":[{"q":"My little brother ______ milk every morning.","options":["drink","drinks","drinking","is drink"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我弟弟每天早上都喝牛奶。every morning 表示習慣，用現在簡單式；主詞是第三人稱單數，動詞加 -s。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Look! Some children ______ kites by the river.","options":["fly","flies","are flying","is flying"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：你看！有些小孩正在河邊放風箏。Look! 表示此刻正在進行，用 be + V-ing；主詞 children 是複數，用 are。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"My dad ______ coffee after dinner. He says it keeps him awake at night.","options":["never drinks","drinks never","never drink","is never drink"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我爸晚餐後從不喝咖啡，他說喝了晚上會睡不著。頻率副詞放在一般動詞前面；主詞 my dad 是第三人稱單數，用 drinks。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"A: Where's Jerry? B: He ______ in the school pool right now.","options":["swims","is swiming","swimming","is swimming"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Jerry 在哪裡？他現在正在學校泳池游泳。right now 用現在進行式；swim 以「子音 + 母音 + 子音」結尾，要重複 m 再加 -ing。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Look at the sky! It ______ dark. I think it's going to rain.","options":["gets","is getting","get","getting"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：你看天空！天色越來越暗，我想快下雨了。眼前正在改變的情況用現在進行式 is getting；gets 用於習慣或事實。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Hurry up! The movie ______ at 7:30, and it's already 7:20.","options":["starts","start","is start","started"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：快點！電影七點半開演，現在已經七點二十了。電影場次是時刻表，用現在簡單式，主詞單數加 -s；started 是過去式，不合句意。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Mr. Huang ______ three noodle shops in Kaohsiung now. He started with just one food stand.","options":["is owning","own","owns","are owning"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：黃先生現在在高雄有三家麵店，當初只從一個小吃攤起家。own 是狀態動詞，即使有 now 也不用進行式；主詞單數用 owns。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"A: Can I talk to Grandma? B: Sorry, she ______ dinner with her friends right now.","options":["has","have","having","is having"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我可以跟奶奶講話嗎？抱歉，她現在正在和朋友吃晚餐。have 表「吃」是動作，可以用進行式；right now 表示此刻正在進行。故選 (D)。"}]},{"id":"g-past","unit":"tense","level":"A2","title":"過去簡單式與過去進行式","en":"Past simple and past continuous","lead":"過去已結束的事用過去式；過去某刻正在做的事用 was/were + V-ing。","goals":["能依時間線索選用過去簡單式或過去進行式","能正確拼寫 -ed 並記住常見不規則動詞","能用 did 造否定句和疑問句，並會用 used to"],"prereq":["g-present"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[1].adv","note":"英式拼字 travelled、cancelled 在統測是否算錯待確認；本章練習只考美式拼字。"}],"sections":[{"h":"過去簡單式的用法","text":["**過去簡單式**表示過去發生、現在**已經結束**的動作、狀態或習慣。","常和明確的過去時間連用（見下表）。「（距今）多久以前」用**一段時間 + ago**（two days ago）。","句中用 yesterday、ago 等明確過去時間說明動作何時發生，就不能用現在完成式，詳見〈完成式〉。"],"adv":["since yesterday、for the last two years、in the past few weeks 指到現在為止的一段時間，常用現在完成式，詳見〈完成式〉。","ago 只從「現在」往回算；從某件事往回算，用 before（two days before the trip）。"],"formula":"S + 過去式動詞（V-ed 或不規則變化）","table":{"cols":["時間詞","例句"],"rows":[["yesterday","I [[saw]] Amy at the MRT station yesterday."],["last + 時間點","We [[visited]] Tainan last weekend."],["一段時間 + ago","Ben [[moved]] to Taoyuan three years ago."],["in + 年份","My parents [[got]] married in 2008."],["when + 過去子句","I [[lived]] in Hualien when I was young."]]},"parse":{"en":"Jenny bought a cute phone case at the night market last night.","zh":"Jenny 昨晚在夜市買了一個可愛的手機殼。","parts":[["Jenny","S"],["bought","V"],["a cute phone case","O"],["at the night market","M","地點"],["last night.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Jenny [[bought]] a cute phone case at the night market last night.","zh":"Jenny 昨晚在夜市買了一個可愛的手機殼。"},{"en":"We [[went]] to Kenting for our class trip two weeks ago.","zh":"我們兩週前去墾丁校外教學。"},{"en":"My grandpa [[opened]] his noodle shop in 1995.","zh":"我爺爺在 1995 年開了他的麵店。"},{"en":"I [[was]] really shy when I was in junior high.","zh":"我國中的時候很害羞。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Jason ______ his grandparents in Yilan two weeks ago.","options":["visited","visits","has visited","is visiting"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：過去簡單式搭配明確的過去時間。two weeks ago 是過去時間，用過去式 visited。(B) visits 是現在式；(C) has visited 是現在完成式，不和 ago 連用；(D) is visiting 是現在進行式。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"規則動詞加 -ed","text":["**規則動詞**的過去式加 -ed，拼字變化見下表。","重複字尾有兩個例外：w、x、y 結尾不重複（fix→fixed）；**重音在前**的雙音節動詞通常不重複（visit→visited）。"],"adv":["美式多寫 traveled、canceled，不重複 l；英式重複（travelled、cancelled），課外讀物可能看到。"],"table":{"cols":["動詞字尾","規則","例子"],"rows":[["大部分動詞","直接加 -ed","watch→watched, help→helped"],["字尾 e","只加 -d","live→lived, dance→danced"],["子音 + y","去 y 加 -ied","study→studied, cry→cried"],["母音 + y","直接加 -ed","stay→stayed, enjoy→enjoyed（pay→paid, say→said 例外）"],["子音 + 母音 + 子音（單音節）","重複字尾加 -ed","stop→stopped, plan→planned"],["同上結尾、重音在後的雙音節","重複字尾加 -ed","prefer→preferred, admit→admitted"]]},"parse":{"en":"The bus stopped right in front of our school.","zh":"公車就停在我們學校正前方。","parts":[["The bus","S"],["stopped","V"],["right in front of our school.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My brother [[studied]] for his math test until midnight.","zh":"我哥為了數學考試讀書讀到半夜。"},{"en":"The bus [[stopped]] right in front of our school.","zh":"公車就停在我們學校正前方。"},{"en":"We [[planned]] a surprise party for Mom's birthday.","zh":"我們為媽媽的生日策劃了一場驚喜派對。"},{"en":"Ella [[stayed]] home and [[watched]] movies all weekend.","zh":"Ella 整個週末都待在家看電影。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My little brother ______ all night because he had a fever.","options":["cries","crying","cryed","cried"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：子音 + y 結尾的動詞，去 y 加 -ied。cry 的 y 前面是子音 r，過去式是 cried。(A) cries 是現在式，和 had 的過去情境不合；(B) crying 前面缺 be 動詞；(C) cryed 拼錯。故選 (D)。"}]},{"h":"常見不規則動詞","text":["很多常用動詞是**不規則動詞**，過去式要直接背。be 動詞的過去式：主詞是 I 或第三人稱單數用 **was**，you 和複數主詞用 were。","一般動詞的過去式**不分人稱**，第三人稱單數也不加 -s：He went home."],"adv":["與現在事實相反的**假設語氣**中，be 動詞在寫作和考試一律用 were（If I were you…），詳見〈條件句與假設語氣〉。"],"table":{"cols":["類型","例子"],"rows":[["be 動詞","am/is→was, are→were"],["最常用","go→went, eat→ate, see→saw, have→had, do→did"],["其他常見","take→took, get→got, come→came, make→made, tell→told"],["i 變 a","drink→drank, swim→swam, sing→sang, begin→began"],["母音變 o","write→wrote, ride→rode, drive→drove, speak→spoke"],["-ought／-aught","buy→bought, think→thought, bring→brought, teach→taught"],["d 變 t","spend→spent, send→sent, build→built, lend→lent"],["原形＝過去式","put, cut, hit, cost, read（過去式唸 /rɛd/）"]]},"parse":{"en":"Grandma taught me how to make dumplings last Sunday.","zh":"奶奶上週日教我包水餃。","parts":[["Grandma","S"],["taught","V"],["me","O","間接受詞"],["how to make dumplings","O","直接受詞"],["last Sunday.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Kevin [[ate]] two bowls of beef noodles for lunch.","zh":"Kevin 午餐吃了兩碗牛肉麵。"},{"en":"I [[left]] my umbrella on the MRT this morning.","zh":"我今天早上把雨傘忘在捷運上了。"},{"en":"Grandma [[taught]] me how to make dumplings last Sunday.","zh":"奶奶上週日教我包水餃。"},{"en":"We [[were]] all exhausted after the basketball tournament at school.","zh":"學校籃球賽結束後，我們都累壞了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Mom ______ me 100 dollars for lunch yesterday.","options":["gived","given","gave","gives"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：不規則動詞的過去式。give 的過去式是 gave，不加 -ed。(A) gived 不存在；(B) given 是過去分詞，不能單獨當動詞；(D) gives 是現在式，和 yesterday 不合。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Ben and I ______ late for class yesterday because of the heavy rain.","options":["was","were","are","been"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：be 動詞的過去式。主詞 Ben and I 是複數，用 were。(A) was 用於 I 或第三人稱單數；(C) are 是現在式，和 yesterday 不合；(D) been 是過去分詞，不能單獨當動詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"否定與疑問：did + 原形","text":["一般動詞的否定句用 **didn't + 原形動詞**；疑問句用 **Did + S + 原形**，wh- 問句把 did 放在疑問詞後。不管主詞是誰都用 did。","be 動詞不用 did：否定用 wasn't／weren't，疑問句把 was/were 移到主詞前（Where were you?）。"],"adv":["主詞疑問句（Who broke the cup?）不加 did，詳見〈疑問句與附加問句〉。"],"formula":"S + didn't + 原形動詞／Did + S + 原形動詞…?","table":{"cols":["句型","一般動詞","be 動詞"],"rows":[["肯定","Ken [[went]] to the gym.","Ken [[was]] at the gym."],["否定","Ken [[didn't go]] to the gym.","Ken [[wasn't]] at the gym."],["疑問","[[Did]] Ken [[go]] to the gym?","[[Was]] Ken at the gym?"],["簡答","Yes, he did. / No, he didn't.","Yes, he was. / No, he wasn't."]]},"parse":{"en":"Did you watch the baseball game yesterday?","zh":"你昨天有看棒球比賽嗎？","parts":[["Did","V","助動詞"],["you","S"],["watch","V"],["the baseball game","O"],["yesterday?","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I [[didn't finish]] my English homework last night.","zh":"我昨晚沒寫完英文作業。"},{"en":"[[Did]] you [[watch]] the baseball game yesterday?","zh":"你昨天有看棒球比賽嗎？"},{"en":"Where [[did]] you [[buy]] that bubble tea?","zh":"你那杯珍奶是在哪裡買的？"},{"en":"Sorry, I [[wasn't]] home when you called.","zh":"抱歉，你打來的時候我不在家。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ your brother go to the basketball game last Saturday?","options":["Do","Does","Did","Was"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：過去簡單式的疑問句用 Did + S + 原形。last Saturday 是過去時間，後面的 go 是原形，用 Did。(A) Do、(B) Does 是現在式；(D) Was 後面不能接原形動詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"______ you at home when I called you last night?","options":["Were","Did","Was","Do"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：be 動詞的過去式疑問句不用 did。句中沒有一般動詞，要用 be 動詞，主詞 you 配 were。(B) Did、(D) Do 後面要接原形動詞，這裡沒有；(C) Was 不配 you。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"過去進行式與 when／while","text":["**過去進行式**表示過去某時刻**正在進行**的動作（at nine last night）。","長動作進行中，發生了另一個**短動作**（常是打斷它）：長動作用過去進行式，短動作用過去簡單式。when 常接短動作，**while** 接進行中的長動作。","兩個持續的動作在過去**同時進行**，兩邊都可用過去進行式，常用 while 連接。"],"adv":["兩個短動作接連發生，都用過去簡單式：When the bell rang, we ran out of the classroom.","know、want 等狀態動詞通常不用進行式，詳見〈現在簡單式與現在進行式〉。"],"formula":"S + was/were + V-ing","table":{"cols":["用法","例句"],"rows":[["過去某時刻正在","I [[was sleeping]] at 11 last night."],["長動作 + when + 短動作","I [[was reading]] when the phone [[rang]]."],["While + 長動作，短動作","While I [[was cooking]], Dad [[came]] home."],["同時進行","Mom [[was cooking]] while I [[was studying]]."]]},"parse":{"en":"Ken was playing basketball when it started to rain.","zh":"Ken 正在打籃球時，開始下起雨來。","parts":[["Ken","S"],["was playing","V"],["basketball","O"],["when it started to rain.","M","時間副詞子句"]]},"ex":[{"en":"At eight last night, I [[was doing]] my homework in my room.","zh":"昨晚八點，我正在房間寫作業。"},{"en":"Amy [[was waiting]] for the MRT when she [[saw]] her old classmate.","zh":"Amy 在等捷運的時候，看到了以前的同學。"},{"en":"While we [[were eating]] at the night market, it [[started]] to rain.","zh":"我們在夜市吃東西的時候，突然下起雨來。"},{"en":"My brother [[was playing]] video games while I [[was studying]] for the test.","zh":"我在準備考試的時候，我弟在打電動。"}],"practice":[{"q":"At ten last night, my sister ______ a Korean drama on her laptop.","options":["watches","is watching","were watching","was watching"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：過去進行式表過去某時刻正在進行的動作。at ten last night 是過去某時刻，主詞 my sister 是單數，用 was watching。(A) watches、(B) is watching 是現在式；(C) were 不配單數主詞。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"While I was doing my homework, the lights suddenly ______ out.","options":["go","went","going","have gone"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：while 接進行中的長動作，其間發生的短動作用過去簡單式。燈突然熄滅是短動作，用 went。(A) go 是現在式；(C) going 前面缺 be 動詞；(D) have gone 是現在完成式，和過去情境不合。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"used to V：以前常…","text":["**used to + 原形動詞**表示過去常做的事或過去的狀態，暗示**現在已經不是這樣**。","否定用 didn't use to，疑問用 Did + S + use to…?（did 後面用 use）。be used to V-ing 是「習慣於」，詳見〈助動詞〉。"],"adv":["**would** + 原形也可說過去常重複的動作（Every summer, Grandpa would take us fishing.），但不能表示過去的狀態。"],"formula":"S + used to + 原形動詞","parse":{"en":"I used to ride my bike to school.","zh":"我以前騎腳踏車上學。","parts":[["I","S"],["used to ride","V"],["my bike","O"],["to school.","M","方向"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I [[used to ride]] my bike to school, but now I take the MRT.","zh":"我以前騎腳踏車上學，現在改搭捷運。"},{"en":"There [[used to be]] a big night market near my house.","zh":"我家附近以前有一個很大的夜市。"},{"en":"Ben [[didn't use to]] like vegetables, but now he eats them every day.","zh":"Ben 以前不愛吃青菜，現在卻每天都吃。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My aunt ______ live in Tainan, but now she lives in Taipei.","options":["used to","use to","is used to"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：used to + 原形表過去的狀態，現在已不是這樣。後半句說她現在住台北，前半句說的是以前。(B) 肯定句不寫 use to；(C) is used to 是「習慣於」，後面要接 V-ing。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"I go to Kenting with my family last summer.","right":"I [[went]] to Kenting with my family last summer.","why":"last summer 是過去時間，動詞要用過去式。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"My family moved to Taichung before three years.","right":"My family moved to Taichung three years [[ago]].","why":"「三年前」說 three years ago，不說 before three years。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"We planed a trip to Hualien for summer vacation.","right":"We [[planned]] a trip to Hualien for summer vacation.","why":"plan 是「子音 + 母音 + 子音」結尾的單音節動詞，要重複 n 再加 -ed。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"Dad buyed me a new phone last week.","right":"Dad [[bought]] me a new phone last week.","why":"buy 是不規則動詞，過去式是 bought。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"My friends was at the night market last night.","right":"My friends [[were]] at the night market last night.","why":"主詞 my friends 是複數，be 動詞過去式用 were。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Did you went to the concert last night?","right":"Did you [[go]] to the concert last night?","why":"有了 did，後面的動詞就要用原形。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Where you went last weekend?","right":"Where [[did]] you [[go]] last weekend?","why":"wh- 問句也要用「疑問詞 + did + S + 原形動詞」。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"I was do my homework when Dad came home.","right":"I [[was doing]] my homework when Dad came home.","why":"過去進行式是 was/were + V-ing，不能接原形。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"Mia was taking a shower when her mom calls.","right":"Mia was taking a shower when her mom [[called]].","why":"整件事發生在過去，when 後面的短動作也要用過去式。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"I used to playing the piano when I was a kid.","right":"I used to [[play]] the piano when I was a kid.","why":"used to 表過去習慣，後面接原形動詞。"}],"tips":["看時間線索：yesterday、last week、ago 用過去式（since 除外）；過去某時刻正在做用過去進行式。","中譯英、句子重組：did、didn't 後面的動詞一律用原形，別因為是過去就寫成過去式。","綜合測驗常考 when／while：長動作用過去進行式，發生在其間的短動作用過去簡單式。"],"quiz":[{"q":"My family ______ to Tainan last weekend to visit my grandparents.","options":["drive","drove","drives","is driving"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我們全家上週末開車去台南看爺爺奶奶。last weekend 是明確的過去時間，用過去式；drive 是不規則動詞，過去式是 drove。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I ______ breakfast this morning, so I'm really hungry now.","options":["don't eat","didn't ate","didn't eat","wasn't eat"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我今天早上沒吃早餐，所以現在好餓。沒吃早餐是今早已發生的事，否定用 didn't + 原形動詞；didn't ate 多用了過去式。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I called you at nine last night, but you didn't answer. What ______ you doing at that time?","options":["were","did","are","was"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我昨晚九點打給你，你沒接，你那時在做什麼？問過去某時刻正在做的事，用過去進行式 was/were + V-ing；主詞 you 用 were。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Yesterday we ______ at a convenience store on the way home to buy some drinks.","options":["stoped","stopping","stops","stopped"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：昨天我們在回家路上停在便利商店買飲料。yesterday 用過去式；stop 是單音節、以「子音 + 母音 + 子音」結尾，要重複 p 再加 -ed，stoped 拼錯。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"I ______ a movie on my phone when my mom walked into my room.","options":["watch","was watching","am watching","have watched"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：媽媽走進我房間時，我正在用手機看電影。看電影是進行中的長動作，媽媽走進來是其間發生的短動作，長動作用過去進行式；(C) am watching 是現在式。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"While my parents ______ TV in the living room, I was cleaning my room.","options":["were watching","was watching","watching","are watching"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：爸媽在客廳看電視時，我正在打掃房間。兩個動作同時進行，可都用過去進行式；主詞 my parents 是複數，用 were。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"My grandpa ______ a taxi driver, but now he runs a small breakfast shop.","options":["use to be","used to being","was used to be","used to be"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我爺爺以前是計程車司機，現在開了一家小早餐店。「以前是…（現在不是）」用 used to + 原形；肯定句不寫 use to；be used to 是「習慣於」，要接 V-ing。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"A: ______ you use to live in Kaohsiung? B: Yes, I lived there until I was ten.","options":["Were","Do","Did","Have"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：你以前住在高雄嗎？是的，我在那裡住到十歲。used to 只用於過去，疑問句用 Did + S + use to + 原形，不能用 Do 或 Were。故選 (C)。"}]},{"id":"g-future","unit":"tense","level":"A2","title":"未來式","en":"Talking about the future","lead":"當下決定用 will，計畫用 be going to；時間條件子句以現在代未來。","goals":["能依情境選用 will 或 be going to","能用現在進行式和現在簡單式表示未來","能在時間、條件副詞子句中以現在式代替未來式"],"prereq":["g-present"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[2].adv","note":"時刻表未來事件用 will 也合文法；若選項同時有 leaves 和 will leave，統測如何給分待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"will + 原形動詞","text":["**will + 原形動詞**用在說話**當下才決定**的事，也用來承諾、主動提議幫忙、預測，或陳述未來的事實（I'll be 18 next year.）。","will 不隨主詞變化，後面一律接原形動詞；否定是 won't（= will not）。預測常配 I think、I'm sure、probably。"],"adv":["probably 的位置：肯定句放 will 後面（It will probably rain.），否定句放 won't 前面（It probably won't rain.）。"],"formula":"S + will (+ not) + 原形動詞","parse":{"en":"I will buy some eggs on my way home.","zh":"我回家路上會順便買些蛋。","parts":[["I","S"],["will buy","V"],["some eggs","O"],["on my way home.","M","途中"]]},"ex":[{"en":"We're out of eggs? OK, [[I'll buy]] some on my way home.","zh":"蛋沒了？好，我回家路上順便買。"},{"en":"I think Taiwan [[will win]] the baseball game tonight.","zh":"我覺得台灣今晚的棒球賽會贏。"},{"en":"Don't worry, Mom. I [[won't be]] late again.","zh":"媽，別擔心，我不會再遲到了。"},{"en":"Ms. Lin, [[I'll clean]] the whiteboard for you.","zh":"林老師，我來幫您擦白板。"}],"practice":[{"q":"It's hot in here. ______ open the window for you.","options":["I'll","I'm","I"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：說話當下主動提議幫忙用 will + 原形動詞。覺得熱才決定開窗，用 I'll open。(B) I'm 後面不能直接接原形動詞 open；(C) 現在簡單式不用來表示當下的提議。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"My sister will ______ 18 next year.","options":["is","be","being","been"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：will + 原形動詞。will 不隨主詞變化，後面一律接原形 be，可用來陳述未來的事實。(A) is 不能接在 will 後面；(C) being、(D) been 都不是原形動詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"be going to + 原形動詞","text":["說話前**早就決定好**的計畫、打算，用 be going to + 原形動詞；be 動詞要隨主詞用 am/is/are。","根據**眼前的跡象**推測將要發生的事，也用 be going to。"],"adv":["單純預測、沒有特別跡象時，will 和 be going to 常可通用：I think it will / is going to be hot tomorrow.","口語常把 going to 說成 gonna，但寫作和考試要寫 going to。"],"formula":"S + am/is/are + going to + 原形動詞","parse":{"en":"Ken is going to work at a convenience store this summer.","zh":"Ken 今年暑假要去超商打工。","parts":[["Ken","S"],["is going to work","V"],["at a convenience store","M","地點"],["this summer.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My family [[is going to have]] a barbecue for the Moon Festival.","zh":"我們家中秋節要烤肉。"},{"en":"Ken [[is going to work]] at a convenience store this summer.","zh":"Ken 今年暑假要去超商打工。"},{"en":"Look at those dark clouds! [[It's going to rain]].","zh":"你看那些烏雲！快下雨了。"},{"en":"Be careful! [[You're going to drop]] your bubble tea!","zh":"小心！你的珍奶快掉了！"}],"practice":[{"q":"We ______ going to visit our grandparents in Tainan this weekend.","options":["is","are","be","will"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：be going to 的 be 動詞要隨主詞變化。主詞 we 是複數，用 are going to。(A) is 用於單數主詞；(C) be 沒有隨主詞變化；(D) will 不能和 going to 連用。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Look at that dark sky! It ______ rain.","options":["going to","is going","is going to"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：根據眼前跡象推測，用 be going to + 原形動詞。看到烏雲推測快下雨，用 is going to rain。(A) 少了 be 動詞 is；(B) 少了 to，is going 後面不能直接接原形動詞。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"現在式也能表示未來","text":["已經約好、票已買好的**個人安排**，常用**現在進行式**表示未來，句中通常有 tonight、tomorrow 等未來時間。","火車、飛機、電影、課程等**時刻表**上的固定時間，常用**現在簡單式**。"],"adv":["時刻表的事用 will 也合文法（The train will leave at 9:10.），但現在簡單式最常見。","個人安排也可以用 be going to（I'm going to meet Amy tonight.）；現在進行式更強調已經約好。"],"table":{"cols":["說法","什麼時候用","例句"],"rows":[["will + 原形","當下決定、承諾、提議、預測","[[I'll have]] the beef noodles."],["be going to + 原形","事先計畫、眼前跡象","[[I'm going to study]] tonight."],["be + V-ing","已約好的個人安排","[[I'm seeing]] the dentist tomorrow."],["現在簡單式","時刻表、課表","The movie [[starts]] at 7:30."]]},"parse":{"en":"I am meeting Amy at Ximending tonight.","zh":"我今晚要和 Amy 在西門町碰面。","parts":[["I","S"],["am meeting","V"],["Amy","O"],["at Ximending","M","地點"],["tonight.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[I'm meeting]] Amy at Ximending tonight.","zh":"我今晚要和 Amy 在西門町碰面。"},{"en":"[[We're flying]] to Osaka next Friday.","zh":"我們下週五要搭飛機去大阪。"},{"en":"The high-speed train to Kaohsiung [[leaves]] at 9:10.","zh":"往高雄的高鐵九點十分發車。"},{"en":"The new semester [[starts]] on September 1.","zh":"新學期 9 月 1 日開學。"}],"practice":[{"q":"I ______ my aunt in Kaohsiung tomorrow. I already bought the train ticket.","options":["visit","am visiting","visited"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：已安排好的個人計畫用現在進行式表示未來。車票已經買好，用 am visiting。(A) 現在簡單式一般不用來表示個人安排；(C) visited 是過去式，不能配 tomorrow。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"According to the schedule, the first train ______ at 6 a.m. tomorrow.","options":["leave","left","leaves"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：時刻表上的未來事件常用現在簡單式。主詞 the first train 是第三人稱單數，用 leaves。(A) leave 少了 -s；(B) left 是過去式，不能配 tomorrow。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"時間、條件子句以現在代未來","text":["when、after、before、as soon as、until、by the time 引導的**時間副詞子句**，講未來時用現在式代替未來式。","if、unless（除非，約等於 if…not）引導的**條件副詞子句**也一樣；主要子句才用 will 等未來說法。","注意：know、ask 後面的 when／if 子句是**名詞子句**，未來的事仍用 will，詳見〈名詞子句與間接問句〉。"],"adv":["unless 是「除非」，不一定能換成 if…not：I'll be sad if you don't come. 不能改用 unless you come.","時間子句說未來「已完成」的事，可用現在完成式：I'll call you after I've finished my homework.（詳見〈完成式〉）"],"formula":"When/If + S + 現在式, S + will + 原形動詞","table":{"cols":["連接詞","例句"],"rows":[["when","When I [[get]] home, I'll text you."],["after","We'll eat after the movie [[ends]]."],["before","Turn off the lights before you [[leave]]."],["as soon as","I'll call you as soon as I [[land]]."],["until","Let's wait here until the rain [[stops]]."],["if","If my parents [[say]] yes, I'll go camping with you."],["unless","My phone will die unless I [[charge]] it soon."]]},"parse":{"en":"When I get home, I will text you.","zh":"我到家後會傳訊息給你。","parts":[["When I get home,","M","時間副詞子句"],["I","S"],["will text","V"],["you.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"When I [[graduate]], I'm going to work at my uncle's restaurant.","zh":"我畢業後要去叔叔的餐廳工作。"},{"en":"If you [[finish]] your homework early, [[I'll take]] you to the night market.","zh":"如果你早點寫完功課，我就帶你去逛夜市。"},{"en":"The bakery will be closed by the time we [[get]] there.","zh":"等我們到那裡，麵包店早就關門了。"},{"en":"I don't know when the test results [[will come]] out.","zh":"我不知道考試成績什麼時候會出來。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Please wait here until I ______ back.","options":["come","will come","came"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：時間副詞子句以現在式代替未來式。until 引導時間副詞子句，講未來的事用現在式 come。(B) will come 不用在時間副詞子句；(C) came 是過去式，不合句意。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"If it ______ sunny tomorrow, we'll go to the beach.","options":["will be","is","was"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：條件副詞子句以現在式代替未來式。主要子句用 we'll，if 子句講明天的事用現在式 is。(A) will be 不用在條件副詞子句；(C) was 是過去式，和 tomorrow 不合。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"be about to 與未來進行式","text":["**be about to + 原形動詞**表示「馬上就要」，比 be going to 更緊迫。","was/were about to 常配 when，表「正要…時，就…」。","**未來進行式** will be + V-ing 表示未來某個時間**正在進行**的動作。未來完成式詳見〈完成式〉。"],"adv":["be about to 通常不和 tomorrow、next week 等時間詞連用，不說 I'm about to leave tomorrow.","未來進行式也常用來客氣地詢問對方的安排：Will you be using your laptop this afternoon?"],"formula":"S + be about to + 原形動詞／S + will be + V-ing","parse":{"en":"This time tomorrow, we will be lying on the beach in Kenting.","zh":"明天這個時候，我們就躺在墾丁的沙灘上了。","parts":[["This time tomorrow,","M","時間"],["we","S"],["will be lying","V"],["on the beach in Kenting.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Hurry up! The movie [[is about to start]].","zh":"快點！電影馬上就要開演了。"},{"en":"We [[were about to order]] when the waiter said the kitchen was closed.","zh":"我們正要點餐，服務生就說廚房已經休息了。"},{"en":"This time tomorrow, we [[will be lying]] on the beach in Kenting.","zh":"明天這個時候，我們就躺在墾丁的沙灘上了。"},{"en":"At 10 a.m. tomorrow, [[I'll be taking]] an English listening test.","zh":"明天早上十點，我會在考英聽。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Hurry up! The bus is about ______.","options":["leave","to leave","leaving"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：be about to + 原形動詞表示「馬上就要」。about 後面接 to leave。(A) 少了 to；(C) be about 後面不接 V-ing 表示「即將」。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"At this time tomorrow, I ______ on a plane to Japan.","options":["will be flying","will flying","was flying"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：未來進行式 will be + V-ing 表示未來某時正在進行的動作。(B) will flying 少了 be；(C) was flying 是過去進行式，不能配 tomorrow。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"My brother will goes to Japan next month.","right":"My brother will [[go]] to Japan next month.","why":"will 後面一律接原形動詞，不加 -s。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"That box looks heavy. I help you.","right":"That box looks heavy. [[I'll help]] you.","why":"說話當下主動提議幫忙要用 will，不能只用現在式。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"I will going to visit my grandma this weekend.","right":"I [[am going to visit]] my grandma this weekend.","why":"will 和 be going to 不能連用，擇一即可；be 動詞不能省略。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"We go to the movies tonight. Dad already bought the tickets.","right":"We [[are going]] to the movies tonight. Dad already bought the tickets.","why":"已安排好的個人計畫用現在進行式表未來，一般不用現在簡單式。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"When I will get home, I'll call you.","right":"When I [[get]] home, I'll call you.","why":"時間、條件副詞子句用現在式代替未來式。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"If it will rain tomorrow, we will stay home.","right":"If it [[rains]] tomorrow, we will stay home.","why":"if 條件副詞子句講未來用現在式，主要子句才用 will。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"I was about to went to bed when the phone rang.","right":"I was about to [[go]] to bed when the phone rang.","why":"be about to 後面接原形動詞，不用過去式。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"I'll be study at the library at 3 p.m. tomorrow.","right":"I'll [[be studying]] at the library at 3 p.m. tomorrow.","why":"未來進行式是 will be + V-ing，be 後面不接原形動詞。"}],"tips":["選擇題常考：when、if、until、as soon as 等副詞子句以現在式代替未來式，主要子句才用 will。","陷阱題：know、ask、wonder 後面的 when／if 是名詞子句，未來的事仍要用 will。","烏雲等眼前跡象推測將發生的事選 be going to；was about to V when… 表「正要…時就…」。"],"quiz":[{"q":"I promise I ______ late for practice again, Coach.","options":["am not","won't be","won't to be","won't being"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：教練，我保證練習不會再遲到了。承諾未來的事用 will，否定 won't + 原形動詞，不加 to、不接 V-ing；am not 是現在式。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"A: What are your plans for this summer? B: I ______ a part-time job at a bakery.","options":["get","going to get","am going to get","will getting"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：你今年暑假有什麼計畫？我打算去麵包店打工。事先計畫好的事用 be going to + 原形動詞，be 動詞不能省略。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I'll text you as soon as the train ______ at Taichung Station.","options":["arrives","will arrive","arrived","arrive"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：火車一到台中站，我就傳訊息給你。as soon as 引導時間副詞子句，用現在式代替未來式；主詞 the train 是第三人稱單數，用 arrives。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"If Jason ______ the bus tomorrow, he will be late for the exam.","options":["will miss","miss","missed","misses"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：如果 Jason 明天錯過公車，他考試就會遲到。if 條件子句用現在式代替未來式，不用 will；主詞是第三人稱單數，用 misses。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"A: Are you free tonight? B: Sorry, I ______ Kevin at Taipei Main Station at seven.","options":["meet","met","am meeting","have met"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：你今晚有空嗎？抱歉，我七點要和 Kevin 在台北車站碰面。已約好的個人安排用現在進行式表未來，不用現在簡單式 meet；met、have met 不表未來。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Don't call Lisa at nine tonight. She ______ for her math test then.","options":["has studied","was studying","studied","will be studying"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：今晚九點別打給 Lisa，她那時正在準備數學考試。未來某個時間點正在進行的動作，用未來進行式 will be + V-ing。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"I ______ go to bed when my best friend called me.","options":["am about to","was about to","will be about to","was about"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我正要上床睡覺時，好朋友打電話來了。be about to + 原形動詞表「正要」；後面的 called 是過去式，所以用 was about to。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Nobody knows if it ______ this afternoon, so take an umbrella with you.","options":["will rain","rains","rained","raining"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：沒人知道今天下午會不會下雨，所以帶把傘吧。if 在此是「是否」，引導 knows 的受詞，是名詞子句而非條件子句，未來的事要用 will，不用 rains。故選 (A)。"}]},{"id":"g-perfect","unit":"tense","level":"B1","title":"完成式","en":"Perfect tenses","lead":"完成式＝have/has/had + p.p.，講到某時為止的經驗、完成或持續。","goals":["能分辨現在完成式和過去簡單式的用法","能用 for、since 和完成進行式表達持續","能用過去完成式、未來完成式表達時間先後"],"prereq":["g-present","g-past","g-future"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[0].adv","note":"美式 have gone to 也常表「去過」；統測是否一律以 been＝去過、gone＝人未回來區分待確認。"},{"where":"sections[1].adv","note":"美式口語 just、already、yet 常配過去式；若選項同時有過去式和完成式，統測如何給分待確認。"},{"where":"sections[5].adv","note":"by + 未來時間配 will + 原形也合文法；若和 will have p.p. 同時出現，統測如何給分待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"現在完成式：經驗","text":["**現在完成式**是 have/has + p.p.，把過去的事和現在連起來。否定用 haven't/hasn't，問句把 have/has 移到主詞前。","第一種用法表示**經驗**，常配 ever、never、before（句尾）、once/twice（次數，放句尾）。ever 多用於問句和最高級後。","表「去過」用 **have been to**；have gone to 通常指「去了，人還不在這裡」。"],"adv":["once 放在動詞前表「曾經」時，多用過去式：I once lived in Tainan.","美式英語 have gone to 也常表「去過」：I've gone to Kenting many times. 考題多以「人還沒回來」區分 gone 和 been。"],"formula":"S + have/has + p.p.","table":{"cols":["說法","意思","例句"],"rows":[["have been to","去過（人已回來）","I [[have been to]] Kenting twice."],["have gone to","去了（通常指人還沒回來）","Dad [[has gone to]] work."]]},"parse":{"en":"My grandma has never taken the high-speed rail.","zh":"我奶奶從來沒搭過高鐵。","parts":[["My grandma","S"],["has","V"],["never","M","否定"],["taken","V"],["the high-speed rail.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Have]] you ever [[tried]] the oyster omelet at Shilin Night Market?","zh":"你吃過士林夜市的蚵仔煎嗎？"},{"en":"My grandma [[has never taken]] the high-speed rail.","zh":"我奶奶從來沒搭過高鐵。"},{"en":"This is the best beef noodle soup I [[have ever had]].","zh":"這是我吃過最好吃的牛肉麵。"},{"en":"Lisa isn't here. She [[has gone to]] the library.","zh":"Lisa 不在，她去圖書館了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Have you ever ______ to Hualien?","options":["be","was","been","being"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：現在完成式表經驗，Have you ever + p.p.。be 的過去分詞是 been。(A) be 是原形；(B) was 是過去式；(D) being 是現在分詞，都不能接在 have 後面。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"My uncle ______ never tried bubble tea.","options":["have","has","is","does"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：現在完成式 have/has + p.p.。主詞 my uncle 是第三人稱單數，用 has never tried。(A) have 用於複數和 I/you；(C) is never tried 是被動，意思不通；(D) does 後面要接原形。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"完成：already/yet/just","text":["第二種用法表示動作**已經完成**，而且影響到現在，例如作業寫完了，所以現在可以出去玩。","**already**（已經）多用於肯定句，和 **just**（剛剛）通常放在 have 和 p.p. 之間；yet 用於否定句（還沒）和問句（了沒），放句尾。"],"adv":["already 也可放句尾，或用在問句表示驚訝：Have you finished already?（這麼快就做完了？）","美式口語也常用過去式（I just ate. / Did you eat yet?），課本和考試則以現在完成式為主。"],"formula":"S + have/has + already/just + p.p.","parse":{"en":"I have already finished my homework.","zh":"我已經寫完功課了。","parts":[["I","S"],["have","V"],["already","M","副詞"],["finished","V"],["my homework.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I [[have already finished]] my homework, so I can play video games now.","zh":"我功課已經寫完了，所以現在可以打電動。"},{"en":"Mia [[has just left]] for her part-time job.","zh":"Mia 剛出門去打工。"},{"en":"We [[haven't decided]] where to go for the class trip [[yet]].","zh":"我們還沒決定校外教學要去哪裡。"},{"en":"Have you [[eaten]] lunch [[yet]]?","zh":"你吃午餐了沒？"}],"practice":[{"q":"Ben has ______ finished his lunch, so he can play basketball now.","options":["yet","already","ago"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：already 用於肯定句，放在 has 和 p.p. 之間。午餐已經吃完，所以現在能打球。(A) yet 用於否定句和問句，而且放句尾；(C) ago 要配過去式，不能放這裡。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Oh no! The bus has just ______.","options":["left","leave","leaving","leaves"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：has just + p.p. 表示剛剛完成。leave 的過去分詞是 left。(B) leave 是原形；(C) leaving 是現在分詞；(D) leaves 是第三人稱單數現在式，都不能接在 has 後面。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"持續：for 與 since","text":["第三種用法：從過去**持續到現在**。for + 一段時間（for a year）；**since** + 過去的起點（since 2023、since I was ten）。","強調動作一直在做，用**現在完成進行式** have/has been + V-ing；know、like 等**狀態動詞**不用進行式。","問「多久了」用 How long have you…?；也常說 It has been + 時間 + since + 過去式。"],"adv":["live、work、study 這類動詞，完成式和完成進行式意思差不多：I have lived / have been living here for ten years.","since 也可當「因為」：Since it was raining, we stayed home. 這時不必用完成式，詳見〈連接詞〉。"],"formula":"S + have/has + p.p. + for 一段時間／since 起點","parse":{"en":"My parents have run this noodle shop for twenty years.","zh":"我爸媽經營這家麵店已經二十年了。","parts":[["My parents","S"],["have run","V"],["this noodle shop","O"],["for twenty years.","M","一段時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My parents [[have run]] this noodle shop [[for]] twenty years.","zh":"我爸媽經營這家麵店已經二十年了。"},{"en":"Kevin [[has lived]] in Taichung [[since]] he was six.","zh":"Kevin 從六歲起就住在台中。"},{"en":"I [[have been waiting]] for the bus for thirty minutes!","zh":"我已經等公車等了三十分鐘！"},{"en":"[[It has been]] two years [[since]] we graduated from junior high.","zh":"我們國中畢業已經兩年了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Amy has played the piano ______ 2019.","options":["for","since","ago"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：現在完成式表持續，since + 過去的起點。2019 是起點，用 since。(A) for 後面接一段時間，如 for five years；(C) ago 要配過去式，而且放在時間後面（two years ago）。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"We ______ in line for the new bubble tea shop for an hour!","options":["wait","are waiting","have been waiting"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：現在完成進行式 have been + V-ing，表示動作從過去一直持續到現在。for an hour 是到現在的一段時間。(A) wait 是現在簡單式；(B) are waiting 只講此刻，不能配 for an hour 表示到現在。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"不與明確過去時間連用","text":["現在完成式和「現在」有關，不能和**明確的過去時間**連用，如 yesterday、ago、last week、in 2020；這些要用**過去簡單式**。","問「什麼時候」也用過去式：When did you buy it?（不說 When have you bought it?）。since yesterday 是起點，可以用完成式。"],"adv":["just now（剛才）也是明確的過去時間，要用過去式：I saw Amy at the MRT station just now."],"table":{"cols":["用法","過去簡單式","現在完成式"],"rows":[["經驗","I [[visited]] Tainan last summer.","I [[have visited]] Tainan twice."],["完成","I [[finished]] it an hour ago.","I [[have]] already [[finished]] it."],["持續","She [[lived]] in Hualien for two years.（現在不住了）","She [[has lived]] in Hualien for two years.（現在還住）"]]},"parse":{"en":"I bought these sneakers two weeks ago.","zh":"我兩週前買了這雙球鞋。","parts":[["I","S"],["bought","V"],["these sneakers","O"],["two weeks ago.","M","明確過去時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I [[bought]] these sneakers [[two weeks ago]].","zh":"我兩週前買了這雙球鞋。"},{"en":"[[When did]] you [[start]] working at the drink shop?","zh":"你是什麼時候開始在飲料店打工的？"},{"en":"Grandpa [[has been]] in the hospital [[since]] last Friday.","zh":"爺爺從上週五住院到現在。"}],"practice":[{"q":"I ______ my phone at the night market yesterday.","options":["lose","lost","have lost"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：明確的過去時間 yesterday 要用過去簡單式。(A) lose 是現在式；(C) have lost 是現在完成式，不能和 yesterday 連用。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"When ______ you buy that new bike?","options":["did","have","has"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：問「什麼時候」要用過去式 When did…?，後面接原形動詞 buy。(B) have、(C) has 是完成式的助動詞，後面要接 p.p.，不能接原形 buy；has 也和主詞 you 不一致。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"過去完成式","text":["講到過去某個時間點時，要說在那**之前**已發生的事，用 had + p.p.（過去的過去），had 不分人稱。照發生順序敘述時，兩件事都用過去式即可。","常見句型 **By the time** + 過去式, S + had p.p.（到…時已經…），也常配 when 子句和 already。"],"adv":["before、after 已說明先後，先發生的動作也可以只用過去式：I (had) finished my homework before I went out.","when 句的意思會隨時態改變：When I got home, Mom cooked dinner.（我到家後才煮）；Mom had cooked dinner.（早就煮好）。"],"formula":"S + had + p.p.（比過去某時間點或動作更早）","parse":{"en":"When I got home, Mom had already cooked dinner.","zh":"我到家時，媽媽已經煮好晚餐了。","parts":[["When I got home,","M","時間子句"],["Mom","S"],["had","V"],["already","M","副詞"],["cooked","V"],["dinner.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[By the time]] we got to the station, the last train [[had left]], so we took a taxi.","zh":"我們到車站時末班車已經開走了，只好搭計程車。"},{"en":"When I got home, Mom [[had already cooked]] dinner.","zh":"我到家時，媽媽已經煮好晚餐了。"},{"en":"Amy [[had never seen]] snow [[before]] she went to Hokkaido.","zh":"Amy 去北海道之前從沒看過雪。"},{"en":"[[After]] Ken [[had finished]] his shift, he went to the night market.","zh":"Ken 下班後就去逛夜市了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"When I got to school, the bell ______ already rung.","options":["has","had","have"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：過去完成式 had + p.p.。打鐘比過去的 got 更早發生，用 had already rung。(A) has、(C) have 是現在完成式，不能配過去的時間點。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Last night I got home and ______ a shower.","options":["took","take","had taken"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：照發生順序敘述過去的事，兩件事都用過去式。先到家、再洗澡，用 took。(B) take 是現在式；(C) had taken 表示洗澡更早發生，和 and 的先後順序不合。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"未來完成式","text":["到**未來某時間點**時已完成、或已持續一段時間（for a year）的事，用 will have + p.p.，常配 **by** + 未來時間（by 2030）。","By the time 子句講未來時要用現在式（By the time you get home, …），詳見〈未來式〉。"],"adv":["by + 時間只表示「最晚在那之前」，所以 I'll finish it by Friday. 也正確；要強調到那時已經完成，才用 will have + p.p.。"],"formula":"S + will have + p.p.（+ by + 未來時間）","parse":{"en":"By next month, I will have worked at the drink shop for a year.","zh":"到下個月，我在飲料店打工就滿一年了。","parts":[["By next month,","M","時間"],["I","S"],["will have worked","V"],["at the drink shop","M","地點"],["for a year.","M","一段時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[By]] next June, I [[will have graduated]] from high school.","zh":"到明年六月，我就高中畢業了。"},{"en":"Hurry up! The concert [[will have started]] by the time we get there.","zh":"快一點！等我們到的時候，演唱會早就開始了。"},{"en":"By the end of this year, Leo [[will have saved]] enough money for a new bike.","zh":"到今年年底，Leo 就會存夠錢買新腳踏車了。"},{"en":"By next month, I [[will have worked]] at the drink shop [[for a year]].","zh":"到下個月，我在飲料店打工就滿一年了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"By the end of this month, I ______ enough money for a new phone.","options":["have saved","had saved","will have saved"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：未來完成式 will have + p.p.，表示到未來某時間點已經完成。by the end of this month 是未來時間。(A) have saved 是現在完成式；(B) had saved 是過去完成式，都不能配未來時間。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"By 2030, my sister will have ______ from college.","options":["graduate","graduated","graduating"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：will have 後面要接過去分詞。graduate 的過去分詞是 graduated。(A) graduate 是原形；(C) graduating 是現在分詞，都不能接在 will have 後面。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"I have ever been to Japan.","right":"I [[have been]] to Japan.","why":"肯定句說「去過」不加 ever；ever 多用於問句和最高級後。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"Have you ever ate stinky tofu?","right":"Have you ever [[eaten]] stinky tofu?","why":"have/has 後面要接過去分詞 eaten，不是過去式 ate。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"I haven't eaten dinner already.","right":"I haven't eaten dinner [[yet]].","why":"否定句表「還沒」用 yet，放句尾；already 多用於肯定句。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"I live in Taoyuan since 2020.","right":"I [[have lived]] in Taoyuan since 2020.","why":"since（自從）表示從過去持續到現在，要用現在完成式。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"We have known each other since five years.","right":"We have known each other [[for]] five years.","why":"five years 是一段時間，用 for；since 後面接起點。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"I have visited Tainan last summer.","right":"I [[visited]] Tainan last summer.","why":"last summer 是明確的過去時間，要用過去簡單式。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"When have you bought these sneakers?","right":"When [[did]] you [[buy]] these sneakers?","why":"問「什麼時候」要用過去式 When did…?，不用完成式。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"When I arrived, the movie has already started.","right":"When I arrived, the movie [[had]] already started.","why":"比過去的 arrived 更早發生，要用過去完成式 had + p.p.。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"By the end of this year, I will work here for two years.","right":"By the end of this year, I [[will have worked]] here for two years.","why":"到未來某時間點已持續一段時間，要用 will have + p.p.。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"The concert will have started by the time we will get there.","right":"The concert will have started by the time we [[get]] there.","why":"by the time 子句講未來時，用現在式代替未來式。"}],"tips":["選擇題先找時間詞：since（自從）、so far（到目前為止）選完成式；ago、last week 等選過去式。","By the time + 過去式，主要子句多選 had p.p.；by + 未來時間多選未來完成式。","been 或 gone 看下文：人還沒回來（She'll be back soon.）選 gone，去過選 been。"],"quiz":[{"q":"A: Have you ever ______ stinky tofu? B: Yes, I love it!","options":["eat","ate","eaten","eating"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：你吃過臭豆腐嗎？吃過，我超愛！問經驗用 Have you ever + p.p.，eat 的過去分詞是 eaten；ate 是過去式。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I haven't finished my science report ______. Can I hand it in tomorrow?","options":["already","yet","just","ago"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我的自然科報告還沒寫完，可以明天交嗎？否定句表「還沒」用 yet，放句尾；already 多用於肯定句，ago 不和完成式連用。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"A: How long have you lived in Kaohsiung? B: My family ______ here three years ago.","options":["moves","has moved","have moved","moved"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：你住在高雄多久了？我們家三年前搬來這裡。three years ago 是明確的過去時間，只能用過去簡單式，不能用 has moved。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"A: Where's Mom? B: She ______ to the night market to buy dinner. She'll be back soon.","options":["has gone","has been","have gone","have been"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：媽媽呢？她去夜市買晚餐了，很快就回來。人還沒回來用 has gone to；has been to 是去過、已回來。主詞 she 用 has。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"I ______ Amy since we were in elementary school. We're best friends.","options":["know","have known","knew","have been knowing"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我從國小就認識 Amy 了，我們是最要好的朋友。since 表示從過去持續到現在，用現在完成式；know 是狀態動詞，不用進行式。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"It ______ since early this morning, so we can't play baseball after school.","options":["rains","is raining","rained","has been raining"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：從一大早就一直在下雨，所以放學後不能打棒球。since 表示持續到現在，雨還在下，用現在完成進行式；is raining 不能配 since。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"By the time we got to the theater, the movie ______.","options":["has started","starts","had started","will have started"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我們到電影院時，電影已經開始了。開演比過去的 got 更早，用過去完成式 had + p.p.；has started 不能配過去時間。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"By the end of this year, Kevin ______ at the convenience store for two years.","options":["will have worked","has worked","had worked","works"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：到今年年底，Kevin 就在便利商店工作滿兩年了。by + 未來時間，表示到那時已完成或持續，用未來完成式 will have + p.p.。故選 (A)。"}]},{"id":"g-modal","unit":"verb","level":"B1","title":"助動詞","en":"Modal verbs","lead":"can 等助動詞後接原形動詞；推測或後悔過去用助動詞 + have p.p.。","goals":["能在助動詞後正確使用原形動詞","能分辨 mustn't 和 don't have to","能用助動詞 + have p.p. 推測過去的事"],"prereq":["g-present","g-perfect"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[2]","note":"mustn't 在美式較少用，常說 must not、can't；統測選項是否仍以 mustn't 為主待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"助動詞 + 原形動詞","text":["can、will、should 等**助動詞**後面接**原形動詞**，本身也不加 -s：說 He can swim，不說 He cans swim 或 He can swims。","否定在助動詞後加 not（can't、shouldn't）；問句把助動詞移到主詞前（Can you…?）。","兩個**情態助動詞**（can、will、must…）不能連用：will can 要改成 will **be able to**；但接 be、have 可以（must be）。"],"adv":["can 的否定通常寫成 cannot 或 can't。助動詞的被動（can be done）詳見〈被動語態〉。"],"formula":"S + 助動詞 (+ not) + 原形動詞","parse":{"en":"My little brother can ride a bike now.","zh":"我弟弟現在會騎腳踏車了。","parts":[["My little brother","S"],["can ride","V"],["a bike","O"],["now.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My little brother [[can ride]] a bike now.","zh":"我弟弟現在會騎腳踏車了。"},{"en":"You [[shouldn't eat]] fried chicken so late at night.","zh":"你不該這麼晚還吃炸雞。"},{"en":"[[Will]] you [[be able to]] come to my birthday party on Saturday?","zh":"你星期六能來參加我的生日派對嗎？"}],"practice":[{"q":"My grandma can ______ dumplings very fast.","options":["makes","make","making","to make"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：助動詞 can 後接原形動詞。主詞雖是第三人稱單數，can 後的動詞也不加 -s。(A) makes 多了 -s；(C) making、(D) to make 都不能直接接在 can 後。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"My little sister ______ swim yet, but she is taking lessons.","options":["doesn't can","not can","can't"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：助動詞的否定是在助動詞後加 not。can 的否定是 can't（cannot）。(A) can 本身就是助動詞，不再用 does 幫忙；(B) not 要放在 can 後面。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"can、could、may、might","text":["**can** 表能力、許可、請求；**could** 是 can 的過去式，也用來客氣地請求：Could you…? 比 Can you…? 有禮貌。","**may** 表許可，比 can 正式；may 和 **might** 也表「可能」，might 的語氣常較不確定。","過去某一次成功辦到用 **was able to**，肯定句通常不用 could；could 指過去一般的能力。"],"adv":["例外：感官動詞可用 could 指過去某一次，如 We could see the fireworks from our balcony last night.","否定句不受此限，couldn't 也可指某一次：I couldn't find my key this morning."],"table":{"cols":["助動詞","用法","例句"],"rows":[["can","能力","Jay [[can play]] the guitar."],["could","過去的能力","I [[could swim]] when I was five."],["can / may","許可（may 較正式）","[[May]] I use the restroom?"],["can / could","請求（could 較客氣）","[[Could]] you pass me the salt?"],["may / might","可能","It [[may rain]] tonight."],["be able to","能力（可放在助動詞後）","We [[won't be able to]] come."]]},"parse":{"en":"Mia might be late because of the heavy rain.","zh":"雨下這麼大，Mia 可能會遲到。","parts":[["Mia","S"],["might be","V"],["late","C","主詞補語"],["because of the heavy rain.","M","原因"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Can]] I borrow your notes? I was sick yesterday.","zh":"你的筆記可以借我嗎？我昨天生病請假。"},{"en":"Mia [[might be]] late because of the heavy rain.","zh":"雨下這麼大，Mia 可能會遲到。"},{"en":"The test was hard, but I [[was able to]] finish it on time.","zh":"考試很難，但我還是在時間內寫完了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"When I was six, I ______ ride a bike without any help.","options":["can","could","may"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：could 表過去一般的能力。When I was six 是過去，用 could。(A) can 是現在式，時態不合；(C) may 表許可或可能，不表能力。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Ask Tom about it. He ______ know the answer, but I'm not sure.","options":["must","has to","might"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：might 表「可能」。後句 but I'm not sure 表示說話者不確定，用 might。(A) must、(B) has to 在這裡是「一定」或「必須」，和「不確定」矛盾。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"義務與建議：must、should","text":["**must** 和 **have to** 都是「必須」。have to 會隨主詞和時態變化（has to、had to）；must 沒有過去式，過去的「必須」用 had to。","兩者否定不同：**must not**（mustn't）是「禁止」，**don't have to**（= don't need to；英式也說 needn't）是「不必」。","**should** 和 ought to 都是「應該」；**had better** 是「最好…（不然會有麻煩）」，否定是 had better not V。"],"adv":["美式口語多用 have to 表「必須」；must 較正式，常見於校規、告示等規定。","had better 雖然有 had，指的卻是現在或未來，口語常縮成 You'd better；ought to 的否定是 ought not to，較少用。"],"table":{"cols":["說法","意思","例句"],"rows":[["must / have to","必須","Students [[must]] wear uniforms."],["had to","過去必須","I [[had to]] wait 30 minutes."],["must not (mustn't)","禁止","You [[must not]] eat on the MRT."],["don't have to","不必","You [[don't have to]] pay. It's free."],["should / ought to","應該","You [[should]] see a doctor."],["had better (not)","最好（不要）","We [[had better]] hurry."]]},"parse":{"en":"Amy has to take care of her little sister after school.","zh":"Amy 放學後得照顧妹妹。","parts":[["Amy","S"],["has to take care of","V"],["her little sister","O"],["after school.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Amy [[has to]] take care of her little sister after school.","zh":"Amy 放學後得照顧妹妹。"},{"en":"We [[don't have to]] wear uniforms on Fridays.","zh":"我們星期五不用穿制服。"},{"en":"You [[ought to]] thank Grandma for the red envelope.","zh":"你應該謝謝奶奶給的紅包。"},{"en":"You [[had better not]] be late again, or Coach Lin will get angry.","zh":"你最好別再遲到，不然林教練會生氣。"}],"practice":[{"q":"You ______ use your phone during the exam. It's against the rules.","options":["don't have to","must not","had better"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：must not 表「禁止」。後句說這違反規定，所以是「不可以」用手機。(A) don't have to 是「不必」，好像用不用都行；(C) had better 是「最好要用」，句意相反。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"It's going to rain. You ______ forget your umbrella.","options":["had better not","had not better","better not had"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：had better 的否定是 had better not + 原形動詞，not 放在 better 後面。(B) not 放錯位置；(C) 字的順序整個顛倒。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"想要與寧願","text":["**would like to V** 同 want to V，但較客氣；would like 也可直接接名詞，不加 to：I'd like a milk tea, please.","**would rather A than B** 表「寧願 A，也不要 B」，A、B 都用原形動詞；否定是 would rather not V。"],"adv":["would like 是「現在想要」，like 是「平常喜歡」：I'd like to swim. 是現在想去游，I like to swim. 是喜歡游泳。","would rather 後接子句（I'd rather you stayed home.）是假設用法，詳見〈條件句與假設語氣〉。"],"formula":"S + would rather + 原形 A + than + 原形 B","parse":{"en":"Kai would rather not talk about his test scores.","zh":"Kai 不太想談他的考試成績。","parts":[["Kai","S"],["would rather","V"],["not","M","否定"],["talk about","V"],["his test scores.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Would]] you [[like to]] go to the night market with us tonight?","zh":"今晚要不要跟我們去逛夜市？"},{"en":"I [[would rather]] walk home [[than]] wait for the bus in the rain.","zh":"我寧願走路回家，也不要在雨中等公車。"},{"en":"Kai [[would rather not]] talk about his test scores.","zh":"Kai 不太想談他的考試成績。"}],"practice":[{"q":"A: Do you want to eat out tonight? B: I'm tired. I'd rather ______ at home.","options":["eating","to eat","eat"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：would rather 後接原形動詞。I'd 是 I would 的縮寫，後面用原形 eat。(A) eating、(B) to eat 都不能接在 would rather 後。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I would like ______ a new phone for my birthday.","options":["to get","get","getting"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：would like 後接動詞用 to V，意思同 want to V，但較客氣。(B) get 少了 to；(C) getting 不能接在 would like 後表「想要」。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"used to 與 be used to","text":["**used to V** 表「以前常…、以前是…」，現在已經不是這樣，後面接原形動詞。","**be used to V-ing/N** 表「習慣於…」，這裡的 to 是介系詞，所以接 V-ing 或名詞；get used to 表「漸漸習慣」。","別和被動的 be used to V（被用來做…）搞混，例如 Bamboo is used to make chopsticks.（竹子被用來做筷子。）"],"adv":["used to 的否定與疑問由 did 承擔，寫成 didn't use to、Did you use to…?（did 後面的 use 不加 -d）。"],"table":{"cols":["句型","意思","例句"],"rows":[["used to + 原形","以前常…／以前是…（現在不再）","I [[used to live]] in Kaohsiung."],["be used to + V-ing / N","習慣於…","Grandpa [[is used to getting]] up at five."],["get used to + V-ing / N","漸漸習慣…","You'll [[get used to]] the new school."]]},"parse":{"en":"Grandpa used to ride his bike to the market every morning.","zh":"爺爺以前每天早上都騎腳踏車去市場。","parts":[["Grandpa","S"],["used to ride","V"],["his bike","O"],["to the market","M","方向"],["every morning.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My dad [[used to smoke]], but he quit three years ago.","zh":"我爸以前抽菸，但三年前戒了。"},{"en":"There [[used to be]] a bookstore across from our school.","zh":"我們學校對面以前有一家書店。"},{"en":"Lily [[is used to taking]] the MRT to school by herself.","zh":"Lily 已經習慣自己搭捷運上學。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My uncle ______ live in Japan, but now he lives in Taichung.","options":["is used to","used to","uses to"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：used to + 原形動詞表「以前…（現在不再）」。後句 but now 表示現在不同了。(A) is used to 表「習慣於」，後面要接 V-ing；(C) 沒有 uses to 的說法。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Mom works at night, so she is used to ______ during the day.","options":["sleep","sleeping","slept"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：be used to + V-ing 表「習慣於…」，這裡的 to 是介系詞，後面接 sleeping。(A) 原形 sleep 是接在沒有 be 的 used to 後；(C) slept 是過去式，不能接在 to 後。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"推測：現在與過去","text":["推測現在：**must** 一定是、may/might 可能是、**can't** 不可能是。表「不可能」用 can't，不用 mustn't（mustn't 是禁止）。","推測過去的事，助動詞後改接 **have p.p.**；can't have p.p. 也常說成 couldn't have p.p.。","**should have p.p.** 常表「應該做卻沒做」，帶有後悔或責備；could have p.p. 常指「本來可以…卻沒有」。"],"adv":["美式英語也常用 must not 表「想必不是」，如 He must not be home.（他想必不在家。）語氣比 can't 弱。","could have p.p. 也可表過去的可能，如 He could have taken the wrong bus.（他可能搭錯車了。）要看上下文判斷。"],"formula":"現在：must/may/can't + 原形；過去：must/may/can't + have p.p.","table":{"cols":["句型","意思","例句"],"rows":[["must have p.p.","（當時）一定…","The ground is wet. It [[must have rained]]."],["can't have p.p.","（當時）不可能…","He [[can't have seen]] me. I wasn't there."],["may / might have p.p.","（當時）可能…","She [[may have missed]] the bus."],["could have p.p.","本來可以…卻沒有；也可表（當時）可能…","You [[could have asked]] me for help."],["should have p.p.","應該…（卻沒有）","I [[should have studied]] harder."],["shouldn't have p.p.","不該…（卻做了）","I [[shouldn't have eaten]] so much."]]},"parse":{"en":"Kevin must have stayed up late last night.","zh":"Kevin 昨晚一定熬夜到很晚。","parts":[["Kevin","S"],["must have stayed up","V"],["late","M"],["last night.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Jenny isn't answering her phone. She [[must be]] in class.","zh":"Jenny 沒接電話，她一定在上課。"},{"en":"Kevin looks so tired. He [[must have stayed up]] late playing games last night.","zh":"Kevin 看起來好累，昨晚一定熬夜打電動。"},{"en":"Leo [[can't have taken]] your umbrella. He was home sick all day.","zh":"Leo 不可能拿走你的傘，他整天都生病在家。"},{"en":"I'm starving. I [[should have eaten]] breakfast this morning.","zh":"我餓扁了，早上真該吃早餐的。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Jenny's eyes are red and puffy. She ______ last night.","options":["must cry","can't have cried","must have cried"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：對過去的肯定推測用 must have p.p.。眼睛紅腫，推測她昨晚「一定哭過」。(A) must cry 沒有 have p.p.，不能推測昨晚的事；(B) can't have cried 是「不可能哭過」，和線索矛盾。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Kevin worked at the night market for ten hours today. He ______ tired now.","options":["must be","must have been","can't be"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：推測現在的狀態用 must + 原形。工作雖然已做完，但「累」是現在（now）的狀態，用 must be。(B) must have been 指過去，和 now 不合；(C) can't be 是「不可能累」，不合句意。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"My sister can speaks three languages.","right":"My sister can [[speak]] three languages.","why":"can 等助動詞後面接原形動詞，不加 -s。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"I will can ride a scooter next year.","right":"I [[will be able to]] ride a scooter next year.","why":"will 和 can 不能連用，can 要改成 be able to。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Tom maybe sick today. He isn't in class.","right":"Tom [[may be]] sick today. He isn't in class.","why":"maybe 是副詞（也許），不能當動詞；「可能是」要用 may be。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"When I was a child, I can swim very well.","right":"When I was a child, I [[could]] swim very well.","why":"過去的能力用 could，不用 can。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"Tomorrow is Sunday, so I mustn't get up early.","right":"Tomorrow is Sunday, so I [[don't have to]] get up early.","why":"「不必」用 don't have to；mustn't 是「禁止」。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"You had not better play games all night.","right":"You [[had better not]] play games all night.","why":"had better 的否定是 had better not + 原形動詞。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"I would like go to Japan this summer.","right":"I would like [[to go]] to Japan this summer.","why":"would like 後面接動詞時要用 to V。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"I'm not used to get up so early.","right":"I'm not used to [[getting]] up so early.","why":"be used to 的 to 是介系詞，後面接 V-ing。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"He must has forgotten my birthday.","right":"He must [[have]] forgotten my birthday.","why":"助動詞後接原形，要寫 must have p.p.，不寫 has。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"I should study for the test yesterday.","right":"I [[should have studied]] for the test yesterday.","why":"昨天「該做卻沒做」要用 should have p.p.。"}],"tips":["mustn't（禁止）和 don't have to（不必）常同時出現在選項，看上下文是「不准」還是「不用」。","used to V＝以前常；be/get used to V-ing／N＝習慣；物 be used to V＝被用來。","被推測的事發生在過去才用助動詞 + have p.p.；「早該…卻沒」用 should have p.p.。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Ben can ______ 100 meters in 13 seconds.","options":["runs","run","running","to run"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Ben 能在 13 秒內跑完 100 公尺。助動詞 can 後面一律接原形動詞，不加 -s，也不接 to V。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"A: Do I have to hand in the report today? B: No, you ______. Friday is fine.","options":["mustn't","can't","shouldn't","don't have to"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我今天一定要交報告嗎？不用，星期五交就可以。「不必」用 don't have to；mustn't 是「禁止」，和後句矛盾。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"My grandpa ______ go fishing in this river when he was young.","options":["used to","is used to","was used to","uses to"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我爺爺年輕時常在這條河釣魚。過去的習慣用 used to + 原形動詞；be used to 表「習慣於」，後面要接 V-ing。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Ken moved to Taipei last year. Now he is used to ______ the MRT every day.","options":["take","took","taking","taken"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Ken 去年搬到台北，現在已經習慣每天搭捷運。be used to 表「習慣於」，to 是介系詞，後面接 V-ing。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Lisa is taking swimming lessons. She hopes she ______ swim by the end of summer.","options":["will can","will able to","can be able","will be able to"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Lisa 在上游泳課，希望夏天結束前能學會游泳。will 和 can 不能連用，未來的能力用 will be able to + 原形；able 是形容詞，前面要有 be。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Ryan would rather walk to school than ______ the crowded bus.","options":["take","taking","to take","took"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：Ryan 寧願走路上學，也不要搭擁擠的公車。would rather A than B，A、B 都用原形動詞，walk 對應 take。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"I failed the math test. I ______ harder last week.","options":["should study","must have studied","should have studied","may study"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我數學考不及格，上週應該更用功的。「應該做卻沒做」用 should have p.p.；must have studied 是「一定讀過」，不合句意。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Emma ______ my message last night. Her phone was at the repair shop.","options":["must have read","can't have read","must read","may read"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Emma 昨晚不可能看到我的訊息，她的手機在送修。對過去的否定推測用 can't have p.p.；must have read 是「一定看過」，和手機送修矛盾。故選 (B)。"}]},{"id":"g-passive","unit":"verb","level":"B1","title":"被動語態","en":"The passive voice","lead":"主詞是「被」做某事的一方時，用 be + p.p.，時態由 be 動詞表現。","goals":["能用 be + p.p. 寫出各時態與助動詞的被動句","能分辨沒有被動的動詞，如 happen、consist of","能用 known for/as、is said to 造句"],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-perfect","g-modal"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[4]","note":"made of／from 依看不看得出原料區分是教學慣例，實際用法有重疊；統測是否只依此命題待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"be + p.p. 與使用時機","text":["主動句的受詞移到句首當主詞，動詞改成 **be + p.p.**，原本的主詞用 **by** 帶出。be 動詞要配合新主詞和時態。","用被動的時機：不知道是誰做的、是誰做的不重要，或想**強調受動者**（被做的人或物）。前兩種情況通常省略 by + 行為者。","中文沒有「被」字也常要用被動，例如「學校創立於 1965 年」「夜市都有賣臭豆腐」。"],"formula":"S + be + p.p. (+ by + 行為者)","table":{"cols":["主動","被動"],"rows":[["Mom [[cleaned]] the kitchen.","The kitchen [[was cleaned]] by Mom."],["Grandma [[makes]] these dumplings.","These dumplings [[are made]] by Grandma."]]},"parse":{"en":"The posters for our school fair were designed by Amy's class.","zh":"我們園遊會的海報是 Amy 他們班設計的。","parts":[["The posters for our school fair","S"],["were designed","V","被動"],["by Amy's class.","M","行為者"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My bike [[was stolen]] outside the MRT station last night.","zh":"我的腳踏車昨晚在捷運站外面被偷了。"},{"en":"Stinky tofu [[is sold]] at almost every night market in Taiwan.","zh":"台灣幾乎每個夜市都有賣臭豆腐。"},{"en":"Our school [[was founded]] in 1965.","zh":"我們學校創立於 1965 年。"},{"en":"The posters for our school fair [[were designed]] [[by]] Amy's class.","zh":"我們園遊會的海報是 Amy 他們班設計的。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The bathrooms at our school ______ by students every afternoon.","options":["clean","are cleaned","are cleaning","cleaned"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：被動語態 be + p.p.。廁所是「被打掃」，every afternoon 表習慣，用 are cleaned。(A) clean、(C) are cleaning 是主動，像是廁所自己打掃；(D) cleaned 前面少了 be 動詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"This song ______ by a high school student in 2020.","options":["wrote","was wrote","is written","was written"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：被動 be + p.p.，p.p. 要用過去分詞。歌是「被寫」，in 2020 用 was written。(A) wrote 是主動；(B) wrote 是過去式，不是 p.p.；(C) is written 是現在式，不合 in 2020。故選 (D)。"}]},{"h":"各時態與助動詞","text":["先想主動句該用什麼時態，再把 **be 動詞**換成那個時態，後面的 p.p. 不變。","進行式加 **being**，完成式加 **been**；助動詞（can、must、should、may）後面接原形 be，再接 p.p.。","否定的 not 放在第一個 be 動詞或助動詞後：wasn't invited、hasn't been fixed。疑問句把它移到主詞前：Has it been fixed?"],"adv":["完成進行式和未來進行式的被動（如 has been being + p.p.）很少用，先熟悉表中的形式即可。使役動詞的被動詳見〈使役動詞與感官動詞〉。"],"table":{"cols":["類型","被動形式","例句"],"rows":[["現在簡單式","am/is/are + p.p.","English [[is spoken]] in many countries."],["過去簡單式","was/were + p.p.","The game [[was canceled]]."],["未來式","will be + p.p.／be going to be + p.p.","Dinner [[will be served]] at six."],["現在進行式","am/is/are being + p.p.","The gym [[is being painted]]."],["過去進行式","was/were being + p.p.","The car [[was being washed]] when it started to rain."],["現在完成式","have/has been + p.p.","My order [[has been shipped]]."],["過去完成式","had been + p.p.","All the bread [[had been sold]] before we arrived."],["助動詞","can/must/should + be + p.p.","This [[can be done]] online."]]},"parse":{"en":"The elevator has not been fixed yet.","zh":"電梯還沒修好。","parts":[["The elevator","S"],["has","V","助動詞"],["not","M","否定"],["been fixed","V","完成式被動"],["yet.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The road in front of our school [[is being repaired]], so traffic is really slow.","zh":"學校前面的路正在整修，所以路上很塞。"},{"en":"My phone screen [[has been fixed]], so I can text you again.","zh":"我的手機螢幕修好了，又可以傳訊息給你了。"},{"en":"The test scores [[will be posted]] online next Monday.","zh":"考試成績下週一會公布在網路上。"},{"en":"Phones [[must be turned off]] during the exam.","zh":"考試時手機必須關機。"}],"practice":[{"q":"This bridge ______ in 1990, and people still use it today.","options":["built","was built","has been built","is built"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：過去簡單式被動 was/were + p.p.。橋是「被建造」，in 1990 是明確的過去時間，用 was built。(A) built 是主動；(C) 現在完成式不能配 in 1990；(D) is built 是現在式。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Food can't ______ on the MRT in Taipei.","options":["eat","eaten","be eaten","be eating"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：助動詞 + be + p.p.。食物是「被吃」，can't 後面接原形 be，再接 eaten。(A) eat、(D) be eating 是主動，像是食物自己在吃；(B) 助動詞後面不能直接接 p.p.。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"不及物動詞沒有被動","text":["被動句的主詞來自主動句的受詞，所以只有**及物動詞**才有被動。不及物動詞後面沒有受詞，**不能改被動**。","常考：happen、occur（發生）、take place（舉行）、appear（出現）、disappear（消失）、consist of（由…組成），都不能寫成被動。","判斷法：happen something 不成立，所以沒有被動。laugh at、take care of 後面接受詞，被動時介系詞要保留：was laughed at。"],"adv":["注意：consist of、have（擁有）、cost、resemble 雖然接受詞，也不用被動：The team consists of ten players."],"parse":{"en":"A car accident happened near the night market last night.","zh":"昨晚夜市附近發生了一場車禍。","parts":[["A car accident","S"],["happened","V","不及物動詞"],["near the night market","M","地點"],["last night.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"A car accident [[happened]] near the night market last night.","zh":"昨晚夜市附近發生了一場車禍。"},{"en":"A big rainbow [[appeared]] after the afternoon rain.","zh":"下午那場雨過後，出現了一道大彩虹。"},{"en":"The basketball tournament [[will take place]] in our school gym next week.","zh":"籃球賽下週將在我們學校的體育館舉行。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The earthquake ______ at 3 a.m. last night, so most people were asleep.","options":["occurred","was occurred","is occurred","has occurred"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：不及物動詞沒有被動。occur（發生）不接受詞，不能寫成被動，直接用過去式 occurred。(B)、(C) 是錯誤的被動；(D) 現在完成式不能配 last night 這種明確的過去時間。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Tim fell off his chair in class, and he ______ by everyone.","options":["laughed at","was laughed","was laughed at","was laughing at"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：laugh at 接受詞，可以改被動，介系詞 at 要保留。Tim 是「被嘲笑」，用 was laughed at。(A) laughed at 是主動；(B) 少了 at；(D) was laughing at 是主動進行式。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"get + p.p.","text":["口語常用 **get + p.p.** 表示發生在主詞身上的事，多指意外、突發的事或狀態改變，如 get hurt、get caught、get stuck。","表狀態的被動不能換成 get：This desk is made of wood. 不能說 gets made of；is known for 也一樣。","get 是**一般動詞**，否定、疑問用 do/does/did：I didn't get invited.／Did you get hurt?"],"adv":["正式寫作仍以 be + p.p. 為主。get + p.p. 也可以用於好事，如 get paid、get promoted。"],"formula":"S + get + p.p.","parse":{"en":"Jason got hurt during basketball practice yesterday.","zh":"Jason 昨天練籃球時受傷了。","parts":[["Jason","S"],["got hurt","V","get 被動"],["during basketball practice","M","時間"],["yesterday.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Jason [[got hurt]] during basketball practice yesterday.","zh":"Jason 昨天練籃球時受傷了。"},{"en":"We [[got stuck]] in traffic on the way to Kenting.","zh":"我們去墾丁的路上遇到塞車。"},{"en":"Be careful, or you'll [[get caught]] using your phone in class.","zh":"小心點，上課滑手機會被抓到喔。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ your brother get caught sleeping in class again?","options":["Did","Was","Is","Has"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：get 是一般動詞，疑問句用 do/does/did。get 是原形，前面用 Did。(B) Was、(C) Is 是 be 動詞，後面不能接原形 get；(D) Has 後面要接 p.p.（gotten），不能接 get。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"My new phone case ______ of leather.","options":["makes","gets made","is made","is making"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：表狀態的被動不能換成 get。手機殼「由皮革製成」是狀態，用 is made of。(A) makes、(D) is making 是主動；(B) get 表發生或變化，不能表狀態。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"被動常接的介系詞","text":["有些被動片語不用 by，而是固定搭配其他介系詞，要整組記。","**made of** 多用於看得出原料（木頭做的桌子）；**made from** 多用於看不出原料（木頭做成的紙）。","**known for** + 特色或原因（因…出名）；**known as** + 名稱或身分（被稱為…）；known to + 人（為…所知）。"],"adv":["interested、crowded 等已當形容詞用，-ed 與 -ing 的差別詳見〈分詞當形容詞〉。","一般教學依「看不看得出原料」區分 of 和 from；但實際上 made from 也常用於看得出原料的東西，如 a table made from recycled wood。"],"table":{"cols":["片語","意思","例句"],"rows":[["be made of","由…製成（多指看得出原料）","This desk [[is made of]] wood."],["be made from","由…製成（多指看不出原料）","Paper [[is made from]] wood."],["be known for","因…而出名","Beitou [[is known for]] its hot springs."],["be known as","被稱為…；以…身分出名","Hsinchu [[is known as]] the Windy City."],["be known to","為（某人）所知","This singer [[is known to]] everyone in Taiwan."],["be covered with","被…覆蓋","The car [[was covered with]] dust."],["be interested in","對…有興趣","Lisa [[is interested in]] cooking."],["be crowded with","擠滿…","The night market [[is crowded with]] tourists."]]},"parse":{"en":"Ken is interested in Japanese anime.","zh":"Ken 對日本動畫有興趣。","parts":[["Ken","S"],["is","V","be 動詞"],["interested in Japanese anime.","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"These chopsticks [[are made of]] bamboo.","zh":"這些筷子是竹子做的。"},{"en":"Tofu [[is made from]] soybeans.","zh":"豆腐是用黃豆做成的。"},{"en":"Lukang [[is known for]] its old streets and tasty snacks.","zh":"鹿港以老街和美味小吃聞名。"},{"en":"Ken [[is interested in]] Japanese anime, so he's learning Japanese.","zh":"Ken 對日本動畫有興趣，所以正在學日文。"}],"practice":[{"q":"After the hike in the rain, my shoes were covered ______ mud.","options":["with","of","for","at"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：be covered with（被…覆蓋）。鞋子沾滿泥巴，用 covered with。(B) of 用於 made of 表原料；(C) for、(D) at 都不和 covered 搭配。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Taichung is known ______ the home of bubble tea.","options":["for","of","with","as"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：be known as + 名稱或身分（被稱為…）。the home of bubble tea 是台中的稱號，用 as。(A) for 後面接特色或原因，如 known for its bubble tea；(B) of、(C) with 不和 known 這樣搭配。故選 (D)。"}]},{"h":"It is said that…","text":["**It is said that** + 子句 表示「據說」。也可以把子句的主詞移到句首，改成 **S + is said to V**。","內容比「說」的時間更早（如過去的事），用 **to have + p.p.**；同時發生則用 to V。believe、think、report 也能用同樣兩種句型。"],"adv":["「說」用過去式時也一樣看先後：It was said that he was rich. → He was said to be rich.（同時，用 to be）"],"formula":"It is said that + S + V = S + is said to + V","parse":{"en":"It is said that this temple is over 300 years old.","zh":"據說這座廟有三百多年的歷史。","parts":[["It","S","虛主詞"],["is said","V","被動"],["that this temple is over 300 years old.","S","名詞子句當真主詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[It is said that]] this temple is over 300 years old.","zh":"據說這座廟有三百多年的歷史。"},{"en":"This temple [[is said to be]] over 300 years old.","zh":"這座廟據說有三百多年的歷史。"},{"en":"Mr. Lin next door [[is said to have been]] a famous baseball player when he was young.","zh":"據說隔壁的林先生年輕時是有名的棒球選手。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Mr. Chang's beef noodle shop is said ______ the best noodles in town.","options":["sells","to sell","selling","that it sells"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：S + is said + to V。主詞放句首時，said 後面接不定詞 to sell。(A) sells 是現在式、(C) selling 是 V-ing，都不能直接接在 is said 後；(D) that 子句要用 It is said that 開頭。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"This email was wrote in English.","right":"This email [[was written]] in English.","why":"be 後面要接過去分詞 written；wrote 是過去式。","sec":0},{"wrong":"A new MRT station will built near our school.","right":"A new MRT station [[will be built]] near our school.","why":"未來式被動是 will be + p.p.，不能漏掉 be。","sec":1},{"wrong":"Our classroom is cleaning now, so we have to wait outside.","right":"Our classroom [[is being cleaned]] now, so we have to wait outside.","why":"教室是被打掃，正在進行的被動用 be being + p.p.。","sec":1},{"wrong":"The accident was happened on my way to school.","right":"The accident [[happened]] on my way to school.","why":"happen 是不及物動詞，沒有被動，直接用過去式。","sec":2},{"wrong":"Our class is consisted of 35 students.","right":"Our class [[consists of]] 35 students.","why":"consist of 沒有被動，直接用主動 consists of。","sec":2},{"wrong":"My cousin got marry last month.","right":"My cousin [[got married]] last month.","why":"get 後面要接過去分詞 married，不能接原形 marry。","sec":3},{"wrong":"Taiwan is known as its night markets.","right":"Taiwan [[is known for]] its night markets.","why":"因特色出名用 known for；known as 後面接名稱或身分。","sec":4},{"wrong":"This table is made by wood.","right":"This table [[is made of]] wood.","why":"表示原料用 made of；by 後面接的是製作的人。","sec":4},{"wrong":"This night market is said that it has the best fried chicken.","right":"This night market [[is said to have]] the best fried chicken.","why":"S is said 後面接 to V；要用 that 子句就改成 It is said that。","sec":5},{"wrong":"Ms. Wu is said to be a top student at our school ten years ago.","right":"Ms. Wu [[is said to have been]] a top student at our school ten years ago.","why":"十年前比「說」的時間早，要用 to have + p.p.。","sec":5}],"tips":["先判斷主詞是「做」還是「被做」，再看時間詞決定 be 的形式，如 next week 選 will be + p.p.。","選項出現 was happened、was disappeared 直接刪掉：不及物動詞沒有被動。","中譯英：據說用 It is said that；以特色聞名用 known for，以身分聞名用 known as。"],"quiz":[{"q":"My scooter ______ last night, so I had to take the bus to school today.","options":["stole","was stolen","has stolen","was stealing"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我的機車昨晚被偷了，所以今天只好搭公車上學。機車是「被偷」，last night 是過去，用 was + p.p.；stole 是過去式，不是 p.p.。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The results of the speech contest ______ on the school website tomorrow.","options":["will announce","announced","are announcing","will be announced"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：演講比賽的結果明天會公布在學校網站上。結果是「被公布」，tomorrow 是未來，用 will be + p.p.；will announce 是主動。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Sorry, you can't use the elevator right now. It ______ by two workers.","options":["is checking","is checked","is being checked","has checked"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：抱歉，電梯現在不能用，兩位工人正在檢查。right now 表示正在進行，被動進行式是 be being + p.p.；is checked 是現在簡單式。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"You don't need to take out the trash. It ______ already.","options":["has been taken out","has taken out","is taking out","took out"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：你不用倒垃圾，已經倒掉了。垃圾是「被拿出去」，配 already 用現在完成式被動 has been + p.p.。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The broken window should ______ before the typhoon comes.","options":["fix","fixed","be fixed","be fixing"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：颱風來之前，那扇破掉的窗戶應該要修好。窗戶是「被修」，助動詞後接 be + p.p.；should 後面不能直接接 fixed。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Amy's puppy ______ yesterday afternoon, and her family is still looking for it.","options":["was disappeared","disappeared","has been disappeared","is disappeared"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Amy 的小狗昨天下午不見了，她的家人還在找。disappear 是不及物動詞，沒有被動，yesterday afternoon 用過去式。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Tainan is known ______ its delicious street food, such as beef soup and milkfish porridge.","options":["as","to","of","for"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：台南以美味的小吃聞名，例如牛肉湯和虱目魚粥。「因…而出名」用 be known for；be known as 後面接名稱或身分。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"The old house next to our school is said ______ a famous writer's home about 100 years ago.","options":["to have been","to be","that it was","being"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：據說學校旁邊的老房子大約一百年前是知名作家的家。S is said 後接 to V；一百年前比「說」的時間早，用 to have + p.p.；to be 表同時，不合 100 years ago。故選 (A)。"}]},{"id":"g-causative","unit":"verb","level":"B1","title":"使役動詞與感官動詞","en":"Causative and sense verbs","lead":"使役動詞 + O 多接原形，get 接 to V；感官動詞接原形或 V-ing。","goals":["能分辨 make/have/let 與 get 的接法","能用 have/get + 物 + p.p. 表示請人做事","能依意思選感官動詞後的原形、V-ing 或 p.p."],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-passive"],"pending":[],"sections":[{"h":"使役動詞：make/have/let","text":["**使役動詞** make、have、let 表示「使、叫、讓」某人做某事，後面接**受詞 + 原形動詞**，不加 to。"],"adv":["make 也常接形容詞當受詞補語：make me happy（讓我開心），詳見〈句子的基本結構〉。"],"formula":"S + make/have/let + O + 原形動詞","table":{"cols":["動詞","意思","例子"],"rows":[["make","強迫、使得","make me [[wait]]"],["have","叫、請人做（工作、服務）","have him [[call]] you back"],["let","讓、允許","let us [[go]] home"]]},"parse":{"en":"The sad ending made everyone in the theater cry.","zh":"悲傷的結局讓整間戲院的人都哭了。","parts":[["The sad ending","S"],["made","V","使役動詞"],["everyone in the theater","O"],["cry.","C","原形當受詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Mom [[made]] me [[wash]] all the dishes after dinner.","zh":"晚餐後媽媽要我把碗全部洗完。"},{"en":"The sad ending [[made]] everyone in the theater [[cry]].","zh":"悲傷的結局讓整間戲院的人都哭了。"},{"en":"Our teacher [[had]] each of us [[read]] a short poem aloud.","zh":"老師叫我們每個人朗讀一首短詩。"},{"en":"My parents [[let]] me [[go]] to the concert with my friends.","zh":"爸媽讓我跟朋友去聽演唱會。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My dad let me ______ his new camera on the school trip.","options":["use","to use","using"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：let + O + 原形動詞。let 是使役動詞，受詞 me 後面直接接原形 use。(B) to use 多了 to；(C) using 不能接在 let + O 後面。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The long line at the night market made us ______ for almost an hour.","options":["to wait","waiting","wait"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：make + O + 原形動詞。make 表「使得」，受詞 us 後面接原形 wait。(A) to wait 多了 to；(B) waiting 不能接在 make + O 後面。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"get 與 help","text":["**get + O + to V** 也是「叫、說服某人做」，但一定要加 **to**，常有「費了點工夫才說動」的意味。","**help + O + (to) V** 接原形或 to V 都對：help me (to) carry the boxes。","ask、tell、want 等動詞也接 O + to V，詳見〈不定詞 to V〉。"],"adv":["美式較常用 help + O + 原形。受詞也可以省略：help (to) clean the classroom。"],"formula":"get + O + to V／help + O + (to) V","parse":{"en":"Jenny finally got her dad to buy her a new phone.","zh":"Jenny 終於說服爸爸幫她買新手機。","parts":[["Jenny","S"],["finally","M"],["got","V"],["her dad","O"],["to buy her a new phone.","C","to V 當受詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Jenny finally [[got]] her dad [[to buy]] her a new phone.","zh":"Jenny 終於說服爸爸幫她買新手機。"},{"en":"Can you [[get]] your brother [[to pick]] us up at the MRT station?","zh":"你可以叫你哥哥來捷運站接我們嗎？"},{"en":"Kevin [[helped]] me [[carry]] the boxes up to the third floor.","zh":"Kevin 幫我把箱子搬上三樓。"},{"en":"Working at a bubble tea shop [[helped]] Amy [[to save]] enough money for her trip to Japan.","zh":"在飲料店打工讓 Amy 存夠了去日本旅行的錢。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Leo couldn't open the jar, so he got his sister ______ it for him.","options":["open","to open","opens"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：get + O + to V 表「叫、說服某人做」。get 和 make、have 不同，受詞後要加 to，用 to open。(A) open 是 make、have 的接法；(C) opens 不能直接接在受詞後面。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Could you help me ______ these chairs into the classroom?","options":["carry","carrying","carried"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：help + O + (to) V。help 後接原形或 to V 都對，選項中只有原形 carry 正確。(B) carrying、(C) carried 都不能接在 help + O 後面。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"have/get + 物 + p.p.","text":["受詞是「被處理」的東西時，用 **have/get + 物 + p.p.**，表示「請別人把…做好」。","判斷方法：受詞會主動去做（通常是人），have 接原形、get 接 to V；受詞是被處理的（通常是物），接 **p.p.**。"],"adv":["這個句型也能表示「遭遇」壞事，例如 have sth stolen（某物被偷）。","make 也可接 p.p.，多用於固定說法：make myself understood（讓別人聽懂我）。"],"formula":"S + have/get + 物 + p.p.","table":{"cols":["受詞","句型","例子"],"rows":[["人（主動去做）","have + 人 + 原形","have the mechanic [[fix]] my bike"],["人（主動去做）","get + 人 + to V","get the mechanic [[to fix]] my bike"],["物（被處理）","have/get + 物 + p.p.","have/get my bike [[fixed]]"]]},"parse":{"en":"Dad got the air conditioner fixed before summer.","zh":"爸爸在夏天前找人把冷氣修好了。","parts":[["Dad","S"],["got","V"],["the air conditioner","O"],["fixed","C","p.p. 當受詞補語"],["before summer.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I [[had]] my hair [[cut]] at a salon near school yesterday.","zh":"我昨天在學校附近的髮廊剪了頭髮。"},{"en":"Dad [[got]] the air conditioner [[fixed]] before summer.","zh":"爸爸在夏天前找人把冷氣修好了。"},{"en":"You should [[have]] your eyes [[checked]] if you can't see the board clearly.","zh":"如果你看不清楚黑板，應該去檢查一下眼睛。"},{"en":"We [[got]] our class T-shirts [[printed]] at a shop near the night market.","zh":"我們請夜市附近的店印了班服。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My phone screen is broken, so I need to get it ______.","options":["repair","repaired","repairing"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：get + 物 + p.p. 表「請人把…做好」。it 指螢幕，是「被修理」的，用 p.p. repaired。(A) repair 是原形，不能接在 get + 物後面；(C) repairing 會變成螢幕自己在修。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Amy ______ her hair cut at a salon near her school last weekend.","options":["had","made","let"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：have + 物 + p.p. 表請人做。頭髮是被剪的，請髮型師剪頭髮說 had her hair cut。(B) made、(C) let 都沒有「請人把某物處理好」的用法。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"感官動詞的三種接法","text":["**感官動詞** see、watch、hear、feel、notice 後面先接受詞，再依意思接原形、V-ing 或 p.p.，都不加 to。","接**原形**表示看到、聽到動作從頭到尾；接 **V-ing** 表示動作當時正在進行，強調過程（常只看到一部分）。","受詞是「被…」的一方時，接 **p.p.**。"],"adv":["很多時候兩者差別不大，原形和 V-ing 都可以用。","listen to、look at 也可以這樣接：listen to Grandma sing。"],"formula":"S + see/hear/feel… + O + 原形／V-ing／p.p.","table":{"cols":["接法","表示","例子"],"rows":[["O + 原形","動作全程、已完成","I saw him [[cross]] the street."],["O + V-ing","當時正在進行","I saw him [[crossing]] the street."],["O + p.p.","受詞被…","I heard my name [[called]]."]]},"parse":{"en":"Did you feel the building shaking last night?","zh":"你昨晚有感覺到大樓在搖嗎？","parts":[["Did","V","助動詞"],["you","S"],["feel","V","感官動詞"],["the building","O"],["shaking","C","V-ing 當受詞補語"],["last night?","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I [[saw]] Leo [[score]] the winning goal in the last minute.","zh":"我看到 Leo 在最後一分鐘踢進致勝的一球。"},{"en":"As I walked by, I [[heard]] someone [[playing]] the piano upstairs.","zh":"我經過時，聽到樓上有人在彈鋼琴。"},{"en":"Did you [[feel]] the building [[shaking]] last night? It was an earthquake!","zh":"你昨晚有感覺到大樓在搖嗎？是地震！"},{"en":"We [[heard]] the winners' names [[announced]] at the end of Sports Day.","zh":"運動會最後，我們聽到大會宣布得獎者的名字。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Look! I can see Ben ______ in the pool over there.","options":["swims","to swim","swimming"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：感官動詞 + O + V-ing 表示正在進行。see 的受詞 Ben 後接 swimming，表示他此刻正在游。(A) swims 不能直接接在受詞後；(B) to swim 多了 to。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"At the clinic, Mia heard her name ______ and walked to the counter.","options":["called","call","calling"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：感官動詞 + O + p.p. 表被動。名字是「被叫」的，用 heard her name called。(B) call、(C) calling 都會變成名字自己在叫，不合理。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"keep/leave/find + O","text":["keep（使保持）、leave（留下、任由）、find（發現）+ O 後面接 **V-ing** 或 **p.p.**，不接原形。","受詞主動在做，接 V-ing：keep you waiting；受詞被…或處於某狀態，接 p.p.：keep the door locked。","也可接形容詞：keep the room clean、leave the door open，詳見〈句子的基本結構〉。"],"adv":["keep 後面直接接 V-ing（沒有受詞）是「一直做」：keep talking，詳見〈動名詞與不定詞的選擇〉。"],"formula":"S + keep/leave/find + O + V-ing／p.p.","table":{"cols":["動詞","+ O + V-ing","+ O + p.p."],"rows":[["keep 使保持","keep the fan [[running]]","keep the door [[locked]]"],["leave 留下、任由","leave the engine [[running]]","leave the door [[unlocked]]"],["find 發現","find her [[crying]]","find the window [[broken]]"]]},"parse":{"en":"When I got home, I found my little brother sleeping on the sofa.","zh":"我回到家時，發現弟弟在沙發上睡著了。","parts":[["When I got home,","M","時間子句"],["I","S"],["found","V"],["my little brother","O"],["sleeping on the sofa.","C","V-ing 當受詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Sorry to [[keep]] you [[waiting]]. The bus was late.","zh":"抱歉讓你久等了，公車誤點。"},{"en":"Don't [[leave]] the water [[running]] while you brush your teeth.","zh":"刷牙時別讓水一直流。"},{"en":"When I got home, I [[found]] my little brother [[sleeping]] on the sofa.","zh":"我回到家時，發現弟弟在沙發上睡著了。"},{"en":"Please [[keep]] the classroom door [[closed]] when the AC is on.","zh":"開冷氣時請把教室的門關著。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Don't leave the door ______ when you go out.","options":["unlock","unlocked","unlocking"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：leave + O + p.p. 表處於某狀態。門是處在「沒上鎖」的狀態，用 p.p. unlocked。(A) unlock 是原形，leave + O 後面不接原形；(C) unlocking 會變成門自己在開鎖。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The noise from the karaoke bar next door kept the baby ______ all night.","options":["cry","crying","to cry"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：keep + O + V-ing 表「讓某人一直…」。寶寶是主動在哭，用 crying。(A) cry 是原形、(C) to cry 是不定詞，都不能接在 keep + O 後面。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"被動：make 要加回 to","text":["make + O + 原形改成被動要加回 **to**：**be made to V**。see、hear 也一樣：be seen to V；進行中用 be seen V-ing。","**let** 一般不用被動，要改用 **be allowed to V**。被動語態的基本規則，詳見〈被動語態〉。"],"adv":["這種加回 to 的被動，最常見的是 make、see、hear；watch 不說 be watched to V。"],"formula":"S + be made to V","table":{"cols":["主動","被動"],"rows":[["The coach made us [[run]].","We were made [[to run]]."],["I saw him [[leave]].","He was seen [[to leave]]."],["They let us [[go]].","We were allowed [[to go]]."]]},"parse":{"en":"The players were made to run extra laps after losing the game.","zh":"輸了比賽後，球員們被罰多跑幾圈。","parts":[["The players","S"],["were made","V","被動"],["to run extra laps","C","主詞補語"],["after losing the game.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Cindy [[was made to rewrite]] her report because she copied it from the Internet.","zh":"Cindy 的報告是抄網路的，所以被要求重寫。"},{"en":"The players [[were made to run]] extra laps after losing the game.","zh":"輸了比賽後，球員們被罰多跑幾圈。"},{"en":"The thief [[was seen running]] out of the convenience store.","zh":"有人看到小偷從便利商店跑出來。"},{"en":"Students [[aren't allowed to use]] their phones during the exam.","zh":"考試時學生不准使用手機。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Kevin was rude to his classmate, so he was made ______ sorry.","options":["say","to say","saying"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：make 的被動是 be made to V。主動是 made him say sorry，改成被動要加回 to。(A) say 少了 to；(C) saying 不能接在 be made 後面。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Students ______ use their phones during class.","options":["aren't allowed to","aren't let to","aren't let"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：let 一般不用被動，改用 be allowed to V。「不准」說 aren't allowed to + 原形 use。(B) aren't let to、(C) aren't let 都不是標準說法。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"My mom made me to clean my room before dinner.","right":"My mom made me [[clean]] my room before dinner.","why":"make + O 後面接原形動詞，不加 to。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"I got my brother help me with my math homework.","right":"I got my brother [[to help]] me with my math homework.","why":"get + O 表示叫某人做時，要接 to V。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Can you help me carrying these bags to the car?","right":"Can you help me [[carry]] these bags to the car?","why":"help + O 後面接原形或 to V，不接 V-ing。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"I need to have my phone screen fix.","right":"I need to have my phone screen [[fixed]].","why":"螢幕是「被修理」，用 have + 物 + p.p.。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"I had the mechanic fixed my scooter.","right":"I had the mechanic [[fix]] my scooter.","why":"受詞是人、主動去修，用 have + 人 + 原形；物才接 p.p.。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"I heard someone to knock on the door.","right":"I heard someone [[knock]] on the door.","why":"感官動詞 + O 後面接原形或 V-ing，不加 to。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"Sorry to keep you wait so long.","right":"Sorry to keep you [[waiting]] so long.","why":"keep + O 接 V-ing 表「讓某人一直…」，不接原形。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"Please don't leave the door opened.","right":"Please don't leave the door [[open]].","why":"表示「開著」的狀態用形容詞 open，不用 opened。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"He was made wash all the dishes.","right":"He was made [[to wash]] all the dishes.","why":"make 改成被動時，要把 to 加回來：be made to V。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"We were let to use our phones after the exam.","right":"We [[were allowed to]] use our phones after the exam.","why":"let 一般不用被動，要改用 be allowed to V。"}],"tips":["make/have/let + O 選原形，get + O 選 to V；感官動詞 + O 選原形或 V-ing。","受詞是物、被處理時選 p.p.；中譯英「去剪頭髮」寫 have/get my hair cut。","看到 be made 的被動，後面選 to V；let 的被動改用 be allowed to V。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Our coach made us ______ ten laps around the track this morning.","options":["run","to run","running","ran"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：教練今天早上叫我們繞跑道跑十圈。make + O + 原形動詞，不加 to，也不用 V-ing。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"After a long talk, Ethan finally got his sister ______ him her old laptop.","options":["lend","to lend","lends","lent"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：談了很久之後，Ethan 終於說服姊姊把舊筆電借他。get + O 表示說服某人做，要接 to V，和 make、have 不同。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"My bike chain broke, so I need to have it ______ before Sunday's ride.","options":["fix","fixing","fixed","to fix"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我的腳踏車鏈條斷了，週日騎車前得找人修好。it 指鏈條，是「被修理」的，用 have + 物 + p.p.。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Look! Can you see that squirrel ______ up the tree? It's so fast!","options":["climbs","climbed","to climb","climbing"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：你看！有看到那隻松鼠正在爬樹嗎？牠好快！see + O + V-ing 表示看到正在進行的動作；松鼠是主動爬，不用 climbed，也不加 to。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"The movie was so funny that it kept us ______ from beginning to end.","options":["laugh","laughing","laughed","to laugh"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：這部電影太好笑了，讓我們從頭笑到尾。keep + O + V-ing 表示讓某人一直做某事；我們是主動在笑，不接原形或 to V。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Tony broke the class rules, so he was made ______ the classroom for a week.","options":["to clean","clean","cleaning","cleaned"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：Tony 違反班規，所以被罰打掃教室一週。主動是 make him clean，改成被動要把 to 加回來：be made to V。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Grandpa loves this old song. Have you ever heard it ______ in Taiwanese?","options":["sing","singing","sung","to sing"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：爺爺很愛這首老歌，你聽過有人用台語唱嗎？歌是「被唱」的，感官動詞 + O + p.p. 表被動；singing 會變成歌自己在唱。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"My scooter is making a strange noise, so I'll have the mechanic ______ it tomorrow.","options":["checked","to check","checks","check"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我的機車有怪聲，所以明天要請技師檢查。受詞是人（the mechanic），由他主動檢查，用 have + 人 + 原形；受詞是機車才用 p.p.。故選 (D)。"}]},{"id":"g-infinitive","unit":"verbal","level":"B1","title":"不定詞 to V","en":"Infinitives","lead":"不定詞是 to + 原形動詞，可當名詞、修飾名詞，也能表示「為了」。","goals":["能用 to V 當主詞、受詞、補語，並會用虛主詞 It","能分辨 It is + adj + for/of sb 句型","能用 to V 表目的、修飾名詞，並會用 too…to"],"prereq":["g-sentence"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[1]","note":"rude、polite、smart 泛指時也接 for（rude for guests to…）；統測是否只依此表待查。"}],"sections":[{"h":"名詞用法：主詞、受詞、補語","text":["**to V** 當名詞用，表示「做某事」。當主詞時動詞用單數，但常改用**虛主詞 It** 開頭，把 to V 移到句尾。","當受詞放在 want、hope、decide 等動詞後；當補語放在 be 動詞後，說明主詞的內容。哪些動詞接 to V，詳見〈動名詞與不定詞的選擇〉。","**疑問詞 + to V** 也當名詞用，意思是「該／如何…」，常可改成 疑問詞 + S + should/can + V：what to do、how to swim。"],"adv":["why 通常不接 to V。表「要不要…」用 **whether to V**，不用 if：I can't decide whether to go.","to V 當受詞，後面又有受詞補語時，用虛受詞 it 代替，把 to V 移到句尾：I find it hard to get up early. 詳見〈代名詞〉。"],"formula":"To V … + is + adj = It is + adj + to V","parse":{"en":"It is fun to ride bikes along the river on weekends.","zh":"週末沿著河邊騎腳踏車很好玩。","parts":[["It","S","虛主詞"],["is","V"],["fun","C","主詞補語"],["to ride bikes along the river on weekends.","S","真主詞（不定詞）"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[It]] is fun [[to ride]] bikes along the river on weekends.","zh":"週末沿著河邊騎腳踏車很好玩。"},{"en":"Yu-chen decided [[to join]] the school band this year.","zh":"郁辰今年決定加入學校樂隊。"},{"en":"My dream is [[to open]] a small coffee shop in Tainan.","zh":"我的夢想是在台南開一間小咖啡店。"},{"en":"I have no idea [[what to buy]] for Mom's birthday.","zh":"我完全不知道媽媽生日該買什麼。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My plan for this summer is ______ a part-time job at a convenience store.","options":["find","to find","found","finds"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：to V 當補語，放在 be 動詞後說明主詞的內容。句子已有動詞 is，計畫的內容用 to find。(A) find、(D) finds 不能接在 is 後面；(C) found 會變成過去式或被動，意思不通。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Can you show me ______ to the night market from here?","options":["how to get","how get","how getting","to get how"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：疑問詞 + to V 當名詞用，表「如何…」。show me how to get to… 是「告訴我怎麼去…」。(B) 少了 to；(C) 疑問詞後不接 V-ing；(D) 疑問詞要放在 to V 前面。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"for sb 還是 of sb？","text":["It is + adj + to V 中間可加 **for/of + sb**，說明是誰去做。形容詞評論事情用 for，評論人的個性、行為用 of。","用 of 的可改成 sb + be + adj：It's kind of you to help me. = You're kind to help me. 用 for 的不行。"],"adv":["easy、hard 等句型可把 to V 的**受詞**移到句首當主詞，句尾不再加 it：This song is easy (for me) to sing.","同一個字也要看評論誰：It's nice of you to help me.（評論人）／It's nice for kids to have a park.（評論事情）"],"formula":"It is + adj + for/of + sb + to V","table":{"cols":["介系詞","形容詞在評論","常見形容詞"],"rows":[["for + sb","事情","easy, hard, important, necessary, impossible"],["of + sb","人的個性、行為","kind, nice, careless, smart, rude, polite"]]},"parse":{"en":"It was careless of Ben to leave his phone on the bus.","zh":"Ben 把手機忘在公車上，真是粗心。","parts":[["It","S","虛主詞"],["was","V"],["careless","C","主詞補語"],["of Ben","M","做這件事的人"],["to leave his phone on the bus.","S","真主詞（不定詞）"]]},"ex":[{"en":"It's important [[for us]] to drink enough water in summer.","zh":"夏天多喝水對我們來說很重要。"},{"en":"It was so [[kind of you]] to give me a ride to the MRT station.","zh":"你真好，還載我去捷運站。"},{"en":"It was [[careless of Ben]] to leave his phone on the bus.","zh":"Ben 把手機忘在公車上，真是粗心。"}],"practice":[{"q":"It was really kind ______ you to lend me your notes.","options":["for","of","to","with"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：It is + adj + of/for sb + to V。kind 評論的是「你」這個人好心，用 of you。(A) for 用在評論事情的形容詞，如 easy、important；(C) to、(D) with 不用在這個句型。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"It's ______ for high school students to get enough sleep.","options":["important","kind","careless"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：for sb 前面的形容詞評論事情。睡飽這件事「很重要」，用 important。(B) kind、(C) careless 評論人的個性或行為，後面要用 of sb，不用 for sb。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"V + O + to V 與否定","text":["ask、tell、want、expect、allow 可接**受詞 + to V**，由受詞去做；want、ask、expect 若是主詞自己做，直接接 to V。","不定詞的否定是 **not + to V**，not 放在 to 前面，不用 don't：tell sb not to V、decide not to V。","使役動詞 make、let、have **+ O** 後面接原形動詞（make me wait），不接 to V；詳見〈使役動詞與感官動詞〉。"],"adv":["want 不接 that 子句：不說 I want that you come，要說 I want you to come。tell、allow 不能省略受詞直接接 to V。","改成被動時，受詞變主詞，to V 保留：Students are not allowed to use phones. 詳見〈被動語態〉。"],"formula":"S + V + O + (not) to V","table":{"cols":["動詞","意思","例子"],"rows":[["ask","要求、請","ask him [[to wait]]"],["tell","叫、吩咐","tell me [[to hurry]]"],["want","要（某人）做…；希望某人…","want you [[to come]]"],["expect","期待、預期","expect us [[to win]]"],["allow","允許","allow students [[to leave]]"],["encourage","鼓勵","encourage her [[to try]]"],["remind","提醒","remind me [[to call]] Mom"]]},"parse":{"en":"The coach expects us to win Friday's game.","zh":"教練期待我們贏下星期五的比賽。","parts":[["The coach","S"],["expects","V"],["us","O"],["to win Friday's game.","C","to V 當受詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Mom told me [[to clean]] my room before dinner.","zh":"媽媽叫我晚餐前把房間整理好。"},{"en":"The coach expects us [[to win]] Friday's game.","zh":"教練期待我們贏下星期五的比賽。"},{"en":"Our school doesn't allow students [[to use]] phones in class.","zh":"我們學校不准學生上課用手機。"},{"en":"Grandma told me [[not to stay up]] too late.","zh":"奶奶叫我不要太晚睡。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Our teacher asked us ______ our phones during the test.","options":["turn off","to turn off","turning off","turned off"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：ask + O + to V。老師要「我們」去關手機，受詞 us 後面接 to turn off。(A) 少了 to；(C) turning off、(D) turned off 不能接在 ask + O 後面。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"My dad told me ______ late for dinner again.","options":["don't be","not to be","to be not","not be"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：不定詞的否定 not to V。tell + O + to V 的否定是 tell + O + not to V，not 放在 to 前面。(A) don't be 不能接在受詞後；(C) not 位置錯；(D) 少了 to。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"修飾名詞：a book to read","text":["to V 放在名詞或 something、anything 後面修飾它，表示「要做的、可以做的」：homework to do、something to drink。","動詞本來要加介系詞時，**介系詞不能省**：a chair to sit on、someone to talk to。","**the first / last / only (+ N) + to V** 表示「第一個／最後一個／唯一做某事的人或事物」。"],"adv":["place 後常省略介系詞：a place to live (in)、a place to stay；其他名詞仍要保留：an apartment to live in。","something、anything 有形容詞時，形容詞放在後面、to V 前面：something cold to drink。"],"formula":"N + to V（+ 介系詞）","parse":{"en":"Lisa needs a friend to talk to.","zh":"Lisa 需要一個可以聊聊的朋友。","parts":[["Lisa","S"],["needs","V"],["a friend","O"],["to talk to.","M","修飾 a friend"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Do you have [[anything to drink]]? I'm so thirsty.","zh":"你有喝的嗎？我好渴。"},{"en":"I still have two reports [[to finish]] this weekend.","zh":"這個週末我還有兩份報告要寫完。"},{"en":"Lisa needs a friend [[to talk to]] right now.","zh":"Lisa 現在需要一個可以聊聊的朋友。"},{"en":"Jerry was [[the first to arrive]] at the basketball court.","zh":"Jerry 是第一個到籃球場的人。"}],"practice":[{"q":"I'm hungry. Is there anything ______ in the fridge?","options":["eat","to eat","eating","ate"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：to V 放在 anything 後面修飾它，表「可以吃的東西」。(A) eat、(D) ate 是動詞，不能直接修飾 anything；(C) eating 表「正在吃」，意思不通。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Jason has no one ______. He feels lonely at his new school.","options":["to talk","to talk to","talking","talk to"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：to V 修飾名詞時，介系詞不能省。talk to someone 要有 to，所以是 no one to talk to。(A) 少了介系詞 to；(C) talking 意思不通；(D) 少了不定詞的 to。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"表目的：為了…","text":["to V 可表示「**為了**做某事」，較正式時用 **in order to V** 或 so as to V。","否定用 in order not to V 或 so as not to V，not 放在 to 前面。","說人做事的目的用 to V，不用 for + V-ing：I went out to buy milk.（不說 for buying milk）"],"adv":["in order to 可放句首，so as to 通常不放句首。for + V-ing 用來說物品的用途：a knife for cutting bread。","for 後面接名詞也可表目的：go to the store for milk、go out for dinner。"],"formula":"S + V … + to V／in order to V／so as to V","parse":{"en":"Kai works at a bubble tea shop to save money.","zh":"阿凱在手搖飲店打工存錢。","parts":[["Kai","S"],["works","V"],["at a bubble tea shop","M","地點"],["to save money.","M","目的"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Kai works at a bubble tea shop [[to save]] money for a new phone.","zh":"阿凱在手搖飲店打工，存錢買新手機。"},{"en":"I got up at five [[in order to catch]] the first train to Hualien.","zh":"為了搭上往花蓮的第一班火車，我五點就起床。"},{"en":"We talked quietly in the library [[so as not to bother]] others.","zh":"我們在圖書館小聲說話，以免吵到別人。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Andy got up early ______ the first bus to school.","options":["catch","to catch","caught","for catching"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：to V 表目的「為了…」。句子已有動詞 got up，表示「為了趕上公車」用 to catch。(A) catch、(C) caught 會讓句子多出一個動詞；(D) 說人做事的目的不用 for + V-ing。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"too…to 與 enough to","text":["**too + adj/adv + to V** 表示「太…而不能…」，本身已含否定，to V 前不再加 not；要說明是誰，加 for sb。","**adj/adv + enough + to V** 表示「夠…可以…」。enough 放在形容詞、副詞後面，但放在名詞前面：old enough、enough time。","主詞就是 to V 的受詞時，句尾不再重複代名詞：The box is too heavy to carry.（不加 it）"],"adv":["too…to 可改成 so…that S can't V，這時子句要有受詞：so heavy that I can't carry it。so…that 詳見〈連接詞〉。"],"formula":"too + adj + (for sb) + to V／adj + enough + to V","parse":{"en":"This curry is too spicy for me to eat.","zh":"這咖哩太辣了，我吃不下。","parts":[["This curry","S"],["is","V"],["too spicy","C","主詞補語"],["for me to eat.","M","修飾 too spicy"]]},"ex":[{"en":"This curry is [[too spicy]] for me [[to eat]].","zh":"這咖哩太辣了，我吃不下。"},{"en":"My little brother is [[old enough to ride]] his bike to school.","zh":"我弟弟夠大了，可以自己騎腳踏車上學。"},{"en":"Jessica didn't have [[enough money to buy]] the concert ticket.","zh":"Jessica 的錢不夠買演唱會門票。"},{"en":"It's [[too late to call]] Grandma now. She's already asleep.","zh":"現在打給奶奶太晚了，她已經睡了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The soup is ______ hot to drink now. Let's wait a few minutes.","options":["too","enough","so"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：too + adj + to V 表「太…而不能…」。湯太燙不能喝，用 too hot to drink。(B) enough 要放在形容詞後面，意思也相反；(C) so 後面要接 that 子句，不接 to V。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Is the water warm ______ to swim in?","options":["too","enough","very"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：adj + enough + to V 表「夠…可以…」。enough 修飾形容詞時放在後面：warm enough to swim in。(A) too、(C) very 要放在形容詞前面，不能放在 warm 後面。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"I don't know how to do.","right":"I don't know [[what to do]].","why":"「不知道怎麼辦」是 what to do；how to do 後面還要接受詞。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"I decided join the dance club.","right":"I decided [[to join]] the dance club.","why":"decide 後面接 to V 當受詞，不能直接接原形動詞。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"It's very kind for you to help me.","right":"It's very kind [[of you]] to help me.","why":"kind 評論的是人，要用 of sb，不用 for sb。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"I am impossible to finish the report today.","right":"[[It]] is impossible [[for me]] to finish the report today.","why":"impossible 評論的是事情，用虛主詞 It 開頭，人放在 for 後面。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"My mom told me don't play games at night.","right":"My mom told me [[not to play]] games at night.","why":"tell + O + to V，否定用 not to V，不用 don't。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"I want that you come to my birthday party.","right":"I want [[you to come]] to my birthday party.","why":"want 後面接受詞 + to V，不接 that 子句。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"There is no chair to sit, so I'll stand.","right":"There is no chair [[to sit on]], so I'll stand.","why":"sit on a chair 要有介系詞，to V 修飾名詞時介系詞不能省。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"I went to the convenience store for buying milk.","right":"I went to the convenience store [[to buy]] milk.","why":"說明做事的目的用 to V，不用 for + V-ing。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"This box is too heavy to carry it.","right":"This box is too heavy [[to carry]].","why":"主詞 this box 就是 carry 的受詞，句尾不再加 it。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"My brother is enough old to drive.","right":"My brother is [[old enough]] to drive.","why":"enough 修飾形容詞時，要放在形容詞後面。"}],"tips":["It is + adj + ___ sb to V：評論人（kind）選 of，評論事情（easy）選 for。","ask、tell、allow + O 的後面選 to V；要否定時選 not to V，不選 don't V。","enough 放形容詞後、名詞前：old enough、enough time。too…to 的 to 前不加 not。"],"quiz":[{"q":"My parents don't allow me ______ out after ten at night.","options":["go","going","to go","went"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我爸媽不准我晚上十點以後出門。allow + O + to V 表示允許某人做某事，不接原形或 V-ing。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I lost my wallet on the MRT, and I don't know ______.","options":["what to do","how to do","what do","to do what"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我在捷運上弄丟了錢包，不知道該怎麼辦。「該怎麼辦」是 what to do；how to do 少了受詞，what do 少了 to。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Mia works part-time at a night market ______ money for college.","options":["save","to save","saved","saves"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Mia 在夜市打工，存錢準備念大學。句子已有動詞 works，表示目的「為了…」用 to V。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"It was ______ of Jason to leave his umbrella on the MRT again.","options":["easy","important","necessary","careless"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Jason 又把雨傘忘在捷運上，真是粗心。of sb 前的形容詞要評論人，只有 careless 能形容 Jason；其他三個評論事情，要用 for。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Ken is moving to Kaohsiung for college, so he needs to find an apartment ______.","options":["to live","to live in","living","lived"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Ken 要去高雄念大學，需要找一間公寓住。live 不及物，要說 live in an apartment，in 不能省；a place to live 省略 in 是慣用說法，不適用 apartment。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Amy isn't tall enough ______ the top shelf, so she asked her brother for help.","options":["to reach","reach","reaching","for reaching"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：Amy 不夠高，拿不到最上層的架子，所以請哥哥幫忙。adj + enough 後面接 to V，表示「夠…可以…」，不接原形動詞、V-ing 或 for + V-ing。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"This box of books is too heavy ______. Could you give me a hand?","options":["carry","carrying","to carry it","to carry"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：這箱書太重了搬不動，可以幫我一下嗎？too + adj + to V；主詞 this box 就是 carry 的受詞，句尾不能再加 it。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Grace set two alarms ______ oversleep on the morning of the exam.","options":["in order to","so that not","in order not to","for not"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Grace 設了兩個鬧鐘，以免考試當天早上睡過頭。表目的的否定用 in order not to V；in order to 意思相反，so that 後面要接子句。故選 (C)。"}]},{"id":"g-gerund","unit":"verbal","level":"B1","title":"動名詞與不定詞的選擇","en":"Gerunds vs infinitives","lead":"接 V-ing 還是 to V 由前面的字或句型決定；介系詞後接 V-ing。","goals":["能判斷動詞後面要接 V-ing 還是 to V","能分辨 stop、remember 兩種接法的意思","能在介系詞和固定句型後正確使用 V-ing"],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-infinitive"],"pending":[],"sections":[{"h":"V-ing 當主詞與受詞","text":["**動名詞**（V-ing）把動作變成名詞，可以當主詞、受詞或補語，也能放在介系詞後面。","一個動名詞（片語）當主詞時，看成一件事，動詞用**單數**。"],"adv":["兩個 V-ing 用 and 連接、指兩件事時，動詞通常用複數，詳見〈主詞與動詞一致〉：Reading and writing are important skills.","to V 也能當主詞，但較正式，常改成 It is…to V，詳見〈不定詞 to V〉。"],"formula":"一個 V-ing 片語 + 單數動詞／S + V + V-ing","parse":{"en":"Making dumplings with Grandma is my favorite weekend activity.","zh":"和奶奶一起包水餃是我週末最喜歡的活動。","parts":[["Making dumplings with Grandma","S","動名詞片語當主詞"],["is","V"],["my favorite weekend activity.","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Taking]] the MRT [[is]] faster than driving in Taipei.","zh":"在台北搭捷運比開車快。"},{"en":"[[Eating]] too much fried food [[is]] bad for your health.","zh":"吃太多炸物對健康不好。"},{"en":"Ken [[enjoys singing]] karaoke with his classmates.","zh":"Ken 喜歡和同學一起唱 KTV。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ comic books before bed helps me relax.","options":["Read","Reading","Reads"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：動名詞當主詞。helps 前面要有名詞性的主詞，動作要改成 V-ing：Reading comic books。(A) Read 是原形動詞，不能當主詞；(C) Reads 是動詞變化，也不能當主詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Playing mobile games for hours ______ bad for your eyes.","options":["is","are","be"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：一個動名詞片語當主詞，動詞用單數。主詞是 Playing mobile games for hours 這一件事，不是 games，所以用 is。(B) are 誤把 games 當主詞；(C) be 是原形，不能直接當句子的動詞。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"只接 V-ing 的動詞","text":["這些動詞後面接動作時要用 **V-ing**，不能用 to V，要直接背起來。"],"adv":["**suggest** 不接「人 + to V」：可說 suggest V-ing，或 suggest that S (should) + 原形動詞。","can't help V-ing（忍不住）也可說 can't help but + 原形，美式常用：I couldn't help but laugh."],"table":{"cols":["動詞","意思","例句"],"rows":[["enjoy","喜歡、享受","We [[enjoy hiking]] on weekends."],["finish","做完","Have you [[finished packing]]?"],["mind","介意","Do you [[mind waiting]] a minute?"],["avoid","避免","I [[avoid drinking]] coffee at night."],["keep","一直、持續","It [[kept raining]] all day."],["practice","練習","She [[practices dancing]] after school."],["consider / suggest","考慮／建議","He [[suggested taking]] a taxi."],["give up / can't help","放棄、戒掉／忍不住","I [[couldn't help laughing]]."]]},"parse":{"en":"Ryan gave up playing online games to study for the exam.","zh":"Ryan 為了準備考試，戒掉了線上遊戲。","parts":[["Ryan","S"],["gave up","V","片語動詞"],["playing online games","O","動名詞當受詞"],["to study for the exam.","M","表目的"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Ryan [[gave up playing]] online games to study for the exam.","zh":"Ryan 為了準備考試，戒掉了線上遊戲。"},{"en":"Would you [[mind turning]] down the music? I'm studying.","zh":"可以把音樂關小聲一點嗎？我在讀書。"},{"en":"Our coach [[suggested practicing]] free throws every morning.","zh":"教練建議我們每天早上練罰球。"},{"en":"My sister is [[considering studying]] in Japan.","zh":"我姊姊正在考慮去日本留學。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Would you mind ______ the window? It's a little cold in here.","options":["close","to close","closing"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：mind 後接 V-ing。mind（介意）屬於只接 V-ing 的動詞，用 closing。(A) close 是原形，不能直接接在 mind 後；(B) to close 也不能接在 mind 後。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"My brother avoids ______ junk food before his basketball games.","options":["eating","eat","to eat"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：avoid 後接 V-ing。avoid（避免）只接 V-ing，用 eating。(B) eat 是原形，不能接在 avoid 後；(C) to eat 也不能接在 avoid 後。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"只接 to V 的動詞","text":["這些動詞後面接 **to V**，多半表示「想要、打算、答應」這類**還沒發生**的事。"],"adv":["want 還能接「人 + to V」（want you to come），hope 不行，詳見〈不定詞 to V〉。","plan 後若加介系詞 on，就改接 V-ing：We plan on visiting Hualien.（美式常用）"],"table":{"cols":["動詞","意思","例句"],"rows":[["want / hope","想要／希望","I [[hope to see]] you soon."],["decide","決定","We [[decided to stay]] home."],["plan","計畫、打算","They [[plan to visit]] Hualien."],["agree / refuse","同意／拒絕","He [[refused to answer]]."],["promise","答應、保證","She [[promised to call]] me."],["afford","負擔得起","I can't [[afford to buy]] it."],["learn","學會","Tim [[learned to swim]] at age six."]]},"parse":{"en":"We decided to take the high-speed train to Kaohsiung.","zh":"我們決定搭高鐵去高雄。","parts":[["We","S"],["decided","V"],["to take the high-speed train to Kaohsiung.","O","不定詞當受詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Amy [[wants to study]] nursing in college.","zh":"Amy 想在大學讀護理。"},{"en":"We [[decided to take]] the high-speed train to Kaohsiung.","zh":"我們決定搭高鐵去高雄。"},{"en":"My parents [[agreed to let]] me work part-time on weekends.","zh":"爸媽同意讓我週末去打工。"}],"practice":[{"q":"We hope ______ Taroko Gorge during summer vacation.","options":["visiting","to visit","visit"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：hope 後接 to V。hope（希望）只接 to V，表示還沒發生、希望做到的事。(A) visiting 不能接在 hope 後；(C) visit 少了 to。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Dad promised ______ me to the night market on Friday.","options":["to take","taking","take"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：promise 後接 to V。promise（答應）只接 to V，表示答應要去做的事。(B) taking 不能接在 promise 後；(C) take 少了 to。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"兩者皆可，意思不同","text":["這五個動詞接 to V 或 V-ing 都可以，但**意思不同**，要看句意判斷。","remember、forget、regret 有個訣竅：**to V 是還沒做的事**，V-ing 是已經做過的事。"],"adv":["stop to V 的 to V 表目的（停下來，為了去做），不是 stop 的受詞。","like、love、start、begin 接兩者意思差不多；但 would like / would love 只接 to V，詳見〈助動詞〉。"],"table":{"cols":["動詞","+ to V","+ V-ing"],"rows":[["stop","停下來去做（to V 表目的）","停止做"],["remember","記得要去做","記得做過"],["forget","忘了要去做","忘了做過（多用 never forget）"],["try","努力、設法去做","試試看做（看有沒有效）"],["regret","遺憾地告知（多接 say/tell/inform）","後悔做過"]]},"parse":{"en":"We stopped to buy some stinky tofu on the way home.","zh":"回家路上，我們停下來買臭豆腐。","parts":[["We","S"],["stopped","V"],["to buy some stinky tofu","M","表目的，非受詞"],["on the way home.","M"]]},"ex":[{"en":"On the way home, we [[stopped to buy]] some stinky tofu.","zh":"回家路上，我們停下來買臭豆腐。"},{"en":"The baby next door finally [[stopped crying]].","zh":"隔壁的寶寶終於不哭了。"},{"en":"[[Remember to bring]] your swimsuit for PE class tomorrow.","zh":"記得明天體育課要帶泳衣。"},{"en":"I [[remember meeting]] Kevin at a night market in Tainan.","zh":"我記得在台南的夜市見過 Kevin。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Please remember ______ off the lights when you leave the classroom.","options":["turn","to turn","turning"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：remember to V 與 remember V-ing。離開教室時關燈是還沒做、要記得去做的事，用 remember to V。(A) turn 少了 to；(C) turning 表示記得做過，不合句意。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"When the teacher walked in, the classroom got quiet because everyone stopped ______.","options":["talk","to talk","talking"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：stop V-ing 與 stop to V。教室安靜下來，表示大家停止說話，用 stop V-ing。(A) talk 是原形，不能接在 stopped 後；(B) to talk 是「停下來去說話」，和教室安靜不合。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"介系詞後接 V-ing","text":["**介系詞**後的動詞用 V-ing，如 be good at、thank you for、without。","片語裡的 **to** 也可能是介系詞，如 look forward to、be used to、object to，後面要接 V-ing，不接原形。","be used to V-ing 是「習慣於」；used to V 是「過去常常」，詳見〈助動詞〉；be used to + 原形是「被用來」。"],"adv":["例外：表「除了」的 but 後接原形或 to V，如 do nothing but + 原形、have no choice but to V（只好…）。"],"table":{"cols":["片語","意思","例句"],"rows":[["be good at","擅長","Lily [[is good at drawing]]."],["look forward to","期待","I'm [[looking forward to seeing]] you."],["be used to","習慣於","He's [[used to eating]] spicy food."],["object to","反對","Many students [[object to wearing]] uniforms."],["in addition to","除了…之外（還）","[[In addition to singing]], Mia plays the guitar."],["when it comes to","說到、談到","[[When it comes to cooking]], Dad is the best."]]},"parse":{"en":"I am looking forward to trying the snacks at Raohe Night Market.","zh":"我很期待去吃饒河夜市的小吃。","parts":[["I","S"],["am looking forward to","V","to 是介系詞"],["trying the snacks at Raohe Night Market.","O","動名詞當受詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Thank you [[for waiting]] for me at the MRT station.","zh":"謝謝你在捷運站等我。"},{"en":"I'm [[looking forward to trying]] all the snacks at Raohe Night Market.","zh":"我很期待吃遍饒河夜市的小吃。"},{"en":"I'm still not [[used to getting up]] at six for school.","zh":"我還是不習慣六點起床上學。"},{"en":"[[When it comes to playing]] basketball, nobody in our class can beat Leo.","zh":"說到打籃球，我們班沒人贏得了 Leo。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Thank you for ______ me with my math homework.","options":["help","helping","to help"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：介系詞後接 V-ing。for 是介系詞，後面的動詞要用 V-ing，用 helping。(A) help 是原形，不能接在介系詞後；(C) to help 也不能接在 for 後。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"When it comes to ______ spicy food, my dad is the champion in our family.","options":["eat","eating","ate"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：when it comes to 的 to 是介系詞，後接 V-ing，用 eating。(A) eat 誤把 to 當成不定詞的 to；(C) ate 是過去式，不能接在介系詞後。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"常用 V-ing 句型","text":["這些句型後面固定接 **V-ing**；spend 和 have trouble/difficulty 句型裡的 in 通常省略。","be worth V-ing 用主動形式表被動意思，不說 worth to visit。"],"adv":["花在某事物上用 on：spend money on clothes（和人共度用 with）。","It takes + 時間 + to V 的句型，詳見〈強調句與常用句型〉。"],"table":{"cols":["句型","意思","例句"],"rows":[["spend + 時間／錢 + (in) V-ing","花時間／錢做…","I [[spent]] two hours [[doing]] my homework."],["have trouble/difficulty (in) V-ing","做…有困難","He [[has trouble sleeping]]."],["It is no use V-ing","做…也沒用","[[It's no use crying]] about it now."],["be busy V-ing","忙著做…","Mom [[is busy cooking]] dinner."],["feel like V-ing","想要做…","I [[feel like eating]] hot pot."],["be worth V-ing","值得做…","This book [[is worth reading]]."]]},"parse":{"en":"The night markets in Tainan are worth visiting.","zh":"台南的夜市很值得一逛。","parts":[["The night markets in Tainan","S"],["are","V"],["worth visiting.","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Kelly [[spends]] most of her allowance [[buying]] bubble tea.","zh":"Kelly 的零用錢大多花在買手搖飲上。"},{"en":"My grandpa [[has trouble reading]] the small text on his phone.","zh":"爺爺看手機上的小字很吃力。"},{"en":"I don't [[feel like going]] out tonight. Let's just order pizza.","zh":"我今晚不想出門，叫披薩外送就好。"},{"en":"Jiufen [[is worth visiting]], but it's always crowded on weekends.","zh":"九份很值得去，但週末總是人擠人。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Grandma is busy ______ zongzi for the Dragon Boat Festival.","options":["make","to make","making"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：be busy V-ing。be busy（忙著）後面固定接 V-ing，用 making。(A) make 是原形，不能接在 busy 後；(B) to make 也不能接在 be busy 後。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Leo spent the whole afternoon ______ for the English test.","options":["studying","study","studied"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：spend + 時間 + (in) V-ing。spend 接時間後，再接 V-ing 表示花時間做某事，用 studying。(B) study 是原形，不能這樣接；(C) studied 是過去式，句中已有動詞 spent。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"Learn a new language takes a lot of time and practice.","right":"[[Learning]] a new language takes a lot of time and practice.","why":"動作當主詞要改成動名詞 V-ing，不能直接用原形動詞。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"Playing online games all night make me tired the next day.","right":"Playing online games all night [[makes]] me tired the next day.","why":"主詞是 Playing… 這一件事，不是 games，動詞用單數。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"I enjoy to play basketball with my friends after school.","right":"I enjoy [[playing]] basketball with my friends after school.","why":"enjoy 後面只能接 V-ing，不能接 to V。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"My teacher suggested me to read more English news.","right":"My teacher suggested [[that I read]] more English news.","why":"suggest 不接「人 + to V」，改用 that 子句或 V-ing。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"We decided going to Kenting during winter vacation.","right":"We decided [[to go]] to Kenting during winter vacation.","why":"decide 後面接 to V，不接 V-ing。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"I forgot locking the door this morning, so Mom was angry.","right":"I forgot [[to lock]] the door this morning, so Mom was angry.","why":"忘了去做而沒做用 forget to V；forget V-ing 是忘了做過。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"I'm looking forward to see you in Kaohsiung.","right":"I'm looking forward to [[seeing]] you in Kaohsiung.","why":"look forward to 的 to 是介系詞，後面要接 V-ing。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"My dad is used to drink coffee every morning.","right":"My dad is used to [[drinking]] coffee every morning.","why":"be used to 表「習慣於」時，to 是介系詞，要接 V-ing。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"Many students have trouble to remember new words.","right":"Many students have trouble [[remembering]] new words.","why":"have trouble 後面接 (in) V-ing，不接 to V。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"This movie is worth to watch in the theater.","right":"This movie is worth [[watching]] in the theater.","why":"be worth 後面接 V-ing，不接 to V。"}],"tips":["看空格前一個字：介系詞（含 look forward to、be used to 的 to）後面選 V-ing。","綜合測驗常考 stop、remember、forget：讀上下文，還沒做選 to V，做過或正在做選 V-ing。","對話題常考 Do you mind V-ing? 答應可回 Not at all.（不介意），回 Yes 反而表示介意。"],"quiz":[{"q":"My little brother enjoys ______ comic books in bed.","options":["read","to read","reading","reads"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我弟弟喜歡在床上看漫畫。enjoy 後面只接 V-ing，不接 to V 或原形動詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Mia decided ______ a part-time job at a coffee shop this summer.","options":["to get","get","getting","got"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：Mia 決定今年暑假去咖啡店打工。decide 後面接 to V，表示決定要去做的事。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"My sister is good at ______ cakes and cookies.","options":["make","to make","made","making"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我姊姊很會做蛋糕和餅乾。at 是介系詞，介系詞後面的動詞要用 V-ing。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Kevin is looking forward to ______ his favorite band in concert next month.","options":["see","seeing","seen","saw"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Kevin 很期待下個月去看他最愛的樂團演唱會。look forward to 的 to 是介系詞，後面接 V-ing，不接原形。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Dad was hungry, so he stopped ______ some fried chicken on the way home.","options":["buy","buying","to buy","bought"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：爸爸餓了，所以回家路上停下來買炸雞。stop to V 是「停下來去做」；stop V-ing 是「停止做」，不合句意。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I'll never forget ______ the sunrise at Alishan with my family last summer.","options":["watch","watching","to watch","watched"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我永遠忘不了去年夏天和家人在阿里山看日出。看日出是做過的事，用 forget V-ing；forget to V 是忘了要去做。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"That new beef noodle shop near the station is really worth ______.","options":["trying","to try","try","tried"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：車站附近那家新開的牛肉麵店很值得一試。be worth 後面接 V-ing，用主動形式表被動意思，不說 worth to try。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"My aunt moved to Canada three years ago, so she is now used to ______ English at work.","options":["speak","spoke","speaks","speaking"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我阿姨三年前搬到加拿大，所以現在已經習慣在工作時說英語。be used to + V-ing 是「習慣於」；be used to + 原形是「被用來」，不合句意。故選 (D)。"}]},{"id":"g-participle","unit":"verbal","level":"B1","title":"分詞當形容詞","en":"Participles as adjectives","lead":"名詞主動做或正在做用 V-ing，被做或已完成用 p.p.；人感到用 -ed。","goals":["能依主動或被動選用 V-ing 或 p.p. 修飾名詞","能分辨情緒動詞的 -ed 和 -ing 用法","能放對分詞位置，並把形容詞子句簡化成分詞"],"prereq":["g-present","g-passive"],"pending":[],"sections":[{"h":"現在分詞 V-ing：主動、進行","text":["**現在分詞 (V-ing)** 當形容詞時，表示名詞**主動**做這個動作，或動作正在進行。","a sleeping baby 就是 a baby who is sleeping（正在睡覺的嬰兒）；boiling water 是正在滾的水。"],"adv":["注意：a sleeping bag（睡袋）、a swimming pool（游泳池）的 V-ing 是動名詞，表示用途，不是「正在…」。"],"formula":"V-ing + N（N 主動做／正在做）","parse":{"en":"The barking dog woke up the whole family.","zh":"那隻一直叫的狗把全家人都吵醒了。","parts":[["The barking dog","S","V-ing 當形容詞"],["woke up","V","片語動詞"],["the whole family.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Shh! Don't wake up my [[sleeping]] baby brother.","zh":"噓！別吵醒正在睡覺的小弟。"},{"en":"The [[barking]] dog next door kept me up all night.","zh":"隔壁那隻一直叫的狗，吵得我整晚睡不著。"},{"en":"Put the noodles into [[boiling]] water and cook them for three minutes.","zh":"把麵放進滾水裡煮三分鐘。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Listen! Can you hear the ______ birds outside?","options":["singing","sung","sing"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：V-ing 當形容詞，表主動、正在進行。鳥正在主動唱歌，用 singing。(B) sung 是 p.p.，表被動，鳥不是被唱；(C) sing 是原形動詞，不能直接放在名詞前修飾。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"過去分詞 p.p.：被動、完成","text":["**過去分詞 (p.p.)** 當形容詞時，及物動詞的 p.p. 表示**被動**：a broken window（被打破的窗戶）、a stolen bike（被偷的腳踏車）。","不及物動詞沒有被動，少數（如 fall、retire）的 p.p. 可表示**已完成**：fallen leaves（落葉）、a retired teacher（退休的老師）。"],"formula":"p.p. + N（N 被…／已經…）","table":{"cols":["動詞","V-ing：主動／進行","p.p.：被動／完成"],"rows":[["boil","[[boiling]] water 滾水","[[boiled]] eggs 水煮蛋"],["fall","[[falling]] leaves 正在飄落的葉子","[[fallen]] leaves 落葉"],["develop","a [[developing]] country 開發中國家","a [[developed]] country 已開發國家"]]},"parse":{"en":"Dad fixed the broken fan yesterday.","zh":"爸爸昨天把壞掉的電風扇修好了。","parts":[["Dad","S"],["fixed","V"],["the broken fan","O","p.p. 當形容詞"],["yesterday.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Watch out for the [[broken]] glass on the floor!","zh":"小心地上的碎玻璃！"},{"en":"Mom always keeps a bag of [[frozen]] dumplings in the freezer.","zh":"媽媽的冷凍庫裡總是放著一包冷凍水餃。"},{"en":"After the typhoon, the road was covered with [[fallen]] branches.","zh":"颱風過後，路上滿是掉下來的樹枝。"},{"en":"Leo bought a [[used]] scooter with money from his part-time job.","zh":"Leo 用打工賺的錢買了一台二手機車。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Mia finally found her ______ wallet under the sofa.","options":["losing","lost","lose"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：及物動詞的 p.p. 當形容詞表被動。錢包是「被弄丟的」，用 lost。(A) losing 表主動，好像錢包自己在弄丟東西；(C) lose 是原形動詞，不能直接修飾名詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"情緒動詞：-ed 還是 -ing","text":["interest、bore、excite 這類**情緒動詞**的意思是「使人感到…」，所以 -ed 是「（人）感到…的」，-ing 是「令人…的」。","簡單記：**感到…用 -ed，令人…用 -ing**。所以人也能用 -ing：He is boring. 是「他這個人很無趣」，He is bored. 才是「他覺得無聊」。"],"adv":["-ed 形容詞常接固定介系詞：interested in、excited about、surprised at；tired of 是「厭倦」，不是「累」。"],"table":{"cols":["動詞","-ed：感到…的","-ing：令人…的"],"rows":[["interest","interested 感興趣的","interesting 有趣的"],["bore","bored 感到無聊的","boring 乏味的、無聊的"],["excite","excited 興奮的","exciting 令人興奮的、刺激的"],["surprise","surprised 驚訝的","surprising 令人驚訝的"],["tire","tired 疲累的","tiring 累人的"],["confuse","confused 困惑的","confusing 令人困惑的"],["disappoint","disappointed 失望的","disappointing 令人失望的"],["embarrass","embarrassed 尷尬的","embarrassing 令人尷尬的、丟臉的"]]},"parse":{"en":"I find this math problem confusing.","zh":"我覺得這題數學很難懂。","parts":[["I","S"],["find","V"],["this math problem","O"],["confusing.","C","受詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The game was [[exciting]], and the fans were really [[excited]].","zh":"比賽很精彩，球迷都超興奮。"},{"en":"I was so [[embarrassed]] when I called my teacher \"Mom\" in class.","zh":"我上課時不小心叫老師「媽」，超尷尬的。"},{"en":"This math problem is really [[confusing]]. Can you explain it again?","zh":"這題數學真的很難懂，可以再講一次嗎？"},{"en":"Ken was [[tired]] after a [[tiring]] day at his part-time job.","zh":"打工忙了一整天，Ken 累壞了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Ms. Chen's explanation wasn't clear, so many students were ______.","options":["confuse","confusing","confused"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：情緒動詞，人感到…用 -ed。學生是「感到困惑」的人，用 confused。(B) confusing 是「令人困惑的」，用來形容說明本身；(A) confuse 是原形動詞，不能放在 were 後當補語。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Our class trip to Kenting was really ______. Everyone had a great time.","options":["exciting","excited","excite"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：情緒動詞，令人…用 -ing。主詞 class trip 是帶來興奮感的事物，用 exciting。(B) excited 是人「感到興奮」；(C) excite 是原形動詞，不能當補語。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"分詞放名詞前還是後","text":["分詞**單獨一個字**時，通常放在名詞前：a crying baby。分詞後面還有受詞、介系詞片語或副詞時，整組**放在名詞後**：the girl standing there。"],"adv":["例外：left（剩下的）通常放在名詞後，例如 no milk left（沒有剩下的牛奶）。","副詞放在分詞前面時，整組仍放名詞前：a newly built MRT station、a well-known singer。"],"formula":"分詞 + N／N + 分詞片語","parse":{"en":"The boy playing the drums is my classmate.","zh":"在打鼓的那個男生是我同學。","parts":[["The boy","S"],["playing the drums","M","分詞片語，修飾 boy"],["is","V"],["my classmate.","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Who's the boy [[playing]] basketball over there?","zh":"在那邊打籃球的男生是誰？"},{"en":"The shaved ice [[sold]] at this stand is cheap and delicious.","zh":"這攤賣的剉冰便宜又好吃。"},{"en":"We watched the [[rising]] sun from the top of Yushan.","zh":"我們在玉山山頂看著太陽慢慢升起。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ is my best friend.","options":["The dancing on the stage girl","The girl dancing on the stage","The girl dances on the stage"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：分詞後面還有 on the stage 時，整組放在名詞後：the girl dancing on the stage（在台上跳舞的女生）。(A) 把分詞片語放在名詞前，不合文法；(C) dances 是動詞，句子已有 is，不能再有第二個動詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Is there any rice ______ in the pot? I'm still hungry.","options":["leave","leaving","left"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：left 表「剩下的」，通常放在名詞後：any rice left（剩下的飯）。(A) leave 是原形動詞，不能修飾名詞；(B) leaving 表主動「正在離開」，不合句意。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"形容詞子句簡化成分詞","text":["名詞後的分詞片語，可看成**形容詞子句的簡化**：把關係代名詞和 be 動詞一起省略，留下 V-ing 或 p.p.。","子句沒有 be 動詞時，表示持續狀態或習慣的主動動詞可改成 **V-ing**：who live → living。只有關係代名詞當主詞時才能這樣簡化。"],"adv":["一次性的過去動作不能改成 V-ing：the boy who broke the window 不寫成 the boy breaking the window（變成正在打破）。","形容詞子句詳見〈關係代名詞〉；由副詞子句簡化而來的句型，詳見〈分詞構句〉。"],"table":{"cols":["形容詞子句","簡化後"],"rows":[["the girl [[who is standing]] there","the girl [[standing]] there"],["the language [[which is spoken]] in Brazil","the language [[spoken]] in Brazil"],["students [[who live]] far from school","students [[living]] far from school"],["a bike [[that was made]] in Taiwan","a bike [[made]] in Taiwan"]]},"parse":{"en":"Students living far from school can take the school bus.","zh":"住得離學校遠的學生可以搭校車。","parts":[["Students","S"],["living far from school","M","簡化的形容詞子句"],["can take","V"],["the school bus.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The man [[sitting]] next to me on the MRT fell asleep on my shoulder.","zh":"捷運上坐我旁邊的男生，靠在我肩膀上睡著了。"},{"en":"This is a photo [[taken]] at Sun Moon Lake last summer.","zh":"這是去年夏天在日月潭拍的照片。"},{"en":"Is there a bus [[going]] to the night market from here?","zh":"這裡有開往夜市的公車嗎？"}],"practice":[{"q":"This is a song ______ by a high school student in Tainan.","options":["written","writing","writes"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：形容詞子句簡化，被動用 p.p.。歌是「被寫的」（= that was written），用 written。(B) writing 表主動，歌不會自己寫；(C) writes 是動詞，句子已有 is，不能再有第二個動詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"People ______ in Taipei often take the MRT to work.","options":["live","lived","living"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：子句沒有 be 動詞時，持續狀態的主動動詞可改成 V-ing：people who live → people living。(A) live 是動詞，句子已有 take；(B) lived 是過去式；這裡的 live 是不及物動詞，p.p. 不能表被動。故選 (C)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"Who is the cry girl in the corner?","right":"Who is the [[crying]] girl in the corner?","why":"cry 是原形動詞，不能直接修飾名詞；女孩正在哭，用 crying。","sec":0},{"wrong":"There's a broke window in our classroom.","right":"There's a [[broken]] window in our classroom.","why":"「被打破的」要用過去分詞 broken，broke 是過去式。","sec":1},{"wrong":"I had two boiling eggs for breakfast.","right":"I had two [[boiled]] eggs for breakfast.","why":"蛋是被煮熟的，用 p.p. boiled；boiling 是「正在滾的」。","sec":1},{"wrong":"I'm really interesting in K-pop.","right":"I'm really [[interested]] in K-pop.","why":"「我」是感到有興趣的人，用 interested；interesting 是「令人感興趣的」。","sec":2},{"wrong":"The movie was so excited that I watched it twice.","right":"The movie was so [[exciting]] that I watched it twice.","why":"電影是令人興奮的事物，要用 exciting。","sec":2},{"wrong":"Do you know the standing by the door girl?","right":"Do you know the girl [[standing by the door]]?","why":"分詞後面還有 by the door，整組要放在名詞後。","sec":3},{"wrong":"Is there any left pizza in the fridge?","right":"Is there any pizza [[left]] in the fridge?","why":"left 表「剩下的」時放在名詞後。","sec":3},{"wrong":"The boy stands over there is my cousin.","right":"The boy [[standing]] over there is my cousin.","why":"句子已有動詞 is，修飾 boy 用分詞 standing（= who is standing）。","sec":4},{"wrong":"The language speaking in Brazil is Portuguese.","right":"The language [[spoken]] in Brazil is Portuguese.","why":"語言是「被說」的，要用過去分詞 spoken。","sec":4}],"tips":["選擇題考情緒動詞，先看被形容的對象：是感受的人選 -ed，是帶來感覺的人事物選 -ing。","空格在名詞後、句子已有動詞，選項是同一動詞的各種形式時，多考分詞：名詞主動做選 V-ing，被做選 p.p.。","中譯英「在台灣製造的手機」這類長修飾語，寫成名詞 + 分詞片語：a phone made in Taiwan。"],"quiz":[{"q":"The movie was so ______ that I fell asleep halfway through.","options":["bored","boring","bore","bores"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：那部電影太無聊，我看到一半就睡著了。電影是帶來無聊感的事物，用 boring；bored 是人感到無聊。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Jenny was ______ to hear that her favorite singer's concert was canceled.","options":["disappointing","disappoint","disappointment","disappointed"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Jenny 聽到最愛歌手的演唱會取消，覺得很失望。Jenny 是感到失望的人，用 disappointed；disappointing 是「令人失望的」。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Please keep your voice down. There's a ______ baby in the next room.","options":["sleeping","slept","sleep","sleeps"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：請小聲一點，隔壁房間有個正在睡覺的嬰兒。嬰兒主動在睡，動作正在進行，用現在分詞 sleeping 修飾名詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Be careful! There's ______ glass all over the kitchen floor.","options":["breaking","broke","break","broken"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：小心！廚房地上到處都是碎玻璃。玻璃是「被打破的」，用過去分詞 broken；broke 是過去式，breaking 表示正在破，都不對。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"The boy ______ a red cap is my cousin.","options":["wears","wearing","worn","is wearing"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：戴紅色帽子的男生是我表哥。句子已有動詞 is，空格修飾 the boy；男生主動戴帽子，用 wearing（= who is wearing）。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The dance video ______ by our class now has over 10,000 views.","options":["made","making","was made","makes"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我們班拍的舞蹈影片現在已超過一萬次觀看。影片是「被做出來的」，用 made（= that was made）；句子已有動詞 has，不能再用 was made。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Mr. Lin tells great stories, so his students find his history class very ______.","options":["interest","interested","interesting","to interest"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：林老師很會說故事，學生覺得他的歷史課很有趣。find + O + 形容詞，形容詞說明的是 class；課是令人感興趣的事物，用 interesting。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Japan is a ______ country, but many other countries are still developing.","options":["developing","development","developed","develop"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：日本是已開發國家，但許多國家仍在開發中。「已開發的」表完成，用過去分詞 developed；developing 是「開發中的」，和後半句的對比矛盾。故選 (C)。"}]},{"id":"g-participle-clause","unit":"verbal","level":"B2","title":"分詞構句","en":"Participle clauses","lead":"主詞相同才能省略：去掉連接詞和主詞，主動用 V-ing，被動用 p.p.。","goals":["能把主詞相同的副詞子句簡化成分詞構句","能依主動、被動和先後關係選對分詞形式","能辨認懸垂分詞，並寫出獨立分詞構句"],"prereq":["g-conj","g-passive","g-participle"],"pending":[],"sections":[{"h":"簡化三步驟","text":["**分詞構句**是把副詞子句（when、because、after…）縮短；兩個子句**主詞相同**才能省略主詞，否則會變成「懸垂分詞」。","步驟：① 去掉連接詞 ② 去掉相同的主詞 ③ 動詞改成 V-ing。進行式 was walking 直接留 walking，不說 being walking。","be 動詞改成 **being**；後面接形容詞或 p.p. 時，being 常省略。"],"adv":["分詞構句也可放在句尾，表示同時進行的動作：Grandpa sat on the sofa, watching TV.","後面接名詞時，being 通常不省略：Being the oldest child, Amy…。"],"formula":"When/Because + S + V…, S + V… → V-ing…, S + V…","table":{"cols":["副詞子句","分詞構句"],"rows":[["When he saw me, he waved.","[[Seeing]] me, he waved."],["Because I felt sick, I stayed home.","[[Feeling]] sick, I stayed home."],["While I was walking home, I saw Ken.","[[Walking]] home, I saw Ken."],["Since she was tired, she went to bed early.","[[(Being) tired]], she went to bed early."]]},"parse":{"en":"Hearing the bell, the students ran out of the classroom.","zh":"一聽到鐘聲，學生們就衝出教室。","parts":[["Hearing the bell,","M","分詞構句表時間"],["the students","S"],["ran","V"],["out of the classroom.","M","方向"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Hearing]] the bell, the students ran out of the classroom.","zh":"一聽到鐘聲，學生們就衝出教室。"},{"en":"[[Feeling]] hungry after basketball practice, Jason bought two scallion pancakes.","zh":"練完籃球覺得餓，Jason 買了兩份蔥油餅。"},{"en":"[[Being]] the oldest child, Amy often cooks dinner for her brothers.","zh":"身為老大，Amy 常幫弟弟們煮晚餐。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ tired after the long trip, Amy went to bed early.","options":["Feel","Felt","Feeling"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：主詞相同時去掉連接詞和主詞，動詞改成 V-ing。原句 Because Amy felt tired…，兩個主詞都是 Amy，改成 Feeling。(A) Feel 是原形動詞，不能這樣用；(B) Felt 當過去式缺主詞，當 p.p. 則表被動，都不對。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"______ for the MRT, Kelly read comics on her phone.","options":["Waiting","Being waiting","Waited"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：進行式的簡化。原句 While Kelly was waiting…，進行式去掉 was，只留 waiting。(B) Being waiting 不合文法；(C) Waited 當過去式缺主詞，當 p.p. 則表被動，都不對。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"主動 V-ing，被動 p.p.","text":["看主要子句的主詞和這個動作的關係：主詞**主動**去做，用 V-ing；主詞**被**做，用 p.p.。","p.p. 開頭的分詞構句，是 Being + p.p. 或 Having been + p.p. 省略 being／having been 而來。"],"adv":["Built in 1738, Longshan Temple is… 的 Built 是 Having been built 省略而來，表示廟早已蓋好。"],"parse":{"en":"Left alone at home, the puppy barked all night.","zh":"小狗被單獨留在家裡，叫了一整晚。","parts":[["Left alone at home,","M","被動分詞構句"],["the puppy","S"],["barked","V"],["all night.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Seen]] from Taipei 101, the cars on the street look like toys.","zh":"從台北 101 看下去，街上的車子小得像玩具。"},{"en":"[[Left]] alone at home, the puppy barked all night.","zh":"小狗被單獨留在家裡，叫了一整晚。"},{"en":"[[Shocked]] by the news, Leo couldn't say a word.","zh":"Leo 被這個消息嚇到，一句話也說不出來。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ the news, Grandpa called us right away.","options":["Hearing","Heard","Hear"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：主動用 V-ing，被動用 p.p.。爺爺是主動「聽到」消息，用 Hearing。(B) Heard 當 p.p. 表示爺爺被聽到，不合理；(C) Hear 是原形動詞，不能這樣用。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"______ with fresh mango, this shaved ice is the most popular dessert at the night market.","options":["Making","Made","Make"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：被動用 p.p.。刨冰是「被做」的，用 Made with fresh mango。(A) Making 表示刨冰自己在做東西，不合理；(C) Make 是原形動詞，不能這樣用。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"Having p.p. 與否定","text":["分詞的動作**比主要子句先發生**，要強調先完成時，用 **Having + p.p.**；被動則用 Having been + p.p.，having been 常可省略。","兩個動作緊接著發生（如 Hearing the bell, …），用 V-ing 就可以。","否定時把 **not** 放在分詞前面：Not + V-ing、Not having + p.p.，不用 don't 或 didn't。"],"adv":["Having finished… 也可寫成保留連接詞的 After finishing…，意思相同，見下一節。"],"formula":"Having (been) + p.p.…, S + V…／Not + V-ing…, S + V…","parse":{"en":"Having finished her homework, Mia went to the night market.","zh":"Mia 寫完功課後去逛夜市。","parts":[["Having finished her homework,","M","先發生的動作"],["Mia","S"],["went","V"],["to the night market.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Having finished]] her homework, Mia went to the night market with friends.","zh":"Mia 寫完功課後，和朋友去逛夜市。"},{"en":"[[Having been warned]] about the typhoon, we stayed home all day.","zh":"事先收到颱風警告，我們整天待在家。"},{"en":"[[Not feeling]] well, Lisa didn't go on the class trip.","zh":"Lisa 身體不舒服，沒去參加校外教學。"},{"en":"[[Not having eaten]] breakfast, I felt hungry all morning.","zh":"我沒吃早餐，整個早上都覺得餓。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ a big lunch, Nina didn't want any dessert.","options":["Eaten","Having eaten","Have eaten"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：Having + p.p. 表先發生。Nina 先吃了一頓大餐，所以不想吃甜點，用 Having eaten。(A) Eaten 是 p.p.，表示 Nina 被吃，不合理；(C) Have eaten 是完成式動詞，缺主詞，不能放在這裡。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"______ enough money, Ted couldn't buy the sneakers he wanted.","options":["Didn't have","Not having","Not have"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：分詞構句的否定是 Not + V-ing。Ted 沒有足夠的錢，用 Not having。(A) Didn't have 是過去式否定，缺主詞又只用逗號連接；(C) Not have 用了原形動詞，要改成 V-ing。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"保留連接詞","text":["為了讓意思更清楚，可以**保留連接詞**，如 when、while、if、though、after、before、since（自從）。","主動用 V-ing（while walking），被動用 p.p.（when asked）；after、before、since 的被動要寫 being + p.p.。","**because 不能保留**：Because feeling tired… 是錯的，要寫 Feeling tired… 或完整的子句。"],"adv":["after、before、since 也是**介系詞**，後面的 V-ing 可看成動名詞，這也是它們的被動要加 being 的原因。"],"parse":{"en":"Before going to bed, Eric always checks his phone.","zh":"Eric 睡前總會看一下手機。","parts":[["Before going to bed,","M","保留連接詞"],["Eric","S"],["always","M","頻率"],["checks","V"],["his phone.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[While walking]] to school, I ran into my English teacher.","zh":"走路上學時，我巧遇英文老師。"},{"en":"[[When asked]] about her plans, Grace said she wanted to be a nurse.","zh":"被問到未來的計畫時，Grace 說她想當護理師。"},{"en":"[[Before going]] to bed, Eric always checks his phone one last time.","zh":"Eric 睡前總會再看一次手機。"}],"practice":[{"q":"While ______ dinner, Mom burned her finger.","options":["cook","cooking","cooked"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：保留連接詞的分詞構句。原句 While Mom was cooking…，媽媽主動煮飯，用 While cooking。(A) cook 是原形動詞，不能直接接在 while 後；(C) cooked 是 p.p.，表示媽媽被煮，不合理。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"After ______ as class leader, Wendy became much busier.","options":["choosing","chosen","being chosen"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：after 後面的被動要用 being + p.p.。Wendy 是「被選為」班長，用 After being chosen。(A) choosing 是主動，表示 Wendy 去選別人；(B) chosen 不能直接接在 after 後面。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"主詞不同：獨立分詞構句","text":["兩個子句的**主詞不同**時，去掉連接詞但保留主詞，動詞改成分詞，叫做**獨立分詞構句**，多用於書面語。","There is/are 的句子簡化時保留 there：There being no seats left, …。"],"adv":["例外：Generally speaking（一般來說）、Judging from…（從…判斷）是慣用語，不必和主詞一致。"],"formula":"S1 + V-ing／p.p.…, S2 + V…","parse":{"en":"The weather being fine, we rode bikes along the Tamsui River.","zh":"天氣很好，我們沿著淡水河騎腳踏車。","parts":[["The weather being fine,","M","獨立分詞構句"],["we","S"],["rode","V"],["bikes","O"],["along the Tamsui River.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[The weather being]] fine, we rode bikes along the Tamsui River.","zh":"天氣很好，我們沿著淡水河騎腳踏車。"},{"en":"[[There being]] no seats left on the train, we stood all the way to Tainan.","zh":"火車上沒有空位了，我們一路站到台南。"},{"en":"[[The last bus having left]], we had to take a taxi home.","zh":"末班公車已經開走，我們只好搭計程車回家。"},{"en":"[[Her homework done]], Annie went out to play badminton with her friends.","zh":"功課寫完了，Annie 就出門和朋友打羽毛球。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The rain ______ heavy, the baseball game was canceled.","options":["was","being","be"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：主詞不同時保留主詞，be 動詞改成 being。the rain 和 the game 主詞不同，要寫 The rain being heavy。(A) was 會變成兩個句子只用逗號相連；(C) be 是原形動詞，不能這樣用。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"with + O + 分詞","text":["**with + O + 分詞**描述動作發生時的附帶狀態或原因。O 主動做用 V-ing，O 被做則用 **p.p.**。","O 後面也可以接形容詞或介系詞片語，如 with the door open、with a book in her hand。"],"formula":"S + V… + with + O + V-ing／p.p.（with 片語也可放句首，後加逗號）","parse":{"en":"Ben listened to the music with his eyes closed.","zh":"Ben 閉著眼睛聽音樂。","parts":[["Ben","S"],["listened to","V"],["the music","O"],["with his eyes closed.","M","附帶狀態"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Ben listened to the music [[with his eyes closed]].","zh":"Ben 閉著眼睛聽音樂。"},{"en":"[[With]] final exams [[coming]] up, Jenny studies until midnight every night.","zh":"期末考快到了，Jenny 每晚都讀到半夜。"},{"en":"I can't focus [[with my phone ringing]] all the time.","zh":"手機一直響，我根本沒辦法專心。"},{"en":"Don't talk [[with your mouth full]].","zh":"嘴裡塞滿食物時不要說話。"}],"practice":[{"q":"I couldn't sleep last night with the neighbor's dog ______.","options":["bark","barked","barking"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：with + O + V-ing／p.p.。狗是主動在叫，用 V-ing：with the dog barking。(A) bark 是原形動詞，不能接在 O 後；(B) barked 當 p.p. 表示狗被叫，不合理。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The students listened to the speech with their phones ______ off.","options":["turning","turned","turn"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：with + O + p.p. 表被動。手機是「被關掉」的，用 with their phones turned off。(A) turning 表示手機自己在關機，不合理；(C) turn 是原形動詞，不能接在 O 後。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"Walking to the MRT station, it started to rain.","right":"[[While I was walking]] to the MRT station, it started to rain.","why":"懸垂分詞：走路的是我，不是 it；主詞不同不能省略，要還原成子句。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"Feel sick, I stayed home from school.","right":"[[Feeling]] sick, I stayed home from school.","why":"去掉連接詞和主詞後，動詞要改成 V-ing，不能留原形動詞。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Seeing from the top of the mountain, the city looks beautiful at night.","right":"[[Seen]] from the top of the mountain, the city looks beautiful at night.","why":"城市是「被看」的，被動要用 p.p. seen。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Locating near the MRT station, the hotel is very convenient.","right":"[[Located]] near the MRT station, the hotel is very convenient.","why":"「位於」是 be located，被動，簡化後用 p.p. Located。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"Didn't know the way, we asked a police officer for help.","right":"[[Not knowing]] the way, we asked a police officer for help.","why":"分詞構句不能用 didn't；否定是把 not 放在 V-ing 前面。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"Finished my homework, I went to the night market.","right":"[[Having finished]] my homework, I went to the night market.","why":"我是主動寫完功課，不能只用 p.p.；先完成用 Having + p.p.。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Because feeling tired, I went to bed early.","right":"[[Feeling]] tired, I went to bed early.","why":"because 不能保留在分詞前，要去掉 because，或寫成完整子句。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"After finished dinner, we went for a walk in the park.","right":"After [[finishing]] dinner, we went for a walk in the park.","why":"保留 after 時，主動要接 V-ing，不能接過去式或 p.p.。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"The weather was nice, we went to the beach.","right":"The weather [[being]] nice, we went to the beach.","why":"兩句不能只用逗號連接；可加連接詞，或主詞不同時改成獨立分詞構句。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"Mr. Lin stood at the classroom door with his arms crossing.","right":"Mr. Lin stood at the classroom door with his arms [[crossed]].","why":"手臂是被交叉起來的，O 與動作是被動關係，要用 p.p.。"}],"tips":["空格在句首、逗號後是完整句子：先找主要子句的主詞，主動選 V-ing，被動選 p.p.。","選項有 Having + p.p. 時，找「已經、做完、…之後」等先發生的線索。","逗號連接兩個主詞不同的句子、又沒有連接詞，答案常是獨立分詞構句（S + being…）。"],"quiz":[{"q":"______ the bus coming, Tina ran to the bus stop as fast as she could.","options":["See","Saw","Seeing","Seen"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Tina 看到公車來了，就拚命跑向公車站。原句 When she saw…，主詞相同，去掉 when 和 she，主動的 saw 改成 Seeing。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"______ in simple English, this novel is easy for high school students to read.","options":["Written","Writing","Wrote","To write"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：這本小說用簡單的英文寫成，高中生很容易讀。小說是「被寫」的，被動用 p.p.；Writing 表示小說自己在寫，不合理。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"______ what to say, Ben just smiled and kept quiet.","options":["Knowing not","Don't know","Not know","Not knowing"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Ben 不知道該說什麼，只是笑笑不說話。分詞構句的否定是把 not 放在 V-ing 前面：Not knowing。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"______ that movie twice already, Peter doesn't want to watch it again.","options":["Seeing","Having seen","Seen","To see"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：那部電影 Peter 已經看過兩次，不想再看了。看過電影發生在「不想看」之前，表先發生用 Having + p.p.。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"When ______ by reporters about the accident, the bus driver said nothing.","options":["ask","to ask","asking","asked"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：記者問起那場車禍時，公車司機什麼都沒說。這是保留 when 的分詞構句；司機是「被問」的一方，要用 p.p.。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"The weather ______ fine, my family went hiking in Yangmingshan.","options":["being","was","is","been"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：天氣很好，我們全家去陽明山健行。兩句主詞不同，保留 the weather，be 動詞改 being；用 was 會變成兩個句子只用逗號相連。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"It isn't safe to leave home with the front door ______.","options":["unlock","unlocking","unlocked","to unlock"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：大門沒鎖就出門很不安全。with + O + 分詞／形容詞：unlocked 表示門處於「沒上鎖」的狀態；unlocking 表示門自己在開鎖，不合理；unlock 是原形，不能這樣用。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Walking along the beach in Kenting, ______.","options":["the sunset looked beautiful","I took many photos of the sunset","the wind blew my hat away","my phone fell into the sea"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：沿著墾丁的海灘散步時，我拍了很多夕陽的照片。省略的主詞要和主要子句相同，只有 I 會散步；其他選項的主詞不會散步，是懸垂分詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"id":"g-adj-adv","unit":"adj","level":"A2","title":"形容詞與副詞","en":"Adjectives and adverbs","lead":"修飾名詞或接在連綴動詞後用形容詞；修飾動詞、形容詞、副詞用副詞。","goals":["能依修飾對象選用形容詞或副詞","能寫對 -ly 副詞，分辨 hard 和 hardly 等字","能正確使用 so／such、enough 與形容詞順序"],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-noun"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[3]","note":"年齡與形狀的先後各書不同（有的把形狀放在年齡前），本章依章節規劃的順序，統測標準待確認。"},{"where":"sections[5]","note":"quite 放 a 前是一般用法；美式也見 a quite different idea，統測是否只認此序待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"形容詞的位置","text":["**形容詞**修飾名詞，通常放在名詞前面：a cute puppy；也可以放在 be 動詞或**連綴動詞**（look、feel、taste）後面當補語。","something、anything、nothing、someone 這類字，形容詞要放在**後面**：something cold、nothing special。"],"adv":["asleep、afraid、alone 不放在名詞前，多放在 be 動詞後（The baby is asleep）。exciting／excited 見〈分詞當形容詞〉。","look、taste 表示動作時是一般動詞，要用副詞修飾：He looked at me angrily（他生氣地看著我）。"],"formula":"形容詞 + 名詞／連綴動詞 + 形容詞／something + 形容詞","parse":{"en":"This mango shaved ice looks delicious!","zh":"這碗芒果冰看起來好好吃！","parts":[["This mango shaved ice","S"],["looks","V","連綴動詞"],["delicious!","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Mom made [[spicy]] hot pot for dinner tonight.","zh":"媽媽今晚煮了麻辣鍋當晚餐。"},{"en":"This mango shaved ice [[looks delicious]]!","zh":"這碗芒果冰看起來好好吃！"},{"en":"I'm so thirsty. Let's get [[something cold]] to drink.","zh":"我好渴，我們去買點冰的來喝吧。"},{"en":"Did you buy [[anything special]] at the night market?","zh":"你在夜市有買什麼特別的東西嗎？"}],"practice":[{"q":"This lemon tea tastes too ______. Can you add some sugar?","options":["sour","sourly","sourness"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：連綴動詞 taste 後面接形容詞當補語。tastes too sour 是喝起來太酸。(B) sourly 是副詞，不能當補語；(C) sourness 是名詞，不能接在 too 後面。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"I'm tired of noodles. Let's try ______ for lunch today.","options":["something different","different something","differently something"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：形容詞修飾 something 時放在它後面。something different 是「不一樣的東西」。(B) 形容詞放錯位置；(C) differently 是副詞，不能修飾 something，位置也錯。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"副詞修飾什麼","text":["**副詞**修飾動詞、形容詞、其他副詞，也能修飾整個句子。頻率副詞的位置見〈現在簡單式與現在進行式〉。","修飾動詞時常放在動詞或**受詞後面**，不夾在動詞和受詞中間：speak English well。修飾形容詞、副詞時放在它前面：really cold（enough 例外）。","修飾整句的副詞常放句首加逗號，如 Luckily、Sadly，表達說話者的看法。"],"adv":["表方式的副詞也可以放在一般動詞前面：Kevin quickly finished his homework（Kevin 很快寫完功課）。"],"table":{"cols":["修飾對象","常見位置","例子"],"rows":[["動詞","動詞或受詞後面","drive [[carefully]] / speak English [[well]]"],["形容詞","形容詞前面","[[really]] hot / [[too]] salty"],["副詞","副詞前面","walk [[very]] slowly"],["整句","句首，加逗號","[[Luckily]], we caught the bus."]]},"parse":{"en":"My grandpa walks very slowly these days.","zh":"爺爺最近走路很慢。","parts":[["My grandpa","S"],["walks","V"],["very slowly","M","修飾 walks"],["these days.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Kevin finished his homework [[quickly]] and went out to play basketball.","zh":"Kevin 很快寫完功課，就跑出去打籃球了。"},{"en":"The MRT is [[really]] crowded during rush hour.","zh":"尖峰時段的捷運真的很擠。"},{"en":"My grandpa walks [[very slowly]] these days.","zh":"爺爺最近走路很慢。"},{"en":"[[Luckily]], it stopped raining before the baseball game.","zh":"還好棒球比賽開始前，雨就停了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Ben lived in Canada for five years, so he speaks ______.","options":["English well","well English","English good"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：修飾動詞的副詞放在受詞後面，不夾在動詞和受詞中間。well 修飾 speaks，放在受詞 English 後。(B) well 夾在動詞和受詞中間；(C) good 是形容詞，不能修飾動詞。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"-ly 副詞與例外","text":["許多副詞由形容詞加 **-ly** 構成（quick → quickly），拼字變化見下表；good 的副詞是 well。","fast、hard、late、early 形容詞、副詞**同形**。**hardly**（幾乎不）、lately（最近）和 hard、late 意思不同。","friendly、lovely、lonely、lively 雖然是 -ly 結尾，卻是**形容詞**，通常不當副詞用；「友善地」要說 in a friendly way。"],"adv":["daily、weekly 也是形容詞、副詞同形：a daily habit、exercise daily。","well 當形容詞指「身體健康」：I don't feel well（我身體不舒服）。"],"table":{"cols":["形容詞","副詞","說明"],"rows":[["quick / careful","quickly / carefully","一般加 -ly"],["easy / happy","easily / happily","子音 + y：改 i 加 -ly"],["gentle / simple","gently / simply","子音 + le：去 e 加 y"],["good","well","不規則"],["fast / hard / late / early","fast / hard / late / early","同形，不加 -ly"],["friendly","in a friendly way","-ly 結尾的形容詞，改用片語"]]},"parse":{"en":"Jenny studies hard because she wants to get into a good university.","zh":"Jenny 很用功，因為她想考上好大學。","parts":[["Jenny","S"],["studies","V"],["hard","M","修飾 studies"],["because she wants to get into a good university.","M","原因子句"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Jenny studies [[hard]] because she wants to get into a good university.","zh":"Jenny 很用功，因為她想考上好大學。"},{"en":"It's so noisy here. I can [[hardly]] hear you.","zh":"這裡好吵，我幾乎聽不到你說話。"},{"en":"Have you seen Ming [[lately]]? He hasn't come to practice all week.","zh":"你最近有看到阿明嗎？他整個禮拜都沒來練習。"},{"en":"The lady at our breakfast shop is always [[friendly]] to us.","zh":"早餐店阿姨對我們總是很親切。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Please close the door ______. The baby is sleeping.","options":["gentle","gently","gentlely","gentley"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：子音 + le 結尾的形容詞變副詞，去 e 加 y。gentle → gently，修飾動詞 close。(A) gentle 是形容詞，不能修飾動詞；(C)(D) 拼字錯誤。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The bus came ______ this morning, so I missed my first class.","options":["late","lately","lateness"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：late 形容詞、副詞同形，「晚」的副詞就是 late。came late 是晚到。(B) lately 是「最近」，不合句意；(C) lateness 是名詞，不能修飾動詞。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"形容詞的順序","text":["名詞前有好幾個形容詞時，大致照這個順序：**意見 → 大小 → 年齡 → 形狀 → 顏色 → 來源 → 材質**，最後才是名詞。","意見放最前面，材質排在最後：a beautiful small old wooden box（意見、大小、年齡、材質）。一般只用兩、三個。"],"adv":["冠詞、所有格、數字放在所有形容詞前面：my two little cats；表用途的名詞又比材質更靠近名詞：a black leather school bag。"],"table":{"cols":["順序","類別","例字"],"rows":[["1","意見","nice, beautiful, cute"],["2","大小","big, small, tall"],["3","年齡","old, new, young"],["4","形狀","round, square"],["5","顏色","red, black, white"],["6","來源","Japanese, Taiwanese"],["7","材質","wooden, plastic, cotton"]]},"parse":{"en":"Dad bought a new black Japanese scooter last month.","zh":"爸爸上個月買了一台全新的黑色日本機車。","parts":[["Dad","S"],["bought","V"],["a new black Japanese scooter","O"],["last month.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My sister just adopted a [[cute little white]] puppy.","zh":"我姊剛領養了一隻可愛的小白狗。"},{"en":"Dad bought a [[new black Japanese]] scooter last month.","zh":"爸爸上個月買了一台全新的黑色日本機車。"},{"en":"Mom gave me a [[lovely red wool]] scarf for my birthday.","zh":"媽媽送我一條好看的紅色羊毛圍巾當生日禮物。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Mia bought a ______ T-shirt at the night market.","options":["cute white cotton","white cotton cute","cotton cute white","cute cotton white"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：形容詞順序是意見 → 顏色 → 材質。cute 是意見，white 是顏色，cotton 是材質。(B)(C) 意見 cute 沒放最前面；(D) 材質 cotton 跑到顏色 white 前面。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"so 與 such","text":["**so** 修飾形容詞或副詞：so hot、so fast。**such** 修飾名詞（名詞前可加形容詞），單數可數名詞要用 such a/an：such a nice day。","複數或不可數名詞前不加 a：such nice people、such good weather。不說 so a hot day。","表數量的 many、much、few、little 前面用 so：so many people、so little time。接 that 子句表結果，詳見〈連接詞〉。"],"adv":["little 當「小的」時是一般形容詞，照 such 的規則：such a little girl。","較正式的 so hot a day 也正確，但一般多說 such a hot day。"],"formula":"so + adj/adv；such a/an + adj + 單數可數名詞；such + adj + 複數／不可數名詞","parse":{"en":"We had such a great time in Hualien last summer.","zh":"去年暑假我們在花蓮玩得超開心。","parts":[["We","S"],["had","V"],["such a great time","O"],["in Hualien","M","地點"],["last summer.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"It's [[so]] hot today. Let's go get some shaved ice.","zh":"今天好熱，我們去吃剉冰吧。"},{"en":"We had [[such a]] great time in Hualien last summer.","zh":"去年暑假我們在花蓮玩得超開心。"},{"en":"Your parents are [[such]] nice people.","zh":"你爸媽人真好。"},{"en":"I have [[so much]] homework this weekend.","zh":"這個週末我的作業好多。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Thanks! This is ______ useful gift.","options":["so","such","such a","so a"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：單數可數名詞用 such a + 形容詞 + 名詞。gift 是單數可數名詞，useful 開頭唸 /j/，用 a。(A) so 不能直接接形容詞 + 單數名詞；(B) 少了 a；(D) 沒有 so a 的說法。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Wow! There are ______ people at the night market tonight.","options":["so many","such many","so much"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：many、much 等數量詞前用 so，不用 such。people 是複數可數名詞，用 so many。(B) many 前不用 such；(C) much 接不可數名詞，people 要用 many。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"enough 與程度副詞","text":["**enough** 修飾形容詞或副詞時放在**後面**：old enough、fast enough；修飾名詞時放在前面：enough money、enough time。","**very**（很）修飾形容詞、副詞，不能單獨修飾動詞，要說 like it very much。**too**（太…）表示超過可接受的程度，多帶負面意思。","**quite**（相當）遇到「a + 形容詞 + 名詞」時放在 a 前面：quite a long time。"],"adv":["very 也不能修飾比較級，要用 much（much better），見〈比較級與最高級〉；too…to V、enough to V 見〈不定詞 to V〉。"],"formula":"adj/adv + enough；enough + 名詞","parse":{"en":"Leo is old enough to get a scooter license now.","zh":"Leo 已經到可以考機車駕照的年紀了。","parts":[["Leo","S"],["is","V"],["old enough to get a scooter license","C","主詞補語"],["now.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Leo is [[old enough]] to get a scooter license now.","zh":"Leo 已經到可以考機車駕照的年紀了。"},{"en":"Do we have [[enough money]] for a taxi?","zh":"我們的錢夠搭計程車嗎？"},{"en":"This ramen is [[too salty]]. I can't finish it.","zh":"這碗拉麵太鹹了，我吃不完。"},{"en":"We waited [[quite a]] long time for the bus to Jiufen.","zh":"我們等去九份的公車等了好一陣子。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The water in the pool isn't ______ for swimming yet.","options":["warm enough","enough warm","warmly enough"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：enough 修飾形容詞時放在形容詞後面。be 動詞後要用形容詞 warm，再接 enough。(B) enough 放錯位置；(C) warmly 是副詞，不能當 be 動詞的補語。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"I like bubble tea ______. I drink it every day.","options":["very","very much","much very"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：very 不能單獨修飾動詞，要用 very much，放在受詞後面。(A) very 不能單獨修飾動詞 like；(C) much very 詞序錯誤。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"Do you want cold something to drink?","right":"Do you want [[something cold]] to drink?","why":"形容詞修飾 something 時要放在它後面。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"This cake tastes deliciously.","right":"This cake tastes [[delicious]].","why":"taste 在這裡是連綴動詞，後面接形容詞當補語，不用副詞。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Amy plays the piano very good.","right":"Amy plays the piano very [[well]].","why":"修飾動詞 plays 要用副詞 well，good 是形容詞。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"Tina studies English hardly every day.","right":"Tina studies English [[hard]] every day.","why":"「努力地」是 hard；hardly 是「幾乎不」，意思完全不同。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"The clerk talked to us friendly.","right":"The clerk talked to us [[in a friendly way]].","why":"friendly 是形容詞，不能修飾動詞，要說 in a friendly way。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"My aunt has a black big dog.","right":"My aunt has a [[big black]] dog.","why":"大小要放在顏色前面：big black dog。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"We had so a great time in Kenting.","right":"We had [[such a]] great time in Kenting.","why":"後面有單數名詞 time，用 such a + 形容詞 + 名詞，不說 so a。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"There were such many people at the concert.","right":"There were [[so many]] people at the concert.","why":"many 前面用 so，不用 such。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"I very like this song.","right":"I like this song [[very much]].","why":"very 不能單獨修飾動詞，要說 like… very much。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"My little brother isn't enough tall to ride the roller coaster.","right":"My little brother isn't [[tall enough]] to ride the roller coaster.","why":"enough 修飾形容詞時放在形容詞後面。"}],"tips":["選擇題先看空格修飾誰：修飾名詞或當連綴動詞補語選形容詞，修飾動作選副詞（looked at me angrily）。","so/such：有名詞用 such（a），沒有用 so；表數量的 many、much、few、little 前用 so。","選擇題常考詞序：old enough、enough money、something cold，及形容詞順序。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Grace won first place in the singing contest. She sings really ______.","options":["good","well","nice","beautiful"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Grace 在歌唱比賽得了第一名，她唱歌真的很好聽。修飾動詞 sings 要用副詞，good 的副詞是 well；good、nice、beautiful 都是形容詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I'm starving. Is there ______ in the fridge?","options":["anything good to eat","good anything to eat","anything to eat good","to eat anything good"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我餓扁了，冰箱裡有什麼好吃的嗎？修飾 anything 的形容詞放在它後面，再接 to V：anything good to eat。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"My aunt is ______ good cook that everyone in the family asks her for recipes.","options":["so","such","so a","such a"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：阿姨很會做菜，家裡每個人都向她要食譜。cook 在這裡是名詞「廚師」，是單數可數名詞，前面要有 a，所以用 such a + 形容詞 + 名詞；so 後面接形容詞，不能直接接 a。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Tim is only fifteen, so he isn't ______ to get a scooter license.","options":["enough old","old enough","enough age","age enough"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Tim 才十五歲，還不到考機車駕照的年紀。enough 修飾形容詞時放在後面：old enough to V。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Our new neighbors seem very ______. They always say hello to us.","options":["politely","warmly","friendly","nicely"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：新鄰居看起來很友善，總是跟我們打招呼。seem 是連綴動詞，後面接形容詞；friendly 雖然是 -ly 結尾，卻是形容詞，其他三個是副詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The music at the party was so loud that I could ______ hear my friends.","options":["hardly","hard","lately","late"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：派對音樂太大聲，我幾乎聽不到朋友說話。hardly 是「幾乎不」；hard 是「努力地、用力地」，lately 是「最近」，都不合句意。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Grandpa gave me ______ on my sixteenth birthday.","options":["an old beautiful Japanese camera","a Japanese old beautiful camera","a beautiful old Japanese camera","a beautiful Japanese old camera"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：爺爺在我十六歲生日時送我一台漂亮的日本老相機。形容詞順序是意見 → 年齡 → 來源，所以是 beautiful old Japanese。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I drank ______ coffee yesterday afternoon that I couldn't fall asleep until 3 a.m.","options":["very much","so much","such much","so many"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我昨天下午喝了太多咖啡，到凌晨三點才睡著。表結果的 that 子句配 so 或 such，very 不行；coffee 不可數，不用 many；much 前用 so，不說 such much。故選 (B)。"}]},{"id":"g-compare","unit":"adj","level":"B1","title":"比較級與最高級","en":"Comparatives and superlatives","lead":"兩者比較用比較級 + than，三者以上用 the + 最高級。","goals":["能正確寫出形容詞、副詞的比較級和最高級","能用比較級 + than、the + 最高級比較人事物","能用 as…as、倍數和「越…越…」句型造句"],"prereq":["g-adj-adv","g-noun","g-pronoun"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[1].adv","note":"than me 在美式口語很普遍；統測選擇題是否只接受 than I (am) 待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"形式變化","text":["單音節字大多直接加 **-er/-est**（tall → taller）；e 結尾只加 -r/-st（nice → nicer）。","單音節字結尾是「子音 + 一個母音 + 一個子音」字母時，先**重複字尾子音**再加（big → bigger、hot → hotter）；w、x、y 結尾不重複（newer）。","**雙音節**、子音 + y 結尾的形容詞：y 改 i 再加 -er/-est（happier）；其他雙音節以上的字和 -ly 副詞大多用 **more/most**。"],"adv":["少數雙音節字也加 -er/-est，如 simpler、quieter；early 雖以 -ly 結尾，比較級卻是 earlier。","far 有兩種比較級：**farther** 多指距離；**further** 也能指距離，還有「進一步」的意思（further information）。"],"table":{"cols":["規則","原級","比較級","最高級"],"rows":[["單音節：加 -er/-est","tall","[[taller]]","[[tallest]]"],["雙音節，子音 + y：y 改 i","happy","[[happier]]","[[happiest]]"],["其他雙音節以上：more/most","careful","[[more careful]]","[[most careful]]"],["不規則","good / well","[[better]]","[[best]]"],["不規則","bad / badly","[[worse]]","[[worst]]"],["不規則","many / much","[[more]]","[[most]]"],["不規則","little（少）","[[less]]","[[least]]"],["不規則","far","[[farther]] / [[further]]","[[farthest]] / [[furthest]]"]]},"parse":{"en":"This year's English test was easier than last year's.","zh":"今年的英文考試比去年簡單。","parts":[["This year's English test","S"],["was","V"],["easier","C","主詞補語"],["than last year's.","M","比較對象"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My younger brother is [[taller]] than my dad now.","zh":"我弟弟現在已經比我爸高了。"},{"en":"This year's English test was [[easier]] than last year's.","zh":"今年的英文考試比去年簡單。"},{"en":"That's the [[most popular]] stall at Shilin Night Market.","zh":"那是士林夜市最受歡迎的攤位。"},{"en":"My cold is [[worse]] today than it was yesterday.","zh":"我的感冒今天比昨天更嚴重。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My mom works at a night market. On weekends, she is ______ than on weekdays.","options":["busyer","busier","busiest","most busy"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：雙音節、子音 + y 結尾，y 改 i 再加 -er。有 than 用比較級 busier。(A) busyer 沒有把 y 改 i；(C) busiest、(D) most busy 是最高級，不能接 than。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"In Taipei, taking the MRT is ______ than driving.","options":["more convenient","convenienter","most convenient"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：多音節的 convenient 用 more 構成比較級。有 than 用 more convenient。(B) convenienter 不存在；(C) most convenient 是最高級，不能接 than。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"比較級 + than","text":["兩者比較用**比較級 + than**，than 後接比較對象：名詞、代名詞或子句（than my sister、than I expected）。","要說「…得多」，在比較級前加 **much、far、a lot**；more + 複數名詞時，much 要改用 **many**（many more students）。","「還要更…」用 even，「稍微」用 a little、a bit。**very 不能修飾比較級**（不說 very taller）。"],"adv":["從兩者中挑出一個時（常帶 of the two），用 **the + 比較級**（Tom is the taller of the two.）；一般「A 比 B」不加 the。","than 後的代名詞，口語常用受格（taller than me），正式寫法用主格加動詞（taller than I am）。"],"formula":"A + V + 比較級 + than + B","parse":{"en":"The MRT is much faster than the bus during rush hour.","zh":"尖峰時段，捷運比公車快得多。","parts":[["The MRT","S"],["is","V"],["much","M","修飾比較級"],["faster","C","主詞補語"],["than the bus","M","比較對象"],["during rush hour.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The MRT is [[much faster]] than the bus during rush hour.","zh":"尖峰時段，捷運比公車快得多。"},{"en":"Amy's new phone is [[even more expensive]] than mine.","zh":"Amy 的新手機比我的還要貴。"},{"en":"I usually get up [[a lot earlier]] than my sister.","zh":"我通常比我妹早起很多。"},{"en":"This bubble tea is [[far sweeter]] than I expected.","zh":"這杯珍奶比我想像的甜得多。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Riding a bike to school is ______ faster than walking.","options":["very","a lot","more","most"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：修飾比較級用 much、far、a lot。a lot faster 表「快得多」。(A) very 不能修飾比較級；(C) more faster 重複比較；(D) most 是最高級，不能放在 faster 前。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"______ students joined the dance club this year than last year.","options":["Much more","Very more","Many more"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：more + 複數可數名詞，用 many more 表「多得多」。students 是可數複數，用 Many more。(A) much more 接不可數名詞；(B) very 不能修飾比較級。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"比較對象要一致","text":["比較的兩邊必須同類。「她的英文比我好」比的是英文，不是人，要說 better than mine，不是 than me。","為了不重複名詞，單數或不可數名詞用 **that**、複數用 **those** 代替，後接 of、in 等介系詞片語；也可用 mine、Tom's 代替「所有格 + 名詞」。"],"adv":["重複名詞也正確（than the population of Tainan），只是較囉唆；寫成 than Tainan 就變成拿人口和城市比。"],"formula":"單數 → than that of …／複數 → than those of …","parse":{"en":"Prices at this night market are lower than those in Ximending.","zh":"這個夜市的東西比西門町便宜。","parts":[["Prices at this night market","S"],["are","V"],["lower","C","主詞補語"],["than those in Ximending.","M","比較對象"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The population of Kaohsiung is larger than [[that of]] Tainan.","zh":"高雄的人口比台南多。"},{"en":"Prices at this night market are lower than [[those]] in Ximending.","zh":"這個夜市的東西比西門町便宜。"},{"en":"Your handwriting is much neater than [[mine]].","zh":"你的字比我的工整多了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My old bike is so heavy. Your new bike is much lighter than ______.","options":["me","my","mine","I"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：比較對象要一致。比的是腳踏車，用 mine（= my bike）。(A) me、(D) I 變成拿腳踏車和人比；(B) my 是所有格，後面一定要接名詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The rooms in this hotel are bigger than ______ in the hotel we stayed at last year.","options":["that","those","it","them"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：用 that/those 代替前面的名詞。rooms 是複數，用 those。(A) that、(C) it 代替單數；(D) them 不能這樣代替後面帶修飾語的名詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"最高級的句型","text":["三者以上用 **the + 最高級**（有所有格不加 the）；範圍常用 in my class、of the three，也可用 on our team 等。","**one of the + 最高級 + 複數名詞**表示「最…的之一」，名詞一定用複數；當主詞時，動詞跟著 one 用單數。","**比較級 + than any other + 單數名詞**也表示最高級；主詞在比較範圍內要加 other（than any other boy in my class）。"],"adv":["副詞最高級的 the 常可省略（Who runs fastest in your class?）；形容詞最高級 + 名詞要用 the 或所有格。","主詞不在範圍內就不加 other：Taipei 101 is taller than any building in Japan.（日本的大樓不包含台北 101）"],"formula":"the + 最高級 (+ N) + in/of + 範圍","parse":{"en":"Jason is the tallest boy in our class.","zh":"Jason 是我們班最高的男生。","parts":[["Jason","S"],["is","V"],["the tallest boy","C","主詞補語"],["in our class.","M","範圍"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Jason is [[the tallest]] boy in our class.","zh":"Jason 是我們班最高的男生。"},{"en":"Of the three bubble tea shops near school, this one is [[the cheapest]].","zh":"學校附近三家飲料店中，這家最便宜。"},{"en":"Jiufen is [[one of the most popular]] tourist [[spots]] in Taiwan.","zh":"九份是台灣最熱門的景點之一。"},{"en":"Taipei 101 is taller [[than any other building]] in Taiwan.","zh":"台北 101 比台灣其他任何大樓都高。"}],"practice":[{"q":"It is so hot outside! Today is ______ day of the summer so far.","options":["hotter","the hotter","the hottest","hottest"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：the + 最高級 + 名詞 + 範圍。在整個夏天裡比出「最熱」，用 the hottest。(A)(B) 是比較級，這裡沒有兩者比較；(D) 最高級 + 名詞前要加 the。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"One of the best players on our team ______ hurt in last week's game.","options":["were","was","are"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：one of the + 最高級 + 複數名詞當主詞，動詞跟 one 用單數。last week 用過去式 was。(A) were 是複數；(C) are 是複數，時態也不對。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"as + 原級 + as 與倍數","text":["**as + 原級 + as** 表示「和…一樣」，中間放形容詞或副詞的原級。否定 **not as/so … as** 表示「不如…」。","倍數放在第一個 as 前：twice as … as（兩倍）、three times as … as（三倍）。","一樣多：**as many** + 複數名詞 + as、**as much** + 不可數名詞 + as（as many books as、as much money as）。"],"adv":["「一半」用 half as … as；倍數也可接 the + 名詞 + of：three times the size of the old one（大小是舊的三倍）。"],"formula":"(倍數) + as + 原級 + as + 比較對象","parse":{"en":"The bus is not as convenient as the MRT.","zh":"公車沒有捷運方便。","parts":[["The bus","S"],["is","V"],["not","M","否定"],["as convenient","C","主詞補語"],["as the MRT.","M","比較對象"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My little sister can run [[as fast as]] I can.","zh":"我妹妹跑得跟我一樣快。"},{"en":"The bus is [[not as convenient as]] the MRT.","zh":"公車沒有捷運方便。"},{"en":"My new backpack cost [[twice as much as]] my old one.","zh":"我的新書包價錢是舊的兩倍。"},{"en":"Our new gym is [[three times as big as]] the old one.","zh":"我們的新體育館是舊的三倍大。"}],"practice":[{"q":"I have a part-time job, so I don't have as ______ free time as my classmates.","options":["many","much","more"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：as much + 不可數名詞 + as。time 是不可數名詞，用 as much。(A) many 接可數複數名詞；(C) more 是比較級，as…as 中間要用原級。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"This new phone costs ______ my old one.","options":["twice as much as","as twice much as","twice much as","as much twice as"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：倍數放在第一個 as 前：twice as much as。(B)(D) 倍數位置錯誤；(C) 少了第一個 as。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"越來越…與越…越…","text":["**比較級 and 比較級**表示「越來越…」，如 hotter and hotter；用 more 的字只重複 more：more and more popular。","**the + 比較級…, the + 比較級…**表示「越…就越…」，兩邊都要有 the，後接 S + V；也可省略成 The more, the better（越多越好）。"],"adv":["比較級帶名詞時，名詞要一起移到前面：The more books you read, the more you learn.","談未來時，前半句通常用現在式，後半句才用 will：The earlier we leave, the sooner we will get there."],"formula":"The + 比較級 + S + V, the + 比較級 + S + V.","parse":{"en":"The more you practice, the better you get.","zh":"你練得越多，就會越厲害。","parts":[["The more you practice,","M","從屬子句，表條件"],["the better","C","主詞補語，前移"],["you","S"],["get.","V","連綴動詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"It's getting [[hotter and hotter]] in Taipei these days.","zh":"台北最近越來越熱。"},{"en":"Online games are becoming [[more and more popular]] among students.","zh":"線上遊戲在學生之間越來越受歡迎。"},{"en":"[[The more]] you practice, [[the better]] you get.","zh":"你練得越多，就會越厲害。"},{"en":"[[The earlier]] we leave, [[the sooner]] we'll get to Kenting.","zh":"我們越早出發，就越快到墾丁。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Summer is coming, and the days are getting ______.","options":["long and long","more and more long","the longer","longer and longer"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：比較級 and 比較級表示「越來越…」。long 是單音節，用 longer and longer。(A) 用了原級；(B) 單音節字不用 more；(C) the longer 要和另一個 the + 比較級搭配。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"The earlier you go to bed, ______ you will feel tomorrow.","options":["the best","better","the better"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：the + 比較級…, the + 比較級…，兩邊都要有 the。後半句用 the better。(A) the best 是最高級；(B) better 少了 the。故選 (C)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"Jenny is more taller than her sister.","right":"Jenny is [[taller]] than her sister.","why":"taller 已經是比較級，前面不能再加 more。","sec":0},{"wrong":"This bag is very cheaper than that one.","right":"This bag is [[much cheaper]] than that one.","why":"very 不能修飾比較級，要改用 much、far 或 a lot。","sec":1},{"wrong":"There are much more students in our club than last year.","right":"There are [[many more]] students in our club than last year.","why":"students 是可數複數名詞，要用 many more，不用 much more。","sec":1},{"wrong":"Her English is better than me.","right":"Her English is better than [[mine]].","why":"比的是英文不是人，要用 mine（= my English）。","sec":2},{"wrong":"Jay is one of the best player on our team.","right":"Jay is one of the best [[players]] on our team.","why":"one of the + 最高級後面要接複數名詞。","sec":3},{"wrong":"Mark is taller than any student in his class.","right":"Mark is taller than any [[other]] student in his class.","why":"Mark 也是班上的學生，要加 other，否則等於說他比自己高。","sec":3},{"wrong":"My backpack is as heavier as yours.","right":"My backpack is as [[heavy]] as yours.","why":"as…as 中間要用原級，不能用比較級。","sec":4},{"wrong":"I don't have as much books as my brother.","right":"I don't have as [[many]] books as my brother.","why":"books 是可數複數名詞，要用 as many…as；much 接不可數名詞。","sec":4},{"wrong":"Taipei is getting more crowded and more crowded.","right":"Taipei is getting [[more and more crowded]].","why":"用 more 的字只重複 more：more and more + 原級。","sec":5},{"wrong":"The more you read, more you learn.","right":"The more you read, [[the more]] you learn.","why":"「越…越…」前後兩邊都要有 the。","sec":5}],"tips":["看到 than 多半選比較級（rather than、other than 除外）；三者以上範圍選 the + 最高級。","修飾比較級選 much、far、a lot，very 是陷阱；one of the 後選複數名詞；as…as 用原級。","中譯英或句子重組遇到「越…越…」，寫成 The + 比較級 + S + V, the + 比較級 + S + V。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Lisa has lived in the U.S. for three years, so her English is ______ than mine.","options":["good","best","better","more good"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Lisa 在美國住了三年，所以她的英文比我好。有 than 要用比較級；good 是不規則變化 good → better → best，沒有 more good。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Many hikers dream of climbing Mount Jade. It is ______ mountain in Taiwan.","options":["higher","the highest","highest","the higher"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：許多登山客夢想爬玉山，它是台灣最高的山。範圍是 in Taiwan，三者以上用最高級，最高級 + 名詞前要加 the。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"My bike is not as ______ as yours, but it still works fine.","options":["newer","newest","more new","new"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我的腳踏車沒有你的新，但還是很好騎。not as…as 表示「不如…」，中間要用原級，不能用比較級或最高級。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Nobody in our class could solve this math problem. It was ______ harder than the last one.","options":["much","very","so","too"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：全班沒人解得出這題數學，它比上一題難得多。修飾比較級用 much、even、far、a lot；very、so、too 都不能直接放在比較級前。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Beef noodle soup is one of the most popular ______ in Taiwan.","options":["dish","dishes","a dish","the dish"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：牛肉麵是台灣最受歡迎的料理之一。one of the + 最高級後面要接複數名詞，表示「最…的…之一」。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Jessica runs ______ than any other girl on our team.","options":["fastest","the fastest","faster","most fast"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Jessica 跑得比隊上其他任何女生都快。有 than 就用比較級；「比較級 + than any other + 單數名詞」意思等於最高級，但形式仍是比較級。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The population of Taipei is smaller than ______ of New Taipei.","options":["it","those","one","that"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：台北市的人口比新北市少。比較對象要一致，用 that 代替前面的單數名詞 the population；those 是用來代替複數名詞。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"______ you exercise, the healthier you will be.","options":["The more","More","The most","Much more"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：你運動得越多，就會越健康。「越…越…」用 the + 比較級…, the + 比較級…，兩邊都要有 the，不能用最高級。故選 (A)。"}]},{"id":"g-conj","unit":"clause","level":"B1","title":"連接詞","en":"Conjunctions","lead":"選連接詞先看兩句的意思關係，再看後面接子句還是名詞。","goals":["能用對等與配對連接詞連接字詞和子句","能分辨連接詞接子句、介系詞接名詞","能依句意選出時間、條件、目的、結果連接詞"],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-future"],"pending":[],"sections":[{"h":"對等連接詞 FANBOYS","text":["**對等連接詞**連接地位相同的單字、片語或子句，共七個（FANBOYS）：for、and、nor、but、or、yet、so，最常用 and、but、or、so。","連接兩個完整的句子時，連接詞前常加逗號。**祈使句 + or** 表「否則」；祈使句 + and 表「就會」。","**however、therefore** 是**副詞**，不是連接詞，不能只靠逗號連接兩句，前面要用分號或句點。"],"adv":["for（因為）、nor（也不）、yet（但是）較書面。nor 後接子句時要倒裝：He can't swim, nor can he ride a bike.（詳見〈倒裝句〉）"],"formula":"S + V, but/so + S + V. ／ S + V; however, S + V.","parse":{"en":"I was really tired, but I still finished my homework.","zh":"我很累，但還是把功課寫完了。","parts":[["I","S"],["was","V"],["really","M","程度"],["tired,","C","主詞補語"],["but","J"],["I","S"],["still","M","副詞"],["finished","V"],["my homework.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I was really tired, [[but]] I still finished my homework.","zh":"我很累，但還是把功課寫完了。"},{"en":"It started to rain, [[so]] we left the night market early.","zh":"開始下雨了，所以我們提早離開夜市。"},{"en":"Hurry up, [[or]] you'll miss the last MRT train.","zh":"快一點，不然你會趕不上捷運末班車。"},{"en":"Amy studied hard for the test[[; however,]] she didn't pass.","zh":"Amy 很用功準備考試，可是沒有及格。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Put on your jacket, ______ you'll catch a cold.","options":["and","or","so"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：祈使句 + or 表「否則」。穿上外套，否則會感冒，用 or。(A) and 表「就會」，變成穿了外套就感冒；(C) so 表結果，意思也不合。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I love spicy food, ______ my sister can't eat it at all.","options":["but","so","or","however"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：前後意思相反用 but。我愛吃辣，我妹卻完全不能吃。(B) so 表結果、(C) or 表選擇，意思不合；(D) however 是副詞，前面只有逗號，不能連接兩句。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"配對連接詞","text":["配對連接詞要成對使用，A 和 B 要**形式對稱**：名詞配名詞、形容詞配形容詞、動詞配動詞。","**neither…nor** 本身是否定，同一子句不再加 not。當主詞時，both A and B 用複數動詞，其餘看靠近動詞的 B，詳見〈主詞與動詞一致〉。"],"adv":["Not only 帶子句放句首要倒裝，but 後面照常語序：Not only did he win, but he also broke the record.（詳見〈倒裝句〉）"],"table":{"cols":["句型","意思","例"],"rows":[["both A and B","A 和 B 都","[[both]] Amy [[and]] Ken"],["either A or B","不是 A 就是 B","[[either]] today [[or]] tomorrow"],["neither A nor B","既不 A 也不 B","[[neither]] hot [[nor]] cold"],["not only A but (also) B","不但 A 而且 B","[[not only]] cheap [[but also]] tasty"],["not A but B","不是 A 而是 B","[[not]] Monday [[but]] Friday"]]},"parse":{"en":"Both my brother and I work part-time at a convenience store.","zh":"我和我哥都在便利商店打工。","parts":[["Both my brother and I","S","複數主詞"],["work","V"],["part-time","M"],["at a convenience store.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Both]] my brother [[and]] I work part-time at a convenience store.","zh":"我和我哥都在便利商店打工。"},{"en":"You can [[either]] take the MRT [[or]] ride a YouBike to school.","zh":"你可以搭捷運或騎 YouBike 上學。"},{"en":"[[Neither]] Jason [[nor]] his sister likes stinky tofu.","zh":"Jason 和他妹妹都不喜歡臭豆腐。"},{"en":"Ms. Lin is [[not only]] our homeroom teacher [[but also]] our basketball coach.","zh":"林老師不只是我們的班導，還是籃球隊教練。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ Amy and Ken are on the school volleyball team.","options":["Both","Either","Neither"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：配對連接詞要配對，both 配 and。空格後有 and，動詞又是複數 are，用 Both。(B) Either 要配 or；(C) Neither 要配 nor。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"My little brother is not only cute but also ______.","options":["smartly","smart","he is smart"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：配對連接詞前後形式對稱。not only 後是形容詞 cute，but also 後也用形容詞 smart。(A) smartly 是副詞；(C) he is smart 是子句，前後不對稱。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"時間連接詞","text":["時間連接詞帶出**副詞子句**，子句放句首時後面加逗號。while 表「在…期間」，常接進行式。","**時間副詞子句**表未來時用現在式代替未來式：as soon as I get home，不寫 will get。詳見〈未來式〉。","**not…until** 表「直到…才」。since 表「自從」時，主要子句常用現在完成式，詳見〈完成式〉。"],"adv":["此規則只限副詞子句：I don't know when she'll come. 的 when 子句是名詞子句，當 know 的受詞，仍用 will，詳見〈名詞子句與間接問句〉。"],"table":{"cols":["連接詞","意思","例"],"rows":[["when","當…的時候","[[when]] I was young"],["while","在…的期間","[[while]] I was cooking"],["before / after","在…之前／之後","[[after]] school ends"],["until","直到…為止","[[until]] the rain stops"],["as soon as","一…就…","[[as soon as]] I arrive"],["since","自從…以來","[[since]] I was ten"]]},"parse":{"en":"I will call you as soon as I get home.","zh":"我一到家就打電話給你。","parts":[["I","S"],["will call","V"],["you","O"],["as soon as I get home.","M","時間副詞子句"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[As soon as]] the bell rings, we'll run to the school store.","zh":"鐘聲一響，我們就要衝去福利社。"},{"en":"I [[didn't]] go to bed [[until]] I finished my science report.","zh":"我直到寫完自然科報告才去睡覺。"},{"en":"Mia [[has worked]] at the bakery [[since]] she started high school.","zh":"Mia 從上高中開始就在麵包店打工。"},{"en":"[[While]] I was waiting for the bus, I ran into an old classmate.","zh":"我在等公車的時候，巧遇以前的同學。"}],"practice":[{"q":"I'll text you when the movie ______.","options":["will end","ends","ending","ended"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：時間副詞子句以現在式代替未來式。主要子句 I'll text 是未來，when 子句用現在式 ends。(A) will end 不用在時間副詞子句；(C) ending 不能單獨當動詞；(D) ended 是過去式，時間不合。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"______ I was waiting for the bus, it started to rain.","options":["While","During","Because of"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：while 是連接詞，後接子句，常配進行式。空格後是子句 I was waiting…，用 While。(B) During 是介系詞，要接名詞；(C) Because of 也是介系詞，意思也不合。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"原因與讓步","text":["表原因、讓步時，**連接詞**後接子句（S + V），**介系詞**後接名詞或 V-ing。選項意思相同時，就看空格後面接什麼。","中文說「雖然…但是…」，英文 although 和 but **只能用一個**；「因為…所以…」的 because 和 so 也一樣。"],"adv":["even though 語氣比 although 強。despite 不加 of；接子句要用 despite the fact that。","since、as 表原因時，多用於對方已知的理由；回答 Why 的問句要用 because。"],"table":{"cols":["意思","連接詞 + 子句","介系詞 + 名詞／V-ing"],"rows":[["因為","because / since / as","because of / due to"],["例","[[because]] it rained","[[because of]] the rain"],["雖然、儘管","although / though / even though","despite / in spite of"],["例","[[although]] it rained","[[in spite of]] the rain"]]},"parse":{"en":"Although it rained, we still went to the night market.","zh":"雖然下雨，我們還是去了夜市。","parts":[["Although it rained,","M","讓步副詞子句"],["we","S"],["still","M","副詞"],["went","V"],["to the night market.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"We stayed home [[because]] a typhoon was coming.","zh":"因為颱風要來，我們待在家裡。"},{"en":"Our school trip was canceled [[due to]] the typhoon.","zh":"我們的校外教學因為颱風取消了。"},{"en":"[[Although]] the beef noodle shop was crowded, we decided to wait for a table.","zh":"雖然那家牛肉麵店人很多，我們還是決定等位子。"},{"en":"[[Despite]] feeling sick, Eric still went to basketball practice.","zh":"儘管身體不舒服，Eric 還是去練球了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Kevin missed the bus ______ he got up late.","options":["because","because of","so"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：連接詞 because 後接子句。空格後是子句 he got up late，用 because。(B) because of 是介系詞，要接名詞；(C) so 表結果，變成「錯過公車，所以晚起」，不合理。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"We went hiking ______ the bad weather.","options":["although","despite","despite of"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：介系詞 despite 後接名詞，不加 of。空格後是名詞 the bad weather，用 despite。(A) although 是連接詞，要接子句；(C) 沒有 despite of 的用法，要用 despite 或 in spite of。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"條件連接詞","text":["if（如果）、unless（除非）、as long as（只要）、in case（以防萬一）帶出**副詞子句**；講未來時一樣用**現在式**。","**unless** 約等於 if…not，已含否定；要表「如果不…」，子句不再加 not（unless you hurry，不寫 unless you don't hurry）。","與事實相反的假設（If I were you…）詳見〈條件句與假設語氣〉。"],"adv":["unless 子句也可以是否定，表「除非…不」：I'll come with you, unless you don't want me to.","Take an umbrella in case it rains. 是先帶傘以防下雨；改成 if it rains 就變成「下雨的話才帶」。"],"parse":{"en":"You can borrow my bike as long as you return it by Sunday.","zh":"只要你星期天前還我，腳踏車就借你。","parts":[["You","S"],["can borrow","V"],["my bike","O"],["as long as you return it by Sunday.","M","條件副詞子句"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[If]] it rains tomorrow, we'll see a movie instead.","zh":"如果明天下雨，我們就改去看電影。"},{"en":"You'll be late for school [[unless]] you leave now.","zh":"除非你現在出門，不然上學會遲到。"},{"en":"You can borrow my bike [[as long as]] you return it by Sunday.","zh":"只要你星期天前還我，腳踏車就借你。"},{"en":"Take a jacket [[in case]] it gets cold in the mountains.","zh":"帶件外套，以防山上變冷。"}],"practice":[{"q":"If it ______ sunny tomorrow, we'll have the class party outdoors.","options":["will be","is","was"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：條件副詞子句以現在式代替未來式。主要子句 we'll have 是未來，if 子句用現在式 is。(A) will be 不用在條件副詞子句；(C) was 是過去式，和 tomorrow 不合。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Take an umbrella ______ it rains this afternoon.","options":["in case","unless","so that"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：in case 表「以防萬一」。帶傘是為了防下午下雨，用 in case。(B) unless 表「除非」，變成「除非下雨，否則帶傘」，不合理；(C) so that 表目的，變成「為了讓天下雨」。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"目的與結果","text":["**so that / in order that** 表目的「以便」，子句常用 can、could、will、would。in order to V 詳見〈不定詞 to V〉。","**so…that / such…that** 表結果「如此…以致於」：so 後接形容詞或副詞；such 後接 (a/an) + (形容詞) + 名詞。"],"adv":["表多寡的 many、much、few、little 加名詞時用 so，不用 such：so many people that…。","正式寫法也有 so + 形容詞 + a/an + 單數名詞 + that：It was so hot a day that…，意思同 such a hot day。"],"formula":"so + adj./adv. + that ／ such + (a/an) + (adj.) + N + that","parse":{"en":"The bubble tea was so sweet that I couldn't finish it.","zh":"這杯珍奶甜到我喝不完。","parts":[["The bubble tea","S"],["was","V"],["so","M","程度"],["sweet","C","主詞補語"],["that I couldn't finish it.","M","結果子句"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I set two alarms [[so that]] I wouldn't miss the early train.","zh":"我設了兩個鬧鐘，以免錯過早班火車。"},{"en":"The bubble tea was [[so]] sweet [[that]] I couldn't finish it.","zh":"這杯珍奶甜到我喝不完。"},{"en":"It was [[such]] a hot day [[that]] we spent the afternoon at the mall.","zh":"那天熱到我們整個下午都待在購物中心。"},{"en":"There were [[so]] many people at the night market [[that]] we could hardly move.","zh":"夜市人多到我們幾乎寸步難行。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The test was ______ difficult that many students couldn't finish it.","options":["so","such","such a"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：so + 形容詞 + that 表結果。空格後是形容詞 difficult，後面沒有名詞，用 so。(B) such、(C) such a 後面都要接名詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"It was ______ great movie that I watched it twice.","options":["so","such","such a"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：such + a/an + 形容詞 + 單數可數名詞 + that。movie 是單數可數名詞，用 such a great movie。(A) so 後接形容詞或副詞，不說 so great movie；(B) such 後少了冠詞 a。故選 (C)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"I was tired, however I kept studying.","right":"I was tired[[; however,]] I kept studying.","why":"however 是副詞，兩句之間要用分號或句點，不能只用逗號。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Neither my brother nor I don't like spicy food.","right":"Neither my brother nor I [[like]] spicy food.","why":"neither…nor 本身已是否定，同一子句不再加 not。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Amy likes both singing and to dance.","right":"Amy likes both singing and [[dancing]].","why":"配對連接詞前後形式要對稱：V-ing 配 V-ing。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"I will call you when I will get home.","right":"I will call you when I [[get]] home.","why":"時間副詞子句以現在式代替未來式，不用 will。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"I went to bed until I finished my homework.","right":"I [[didn't go]] to bed until I finished my homework.","why":"「直到…才」要用 not…until，主要子句用否定。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Although it rained, but we still went to the night market.","right":"[[Although]] it rained, we still went to the night market.","why":"although 和 but 不能同時用，只能留一個。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Because of it was raining, we stayed home.","right":"[[Because]] it was raining, we stayed home.","why":"後面是子句（S + V），要用連接詞 because，不是 because of。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"Unless you don't hurry, you will be late.","right":"[[Unless you hurry]], you will be late.","why":"要表「如果不趕快」，unless 已含否定，不再加 not。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"It was so a hot day that we stayed home.","right":"It was [[such a hot day]] that we stayed home.","why":"不說 so a hot day；有「a + 形容詞 + 名詞」時用 such。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"There were such many people that we couldn't get in.","right":"There were [[so many]] people that we couldn't get in.","why":"表多寡的 many 加名詞時用 so，不用 such。"}],"tips":["選項同時有 because 與 because of、although 與 despite 時，看空格後接子句還是名詞。","綜合測驗先判斷前後句關係：相反選 but、although，因果選 so、because，條件選 if、unless。","句中已有 although 就不選 but；兩句之間只有逗號時，不選 however、therefore。"],"quiz":[{"q":"The baseball game was canceled ______ the heavy rain.","options":["because","because of","although","so"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：棒球賽因為大雨取消了。空格後是名詞 the heavy rain，要用介系詞 because of；because 後面要接子句。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"______ Ben was very tired, he still finished all his homework.","options":["Because","But","Although","So"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：雖然 Ben 很累，他還是把功課全寫完了。still 表前後相反，用 Although；but、so 是對等連接詞，要放在兩句中間。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"______ Leo nor his sister can swim.","options":["Either","Both","Not only","Neither"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Leo 和他妹妹都不會游泳。空格後有 nor，要和 Neither 配對；Either 配 or，Both 配 and，Not only 配 but also。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"You can't get into the concert ______ you have a ticket.","options":["unless","if","because","since"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：除非你有票，否則不能進演唱會。unless 約等於 if…not；用 if 會變成「有票就不能進場」，不合理。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The night market was really crowded; ______, we still had a great time.","options":["but","however","although","because"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：夜市非常擁擠，不過我們還是玩得很開心。分號後接副詞 however 再加逗號；but、although、because 是連接詞，不能這樣用。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Jenny wants a new phone. She is saving money from her part-time job ______ she can buy one.","options":["in order to","because of","so that","so as to"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Jenny 想要新手機，她正在存打工的錢，好買一支。空格後是子句 she can buy one，要用連接詞 so that；in order to、so as to 接原形動詞，because of 接名詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"______ his hard work, Kevin failed the math test again.","options":["Although","Because of","Even though","Despite"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：儘管 Kevin 很努力，數學考試還是又沒及格。his hard work 是名詞，用介系詞 Despite；Although、Even though 要接子句，Because of 意思不合。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"It was ______ hot weather that we stayed inside all day.","options":["such","so","such a","too"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：天氣熱到我們整天都待在室內。weather 不可數，用 such + 形容詞 + 名詞，不加 a；so hot weather、too hot weather 都不對。故選 (A)。"}]},{"id":"g-relative","unit":"clause","level":"B1","title":"關係代名詞","en":"Relative pronouns","lead":"先看先行詞是人還是事物，再看關代在子句中當主詞、受詞還是所有格。","goals":["能依先行詞和子句缺的成分選對關代","能分辨限定與非限定用法，知道何時不用 that","能使用介系詞 + whom/which 的句型"],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-pronoun","g-agree"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[2]","note":"one of the… who 後接複數動詞為傳統文法；母語者也常用單數，統測以複數為準待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"先行詞與關係子句","text":["**關係子句**放在名詞或代名詞（如 everything、those）後面修飾它，也叫形容詞子句；被修飾的字叫**先行詞**。關係代名詞（關代）引導子句，並在子句中代替先行詞。","先行詞是人用 who，事物或動物用 which，that 兩者皆可（有逗號或前有介系詞時不能用 that）。關代後面直接接動詞時，它是子句的**主詞**，不能省略。"],"adv":["先行詞是 those、anyone 等指人的代名詞時，常用 who：Those who finish early can go home.（those 是複數，動詞用複數）"],"formula":"人 + who/that + V…／事物 + which/that + V…","parse":{"en":"The bus that goes to my school is always crowded.","zh":"開往我們學校的公車總是很擠。","parts":[["The bus","S"],["that goes to my school","M","關係子句，修飾 bus"],["is","V"],["always","M","頻率副詞"],["crowded.","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I have a cousin [[who]] works part-time at a bubble tea shop.","zh":"我有個表姊在手搖飲店打工。"},{"en":"The bus [[that]] goes to my school is always crowded.","zh":"開往我們學校的公車總是很擠。"},{"en":"Mom bought a rice cooker [[which]] can also bake cakes.","zh":"媽媽買了一台還能烤蛋糕的電子鍋。"}],"practice":[{"q":"I have a classmate ______ can play the guitar really well.","options":["who","which","whose"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：先行詞是人，關代當主詞用 who。空格後直接接 can play，子句缺主詞，先行詞 classmate 是人，用 who。(B) which 用於事物；(C) whose 後面要接名詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The MRT line ______ goes to Tamsui is always busy on weekends.","options":["who","which","whom"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：先行詞是事物，主格關代用 which。先行詞 MRT line 是事物，空格後接動詞 goes，用 which。(A) who 只指人；(C) whom 指人，而且是受格。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"受格 whom 與所有格 whose","text":["關代在子句中當**受詞**時，人用 whom 或 who，事物用 which，兩者也都能用 that，還**可以省略**；但有逗號或前有介系詞時，不能用 that，也不能省略。","判斷：關代後面接 S + V，且子句缺受詞，就是受格。whose 表「…的」，後面一定接名詞，先行詞是人或事物都能用。"],"adv":["whom 較正式，口語多用 who 或直接省略；但介系詞後面只能用 whom，不用 who。"],"table":{"cols":["先行詞","主格","受格","所有格"],"rows":[["人","who / that","whom / who / that","whose + N"],["事物、動物","which / that","which / that","whose + N"]]},"parse":{"en":"The shoes I bought at the night market are already falling apart.","zh":"我在夜市買的鞋子已經快壞了。","parts":[["The shoes","S"],["I bought at the night market","M","關係子句，省略 that"],["are","V"],["already","M"],["falling apart.","V"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Ms. Lin is the teacher [[whom]] everyone in our class likes best.","zh":"林老師是我們班每個人最喜歡的老師。"},{"en":"The shoes [[(that)]] I bought at the night market are already falling apart.","zh":"我在夜市買的鞋子已經快壞了。"},{"en":"I have a friend [[whose]] parents run a beef noodle shop.","zh":"我有個朋友，他爸媽開牛肉麵店。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The bubble tea ______ I ordered was too sweet.","options":["who","whose","which"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：受格關代。空格後接 I ordered，ordered 缺受詞，先行詞 bubble tea 是事物，用 which。(A) who 指人；(B) whose 後面要接名詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I met a girl ______ brother plays on the school basketball team.","options":["who","whose","which","that"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：所有格 whose + 名詞。空格後接名詞 brother，表「那個女孩的兄弟」，用 whose。(A) who 和 (D) that 都不表所有格；(C) which 指事物，也不表所有格。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"動詞與先行詞一致","text":["主格關代後的動詞，單複數看**先行詞**：先行詞單數用單數動詞，複數用複數動詞。","one of the + 複數名詞 + who/that：先行詞是那個**複數名詞**，動詞用複數。"],"adv":["the only one of the + 複數名詞 + who/that：先行詞是 the only one，動詞用單數。"],"parse":{"en":"The boy who lives next door plays basketball every night.","zh":"住隔壁的男生每天晚上都在打籃球。","parts":[["The boy","S"],["who lives next door","M","關係子句，修飾 boy"],["plays","V"],["basketball","O"],["every night.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The [[boy]] who [[lives]] next door plays basketball every night.","zh":"住隔壁的男生每天晚上都在打籃球。"},{"en":"I like [[teachers]] who [[give]] us less homework.","zh":"我喜歡少出功課的老師。"},{"en":"Amy is one of the [[students]] who [[play]] in the school band.","zh":"Amy 是學校管樂隊的成員之一。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The students who ______ in the front row always ask questions.","options":["sit","sits","sitting"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：主格關代後的動詞看先行詞。who 的先行詞 students 是複數，動詞用 sit。(B) sits 是單數形；(C) sitting 不能單獨當動詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The teacher who ______ us English is from Canada.","options":["teach","teaches","teaching"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：主格關代後的動詞看先行詞。who 的先行詞 the teacher 是單數，現在式動詞用 teaches。(A) teach 少了 -es；(C) teaching 不能單獨當動詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"介系詞 + whom/which","text":["子句裡的介系詞可以移到關代前面，變成**介系詞 + whom/which**，語氣較正式。介系詞後面**不能用 that**，也不用 who。","介系詞留在子句尾時，可用 who、whom、which、that，也可以省略關代。","in which 表地點時可換成 where，詳見〈關係副詞與複合關係詞〉。"],"adv":["意思固定的片語動詞（如 look after 照顧、put up with 忍受），介系詞不前移：the kids she looks after。"],"formula":"先行詞 + 介系詞 + whom/which + S + V","table":{"cols":["寫法","說明"],"rows":[["the house [[in which]] he lives","介系詞在前，只能用 which"],["the house [[that]] he lives [[in]]","介系詞留子句尾，可用 that/which"],["the house he lives [[in]]","受格關代省略"],["the house [[where]] he lives","in which = where"]]},"parse":{"en":"The apartment in which my aunt lives is right next to a night market.","zh":"我阿姨住的公寓就在夜市旁邊。","parts":[["The apartment","S"],["in which my aunt lives","M","關係子句"],["is","V"],["right next to a night market.","C","地點補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"The classmate [[to whom]] I lent my notes never gave them back.","zh":"我借他筆記的那個同學，一直沒還我。"},{"en":"This is the song [[that]] I told you [[about]].","zh":"這就是我跟你說過的那首歌。"},{"en":"The apartment [[in which]] my aunt lives is right next to a night market.","zh":"我阿姨住的公寓就在夜市旁邊。"}],"practice":[{"q":"This is the classroom in ______ we have our club meetings.","options":["that","which","who"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：介系詞 + which。介系詞 in 移到關代前面，先行詞 classroom 是事物，用 which。(A) 介系詞後面不能用 that；(C) who 指人，也不放在介系詞後。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The man ______ I talked to at the station was very kind.","options":["which","whom","whose","to whom"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：介系詞留在子句尾。to 已經在子句尾，前面可用受格關代 whom（who、that 或省略也可，但不在選項中）。(A) which 不指人；(C) whose 後面要接名詞；(D) to whom 會讓 to 出現兩次。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"限定與非限定","text":["**限定用法**不加逗號，說明「是哪一個」；**非限定用法**加逗號，只是補充說明，先行詞通常已經很明確。","非限定用法的關代用 who、whom、which、whose，**不能用 that**，關代也不能省略。","逗號 + which 還可以指**前面整句話**，這時子句動詞用單數。"],"adv":["先行詞是專有名詞（Jiufen、Ms. Lin）或 my mom 這類只有一個的人事物時，通常用非限定，要加逗號。"],"table":{"cols":["句子","意思"],"rows":[["My sister [[who]] lives in Taichung is a nurse.","住台中的那個姊姊是護理師（姊姊不只一個）"],["My sister, [[who]] lives in Taichung, is a nurse.","我姊姊是護理師，她住台中（只有一個姊姊，補充說明）"]]},"parse":{"en":"Our P.E. teacher, who used to play pro baseball, is really strict.","zh":"我們體育老師以前是職棒選手，他超嚴格。","parts":[["Our P.E. teacher,","S"],["who used to play pro baseball,","M","非限定，補充說明"],["is","V"],["really strict.","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Our P.E. teacher, [[who]] used to play pro baseball, is really strict.","zh":"我們體育老師以前是職棒選手，他超嚴格。"},{"en":"We visited Jiufen, [[which]] was full of tourists that day.","zh":"我們去了九份，那天到處都是觀光客。"},{"en":"Leo always leaves his socks on the floor, [[which]] [[drives]] his mom crazy.","zh":"Leo 總是把襪子丟在地上，讓他媽媽很抓狂。"}],"practice":[{"q":"My best friend Amy, ______ lives in Kaohsiung, visits me every summer.","options":["that","who","which"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：非限定用法不能用 that。逗號後補充說明 Amy，先行詞是人，子句缺主詞，用 who。(A) that 不能放在逗號後；(C) which 用於事物。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"We went to Taipei 101, ______ was crowded with tourists.","options":["who","that","which"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：非限定用法的事物用 which。逗號後補充說明 Taipei 101，是事物，用 which。(A) who 只指人；(B) that 不能放在逗號後。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"要用 that 的情況","text":["**限定用法**中，先行詞是事物，且有**最高級**、序數、the only、all 修飾，或是 everything、nothing 等字時，一般用 that，不用 which。","限定用法中，先行詞同時有**人和物**時，who 和 which 都不適用，要用 that（當受詞時也可省略）。","有逗號的非限定用法不能用 that：即使先行詞有最高級或序數，事物仍用 which，人用 who。"],"adv":["先行詞只有人時，上述情況也常用 who，例如 the only person who、the first student who。"],"parse":{"en":"This is the best stinky tofu that I've ever had.","zh":"這是我吃過最好吃的臭豆腐。","parts":[["This","S"],["is","V"],["the best stinky tofu","C","主詞補語"],["that I've ever had.","M","關係子句，修飾 tofu"]]},"ex":[{"en":"This is the best stinky tofu [[that]] I've ever had.","zh":"這是我吃過最好吃的臭豆腐。"},{"en":"Thanks for everything [[that]] you've done for our class.","zh":"謝謝你為我們班做的一切。"},{"en":"These photos show the people and places [[that]] we saw in Tainan.","zh":"這些照片拍的是我們在台南遇到的人和去過的地方。"},{"en":"We went to the most famous shaved ice shop in Tainan, [[which]] was packed.","zh":"我們去了台南最有名的剉冰店，店裡擠滿了人。"}],"practice":[{"q":"This is the longest movie ______ I have ever watched.","options":["that","who","whose","what"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：先行詞有最高級時用 that。先行詞 the longest movie 是事物，又有最高級，限定用法用 that。(B) who 指人；(C) whose 後面要接名詞；(D) what 前面不能有先行詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"My brother bought the cheapest phone in the store, ______ broke after a week.","options":["that","which","who"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：有逗號的非限定用法用 which。先行詞有最高級 cheapest，但逗號後不能用 that；先行詞是事物，用 which。(A) that 不能放在逗號後；(C) who 指人。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"I have a friend which can speak Korean.","right":"I have a friend [[who]] can speak Korean.","why":"先行詞 friend 是人，要用 who 或 that，不能用 which。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"The girl sings in the choir is my classmate.","right":"The girl [[who sings]] in the choir is my classmate.","why":"主格關代不能省略：girl 後面要有 who，才能再接 sings。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"This is the phone which I bought it last week.","right":"This is the phone [[which I bought]] last week.","why":"which 已經當 bought 的受詞，後面不能再加 it。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"I have a classmate who his father is a chef.","right":"I have a classmate [[whose father]] is a chef.","why":"「同學的爸爸」要用 whose + 名詞，不能寫 who his。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"The students who lives in Keelung take the train to school.","right":"The students who [[live]] in Keelung take the train to school.","why":"先行詞 students 是複數，子句動詞用 live。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"The girl with that I went to the movies is my cousin.","right":"The girl [[with whom]] I went to the movies is my cousin.","why":"介系詞後面不能接 that，先行詞是人要用 whom。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"My mom, that is a nurse, often works night shifts.","right":"My mom, [[who]] is a nurse, often works night shifts.","why":"有逗號的非限定用法不能用 that，人要用 who。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"I loved the first song, that was really catchy.","right":"I loved the first song, [[which]] was really catchy.","why":"有逗號是非限定用法，即使有 first 也不能用 that，要用 which。"}],"tips":["先看先行詞是人或物，再看空格後：接動詞選主格，接 S + V 且缺受詞選受格，表「…的」選 whose。","空格前有逗號就不能選 that；逗號後的 which 可以指前面整句話。","空格前有介系詞，不選 that/who，人用 whom、物用 which；無逗號且先行詞有人又有物，選 that。"],"quiz":[{"q":"The girl ______ sits next to me in class is from Hualien.","options":["which","who","whose","whom"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：上課坐我旁邊的女生是花蓮人。先行詞 the girl 是人，空格後直接接動詞 sits，缺主詞，用主格 who；whom 是受格。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I lost the umbrella ______ my mom bought for me last week.","options":["who","whose","which","what"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我把媽媽上週買給我的傘弄丟了。先行詞 umbrella 是事物，bought 缺受詞，用 which；what 前面不能有先行詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"My neighbor has a dog ______ name is Lucky.","options":["who","which","that","whose"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我鄰居養了一隻叫 Lucky 的狗。空格後接名詞 name，表示「狗的名字」，用所有格 whose；先行詞是動物也能用 whose。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"My aunt has two cats that ______ on her bed every night.","options":["sleeps","sleep","sleeping","is sleeping"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我阿姨有兩隻貓，每天晚上都睡在她床上。that 的先行詞是 two cats，是複數，動詞用 sleep；sleeping 不能單獨當動詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"My grandmother, ______ is 85 years old, still goes jogging every morning.","options":["that","which","who","whom"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我奶奶 85 歲了，還是每天早上去慢跑。逗號後是非限定用法，不能用 that；先行詞是人，子句又缺主詞，用 who。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"The girl ______ Jason is talking is his cousin.","options":["to whom","to that","to which","whom"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：正在和 Jason 說話的女生是他表妹。talk to sb 的 to 移到關代前面時，人要用 whom，介系詞後不能接 that；只填 whom 會少了 to。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Kevin got a perfect score on the math test, ______ surprised everyone in our class.","options":["that","what","it","which"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Kevin 數學考滿分，讓全班都很驚訝。逗號 + which 可以指前面整句話；逗號後不能用 that，用 it 則兩個句子之間少了連接詞。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Grandpa often talks about the people and places ______ he remembers from his childhood.","options":["who","which","that","whose"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：爺爺常聊起童年記憶中的人和地方。先行詞 the people and places 同時有人和地方，限定用法中 who 和 which 都不適用，要用 that。故選 (C)。"}]},{"id":"g-relative-adv","unit":"clause","level":"B2","title":"關係副詞與複合關係詞","en":"Relative adverbs and what / -ever","lead":"關係副詞後面接完整句子；子句缺主詞或受詞，就改用關係代名詞。","goals":["能依子句是否完整，分辨 where/when 和 which","能分辨 what 與 that，寫出 what 子句","能用 -ever 字與 however + adj 造句"],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-relative"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[4].adv","note":"whenever 表「每當」時，有些句子也能換成 no matter when，可換與否的界線待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"where 與 when","text":["**關係副詞**引導形容詞子句修飾先行詞，並在子句中當副詞。先行詞是地方、且子句完整時用 **where**；是時間、且子句完整時用 when。","where 相當於 in/at which，when 相當於 in/on/at which。關係副詞已代替介系詞片語，所以後面接**完整句子**。","限定用法（前面沒有逗號）的 when 常可省略：the day (when) we met；逗號後的 when 不可省略。"],"adv":["逗號 + when/where 是**非限定用法**，補充說明先行詞，例如 in 2020, when I was ten。限定與非限定詳見〈關係代名詞〉。"],"formula":"地方 + where + S + V／時間 + when + S + V（子句完整）","parse":{"en":"This is the night market where my parents first met.","zh":"這就是我爸媽第一次相遇的夜市。","parts":[["This","S"],["is","V"],["the night market","C","主詞補語"],["where my parents first met.","M","關係子句，修飾先行詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"This is the night market [[where]] my parents first met.","zh":"這就是我爸媽第一次相遇的夜市。"},{"en":"Do you know a café [[where]] we can study after school?","zh":"你知道有什麼放學後可以去讀書的咖啡廳嗎？"},{"en":"Summer vacation is the time [[when]] I can finally sleep late.","zh":"暑假是我終於可以睡晚一點的時候。"}],"practice":[{"q":"The library is a quiet place ______ I can do my homework after school.","options":["when","where","what","who"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：先行詞是地方、子句完整，用 where。I can do my homework 不缺主詞或受詞，where = in which。(A) when 用於時間；(C) what 前面不能有先行詞；(D) who 指人。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Sunday is the only day ______ my dad doesn't have to work.","options":["where","who","when","what"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：先行詞是時間、子句完整，用 when。my dad doesn't have to work 不缺主詞或受詞，when = on which。(A) where 用於地方；(B) who 指人；(D) what 前面不能有先行詞。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"why 與 how","text":["**why** 的先行詞是 the reason，why 常可省略：the reason (why) Jason quit his job。","**how** 表示方法，但 the way 和 how 不能並用，二者擇一：the way he talks 或 how he talks。","This is why…（這就是為什麼…）、That's how…（就是這樣…）省略了先行詞，很常見。"],"adv":["the reason why 也可說 the reason that／for which；the way 也可說 the way that／in which。"],"formula":"the reason (why) + S + V／the way + S + V = how + S + V","parse":{"en":"I love the way my grandma makes braised pork rice.","zh":"我超愛阿嬤滷肉飯的做法。","parts":[["I","S"],["love","V"],["the way","O"],["my grandma makes braised pork rice.","M","關係子句，修飾先行詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"That's the reason [[why]] Jason quit his job at the convenience store.","zh":"這就是 Jason 辭掉便利商店工作的原因。"},{"en":"I love [[the way]] my grandma makes braised pork rice.","zh":"我超愛阿嬤滷肉飯的做法。"},{"en":"This is [[how]] I saved money for my trip to Japan.","zh":"我就是這樣存到去日本玩的錢。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Nobody knows the reason ______ Tina was late for class today.","options":["why","how","where","what"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：先行詞是 reason，用關係副詞 why。Tina was late 子句完整，the reason why = the reason for which。(B) how 表方法；(C) where 用於地方；(D) what 前面不能有先行詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Can you show me ______ you edited this video?","options":["the way how","what","how","the way which"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：表方法用 how 或 the way，二者不能並用。(A) the way how 並用了；(B) what 後面的子句要缺主詞或受詞，但 you edited this video 已完整；(D) the way which 要寫成 the way in which。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"where 還是 which？","text":["判斷關鍵是子句**缺不缺主詞或受詞**，不是先行詞是不是地方。子句完整用 where/when；缺主詞或受詞，用 **which/that**。","先看動詞：visit、love 是及物動詞，後面要受詞；live、grow up 不及物，子句已完整。","which/that 的其他用法詳見〈關係代名詞〉。"],"adv":["動詞後有介系詞時，看介系詞後缺不缺受詞：the house which I live in（in 缺受詞）= the house where I live。"],"table":{"cols":["例子","判斷"],"rows":[["the city [[which]] I visited","visited 缺受詞 → which"],["the city [[where]] I live","I live 已完整 → where"],["the town [[which]] is famous for its tea","缺主詞 → which"],["the house [[which]] I live in","in 後缺受詞 → which"],["the day [[which]] we spent in Kenting","spent 缺受詞 → which"],["the day [[when]] we arrived in Kenting","we arrived 已完整 → when"]]},"parse":{"en":"Tainan is the city which I most want to visit.","zh":"台南是我最想去的城市。","parts":[["Tainan","S"],["is","V"],["the city","C","主詞補語"],["which I most want to visit.","M","關係子句，修飾先行詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Tainan is the city [[which]] I most want to visit.","zh":"台南是我最想去的城市。"},{"en":"Tainan is the city [[where]] my grandparents live.","zh":"台南是我爺爺奶奶住的城市。"},{"en":"Is this the café [[which]] you told me about?","zh":"這就是你跟我說過的那間咖啡廳嗎？"}],"practice":[{"q":"This is the bakery ______ sells the best pineapple cakes in town.","options":["where","which","when"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：子句缺主詞，用關係代名詞 which。sells 前面沒有主詞，要由 which 來當主詞。(A) where、(C) when 是關係副詞，後面要接完整句子。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The park ______ we play basketball after school is near the MRT station.","options":["where","which","what"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：子句完整，用 where。play 已有受詞 basketball，子句不缺主詞或受詞，where = in which。(B) which 後面的子句要缺主詞或受詞；(C) what 前面不能有先行詞。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"複合關係代名詞 what","text":["**what** = the thing(s) that，本身已含先行詞，前面**不能再有先行詞**。what 在子句中通常當主詞或受詞，整個子句可當主詞、受詞或補語。","有先行詞用 that/which，沒有先行詞才用 what。","先行詞是 all、everything 時用 that：all that I have、everything that he said。"],"adv":["what 子句當主詞，動詞通常用單數：What he said is true. 詳見〈主詞與動詞一致〉。"],"formula":"what (+ S) + V = the thing(s) that (+ S) + V","parse":{"en":"What my mom cooks is always delicious.","zh":"我媽煮的東西總是很好吃。","parts":[["What my mom cooks","S","名詞子句當主詞"],["is","V"],["always","M","頻率"],["delicious.","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[What]] Ming told me about the quiz turned out to be true.","zh":"阿明跟我說的小考消息，後來證實是真的。"},{"en":"This is exactly [[what]] I wanted for my birthday!","zh":"這正是我想要的生日禮物！"},{"en":"Don't believe [[everything that]] you see online.","zh":"網路上看到的東西別全信。"}],"practice":[{"q":"This backpack is just ______ I was looking for.","options":["that","what","which","where"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：what = the thing that，前面不能有先行詞。for 後面缺受詞，空格前又沒有先行詞，用 what。(A) that、(C) which 當關代時前面要有先行詞；(D) where 後面要接完整句子。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"You can take everything ______ is on the table.","options":["what","that","where"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：先行詞是 everything 時用 that。is 前面缺主詞，空格前有先行詞 everything，用 that。(A) what 前面不能有先行詞；(C) where 後面要接完整句子。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"-ever 複合關係詞","text":["**whoever、whatever** 等已含先行詞，前面不能再有先行詞：whoever = anyone who，whatever = anything that。","-ever 字引導**讓步**副詞子句（無論…）時，可換成 **no matter** + 疑問詞：Whatever you do = No matter what you do。","當名詞子句，或表「任何…的地方」（Sit wherever you like.）時，只能用 -ever 字。"],"adv":["whenever 表「每當、任何時候」時，一般也不換成 no matter：Call me whenever you need help."],"table":{"cols":["複合關係詞","意思","例子"],"rows":[["whoever","任何…的人；無論誰","[[Whoever]] wins gets a free drink."],["whatever","任何…的事物；無論什麼","Order [[whatever]] you like."],["whichever","（有範圍）任何一個；無論哪個","Take [[whichever]] seat you want."],["whenever","每當；無論何時","Call me [[whenever]] you need help."],["wherever","任何地方；無論哪裡","Sit [[wherever]] you like."],["however","無論多麼；無論用什麼方式","[[However hard]] it is, don't give up."]]},"parse":{"en":"Whoever finishes the quiz first can leave early.","zh":"最先寫完小考的人可以先走。","parts":[["Whoever finishes the quiz first","S","名詞子句當主詞"],["can leave","V"],["early.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Whoever]] finishes the quiz first can leave early.","zh":"最先寫完小考的人可以先走。"},{"en":"[[Whatever]] happens tomorrow, I'll be at your game.","zh":"明天不管發生什麼事，我都會去看你比賽。"},{"en":"[[Wherever]] you go in Taiwan, you can find a convenience store.","zh":"在台灣不管走到哪裡，都找得到便利商店。"}],"practice":[{"q":"You can eat ______ you like from the fridge.","options":["whoever","whatever","no matter what","wherever"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：whatever = anything that，可引導當受詞的名詞子句。eat 後要受詞，like 後也缺受詞，指事物用 whatever。(A) whoever 指人；(C) no matter what 只引導副詞子句；(D) wherever 指地方。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The seats aren't numbered, so you can sit ______ you want.","options":["wherever","no matter where","whatever","whoever"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：wherever 表「任何…的地方」。這裡是「坐任何你想坐的地方」，不是「無論」，只能用 wherever。(B) no matter where 只用於讓步；(C) whatever 指事物；(D) whoever 指人。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"however + 形容詞","text":["however 表「無論多麼」時，形容詞或副詞要緊跟在後：**However + adj/adv + S + V**，等於 No matter how + adj/adv。","不能寫成 However he is tired。句首 However 後直接加逗號（However, …）是轉折副詞「然而」，用法詳見〈連接詞〉。"],"formula":"However + adj/adv + S + V, S + V","parse":{"en":"However tired Ben is, he always helps at his family's noodle stand.","zh":"Ben 不管多累，總是會去家裡的麵攤幫忙。","parts":[["However tired Ben is,","M","讓步子句"],["he","S"],["always","M","頻率"],["helps","V"],["at his family's noodle stand.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[However tired]] Ben is, he always helps at his family's noodle stand.","zh":"Ben 不管多累，總是會去家裡的麵攤幫忙。"},{"en":"[[However hard]] I try, I can't wake up before seven.","zh":"不管我多努力，就是沒辦法七點前起床。"},{"en":"[[No matter how busy]] she is, Lisa calls her mom every night.","zh":"不管多忙，Lisa 每天晚上都會打電話給媽媽。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ busy she is, Mia always eats breakfast with her family.","options":["However","Whatever","Whenever"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：However + adj + S + V 表「無論多麼」。空格後緊接形容詞 busy，只能用 However。(B) Whatever 後面不接形容詞；(C) Whenever 表時間，後面要直接接 S + V。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"However ______, Leo never takes a taxi to school.","options":["he is tired","tired he is","he tired is"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：表「無論多麼」時，形容詞要緊跟在 however 後面，語序是 However + tired + he is。(A) 把形容詞放到句尾；(C) he tired is 語序錯誤。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"This is the apartment where I lived in when I was a kid.","right":"This is the apartment [[where]] I lived when I was a kid.","why":"where 已等於 in which，後面不可再加 in。","sec":0},{"wrong":"I don't like the way how he talks to his mom.","right":"I don't like [[the way]] he talks to his mom.","why":"the way 和 how 不能並用，二者擇一。","sec":1},{"wrong":"Kenting is the place where we visited last summer.","right":"Kenting is the place [[which]] we visited last summer.","why":"visit 是及物動詞，子句缺受詞，要用 which/that，不能用 where。","sec":2},{"wrong":"Yilan is a county where is famous for its hot springs.","right":"Yilan is a county [[which]] is famous for its hot springs.","why":"子句缺主詞，要用關係代名詞 which/that 當主詞。","sec":2},{"wrong":"Everything what the coach said was right.","right":"Everything [[that]] the coach said was right.","why":"有先行詞 everything 時用 that，what 前面不能有先行詞。","sec":3},{"wrong":"No matter who wants the extra ticket can have it.","right":"[[Whoever]] wants the extra ticket can have it.","why":"當主詞的名詞子句只能用 whoever，no matter who 只引導副詞子句。","sec":4},{"wrong":"You can sit no matter where you like.","right":"You can sit [[wherever]] you like.","why":"這裡是「任何…的地方」，不是「無論」，只能用 wherever。","sec":4},{"wrong":"However he is tired, he always walks his dog.","right":"[[However tired]] he is, he always walks his dog.","why":"「無論多麼」要把形容詞緊放在 however 後面。","sec":5}],"tips":["選擇題 where/which 二選一：讀空格後的子句，缺主詞或受詞選 which，完整選 where/when。","空格前沒有先行詞、子句缺主詞或受詞：指事物選 what，指「任何…的人」選 whoever；有先行詞就不能選 what。","中譯英「無論多…」寫 However + adj + S + V；當主詞的「任何…的人」用 Whoever。"],"quiz":[{"q":"My grandparents still live in the small town ______ my dad grew up.","options":["which","where","when","who"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我爺爺奶奶還住在我爸長大的那個小鎮。grow up 是不及物動詞，子句不缺受詞，先行詞又是地方，用 where（= in which）。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I still remember the day ______ I rode the MRT by myself for the first time.","options":["where","which","why","when"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我還記得第一次自己搭捷運的那天。子句 I rode the MRT 已完整，先行詞是時間，用 when（= on which）。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"That's the reason ______ Amy moved to Taichung last year.","options":["why","which","where","what"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：那就是 Amy 去年搬到台中的原因。先行詞是 reason，子句完整，用關係副詞 why（= for which）。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"______ the coach said after the game made everyone feel better.","options":["That","Which","What","Where"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：教練賽後說的話讓大家心情好多了。空格前沒有先行詞，said 又缺受詞，用 what（= the thing that）；名詞子句的 that 和關係副詞 where 後面都要接完整句子，which 前面則要有先行詞。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"I really like ______ my aunt decorates her coffee shop.","options":["the way how","the way which","the way what","the way"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我很喜歡阿姨布置咖啡店的方式。the way 和 how 不能並用；the way which 要寫成 the way in which，what 前面不能有先行詞。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"______ breaks the class rules will have to clean the classroom.","options":["No matter who","Whoever","Whatever","Anyone"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：違反班規的人都要打掃教室。空格引導當主詞的名詞子句，指人用 whoever（= anyone who）；no matter who 只能引導副詞子句；Anyone 後面要加 who。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"______ the math problems are, Kevin never gives up.","options":["However difficult","Whatever difficult","How difficult","However difficulty"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：不管數學題目多難，Kevin 都不會放棄。「無論多麼」用 however + 形容詞 + S + V，形容詞 difficult 要緊跟在 however 後面；How 沒有「無論」之意，difficulty 是名詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"I'll never forget the summer ______ I spent with my grandparents in Hualien.","options":["when","where","which","what"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我永遠忘不了和爺爺奶奶在花蓮度過的那個夏天。spent 後面缺受詞，要用關係代名詞 which，不能因為先行詞是時間就選 when。故選 (C)。"}]},{"id":"g-noun-clause","unit":"clause","level":"B1","title":"名詞子句與間接問句","en":"Noun clauses and indirect questions","lead":"名詞子句把整個句子當名詞用；間接問句用直述句語序：疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞。","goals":["能用 that 子句當主詞、受詞、補語和同位語","能依子句的位置選用 whether 或 if","能寫出語序正確的間接問句和 do you think 問句"],"prereq":["g-sentence","g-question"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[0]","note":"形容詞後的 that 子句（I'm sure that…），教材有形容詞受詞、補語或原因子句等說法，統測用語待確認。"},{"where":"sections[3]","note":"be 動詞後的補語用 if（The question is if…）口語偶見，表中寫「不宜」；統測是否一律判錯待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"that 子句接在動詞、形容詞後","text":["**名詞子句**就是當名詞用的子句。最常見的是「that + 完整句子」，放在 think、know、hope、say 等動詞後當**受詞**。","當受詞時 **that 常省略**，口語尤其如此：I think (that) he's right.","sure、glad、afraid 等形容詞後也常接 that 子句（I'm sure that…），that 一樣可省略。這時 that 子句說明形容詞，不算動詞的受詞。"],"formula":"S + V + (that) + S + V …","parse":{"en":"My coach says that practice is canceled today.","zh":"教練說今天的練習取消了。","parts":[["My coach","S"],["says","V"],["that practice is canceled today.","O","名詞子句當受詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My coach says [[that]] practice is canceled today.","zh":"教練說今天的練習取消了。"},{"en":"I think [[the MRT is faster than the bus]].","zh":"我覺得捷運比公車快。"},{"en":"I'm sure [[that]] Ben will do well in the speech contest.","zh":"我相信 Ben 在演講比賽會表現得很好。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Amy says ______ she will join the dance club this year.","options":["what","that","which"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：that 子句當動詞的受詞。空格後 she will join the dance club 是完整句子，當 says 的受詞，用 that 引導。(A) what 要在子句裡當主詞或受詞，但子句不缺；(C) which 是關代，前面要有先行詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I'm sure ______ you will love the beef noodles at this shop.","options":["about","what","that"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：形容詞 sure 後接 that 子句。you will love… 是完整句子，說明確定的內容，用 that（也可省略）。(A) 介系詞 about 後面不能接完整句子；(B) what 要在子句裡當主詞或受詞，但子句不缺。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"當主詞與補語","text":["that 子句當**主詞**時 that 不能省略，動詞用單數。主詞太長不好讀，通常用**虛主詞 It** 放句首，把 that 子句移到句尾。","放在 be 動詞後當**補語**也可以：The problem is that…，書面上 that 通常保留。"],"adv":["別和強調句 It was Tom that broke the window. 混淆，詳見〈強調句與常用句型〉。"],"formula":"That + S + V + V … → It + V …（如 is + adj./N）+ that + S + V …","parse":{"en":"It is true that Kevin got a part-time job at a bakery.","zh":"Kevin 真的在麵包店找到打工了。","parts":[["It","S","虛主詞"],["is","V"],["true","C","主詞補語"],["that Kevin got a part-time job at a bakery.","S","名詞子句當真主詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[That]] Lisa moved to Kaohsiung surprised the whole class.","zh":"Lisa 搬去高雄，讓全班都很驚訝。"},{"en":"[[It]] is true [[that]] Kevin got a part-time job at a bakery.","zh":"Kevin 真的在麵包店找到打工了。"},{"en":"[[It's]] a pity [[that]] you can't come to my birthday party.","zh":"你不能來我的生日派對，真可惜。"},{"en":"The problem is [[that]] we missed the last train home.","zh":"問題是我們錯過了回家的末班車。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ Ken won first prize in the speech contest surprised everyone.","options":["That","It","What"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：that 子句當主詞，that 不能省略。Ken won first prize… 是完整句子，整個子句當 surprised 的主詞，要用 That 引導。(B) It 當虛主詞時，that 子句要移到句尾；(C) What 要在子句裡當主詞或受詞，但子句不缺。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"The problem is ______ the bus is always late in the morning.","options":["what","that","which"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：that 子句當補語。the bus is always late… 是完整句子，放在 is 後說明 problem 的內容，用 that。(A) what 要在子句裡當主詞或受詞，但子句不缺；(C) which 是關代，前面要有先行詞。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"同位語：the fact that","text":["that 子句放在 fact、news、idea、rumor 等名詞後，說明名詞的內容，叫**同位語**。這個 that 通常不省略。","同位語 that 後面是**完整句子**；關係代名詞 that 則在子句裡當主詞或受詞，詳見〈關係代名詞〉。"],"formula":"the fact / news / idea + that + S + V …","parse":{"en":"The fact that Leo skipped class made his mom really angry.","zh":"Leo 翹課這件事讓他媽媽非常生氣。","parts":[["The fact that Leo skipped class","S","fact + 同位語子句"],["made","V"],["his mom","O"],["really angry.","C","受詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[The fact that]] Leo skipped class made his mom really angry.","zh":"Leo 翹課這件事讓他媽媽非常生氣。"},{"en":"Everyone cheered at [[the news that]] classes were canceled because of the typhoon.","zh":"聽到颱風停課的消息，大家都歡呼起來。"},{"en":"[[The rumor that]] our homeroom teacher is getting married spread quickly.","zh":"班導要結婚的傳言很快就傳開了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Mom loves the idea ______ we cook dinner together every Sunday.","options":["that","which","what"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：同位語 that 子句。we cook dinner together… 是完整句子，說明 idea 的內容，用 that。(B) which 是關代，要在子句裡當主詞或受詞，但子句不缺；(C) what 不能用來說明前面名詞的內容。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"whether / if：是否","text":["Yes/No 問句變成名詞子句時，用 **whether** 或 **if** 連接，意思是「是否」，後面接直述句語序。","當動詞受詞或放形容詞後兩者皆可；**放句首當主詞**、放介系詞後、接 to V 或緊接 or not，只能用 **whether**；be 動詞後當補語也用 whether。","表「是否」的 if 子句是名詞子句，未來的事要用 will：I don't know if it will rain tomorrow."],"adv":["用虛主詞 It 把子句移到句尾時，if 也可以：It doesn't matter if/whether we win or lose.","if 和 or not 拆開可以：I don't know if he'll come or not."],"table":{"cols":["位置","例句","whether","if"],"rows":[["動詞後當受詞","I wonder [[whether/if]] he's home.","可","可"],["句首當主詞","[[Whether]] he comes is up to him.","可","不可"],["介系詞後","It depends on [[whether]] it rains.","可","不可"],["緊接 or not","Tell me [[whether or not]] you agree.","可","不可"],["be 動詞後當補語","The question is [[whether]] it's safe.","可","不宜"],["接 to V","I can't decide [[whether to]] go.","可","不可"]]},"parse":{"en":"Nobody knows if the typhoon will hit Taiwan this weekend.","zh":"沒人知道颱風這週末會不會侵襲台灣。","parts":[["Nobody","S"],["knows","V"],["if the typhoon will hit Taiwan this weekend.","O","是否，名詞子句當受詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I'm not sure [[if]] the library is open on Sundays.","zh":"我不確定圖書館星期天有沒有開。"},{"en":"[[Whether]] we go to Kenting depends on the weather.","zh":"我們去不去墾丁要看天氣。"},{"en":"Mom asked me [[whether or not]] I had finished my homework.","zh":"媽媽問我功課寫完了沒。"},{"en":"Nobody knows [[if]] the typhoon [[will hit]] Taiwan this weekend.","zh":"沒人知道颱風這週末會不會侵襲台灣。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Ask Amy ______ she wants to join us for hot pot tonight.","options":["what","if","that"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：if 表「是否」，引導名詞子句。要問 Amy 要不要一起吃火鍋，是 Yes/No 的內容，用 if（也可用 whether）。(A) what 要在子句裡當主詞或受詞，但子句不缺；(C) that 不能接在 ask 後表「是否」。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I can't decide ______ to buy the red sneakers or the white ones.","options":["if","that","whether"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：「是否」接 to V 只能用 whether。空格後是 to buy…or…，表「要買紅的還是白的」，用 whether。(A) if 不能直接接 to V；(B) that 後面要接完整句子，也沒有「是否」的意思。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"間接問句的語序","text":["wh- 問句放進另一句（Do you know…? I wonder…）就成了**間接問句**，語序改成**疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞**，do/does/did 不放在主詞前。","疑問詞本身是主詞時，語序不變：Who took my pen? → I don't know who took my pen.","wh- 子句也能當主詞，動詞通常用單數。what 表「所…的事物」（What he said is true.），詳見〈關係副詞與複合關係詞〉。"],"adv":["否定句照樣用 don't/doesn't/didn't，只是放在主詞後：Why didn't he come? → I don't know why he didn't come.","Who is that girl? 的主詞是 that girl，who 是補語，所以要寫成 Do you know who that girl is?"],"formula":"Do you know / I wonder + 疑問詞 + S + V …","table":{"cols":["直接問句","間接問句"],"rows":[["[[Where does he live]]?","Do you know [[where he lives]]?"],["[[What time is it]]?","Can you tell me [[what time it is]]?"],["[[Why was she]] late?","I wonder [[why she was]] late."],["[[How much did it cost]]?","I forgot [[how much it cost]]."],["[[Who took]] my pen?","I don't know [[who took]] my pen."],["[[Is he]] home?","I'm not sure [[if he is]] home."]]},"parse":{"en":"Do you know where the nearest MRT station is?","zh":"你知道最近的捷運站在哪裡嗎？","parts":[["Do","V","助動詞"],["you","S"],["know","V"],["where the nearest MRT station is?","O","間接問句當受詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Do you know [[where the nearest MRT station is]]?","zh":"你知道最近的捷運站在哪裡嗎？"},{"en":"Can you tell me [[what time]] the night market [[opens]]?","zh":"可以告訴我夜市幾點開嗎？"},{"en":"I can't remember [[how much]] I [[paid]] for these sneakers.","zh":"我不記得這雙球鞋花了多少錢。"},{"en":"[[Why Jenny quit the volleyball team]] is still a mystery.","zh":"Jenny 為什麼退出排球隊，到現在還是個謎。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Excuse me. Can you tell me where ______?","options":["is the train station","the train station is","the train station"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：間接問句用直述句語序。where 後面要接「主詞 + 動詞」，be 動詞 is 放在主詞 the train station 後面。(A) 仍是疑問句語序；(C) 少了動詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I wonder what time ______.","options":["the movie starts","does the movie start","the movie start"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：間接問句裡 do/does 不放在主詞前。What time does the movie start? 放進 I wonder 後，去掉 does，動詞改成 starts。(B) 仍是疑問句語序；(C) 主詞是第三人稱單數，start 要加 -s。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"think 的問句與否定轉移","text":["問「你認為誰／什麼…？」時，疑問詞**移到句首**，接 do you think + S + V：What do you think he wants? believe 也一樣。","這類問句要回答內容，不能只答 Yes/No。疑問詞是主詞時直接接動詞：Who do you think will win?","**否定轉移**：「我想他不會來」習慣說 I don't think he'll come，把否定放在 think、believe、suppose 上。"],"adv":["hope 不做否定轉移：「我希望不會下雨」是 I hope it won't rain，不說 I don't hope it will rain。","I think he won't come. 文法沒有錯，只是不如 I don't think he'll come. 常用。"],"formula":"疑問詞 + do you think + (S) + V …?","parse":{"en":"I do not think the bubble tea shop is open this late.","zh":"我想那家手搖飲店這麼晚應該沒開了。","parts":[["I","S"],["do","V","助動詞"],["not","M","否定（否定轉移）"],["think","V"],["the bubble tea shop is open this late.","O","名詞子句當受詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[What do you think]] Dad wants for Father's Day?","zh":"你覺得爸爸父親節想要什麼？"},{"en":"[[Who]] do you think [[will win]] the basketball game tonight?","zh":"你覺得今晚的籃球賽誰會贏？"},{"en":"I [[don't think]] the bubble tea shop is open this late.","zh":"我想那家手搖飲店這麼晚應該沒開了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"A: ______ is the best singer in our class? B: Amy, for sure!","options":["Do you think who","Who do you think","Who you think"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：疑問詞 + do you think 的問句。問「你認為是誰」，疑問詞 who 放句首，再接 do you think；who 在子句中當主詞，直接接 is。(A) 疑問詞沒有移到句首；(C) 少了助動詞 do。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"I think is a great movie.","right":"I think [[it is]] a great movie.","why":"that 子句要是完整句子，不能少了主詞。","sec":0},{"wrong":"Lisa moved to Kaohsiung surprised everyone.","right":"[[That]] Lisa moved to Kaohsiung surprised everyone.","why":"that 子句放句首當主詞時，that 不能省略。","sec":1},{"wrong":"Is too bad that the concert was canceled.","right":"[[It's]] too bad that the concert was canceled.","why":"that 子句移到句尾時，句首要補虛主詞 It。","sec":1},{"wrong":"The news which our team won the game made everyone happy.","right":"The news [[that]] our team won the game made everyone happy.","why":"說明 news 內容的同位語子句用 that，不用 which。","sec":2},{"wrong":"I'm not sure if or not he will come.","right":"I'm not sure [[whether or not]] he will come.","why":"後面緊接 or not 時只能用 whether。","sec":3},{"wrong":"If we win or lose doesn't matter.","right":"[[Whether]] we win or lose doesn't matter.","why":"名詞子句放句首當主詞，要用 whether，不能用 if。","sec":3},{"wrong":"Do you know where does Amy live?","right":"Do you know where [[Amy lives]]?","why":"間接問句用「疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞」，主詞前不放 does，動詞加 -s。","sec":4},{"wrong":"Can you tell me where is the restroom?","right":"Can you tell me where [[the restroom is]]?","why":"間接問句裡 be 動詞要放在主詞後面。","sec":4},{"wrong":"Do you think what she wants for her birthday?","right":"[[What do you think]] she wants for her birthday?","why":"問「你認為…」時，疑問詞要移到句首。","sec":5},{"wrong":"I don't hope it will rain on our class trip.","right":"I [[hope]] it [[won't rain]] on our class trip.","why":"hope 不做否定轉移，否定要放在 that 子句裡。","sec":5}],"tips":["間接問句用「疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞」，疑問詞當主詞就直接接動詞；主詞前有 do/does/did 的選項先刪。","表「是否」的子句放句首當主詞、放介系詞後或緊接 or not 時，選 whether，排除 if。","句子重組看到 do you think，疑問詞放最前面；中譯英「我認為他不會…」寫成 I don't think…。"],"quiz":[{"q":"A: Do you know where ______? B: Sure. He lives near Ximen.","options":["does Kevin live","Kevin living","Kevin lives","lives Kevin"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：你知道 Kevin 住哪裡嗎？知道，他住西門附近。間接問句用「疑問詞 + 主詞 + 動詞」，主詞前不放 does。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"A: Does Amy want to see a movie with us? B: I don't know. I'll ask her ______ she is free tonight.","options":["what","if","which","that"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：Amy 想跟我們去看電影嗎？不知道，我會問她今晚有沒有空。問對方「是否」有空，用 if 或 whether 引導名詞子句。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"______ is true that Mr. Chen is leaving our school next year.","options":["This","What","That","It"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：陳老師明年真的要離開我們學校。that 子句當主詞太長，用虛主詞 It 放句首，形成 It is + adj. + that…；This、That 不能當虛主詞，That is true that… 不成立。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"______ we can go to the night market tonight depends on how much homework we have.","options":["If","That","Whether","What"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：我們今晚能不能去夜市，要看功課有多少。表「是否」的名詞子句放句首當主詞，只能用 whether，不能用 if；that 子句表事實，不合「要看…」。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"A: ______ we should give Grandma for her birthday? B: How about a warm scarf?","options":["What do you think","Do you think what","What you think","Do you think that"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：你覺得我們該送奶奶什麼生日禮物？送一條保暖的圍巾如何？問「你認為…什麼」，疑問詞放句首，接 do you think + 主詞 + 動詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Everyone at school was surprised by the news ______ Coach Lin was moving to Japan.","options":["which","that","what","whether"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：林教練要搬去日本的消息讓全校都很驚訝。that 子句說明 news 的內容，是同位語；後面是完整句子，不能用 which 或 what。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"A: Is Jason coming to the party tonight? B: I ______ he will. He has to work at the convenience store.","options":["don't think","think not","think","not think"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：Jason 今晚會來派對嗎？我想他不會來，他得在超商打工。英文習慣把否定放在 think 上（否定轉移）；(B)(D) 否定的位置不對，(C) 和「得打工」矛盾。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"A: Do you know ______? B: Yes. It's a birthday gift for Amy.","options":["what in the box is","what is it in the box","what does the box have","what is in the box"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：你知道盒子裡裝什麼嗎？知道，是送 Amy 的生日禮物。what 本身是主詞，後面直接接動詞 is，語序不變；(A) 誤把 is 移到句尾。故選 (D)。"}]},{"id":"g-conditional","unit":"special","level":"B2","title":"條件句與假設語氣","en":"Conditionals and the subjunctive","lead":"與事實相反時，if 子句往過去退一格：現在用過去式，過去用 had p.p.。","goals":["能分辨真實條件和與事實相反的假設","能依時間配對 if 子句與主要子句的動詞","能運用 wish、as if 與省略 if 的倒裝"],"prereq":["g-past","g-perfect","g-future"],"pending":[],"sections":[{"h":"真實條件：if + 現在式","text":["**真實條件**指有可能發生的事。表條件的 if 子句即使講未來，也用**現在式**代替未來式；主要子句常用 will、can、may + 原形。","if 作「是否」時是名詞子句，講未來仍用 will：I wonder if it will rain. 詳見〈名詞子句與間接問句〉。"],"adv":["講事實或習慣時，兩邊都用現在式：If you heat ice, it melts. 時間子句（when、as soon as 等）講未來也用現在式，詳見〈未來式〉。"],"formula":"If + S + 現在式, S + will/can/may + 原形","parse":{"en":"If you hurry, you can catch the last MRT train.","zh":"動作快一點的話，你還趕得上末班捷運。","parts":[["If you hurry,","M","條件子句"],["you","S"],["can catch","V"],["the last MRT train.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"If it [[rains]] tomorrow, we [[will stay]] home and watch movies.","zh":"如果明天下雨，我們就待在家看電影。"},{"en":"If you [[hurry]], you [[can catch]] the last MRT train.","zh":"動作快一點的話，你還趕得上末班捷運。"},{"en":"If Kai [[doesn't finish]] his homework, his mom [[won't let]] him play games.","zh":"Kai 如果沒寫完功課，他媽媽就不讓他打電動。"}],"practice":[{"q":"If Ruby ______ her homework tonight, she can go to the night market with us.","options":["finishes","will finish","finished","finish"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：表條件的 if 子句以現在式代替未來式。主詞 Ruby 是第三人稱單數，用 finishes。(B) will finish 不用在條件子句；(C) finished 是過去式，若表假設，主要子句要用 could，不用 can；(D) finish 少了 -es。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"I wonder if it ______ tomorrow. We want to go hiking.","options":["rains","will rain","rained"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：if 作「是否」時是名詞子句，講未來仍用 will。這裡 if 子句是 wonder 的受詞，又有 tomorrow，用 will rain。(A) rains 是表條件 if 子句的用法；(C) rained 是過去式，與 tomorrow 不合。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"與現在事實相反","text":["假設和**現在事實相反**的情況時，if 子句用**過去式**，主要子句用 would、could、might + 原形。動詞雖是過去式，講的卻是現在或不太可能的未來。","這種 if 子句的 be 動詞不分人稱，一律用 **were**：If I were you…。口語常聽到 was，考試請用 were。"],"formula":"If + S + 過去式 (be → were), S + would/could/might + 原形","parse":{"en":"If I had a scooter, I would ride it to school.","zh":"要是我有機車，我就會騎車上學。","parts":[["If I had a scooter,","M","條件子句"],["I","S"],["would ride","V"],["it","O"],["to school.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"If I [[were]] you, I [[would apologize]] to Grace first.","zh":"如果我是你，我會先向 Grace 道歉。"},{"en":"If I [[had]] a scooter, I [[wouldn't have to]] take the bus to school.","zh":"要是我有機車，就不用搭公車上學了。"},{"en":"If our school [[were]] closer to home, I [[could sleep]] later every morning.","zh":"學校要是離家近一點，我每天早上就能多睡一會兒。"},{"en":"If it [[snowed]] in Taipei tomorrow, everyone [[would run]] outside to take photos.","zh":"台北明天要是下雪，大家都會衝出去拍照。"}],"practice":[{"q":"If my family ______ a bigger apartment, I would have my own room.","options":["has","had","will have","has had"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：與現在事實相反，if 子句用過去式。主要子句是 would + 原形，表示家裡現在其實沒有大房子，用 had。(A) has、(C) will have 是真實條件的用法；(D) has had 是現在完成式，不用在這種 if 子句。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"If Leo were here, he ______ us fix the computer.","options":["will help","helps","would help","helped"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：與現在事實相反，主要子句用 would + 原形。if 子句用 were，表示 Leo 現在不在，用 would help。(A) will help、(B) helps 是真實條件的用法；(D) helped 不對，退成過去式的只有 if 子句。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"與過去事實相反、混合","text":["假設和**過去事實相反**時，if 子句用 **had p.p.**，主要子句用 would、could、might + have p.p.，常帶有後悔的語氣。","**混合假設**最常見的是條件在過去、結果在現在：if 子句用 had p.p.，主要子句用 would、could + 原形，句中常有 now、today 等線索。"],"adv":["反過來，條件在現在、結果在過去：If I were taller, I would have made the basketball team.（我要是高一點，當初就進籃球隊了。）"],"formula":"If + S + had p.p., S + would/could/might + have p.p.","table":{"cols":["類型","if 子句","主要子句"],"rows":[["真實條件","現在式","will + 原形"],["與現在事實相反","過去式（be 用 were）","would + 原形"],["與過去事實相反","had p.p.","would have p.p."],["混合（過去→現在）","had p.p.","would + 原形"]]},"parse":{"en":"If Ben had studied harder, he could have passed the math test.","zh":"Ben 要是再用功一點，數學考試就能及格了。","parts":[["If Ben had studied harder,","M","條件子句"],["he","S"],["could have passed","V"],["the math test.","O"]]},"ex":[{"en":"If I [[had left]] home earlier, I [[wouldn't have missed]] the bus.","zh":"我要是早點出門，就不會錯過公車了。"},{"en":"If Ben [[had studied]] harder, he [[could have passed]] the math test.","zh":"Ben 要是再用功一點，數學考試就能及格了。"},{"en":"If I [[hadn't stayed up]] so late last night, I [[wouldn't be]] so sleepy now.","zh":"要是昨晚沒熬夜到那麼晚，我現在就不會這麼睏了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"We got to the theater late last night. If we had left home earlier, we ______ the start of the movie.","options":["won't miss","didn't miss","wouldn't miss","wouldn't have missed"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：與過去事實相反，主要子句用 would have p.p.。昨晚已經遲到，錯過開場也是過去的事，用 wouldn't have missed。(A) won't miss 是真實條件；(B) didn't miss 不是假設語氣；(C) wouldn't miss 講的是現在。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"I lost my phone yesterday. If I hadn't lost it, I ______ you the photos now.","options":["could send","could have sent","can send"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：混合假設，條件在過去、結果在現在。if 子句是 hadn't lost（過去），句尾有 now，主要子句用 could + 原形。(B) could have sent 講過去的結果，與 now 不合；(C) can send 是真實條件的用法。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"I wish 與 if only","text":["**I wish** 表達不可能或不太可能實現的願望：對現在的願望用**過去式**（be 用 were，can 改 could），對過去的遺憾用 **had p.p.**。","**If only** 是「要是…就好了」，時態規則和 wish 一樣，語氣更強烈。有可能實現的希望則用 hope：I hope you win."],"adv":["希望別人改變做法或情況改變，常用 wish + S + would + 原形，多帶抱怨：I wish my brother would stop shouting.","wish 也可接 to V（= want to，較正式）或 sb + sth（I wish you a happy birthday.），這兩種不是假設語氣。"],"formula":"S + wish + S + 過去式（現在）／had p.p.（過去）","parse":{"en":"I wish I had my own room.","zh":"真希望我有自己的房間。","parts":[["I","S"],["wish","V"],["I had my own room.","O","名詞子句當受詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"I [[wish]] I [[had]] my own room. I share one with my brother.","zh":"真希望有自己的房間，我現在跟哥哥共用一間。"},{"en":"I [[wish]] I [[could]] go to the concert with you, but I have to work.","zh":"真希望能跟你去演唱會，可是我要打工。"},{"en":"Amy [[wishes]] she [[hadn't eaten]] so much stinky tofu last night.","zh":"Amy 真希望昨晚沒吃那麼多臭豆腐。"},{"en":"[[If only]] I [[had brought]] an umbrella this morning!","zh":"要是我早上有帶傘就好了！"}],"practice":[{"q":"I don't have a bike. I wish I ______ one.","options":["have","had","will have","have had"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：wish 表現在不可能實現的願望，用過去式。現在沒有腳踏車，用 had。(A) have、(C) will have 不能表達 wish 後與現在事實相反的願望；(D) have had 是現在完成式。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"The weather looks great. I ______ we can go to the beach this weekend.","options":["hope","wish","wished"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：有可能實現的希望用 hope，不太可能實現的願望才用 wish。天氣好，真的可能去海邊，後面又是 can，用 hope。(B) wish 後面要用 could，不用 can；(C) wished 時態不合，後面也不接 can。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"as if、It's time 等","text":["**as if / as though** 表「好像…」。與事實相反時，和主要動詞同時用**過去式**（be 用 were），比主要動詞更早用 had p.p.。","**It's (high) time + S + 過去式**表「早該…了」，動詞雖是過去式，講的是現在；也可說 It's time (for sb) to V。","表「建議、要求」的 suggest、demand、require 等，that 子句用 **(should) + 原形**，也屬於假設語氣。"],"adv":["as if 後說的可能是真的時，照一般時態：It looks as if it is going to rain.","suggest 作「暗示」時不用 (should) + 原形，照一般時態：His red eyes suggested that he had been crying."],"parse":{"en":"Jason talks as if he knew everything about baseball.","zh":"Jason 講得好像他對棒球無所不知。","parts":[["Jason","S"],["talks","V"],["as if he knew everything about baseball.","M","as if 副詞子句"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Jason talks [[as if]] he [[knew]] everything about baseball.","zh":"Jason 講得好像他對棒球無所不知。"},{"en":"Mia looked at me [[as though]] she [[had seen]] a ghost.","zh":"Mia 看著我，一副見到鬼的樣子。"},{"en":"It's almost midnight. [[It's high time]] you [[went]] to bed.","zh":"都快半夜了，你早該去睡了。"},{"en":"The doctor [[suggested]] that Grandpa [[walk]] for 30 minutes every day.","zh":"醫生建議爺爺每天走路 30 分鐘。"}],"practice":[{"q":"When I told Mia the news, she looked as if she ______ it before.","options":["hears","has heard","had heard","will hear"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：as if 子句的事比主要動詞更早，用 had p.p.。她聽說這消息在 looked 之前，用 had heard。(A) hears、(B) has heard 是現在時態，和過去的 looked 不合；(D) will hear 時間不對。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"It's 11 p.m. It's high time Ben ______ to bed.","options":["will go","going","goes","went"],"answer":3,"explain":"考點：It's (high) time + S + 過去式，表「早該…了」。雖然講的是現在，動詞仍用過去式 went。(A) will go、(C) goes 不用在這個句型；(B) going 不能單獨當動詞。故選 (D)。"}]},{"h":"省略 if 倒裝與 without","text":["if 子句的 **were、should、had**（限 had p.p.）可移到主詞前並省略 if。否定寫 Had I not…，不能寫 Hadn't I…。","**Should + S + 原形**表「萬一…」，主要子句常用 will 或祈使句。","假設句的 **without / but for** 是「要不是」，等於 if it were not for（現在）或 if it had not been for（過去）。"],"adv":["without 本身只是「沒有」，主要子句用一般時態時就不是假設：Without a map, we got lost yesterday.（事實）"],"table":{"cols":["一般 if 子句","省略 if 的倒裝"],"rows":[["If I were you, …","[[Were I]] you, …"],["If I had known, …","[[Had I known]], …"],["If you should need help, …","[[Should you need]] help, …"],["If it were not for …","[[Were it not for]] …"],["If it had not been for …","[[Had it not been for]] …"]]},"parse":{"en":"Had I known about the quiz, I would have studied last night.","zh":"早知道有小考，我昨晚就會念書了。","parts":[["Had I known about the quiz,","M","倒裝的條件子句"],["I","S"],["would have studied","V"],["last night.","M","時間"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Had I known]] about the quiz, I [[would have studied]] last night.","zh":"早知道有小考，我昨晚就會念書了。"},{"en":"[[Should]] it [[rain]] tomorrow, our sports day will be postponed.","zh":"萬一明天下雨，運動會就會延期。"},{"en":"[[Without]] the MRT, getting around Taipei [[would be]] much harder.","zh":"要是沒有捷運，在台北到處跑會麻煩得多。"},{"en":"[[But for]] your help, I [[would have failed]] the English test.","zh":"要不是有你幫忙，我英文考試就不及格了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ you need any help, please call me.","options":["Should","Had","Were"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：Should + S + 原形表「萬一…」，是 If you should need 省略 if 的倒裝。空格後是原形 need，主要子句是祈使句，用 Should。(B) Had 後面要接 p.p.；(C) Were 後面不接原形動詞。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"______ the fan, this classroom would be too hot to study in.","options":["Unless","Without","Because","With"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：without 表「要不是」，等於 if it were not for，主要子句用 would + 原形。(A) Unless、(C) Because 是連接詞，後面要接子句；(D) With 意思相反，有電扇不會太熱。故選 (B)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"If it will rain tomorrow, we will stay home.","right":"If it [[rains]] tomorrow, we will stay home.","why":"表條件的 if 子句用現在式代替未來式。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"I wonder if it rains tomorrow.","right":"I wonder if it [[will rain]] tomorrow.","why":"if 作「是否」是名詞子句，講未來仍要用 will。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"If I was you, I would tell the teacher.","right":"If I [[were]] you, I would tell the teacher.","why":"與現在事實相反，be 動詞考試一律用 were。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"If I had more time, I will join the dance club.","right":"If I had more time, I [[would join]] the dance club.","why":"if 子句用過去式表與現在事實相反，主要子句要用 would + 原形。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"If I had known her number, I would call her yesterday.","right":"If I had known her number, I [[would have called]] her yesterday.","why":"與過去事實相反，主要子句用 would have p.p.。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"If I had eaten breakfast, I wouldn't have been so hungry now.","right":"If I had eaten breakfast, I [[wouldn't be]] so hungry now.","why":"條件在過去、結果在現在（now），主要子句用 would + 原形。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"I wish I can speak English as well as you.","right":"I wish I [[could]] speak English as well as you.","why":"wish 表現在不可能的願望，can 要改成過去式 could。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"It's high time Ben cleans his messy room.","right":"It's high time Ben [[cleaned]] his messy room.","why":"It's (high) time + S 後接過去式，表「早該…了」。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"Hadn't I missed the bus, I would have been on time.","right":"[[Had I not]] missed the bus, I would have been on time.","why":"省略 if 的倒裝，否定要寫 Had I not，不能用 Hadn't I。"}],"tips":["過去式配 would + 原形，had p.p. 配 would have p.p.；句中有 now 要想到混合假設。","句首是 Were、Had、Should + 主詞，又不是問句，就是省略 if 的倒裝，主要子句照假設時間配對。","wish、as if 的空格多選過去式或 had p.p.，看時間詞決定；It's time + S 後用過去式。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Don't worry. If you ______ the 7:10 bus, you will get to school on time.","options":["take","will take","took","had taken"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：別擔心，如果你搭 7:10 的公車，就能準時到校。真實條件的 if 子句用現在式代替未來式，不用 will take。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"If I ______ a bird, I would fly to my grandma's house in Hualien.","options":["am","were","have been","will be"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：如果我是一隻鳥，就會飛去花蓮的奶奶家。主要子句是 would + 原形，表與現在事實相反，if 子句用過去式，be 動詞一律用 were。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Sam was late for school this morning. If he ______ his alarm, he wouldn't have been late.","options":["sets","set","had set","has set"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Sam 今早上學遲到，要是他有設鬧鐘就不會遲到了。主要子句是 wouldn't have p.p.，與過去事實相反，if 子句用 had p.p.；set 是過去式，要配 would + 原形。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Ann missed her favorite band's concert last night. She wishes she ______ there.","options":["is","has been","will be","had been"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Ann 錯過了她最愛的樂團昨晚的演唱會，真希望自己當時在場。wish 表達對過去的遺憾，用 had p.p.。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Kevin isn't the class leader, but he acts ______ he were in charge.","options":["even though","so that","as if","because"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Kevin 不是班長，卻表現得好像他是負責人。空格後接 were，表與事實相反的「好像…」，用 as if；even though、because 後面接事實，不用 were。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Thanks, Amy! Without your help, I ______ the math test last week.","options":["will fail","failed","would fail","would have failed"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：謝謝你，Amy！要不是你幫忙，我上週數學考試就不及格了。without 表「要不是」，又有 last week，是與過去事實相反，用 would have p.p.。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"______ I known about the sale, I would have bought those sneakers.","options":["If","Had","Were","Should"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：早知道有特價，我就會買那雙球鞋了。主要子句是 would have p.p.，原句為 If I had known；省略 if 後，把 had 移到主詞前。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"If Tom had taken my advice last week, he ______ in trouble now.","options":["wouldn't be","isn't","won't be","hadn't been"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：如果 Tom 上週聽了我的建議，現在就不會有麻煩了。條件在過去（had p.p.），結果在現在（now），是混合假設，主要子句用 would + 原形。故選 (A)。"}]},{"id":"g-inversion","unit":"special","level":"B2","title":"倒裝句","en":"Inversion","lead":"否定副詞或 Only + 副詞語放句首，用疑問句語序：助動詞/be + 主詞。","goals":["能把否定副詞或 Only 放句首的句子正確倒裝","能用 So／Neither + 助動詞/be 附和別人","能辨認地方副詞放句首與省略 if 的倒裝"],"prereq":["g-question","g-perfect","g-conditional"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[2]","note":"Hardly/No sooner 後接 did + S + 原形的寫法也有人用，統測是否接受待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"否定副詞放句首","text":["**否定副詞**（never、seldom、rarely、little、not once）放句首時，改用疑問句語序，叫**部分倒裝**；祈使句 Never give up! 除外。","把**第一個**助動詞或 be 動詞移到主詞前（has been seen 只移 has）；只有一般動詞時，補 **do/does/did**，動詞改回原形。","**Not only** 帶子句放句首也要倒裝，但 but 後面照常語序。Not only 修飾主詞時不倒裝：Not only Amy but also Ken passed。"],"adv":["little 放句首表「完全不…」，常接 know、realize：Little did I know…。hardly ever 放句首也一樣要倒裝。"],"formula":"否定副詞 + 助動詞/be + S + (V)","table":{"cols":["一般句","倒裝句"],"rows":[["I have never seen such a thing.","Never [[have I]] seen such a thing."],["She is seldom late.","Seldom [[is she]] late."],["He rarely eats breakfast.","Rarely [[does he eat]] breakfast."],["I didn't cry once.","Not once [[did I cry]]."]]},"parse":{"en":"Never have I seen such a long line at the night market.","zh":"我從沒在夜市看過排這麼長的隊伍。","parts":[["Never","M","否定副詞放句首"],["have","V","助動詞"],["I","S"],["seen","V"],["such a long line","O"],["at the night market.","M","地點"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Never [[have I]] seen such a long line at the night market.","zh":"我從沒在夜市看過排這麼長的隊伍。"},{"en":"Seldom [[does]] my brother [[eat]] breakfast before school.","zh":"我哥很少在上學前吃早餐。"},{"en":"Little [[did I know]] that my friends were planning a surprise party for me.","zh":"我完全不知道朋友們正在幫我籌備驚喜派對。"},{"en":"Not only [[did]] Kevin [[finish]] his homework, but he also cleaned his room.","zh":"Kevin 不只寫完功課，還打掃了房間。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Amy always comes to school early. Rarely ______ late for class.","options":["Amy is","is Amy","does Amy be","Amy does"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：否定副詞放句首要倒裝。這句的動詞是 be 動詞 is，直接移到主詞前：is Amy。(A) 沒有倒裝；(C) be 動詞不需要補 does；(D) 語序錯，也少了 be 動詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Not once ______ late for school this year.","options":["has Ken been","Ken has been","has been Ken","have Ken been"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：倒裝時只把第一個助動詞移到主詞前。has been 只移 has：has Ken been。(B) 沒有倒裝；(C) 把 been 也移到主詞前；(D) 主詞 Ken 是單數，不用 have。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"Not until 與 Only","text":["**Not until** + 時間或子句放句首，意思是「直到…才…」。倒裝的是後面的**主要子句**，not until 帶的子句照常語序。","**Only** + 副詞、片語或子句（only then、only after…、only by V-ing）放句首時，主要子句同樣要倒裝。","Only 修飾主詞時不倒裝，例如 Only Amy knew the answer。"],"adv":["Not until 不在句首時不倒裝：I didn't know it until I got home。It was not until…that… 詳見〈強調句與常用句型〉。"],"formula":"Not until/Only + 時間/片語/子句 + 助動詞/be + S (+ V)","parse":{"en":"Not until I got home did I realize my phone was gone.","zh":"直到回到家，我才發現手機不見了。","parts":[["Not until I got home","M","時間，放句首"],["did","V","助動詞"],["I","S"],["realize","V"],["my phone was gone.","O","名詞子句當受詞"]]},"ex":[{"en":"Not until I got home [[did I realize]] my phone was gone.","zh":"直到回到家，我才發現手機不見了。"},{"en":"Not until midnight [[did]] my sister [[finish]] her report.","zh":"我妹直到半夜才把報告寫完。"},{"en":"Only then [[did I understand]] why my parents work so hard.","zh":"那時我才明白爸媽為什麼那麼拚。"},{"en":"Only by practicing every day [[can you]] improve your English.","zh":"只有每天練習，英文才會進步。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Ben stayed up late last night. Not until midnight ______ to bed.","options":["he went","did he go","did he went","he did go"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：Not until 放句首，倒裝的是主要子句。went 是一般動詞過去式，補 did 放主詞前，動詞改回原形：did he go。(A) 沒有倒裝；(C) did 後面要接原形 go；(D) he did go 仍是一般語序。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Only ______ the answer to the last question.","options":["Leo knew","did Leo know","knew Leo"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：Only 修飾主詞時不倒裝。這裡 Only 修飾 Leo，句子照常語序：Leo knew。(B) 把 Only 當成句首副詞語而倒裝，錯；(C) 動詞不能直接放在主詞前。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"Hardly 與 No sooner","text":["**Hardly…when** 與 **No sooner…than** 都表示「一…就…」。放句首時倒裝，敘述過去通常前半句用 had + S + p.p.，後半句用過去式。","scarcely 用法同 hardly。hardly、scarcely 配 when，no sooner 只配 than，不能混用。"],"adv":["hardly、scarcely 也可配 before。不放句首時不倒裝：I had hardly sat down when…，同 As soon as I sat down…。"],"table":{"cols":["前半句","連接","後半句"],"rows":[["Hardly had + S + p.p.","[[when]]","S + 過去式"],["Scarcely had + S + p.p.","[[when]]","S + 過去式"],["No sooner had + S + p.p.","[[than]]","S + 過去式"]]},"parse":{"en":"Hardly had I sat down when the teacher called my name.","zh":"我才剛坐下，老師就叫到我的名字。","parts":[["Hardly","M","否定副詞放句首"],["had","V","助動詞"],["I","S"],["sat down","V"],["when the teacher called my name.","M","時間子句"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Hardly had]] I sat down [[when]] the teacher called my name.","zh":"我才剛坐下，老師就叫到我的名字。"},{"en":"[[No sooner had]] we reached the station [[than]] the train left.","zh":"我們一到車站，火車就開走了。"},{"en":"[[Scarcely had]] the movie started [[when]] the power went out.","zh":"電影才剛開始就停電了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Hardly ______ the classroom when the bell rang.","options":["had we entered","we had entered","had we enter","we entered"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：Hardly 放句首要倒裝成 had + S + p.p.。had 移到主詞前，後面接 p.p. entered。(B)、(D) 都沒有倒裝；(C) had 後面要接 p.p.，不能接原形 enter。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Hardly had the game started ______ it began to rain.","options":["when","than","then"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：Hardly had + S + p.p. 後面配 when，表「一…就…」。(B) than 是配 no sooner；(C) then 是副詞，不能連接兩個子句。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"So／Neither／Nor 開頭","text":["附和肯定句「…也是」用 **So + 助動詞/be + S**；附和否定句「…也不」用 **Neither/Nor + 助動詞/be + S**。","前句有 be 動詞或助動詞就照用，只有一般動詞時用 do/does/did；單複數看新的主詞：I love it, and so does Tom。","neither、nor 本身已含否定，後面的助動詞或 be 不再加 not。"],"adv":["**So + adj** 放句首強調也要倒裝，表「如此…以致於…」：So tired was I that I fell asleep。","口語也可簡答 Me too.（我也是）或 Me neither.（我也不）。"],"formula":"So + 助動詞/be + S（也是）／Neither/Nor + 助動詞/be + S（也不）","parse":{"en":"My sister loves spicy hot pot, and so do I.","zh":"我妹超愛麻辣鍋，我也是。","parts":[["My sister","S"],["loves","V"],["spicy hot pot,","O"],["and","J"],["so","M","表「也」"],["do","V","代替前面的動詞"],["I.","S"]]},"ex":[{"en":"My sister loves spicy hot pot, and [[so do I]].","zh":"我妹超愛麻辣鍋，我也是。"},{"en":"Ken can't ride a scooter yet, and [[neither can]] his twin brother.","zh":"Ken 還不會騎機車，他的雙胞胎兄弟也不會。"},{"en":"Jenny has finished her science report, and [[so has]] Ben.","zh":"Jenny 已經寫完自然科報告，Ben 也是。"},{"en":"My dad is a big baseball fan, and [[so is]] my uncle.","zh":"我爸是超級棒球迷，我叔叔也是。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Tom is good at basketball, and so ______ his brother.","options":["does","is","do","has"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：附和肯定句用 So + 助動詞/be + S。前句動詞是 be 動詞 is，附和也用 be；主詞 his brother 是單數，用 is。(A)、(C) 是附和一般動詞用的；(D) has 是附和完成式用的。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I can't swim, and ______ can my sister.","options":["so","neither","either"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：附和否定句用 Neither + 助動詞/be + S。前句 can't swim 是否定，用 neither can。(A) so 是附和肯定句；(C) either 要放句尾，寫成 my sister can't either。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"地方副詞放句首","text":["**地方副詞**或地方片語（here、there、behind the house）放句首時，常把整個動詞移到主詞前，叫**完全倒裝**，不加 do/does/did。","動詞多為 be 動詞或 come、go、stand、lie 等不及物動詞，單複數看後面的主詞：Here are your keys。","主詞是**代名詞**時不倒裝：說 Here it comes，不說 Here comes it。"],"adv":["地方片語放句首不一定倒裝，動詞有受詞時照常語序：In the park, we played basketball。","方向副詞 up、down、out、away 放句首也常完全倒裝：Out ran the kids。主詞是代名詞時照常語序：Out they ran。"],"formula":"地方副詞/片語 + V + S（S 是名詞）","parse":{"en":"Inside the box were three tiny kittens.","zh":"箱子裡有三隻小貓咪。","parts":[["Inside the box","C","地點補語，放句首"],["were","V"],["three tiny kittens.","S","主詞在動詞後"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Here comes]] the bus! Hurry up!","zh":"公車來了！快一點！"},{"en":"Behind our school [[stands]] a small temple.","zh":"我們學校後面有一座小廟。"},{"en":"Inside the box [[were]] three tiny kittens.","zh":"箱子裡有三隻小貓咪。"},{"en":"Where's my phone? Oh, [[here it is]].","zh":"我手機呢？喔，在這裡。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Look! Here ______ our bus.","options":["come","comes","is coming"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：地方副詞 here 放句首，動詞移到主詞前，單複數看後面的主詞。our bus 是單數，用 comes。(A) come 和單數主詞不一致；(C) 這種倒裝不用進行式。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Where are my glasses? Oh, here ______.","options":["are they","they are","is it","it is"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：主詞是代名詞時，地方副詞放句首也不倒裝：here + 代名詞 + V。glasses 是複數，用 they are。(A) 代名詞主詞不倒裝；(C)、(D) it/is 是單數，不合 glasses。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"假設語氣的倒裝","text":["假設語氣的 if 子句含 **were、should、had**（限 had p.p.）時，可以省略 if，把這個字移到主詞前。","否定要寫 Had I not…，不能寫成 Hadn't I…。完整用法詳見〈條件句與假設語氣〉。"],"table":{"cols":["if 子句","省略 if 倒裝"],"rows":[["If I were you, …","[[Were I]] you, …"],["If I had known, …","[[Had I]] known, …"],["If you should need help, …","[[Should you]] need help, …"]]},"parse":{"en":"Were I you, I would take the MRT instead.","zh":"如果我是你，我會改搭捷運。","parts":[["Were I you,","M","倒裝的條件子句"],["I","S"],["would take","V"],["the MRT","O"],["instead.","M"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[Were I]] you, I would take the MRT instead.","zh":"如果我是你，我會改搭捷運。"},{"en":"[[Had he]] listened to his doctor, he would have recovered sooner.","zh":"要是他當初有聽醫生的話，早就康復了。"},{"en":"[[Should you]] have any questions, please ask the librarian.","zh":"如有任何問題，請洽圖書館員。"}],"practice":[{"q":"______ I you, I would say sorry to her.","options":["Were","Had","Did"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：If I were you 省略 if 後，were 移到主詞前：Were I you。(B) Had 後面要接 p.p.；(C) Did 不能用在這種倒裝，後面也沒有原形動詞。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"sec":0,"wrong":"Seldom he goes to the gym on weekends.","right":"Seldom [[does he go]] to the gym on weekends.","why":"Seldom 放句首要倒裝；一般動詞要補 does，動詞改回原形 go。"},{"sec":0,"wrong":"Never have been I so nervous before a test.","right":"Never [[have I been]] so nervous before a test.","why":"只把第一個助動詞 have 移到主詞前，been 留在主詞後。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Not until I got home I realized I had lost my key.","right":"Not until I got home [[did I realize]] I had lost my key.","why":"Not until 子句放句首，主要子句要倒裝成 did + S + 原形。"},{"sec":1,"wrong":"Only by taking the MRT we can get there on time.","right":"Only by taking the MRT [[can we]] get there on time.","why":"Only + 片語放句首，主要子句要倒裝，can 移到主詞前。"},{"sec":2,"wrong":"No sooner had we left the house when it started to rain.","right":"No sooner had we left the house [[than]] it started to rain.","why":"No sooner 要配 than；when 是配 hardly、scarcely。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Lisa doesn't eat beef, and neither doesn't her sister.","right":"Lisa doesn't eat beef, and [[neither does]] her sister.","why":"neither 已含否定，後面的助動詞不再加 not。"},{"sec":3,"wrong":"Mark is tired, and so does Jenny.","right":"Mark is tired, and [[so is]] Jenny.","why":"前句動詞是 be 動詞，附和也用 be，不用 does。"},{"sec":4,"wrong":"Look, here comes she.","right":"Look, [[here she comes]].","why":"主詞是代名詞時不倒裝，要用 here + 代名詞 + V。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"Hadn't I missed the bus, I would have been on time.","right":"[[Had I not]] missed the bus, I would have been on time.","why":"倒裝的否定要寫 Had I not，不能寫成 Hadn't I。"},{"sec":5,"wrong":"If had I known about the test, I would have studied.","right":"[[Had I known]] about the test, I would have studied.","why":"倒裝就要省略 if；保留 if 時照常語序 If I had known。"}],"tips":["句首為否定副詞、Not until、Only + 副詞語，空格選「助動詞/be + 主詞」；Only + 主詞不倒裝。","Not until、Only 的子句不倒裝，倒裝主要子句；No sooner 配 than，Hardly 配 when。","附和題先看前句是肯定或否定、用什麼動詞和時態，再選 So 或 Neither + 對應的助動詞/be。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Never ______ such delicious beef noodles.","options":["I have tasted","have I tasted","I tasted","did I tasted"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我從沒吃過這麼好吃的牛肉麵。否定副詞 Never 放句首要倒裝，助動詞 have 移到主詞前；did 後面要接原形 taste。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Amy works part-time after school. Seldom ______ TV on weeknights.","options":["she watches","does she watches","does she watch","she does watch"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Amy 放學後要打工，平日晚上很少看電視。Seldom 放句首要倒裝，一般動詞要補 does 放主詞前，動詞改回原形 watch。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Not until I got to school ______ that I had left my lunch at home.","options":["did I realize","I realized","I did realize","did I realized"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：我到了學校才發現午餐忘在家裡。Not until 子句放句首，倒裝的是主要子句：did + I + 原形 realize。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"Mia didn't go to the concert last night, and ______ her brother.","options":["so did","neither was","so wasn't","neither did"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Mia 昨晚沒去演唱會，她哥哥也沒去。附和否定句用 neither + 助動詞/be + S；前句是一般動詞過去式 didn't go，要用 did，不用 was。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"Only after the teacher gave us an example ______ how to solve the problem.","options":["I understood","did I understand","I did understand","understood I"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：老師舉了例子之後，我才懂這題怎麼解。Only + 副詞子句放句首，主要子句要倒裝成 did + I + 原形動詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"No sooner had Jason gotten off the bus ______ it started to rain.","options":["when","then","than","until"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：Jason 一下公車就開始下雨了。No sooner had + S + p.p. 固定搭配 than；when 是和 hardly、scarcely 搭配。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"In front of our school ______ two tall trees.","options":["stands","stand","standing","is standing"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：我們學校前面有兩棵高大的樹。地方片語放句首，動詞移到主詞前；主詞 two tall trees 是複數，動詞用 stand。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"______ about the typhoon, we wouldn't have gone to Kenting.","options":["Had we known","We had known","Have we known","Did we know"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：要是早知道有颱風，我們就不會去墾丁了。與過去事實相反用 If we had known，省略 if 後 had 移到主詞前：Had we known；We had known 少了 if，無法連接兩句。故選 (A)。"}]},{"id":"g-emphasis","unit":"special","level":"B1","title":"強調句與常用句型","en":"Cleft sentences and useful patterns","lead":"要強調主詞、受詞或時間地點，放進 It is/was … that 中間。","goals":["能用 It is/was … that 強調句中一部分","能用 What 子句和 do/did 強調重點","能選對 There 句的分詞、花費動詞和 seem 句型"],"prereq":["g-relative","g-relative-adv","g-participle"],"pending":[{"where":"sections[0]","note":"第一、二節的強調句圖解把強調部分標 C、that/who 子句標 M；各教材分析方式不一，待確認。"},{"where":"sections[3]","note":"圖解把 There 標為虛主詞、後面名詞標為真主詞；也有教材稱 There 為引導詞，待確認。"}],"sections":[{"h":"It is/was … that","text":["這種句型叫**強調句**（又稱分裂句）：把要強調的部分（主詞、受詞、時間、地點）放在 **It is/was** 和 **that** 中間，其餘照原句順序放在後面。","be 動詞用單數，強調部分是複數也不用 are/were；原句是過去式時通常用 It was。強調的是人時，that 可換成 **who**。","判斷法：拿掉 It is/was 和 that/who，把強調部分放回原位，仍是完整句（It was Amy that I met → I met Amy）。"],"adv":["強調主詞時，that/who 後的動詞跟它一致：It is my parents who help me。強調時間、地點時，標準用法仍是 that，不用 when、where。","It 後也可以用助動詞：It must have been Tom who broke it.（一定是 Tom 打破的。）"],"formula":"It is/was + 強調部分 + that/who + 其餘部分","table":{"cols":["強調","句子"],"rows":[["原句","Tom broke the window yesterday."],["主詞","It was [[Tom]] who broke the window yesterday."],["受詞","It was [[the window]] that Tom broke yesterday."],["時間","It was [[yesterday]] that Tom broke the window."]]},"parse":{"en":"It was my grandma who taught me how to make dumplings.","zh":"是我阿嬤教我包水餃的。","parts":[["It","S","強調句的 it"],["was","V"],["my grandma","C","強調部分"],["who taught me how to make dumplings.","M","who 子句"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[It was]] my grandma [[who]] taught me how to make dumplings.","zh":"是我阿嬤教我包水餃的。"},{"en":"[[It was]] in Tainan [[that]] I first tried milkfish soup.","zh":"我是在台南第一次喝到虱目魚湯的。"},{"en":"[[It was]] my phone [[that]] I left on the MRT, not my wallet.","zh":"我忘在捷運上的是手機，不是錢包。"}],"practice":[{"q":"It was my uncle ______ drove me to the train station this morning.","options":["which","who","where"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：強調句 It was + 強調部分 + who/that。強調的是人 my uncle，他在後面當主詞，用 who（也可用 that）。(A) which 不能指人；(C) where 不用在強調句，也不能指人。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"It ______ my parents who taught me how to ride a bike.","options":["was","were","are"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：強調句的 be 動詞用單數。my parents 雖是複數，It 後面仍用 is/was；taught 是過去式，用 was。(B) were、(C) are 都不能接在強調句的 It 後面。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"It was not until","text":["**It was not until + 時間/子句 + that + S + V** 表示「直到…才…」，是 not…until 的強調寫法。","not 已經移到前面，that 後面要用**肯定句**，照一般語序寫，不倒裝。"],"adv":["不用 It was，直接把 Not until 放句首時，主要子句要倒裝，詳見〈倒裝句〉。"],"formula":"It is/was not until + 時間/子句 + that + S + V（肯定）","table":{"cols":["寫法","例句"],"rows":[["一般句","I didn't go to bed until midnight."],["強調句","[[It was not until]] midnight [[that]] I went to bed."],["倒裝句","Not until midnight [[did I go]] to bed."]]},"parse":{"en":"It was not until 11 p.m. that my dad got home from work.","zh":"我爸直到晚上十一點才下班回到家。","parts":[["It","S","強調句的 it"],["was","V"],["not","M","否定"],["until 11 p.m.","C","強調部分"],["that my dad got home from work.","M","that 子句（肯定）"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[It wasn't until]] I got sick [[that]] I realized how important sleep is.","zh":"直到生病，我才明白睡眠有多重要。"},{"en":"[[It was not until]] 11 p.m. [[that]] my dad got home from work.","zh":"我爸直到晚上十一點才下班回到家。"},{"en":"[[It wasn't until]] high school [[that]] Amy started to enjoy English.","zh":"Amy 到了高中才開始喜歡英文。"}],"practice":[{"q":"It was not until midnight that Jason ______ his science report.","options":["didn't finish","finished","doesn't finish"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：It was not until…that 後接肯定句。not 已移到前面，that 後面用肯定的過去式 finished。(A) didn't finish 多了否定；(C) doesn't finish 也是否定，時態也不合。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"What 句與 do 強調","text":["**What (+ S) + V + is/was + 重點**：what 子句當主詞，把要強調的內容放在 be 動詞後面，表示「…的是…」。be 動詞通常用單數。","肯定句的一般動詞前加 **do/does/did**，動詞改**原形**，表示「真的、確實」；說過去的事用 did。"],"adv":["what 子句裡有 do 時，is 後面常接原形動詞（也可用 to V）：What I want to do is sleep。what 的用法詳見〈關係副詞與複合關係詞〉。","直述句的 be 動詞和助動詞不加 do，直接重讀即可；祈使句前加 Do 表示「務必」：Do come to my party!"],"formula":"What (+ S) + V + is/was + 重點；S + do/does/did + 原形 V","parse":{"en":"What I need right now is a big bowl of beef noodles.","zh":"我現在最需要的是一大碗牛肉麵。","parts":[["What I need right now","S","名詞子句當主詞"],["is","V"],["a big bowl of beef noodles.","C","主詞補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[What I need]] right now [[is]] a big bowl of beef noodles.","zh":"我現在最需要的是一大碗牛肉麵。"},{"en":"[[What]] surprised me [[was]] how cheap the concert tickets were.","zh":"讓我驚訝的是演唱會門票竟然那麼便宜。"},{"en":"I [[do like]] stinky tofu. I just can't eat too much of it.","zh":"我真的很喜歡臭豆腐，只是不能吃太多。"},{"en":"Kevin [[did study]] for the test, but he was too nervous.","zh":"Kevin 真的有準備考試，只是太緊張了。"}],"practice":[{"q":"What I need now ______ a cup of hot milk tea.","options":["are","is","be"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：What 子句當主詞，be 動詞通常用單數。What I need now 是一件事，後面的 a cup of hot milk tea 也是單數，用 is。(A) are 用於複數；(C) be 是原形，不能當句子的動詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"I ______ call you last night, but you didn't answer your phone.","options":["did","do","was"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：did + 原形動詞，強調過去「真的有」做。last night 是過去，用 did，後面 call 用原形。(B) do 是現在式，時間不合；(C) was 後面不能接原形動詞 call。故選 (A)。"}]},{"h":"There + N + 分詞","text":["**There is/are + N + V-ing**：N 主動，多表示「有…正在…」；**There is/are + N + p.p.**：N 被動，表示「有…被…」。","There is/are 已是句子的動詞，名詞後不能再接 stands、was left 這類動詞，要改用分詞（或關係子句）。","be 動詞的單複數看後面的名詞。There is/are + N + left 常用來表示「還剩…」。"],"adv":["V-ing 不一定表示正在進行，也可表示狀態：There is a road leading to the station.（有一條通往車站的路）","There is/are 的單複數詳見〈主詞與動詞一致〉；分詞放在名詞後修飾名詞，詳見〈分詞當形容詞〉。"],"formula":"There is/are + N + V-ing（主動）/ p.p.（被動）","parse":{"en":"There are a lot of people waiting in line for the MRT.","zh":"有很多人在排隊等捷運。","parts":[["There","S","虛主詞"],["are","V"],["a lot of people","S","真主詞"],["waiting in line for the MRT.","M","修飾 people"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[There are]] a lot of people [[waiting]] in line for the MRT.","zh":"有很多人在排隊等捷運。"},{"en":"There's a stray cat [[sleeping]] under my scooter.","zh":"有隻流浪貓在我的機車底下睡覺。"},{"en":"There were only two pieces of cake [[left]] when I got home.","zh":"我回到家時只剩兩塊蛋糕。"},{"en":"There is a notice [[posted]] on the classroom door.","zh":"教室門上貼了一張公告。"}],"practice":[{"q":"There is a girl ______ the guitar in the park.","options":["plays","playing","played"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：There is + N + V-ing（主動）。There is 已是句子的動詞，女孩自己彈吉他，用 playing。(A) plays 讓句子多了一個動詞；(C) played 表被動，女孩不是被彈的。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"There is a message ______ on the board for our class.","options":["writing","writes","written"],"answer":2,"explain":"考點：There is + N + p.p.（被動）。訊息是「被寫」在白板上的，用過去分詞 written。(A) writing 表主動，訊息不會自己寫；(B) writes 讓句子多了一個動詞。故選 (C)。"}]},{"h":"花時間與花錢","text":["**It takes (sb) + 時間 + to V**：做某事花（某人）多少時間，it 是虛主詞。","**S + spend + 時間/錢 + (in) V-ing 或 on + N**：主詞是人，可以花時間也可以花錢；spend 後面不接 to V。","**It costs (sb) + 錢 + to V** 或「物 + cost + 錢」；人付錢用 **pay + 錢 + for + 物**。cost 三態同形。"],"adv":["take 的主詞也可以是人或事物：I took an hour to finish it. The trip took three hours."],"table":{"cols":["動詞","主詞","例句"],"rows":[["take","it、事物（人亦可）","It [[takes]] me ten minutes to walk to school."],["spend","人","I [[spend]] an hour on homework every night."],["cost","it 或物","This bento [[costs]] NT$90."],["pay","人","I [[paid]] NT$90 for this bento."]]},"parse":{"en":"It takes me about 30 minutes to get to school by MRT.","zh":"我搭捷運上學大約要三十分鐘。","parts":[["It","S","虛主詞"],["takes","V"],["me","O","間接受詞"],["about 30 minutes","O","直接受詞"],["to get to school by MRT.","S","真主詞（不定詞）"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[It takes]] me about 30 minutes [[to get]] to school by MRT.","zh":"我搭捷運上學大約要三十分鐘。"},{"en":"My brother [[spends]] too much time [[playing]] mobile games.","zh":"我弟花太多時間打手遊。"},{"en":"[[It cost]] us NT$1,200 [[to fix]] my scooter.","zh":"修我的機車花了我們一千兩百元。"},{"en":"Lisa [[paid]] NT$3,000 [[for]] her concert ticket.","zh":"Lisa 花了三千元買演唱會門票。"}],"practice":[{"q":"It ______ me 20 minutes to ride my bike to school.","options":["spends","takes","pays"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：It takes (sb) + 時間 + to V。虛主詞 it 說做某事花多少時間，用 takes。(A) spends 的主詞要是人；(C) pays 用於付錢，不用於花時間。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Amy ______ NT$500 for her new phone case.","options":["cost","paid","bought"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：人 + pay + 錢 + for + 物。主詞 Amy 是人，付錢買東西用 paid…for。(A) cost 的主詞要是物或 it；(C) bought 後面要接買的東西，不接錢。故選 (B)。"}]},{"h":"It seems 與 seem to V","text":["that 子句和 seem 同時：**It seems (that) + S + V** = **S + seem(s) + to V**，都是「似乎…」。過去用 seemed。","that 子句的事比 seem 早發生時，用 to have + p.p.：It seems that he lied. = He seems to have lied.","seem 後面也可以直接接形容詞（She seems tired.），屬連綴動詞，詳見〈句子的基本結構〉。"],"adv":["that 子句是進行式時用 to be V-ing：It seems that he is sleeping. = He seems to be sleeping.","that 子句說未來（will）時不能直接這樣改寫：It seems that Tom will be late. 不等於 Tom seems to be late."],"formula":"It seems/seemed (that) + S + V = S + seem(s)/seemed + to V","parse":{"en":"Our new classmate seems to know a lot about baseball.","zh":"我們的新同學好像很懂棒球。","parts":[["Our new classmate","S"],["seems","V","連綴動詞"],["to know a lot about baseball.","C","不定詞當補語"]]},"ex":[{"en":"[[It seems that]] the bubble tea shop is closed today.","zh":"那家手搖飲店今天好像沒開。"},{"en":"Our new classmate [[seems to know]] a lot about baseball.","zh":"我們的新同學好像很懂棒球。"},{"en":"Mia [[seems to have caught]] a cold. She keeps coughing.","zh":"Mia 好像感冒了，一直在咳嗽。"}],"practice":[{"q":"Leo seems ______ very busy today. He hasn't answered any messages.","options":["being","to be","is"],"answer":1,"explain":"考點：S + seem(s) + to V。人當主詞時，seem 後面接不定詞 to be。(A) being 不能接在 seem 後面；(C) is 讓句子多了一個動詞。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"It seems ______ the MRT is running late again this morning.","options":["that","to","what"],"answer":0,"explain":"考點：It seems (that) + S + V。空格後 the MRT is running late 是完整句子，用 that 引導。(B) to 後面要接原形動詞；(C) what 要在子句裡當主詞或受詞，但這個子句不缺。故選 (A)。"}]}],"mistakes":[{"wrong":"It were my classmates who planned the party.","right":"It [[was]] my classmates who planned the party.","why":"強調句的 be 動詞用單數，強調部分是複數也用 was。","sec":0},{"wrong":"It is my parents who always helps me with math.","right":"It is my parents who always [[help]] me with math.","why":"強調主詞時，who 後的動詞跟它一致；parents 是複數。","sec":0},{"wrong":"It was not until midnight that my brother didn't come home.","right":"It was not until midnight that my brother [[came]] home.","why":"not 已經移到前面，that 後面要用肯定句。","sec":1},{"wrong":"I did finished my homework last night.","right":"I did [[finish]] my homework last night.","why":"did 已經表示過去，後面的動詞要用原形。","sec":2},{"wrong":"There is a boy stands at the school gate.","right":"There is a boy [[standing]] at the school gate.","why":"There is 已是句子的動詞，後面的動作要改成 V-ing。","sec":3},{"wrong":"There was a wallet leaving on the bus seat.","right":"There was a wallet [[left]] on the bus seat.","why":"錢包是「被留下」的，要用 p.p. left，不用 V-ing。","sec":3},{"wrong":"I spent three hours to finish the science report.","right":"I spent three hours [[finishing]] the science report.","why":"spend + 時間 + (in) V-ing，不接 to V。","sec":4},{"wrong":"It spent me two hours to clean my room.","right":"It [[took]] me two hours to clean my room.","why":"虛主詞 it + 時間 + to V 用 take；spend 的主詞要是人。","sec":4},{"wrong":"Ben seems that he is really tired today.","right":"Ben [[seems to be]] really tired today.","why":"人當主詞用 seem to V；要接 that 子句，主詞要用 It。","sec":5},{"wrong":"Mia seems to catch a cold. She keeps coughing.","right":"Mia seems [[to have caught]] a cold. She keeps coughing.","why":"感冒是先前發生的事，要用 seem to have + p.p.。","sec":5}],"tips":["分裂句空格填 that（強調人可用 who）；It was not until…that 後接肯定句，不加 not。","花費題：物 cost 錢；It takes sb 時間 to V；人 spend…V-ing/on N、pay…for。","the + 比較級…, the + 比較級…（越…就越…）也常考，詳見〈比較級與最高級〉。"],"quiz":[{"q":"Someone broke the classroom window. It was Tom ______ did it.","options":["whom","who","what","which"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：有人打破了教室的窗戶，是 Tom 做的。分裂句 It was + 強調部分 + that/who；強調的是人，又在子句中當主詞，用 who，不用受格 whom。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"Mr. Lee, I ______ my homework last night! I just left it at home.","options":["did finished","do finish","did finish","was finished"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：李老師，我昨晚真的有寫完作業！只是忘在家裡。強調過去的動作用 did + 原形動詞；last night 是過去，不用 do，did 後面也不能接 finished。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"Jenny spends two hours ______ the piano every day.","options":["practicing","to practice","practice","practiced"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：Jenny 每天花兩小時練鋼琴。S + spend + 時間 + (in) V-ing，spend 後面不接 to V。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"______ I want for my birthday is a new pair of running shoes.","options":["That","Which","It","What"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：我生日想要的是一雙新的慢跑鞋。空格引導的子句當主詞，且 want 缺受詞，要用 What（= the thing that）；That 子句不能缺受詞。故選 (D)。"},{"q":"These headphones ______ me only NT$800 at the night market.","options":["spent","cost","paid","bought"],"answer":1,"explain":"句意：這副耳機在夜市只花了我八百元。主詞是物，用 物 + cost + sb + 錢；spend 和 pay 的主詞要是人。故選 (B)。"},{"q":"There are only two seats ______ on the bus, so some of us have to stand.","options":["leaving","leave","left","to leave"],"answer":2,"explain":"句意：公車上只剩兩個座位，所以我們有些人得站著。There are + N + p.p. 表被動，座位是「被留下」的，用 left。故選 (C)。"},{"q":"It wasn't until I lost my phone that I ______ how much I needed it.","options":["realized","didn't realize","hadn't realized","realize"],"answer":0,"explain":"句意：直到弄丟手機，我才發現自己有多需要它。It was not until…that 的 not 已在前面，that 後面用肯定句，時態用過去式。故選 (A)。"},{"q":"It seems that Ken forgot about our plans. In other words, Ken seems ______ about our plans.","options":["to forget","forgetting","forgot","to have forgotten"],"answer":3,"explain":"句意：Ken 好像忘了我們的約。forgot 比 seems 早發生，要用 seem + to have + p.p.；to forget 表示與 seem 同時，時間不合。故選 (D)。"}]}]};
